window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Level 2 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過 Level 2 考試的學習路徑，只需回答 5 個簡單問題。","The vine and the grape":"葡萄樹與葡萄","Climate, weather and site":"氣候、天氣與園地","Choices in the vineyard":"葡萄園裡的選擇","Reading the label: origin and rules":"讀懂酒標：產地與法規","Winery choices and ageing":"酒廠的選擇與熟成","Pinot Grigio / Pinot Gris":"灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio / Pinot Gris）","Syrah / Shiraz":"希哈／希拉茲（Syrah / Shiraz）","Label terms: Burgundy, Bordeaux, Alsace, Germany":"酒標術語：布根地、波爾多、阿爾薩斯、德國","Reds of France and Spain":"法國與西班牙的紅酒","Reds of Italy":"義大利的紅酒","New World reds":"新世界的紅酒","Regional whites":"地區性白酒","Sherry":"Sherry","Serving wine":"侍酒","Tasting with a method":"有方法地品飲","From vineyard to winery":"從葡萄園到酒廠","The principal grapes":"主要葡萄品種","Regional grapes":"地區性葡萄品種","r3":"r3","Sparkling and fortified":"氣泡酒與加烈酒","s3":"s3","Service, storage and food":"侍酒、儲存與餐酒搭配","Which part of the grape gives a red wine its colour?":"葡萄的哪個部位讓紅酒有顏色？","The seeds":"葡萄籽","The stems":"果梗","Colour is held in the skins of black grapes; the pulp is almost always pale.":"顏色存在於黑葡萄的果皮中；果肉幾乎都是淺色的。","With very few exceptions, the pulp of white and black grapes is the same pale colour. The skin holds colour and tannin, both much more plentiful in black grapes. So a red wine only gains its colour if the juice stays in contact with the skins; seeds and stems mainly bring tannin, not colour.":"除了極少數例外，白葡萄和黑葡萄的果肉都是同樣的淺色。果皮含有顏色和單寧，而黑葡萄的果皮含量多得多。所以紅酒只有在葡萄汁與果皮保持接觸時才會染上顏色；葡萄籽和果梗主要帶來單寧，而不是顏色。","What is grape pulp mainly made of?":"葡萄果肉主要由什麼組成？","Water and sugar":"水和糖","Colour and flavour":"顏色和風味","Tannin and acids":"單寧和酸","Pulp is mostly water and sugar, with some acids and flavours.":"果肉主要是水和糖，還有一些酸和風味物質。","The pulp is the juicy part of the grape: water and sugar are its main components, along with acids and flavours. Colour and tannin are concentrated in the skin, while seeds and stems are rich in tannin. Knowing what each part contains helps explain how white, rosé and red wines are made.":"果肉是葡萄多汁的部分：主要成分是水和糖，另外還有酸和風味物質。顏色和單寧集中在果皮，而葡萄籽和果梗富含單寧。了解每個部位含有什麼，有助於理解白酒、粉紅酒和紅酒的釀造方式。","Why must seeds and stems be handled gently in the winery?":"為什麼在酒廠裡必須輕柔處理葡萄籽和果梗？","They are high in tannins that can make wine bitter":"它們含有大量單寧，可能讓酒變苦","They contain almost all of the grape's sugar":"它們含有葡萄幾乎所有的糖分","They are the main source of the wine's colour":"它們是葡萄酒顏色的主要來源","They release acids that make the wine too sour":"它們會釋放讓酒過酸的酸","Seeds and stems hold a lot of tannin, which turns bitter if they are handled roughly.":"葡萄籽和果梗含有大量單寧，處理過於粗暴就會變苦。","Seeds and stems contain plenty of tannin, and if they are crushed or worked roughly this passes into the wine and makes it very bitter. Sugar is found in the pulp and colour in the skins of black grapes, so the other answers give seeds and stems a role they do not play.":"葡萄籽和果梗含有大量單寧，如果被壓碎或粗暴處理，單寧就會進入酒中，讓酒非常苦澀。糖存在於果肉，顏色存在於黑葡萄的果皮，所以其他選項賦予了葡萄籽和果梗它們並不具備的作用。","Which process allows the vine to produce sugars?":"哪個過程讓葡萄樹能夠產生糖分？","Photosynthesis":"光合作用","Pollination":"授粉","In photosynthesis, sunlight lets the vine combine CO2 and water into sugars.":"光合作用中，陽光讓葡萄樹把 CO2 和水結合成糖。","The leaves take in carbon dioxide from the air and the roots take up water from the soil. Using sunlight, the vine combines these to make sugars: this is photosynthesis. The sugars fuel the plant's growth and the ripening of the grapes. Véraison, pollination and fruit set are stages in the development of the grape itself.":"葉片從空氣中吸收二氧化碳，根部從土壤中吸收水分。葡萄樹利用陽光把兩者結合成糖：這就是光合作用。這些糖為植株的生長和葡萄的成熟提供能量。轉色期、授粉和著果則是葡萄本身發育的不同階段。","Why does the vine go dormant in winter?":"為什麼葡萄樹在冬天會進入休眠？","There is not enough heat for it to grow":"熱量不足，無法生長","The soil no longer contains nutrients":"土壤中已經沒有養分","The roots stop absorbing CO2":"根部停止吸收 CO2","The plant has just been pruned":"植株剛被修剪過","Without enough heat a vine cannot grow, so in winter it stops.":"沒有足夠的熱量，葡萄樹就無法生長，所以冬天會停止生長。","Heat, supplied by the sun, is one of the vine's five needs. When it is too cold the plant cannot grow and becomes dormant, having dropped its leaves in autumn. CO2 is taken in by the leaves, not the roots, and winter pruning happens precisely because the vine is already dormant.":"由太陽提供的熱量是葡萄樹的五大需求之一。天氣太冷時，植株無法生長而進入休眠，葉子在秋天就已掉落。CO2 是由葉片而不是根部吸收的，而冬季修剪正是因為葡萄樹已經在休眠才進行的。","What does the vine take in through its leaves?":"葡萄樹透過葉片吸收什麼？","Nutrients":"養分","Leaves take in CO2 from the air; water and nutrients come through the roots.":"葉片從空氣中吸收 CO2；水和養分則由根部吸收。","A vine takes what it needs either from the soil through its roots or from the air through its leaves. Carbon dioxide enters through the leaves; water and small amounts of nutrients come in through the roots. Sugars are not absorbed at all: the plant makes them itself by photosynthesis, using light, CO2 and water.":"葡萄樹所需的東西，不是透過根部從土壤中取得，就是透過葉片從空氣中取得。二氧化碳從葉片進入；水和少量養分從根部進入。糖完全不是吸收來的：植株利用光、CO2 和水，透過光合作用自己製造糖。","How are vine flowers pollinated?":"葡萄樹的花是怎麼授粉的？","They pollinate themselves":"自花授粉","By bees":"靠蜜蜂","By birds":"靠鳥類","By hand, by the grower":"由種植者人工授粉","Vines are self-pollinating, so they do not need showy flowers to attract insects.":"葡萄樹會自花授粉，所以不需要鮮豔的花朵來吸引昆蟲。","Many plants have colourful flowers to attract pollinating insects. Vines do not: their flowers pollinate themselves. Each pollinated flower can then grow seeds and swell, becoming a grape at fruit set. That is why vine flowers are small and inconspicuous.":"許多植物有色彩鮮豔的花朵來吸引授粉昆蟲。葡萄樹不需要：它的花會自花授粉。每朵授粉的花接著就能長出種子並膨大，在著果時成為一顆葡萄。這就是為什麼葡萄樹的花又小又不顯眼。","What is the stage called when the pollinated flower swells into a grape?":"授粉後的花膨大成葡萄的階段叫什麼？","Extra-ripening":"過熟","At fruit set the flower grows seeds, swells and becomes a small green grape.":"著果時，花朵長出種子、膨大，變成一顆綠色小葡萄。","The order is: flowering in spring, fruit set when the pollinated flower starts to grow seeds and swell, then summer growth, véraison in mid-summer and finally ripening. Newly set grapes are small, hard, green and unpleasant; they still need to grow and ripen to become wine grapes.":"順序是：春天開花，授粉的花開始長出種子並膨大時為著果，接著是夏季生長、盛夏的轉色期，最後是成熟。剛著果的葡萄又小又硬、呈綠色且難吃；它們還需要長大、成熟，才能成為釀酒葡萄。","What happens at véraison?":"轉色期會發生什麼？","Grapes lose their green colour and ripening begins":"葡萄褪去綠色，開始成熟","Flowers are pollinated and start forming seeds":"花朵授粉並開始形成種子","The vine drops its leaves and goes dormant":"葡萄樹落葉並進入休眠","Grapes shrivel and turn into raisins":"葡萄乾縮變成葡萄乾","Véraison marks the start of ripening, when grapes change colour.":"轉色期標誌著成熟的開始，葡萄在這時改變顏色。","By mid-summer the grapes are big enough for the vine to start ripening them. Véraison is when they lose their green colour: white grapes turn golden, black grapes go red and then purple. Pollination happens much earlier, leaf fall comes in autumn, and shrivelling only occurs if picking is delayed a long time.":"到了盛夏，葡萄已經長得夠大，葡萄樹開始讓它們成熟。轉色期就是葡萄褪去綠色的時候：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄先變紅再變紫。授粉發生得早得多，落葉在秋天，而乾縮只有在採收大幅延後時才會出現。","What colour do black grapes turn during véraison?":"黑葡萄在轉色期會變成什麼顏色？","Red, then purple":"先紅後紫","Golden, then red":"先金黃後紅","Purple, then red":"先紫後紅","Yellow, then brown":"先黃後褐","At véraison black grapes go from green to red and then purple.":"轉色期時，黑葡萄從綠色變成紅色，再變成紫色。","Véraison is the colour change that opens the ripening period. White grapes go from green to golden, while black grapes first turn red and then purple. The colour sits in the skin, which is exactly where a red wine gets its hue during winemaking.":"轉色期是開啟成熟期的顏色變化。白葡萄從綠色轉為金黃色，黑葡萄則先轉紅再轉紫。顏色存在於果皮中，而紅酒在釀造過程中正是從果皮獲得色澤。","How do acidity and sugar change during ripening?":"成熟過程中，酸度和糖分如何變化？","Acidity falls and sugar rises":"酸度下降，糖分上升","Acidity rises and sugar falls":"酸度上升，糖分下降","Both rise":"兩者都上升","Both fall":"兩者都下降","As grapes ripen they lose acidity and build up sugar.":"葡萄成熟時會失去酸度並累積糖分。","Unripe grapes are very acidic with hardly any sugar. As they ripen, they swell with water, acidity drops and sugar rises, while herbaceous notes give way to the variety's signature flavours. Only with extra-ripeness and shrivelling do acids and sugars become concentrated together, because water evaporates.":"未成熟的葡萄非常酸，幾乎沒有糖分。隨著成熟，葡萄吸水膨大，酸度下降、糖分上升，草本氣息也逐漸讓位給品種的招牌風味。只有在過熟和乾縮時，由於水分蒸發，酸和糖才會一起濃縮。","A black grape is picked with unripe tannins. Which fault is most likely in the wine?":"一批黑葡萄在單寧尚未成熟時採收。酒中最可能出現哪種缺點？","Bitterness":"苦味","Excessive sweetness":"過甜","Dried-fruit aromas":"乾果香氣","Overly deep colour":"顏色過深","Unripe tannins can make a red wine taste bitter.":"未成熟的單寧可能讓紅酒嚐起來有苦味。","During ripening, along with sugar and flavours, the tannins in black grape skins also ripen. Tannins shape the mouthfeel of red wines, but unripe tannins taste bitter. So the grower must time the harvest by checking not just the sugar level but also how ripe the tannins are.":"成熟過程中，除了糖分和風味，黑葡萄果皮中的單寧也會成熟。單寧塑造紅酒的口感，但未成熟的單寧嚐起來是苦的。所以種植者決定採收時機時，不只要檢查糖分，也要檢查單寧的成熟度。","In some white grapes, how do aromas develop as ripeness increases?":"對某些白葡萄來說，隨著成熟度提高，香氣如何發展？","From green fruit to stone fruit to tropical fruit":"從綠色水果到核果再到熱帶水果","From tropical fruit to stone fruit to green fruit":"從熱帶水果到核果再到綠色水果","From fresh fruit to cooked fruit":"從新鮮水果到煮熟的水果","From dried fruit to fresh fruit":"從乾果到新鮮水果","The riper a white grape gets, the more its aromas move from green to stone to tropical fruit.":"白葡萄越成熟，香氣就越從綠色水果轉向核果，再轉向熱帶水果。","As grapes ripen, herbaceous notes fade and varietal flavours appear. For some white grapes the typical path is green fruit, then stone fruit, then tropical fruit. The shift from fresh to cooked fruit describes black grapes instead, while dried-fruit aromas only come with extra-ripeness.":"葡萄成熟時，草本氣息減弱，品種風味出現。對某些白葡萄來說，典型的路徑是綠色水果、核果，然後是熱帶水果。從新鮮水果到煮熟水果描述的是黑葡萄，而乾果香氣只在過熟時才會出現。","Why is dry weather needed to leave grapes on the vine beyond the normal harvest?":"為什麼要把葡萄留在樹上超過正常採收期，必須有乾燥的天氣？","Rain can lead to fungal diseases":"下雨可能引發真菌病害","Rain makes acidity rise too much":"下雨會讓酸度上升太多","Rain makes the skins darker":"下雨會讓果皮顏色變深","Rain stops photosynthesis":"下雨會中止光合作用","Rain brings moisture that encourages fungi which can spoil the grapes.":"下雨帶來濕氣，助長可能破壞葡萄的真菌。","For extra-ripening the weather must stay dry, because rain encourages fungal diseases, and warm enough for ripening to carry on. Under these conditions aromas become riper, sugar rises and, over time, the grapes shrivel, concentrating sugars and acids: ideal fruit for sweet wines.":"要讓葡萄過熟，天氣必須保持乾燥，因為下雨會助長真菌病害；也必須夠溫暖，讓成熟得以持續。在這樣的條件下，香氣變得更成熟、糖分上升，久而久之葡萄乾縮，糖和酸隨之濃縮：這是釀造甜酒的理想果實。","A grape left on the vine for a long time shrivels. Which aromas does it tend to develop?":"一顆葡萄在樹上留了很久而乾縮。它傾向於發展出哪種香氣？","Dried fruit":"乾果","Herbaceous":"草本","Green fruit":"綠色水果","Fresh floral":"清新花香","As the grapes shrivel, water evaporates and dried-fruit aromas appear.":"葡萄乾縮時水分蒸發，乾果香氣隨之出現。","In the early stages of extra-ripeness, aromas become very ripe and sugar rises. If the grapes stay on the vine longer, water evaporates and they turn almost into raisins: acids and sugars concentrate and dried-fruit aromas develop. Herbaceous and green-fruit notes, by contrast, are typical of unripe grapes.":"在過熟的初期，香氣變得非常成熟，糖分上升。如果葡萄在樹上留得更久，水分蒸發，它們幾乎變成葡萄乾：酸和糖濃縮，發展出乾果香氣。相反地，草本和綠色水果的氣息是未成熟葡萄的典型特徵。","Which of these is NOT one of the five things a vine needs?":"下列哪一項不是葡萄樹的五大需求之一？","Insects to pollinate its flowers":"為花朵授粉的昆蟲","Warmth":"溫暖","Carbon dioxide taken from the air by the leaves":"葉片從空氣中吸收的二氧化碳","Vines pollinate themselves: they need warmth, sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and nutrients, not insects.":"葡萄樹會自花授粉：它需要溫暖、陽光、二氧化碳、水和養分，而不需要昆蟲。","A vine's five needs are warmth, sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and nutrients, so warmth, CO2 and nutrients are all essential. Unlike many plants with bright flowers, the vine does not need to attract insects, because its flowers pollinate themselves.":"葡萄樹的五大需求是溫暖、陽光、二氧化碳、水和養分，所以溫暖、CO2 和養分都不可或缺。不同於許多花朵鮮豔的植物，葡萄樹不需要吸引昆蟲，因為它的花會自花授粉。","Through which part does the vine take up water and nutrients?":"葡萄樹透過哪個部位吸收水和養分？","The roots":"根部","The leaves":"葉片","The flowers, during spring":"春天時的花朵","The skins of the ripening grapes":"成熟中的葡萄果皮","Water and nutrients come from the soil and are taken up by the roots.":"水和養分來自土壤，由根部吸收。","Because it is rooted to the ground, the vine takes what it needs either from the soil, through its roots, or from the air, through its leaves. The leaves take in carbon dioxide, not water. Flowers and grape skins play no part in this.":"由於扎根於地面，葡萄樹所需的東西不是透過根部從土壤中取得，就是透過葉片從空氣中取得。葉片吸收的是二氧化碳，不是水。花朵和葡萄果皮在這方面都不起作用。","What does the vine use the sugars made by photosynthesis for?":"葡萄樹用光合作用產生的糖來做什麼？","To power its growth and ripen its grapes":"為生長提供能量，並讓葡萄成熟","To protect itself from frost during winter dormancy":"在冬季休眠期保護自己免受霜害","To attract insects to its flowers":"吸引昆蟲到花朵上","To make tannins in the seeds":"在葡萄籽中製造單寧","Sugars from photosynthesis fuel the plant's growth and the ripening of its grapes.":"光合作用產生的糖為植株生長和葡萄成熟提供能量。","Sunlight lets the vine combine CO2 and water into sugars, which are its source of energy. In winter the vine is dormant because there is not enough heat, not because it uses sugar against frost. It has no need to attract insects, since it pollinates itself.":"陽光讓葡萄樹把 CO2 和水結合成糖，這是它的能量來源。葡萄樹冬天休眠是因為熱量不足，而不是因為用糖來抵抗霜凍。它也不需要吸引昆蟲，因為它會自花授粉。","How long can a vine live?":"葡萄樹可以活多久？","60 years or more":"60 年或更久","A single growing season":"只有一個生長季","About 5 years, then it must be replaced":"大約 5 年，之後就必須更換","No more than 15–20 years in most vineyards":"在多數葡萄園裡不超過 15–20 年","The vine is a long-lived plant that can live for 60 years or more, repeating the same cycle every year.":"葡萄樹是長壽的植物，可以活 60 年或更久，每年重複同樣的週期。","The vine is not an annual plant: each spring it starts again from the same trunk. This long life is what makes 'old vines' possible, prized for the quality of their grapes. The other lifespans offered are far too short.":"葡萄樹不是一年生植物：每年春天都從同一根主幹重新開始。正是這種長壽造就了備受珍視、葡萄品質出眾的「老藤」。其他選項的壽命都太短了。","Which description of the vine's yearly cycle is correct?":"下列哪一項對葡萄樹年度週期的描述是正確的？","Shoots and flowers in spring, ripe grapes by late summer, leaves dropping in autumn":"春天長出新梢和花朵，夏末葡萄成熟，秋天落葉","Flowers in winter, fruit in spring, dormancy in summer":"冬天開花，春天結果，夏天休眠","Leaves dropping in spring, flowers in summer and grapes ripe only in the middle of winter":"春天落葉，夏天開花，直到隆冬葡萄才成熟","Continuous growth all year, with no real pause":"全年持續生長，沒有真正的停頓","The growing season runs from spring to autumn; in winter the vine rests.":"生長季從春天持續到秋天；冬天葡萄樹休息。","In spring the vine grows shoots, leaves and flowers; by late summer the flowers have become ripe grapes. Leaf fall in autumn ends the season, and in winter the plant is dormant because it is too cold to grow. Year-round growth is therefore impossible.":"春天葡萄樹長出新梢、葉子和花朵；到了夏末，花朵已經變成成熟的葡萄。秋天落葉結束這一季，冬天植株因為太冷無法生長而休眠。所以全年生長是不可能的。","Riesling and Cabernet Sauvignon differ greatly in colour and flavour. What are they, botanically?":"麗絲玲和卡本內蘇維濃在顏色和風味上差異很大。從植物學上看，它們是什麼？","Two varieties of the same European species":"同一個歐洲物種的兩個品種","Two different species, one European and one American":"兩個不同物種，一個是歐洲種，一個是美洲種","Two wild species gathered in nature":"在野外採集的兩個野生物種","Two recent crosses between North American and Asian species":"北美與亞洲物種的兩個近期雜交種","Almost all wine comes from one European species, which exists in many different varieties.":"幾乎所有葡萄酒都來自同一個歐洲物種，它有許多不同的品種。","There are several vine species native to Eurasia or North America, but wine is almost always made from the European one. Its varieties differ in the look of the grapes, their taste and their flavours. Wine grapes are not gathered from the wild either: they are grown in carefully managed vineyards.":"原生於歐亞大陸或北美洲的葡萄屬物種有好幾種，但葡萄酒幾乎都是用歐洲種釀造的。它的各個品種在葡萄外觀、味道和風味上各不相同。釀酒葡萄也不是從野外採集的：它們種植在精心管理的葡萄園裡。","What does each cluster of vine flowers become?":"葡萄樹的每一串花會變成什麼？","A bunch of grapes":"一串葡萄","A new shoot for the following year":"來年的一根新梢","One single, very large grape":"一顆非常大的葡萄","A leaf, while the single flowers become grapes":"一片葉子，而單朵花才會變成葡萄","Each flower cluster becomes a bunch of grapes; each pollinated flower becomes one grape.":"每一串花會變成一串葡萄；每一朵授粉的花會變成一顆葡萄。","In spring the vine produces clusters of flowers. Each individual flower, once pollinated, grows seeds and swells into a grape, and together they form the bunch. That is why poor flowering directly reduces the crop.":"春天葡萄樹長出一串串花。每一朵花授粉後長出種子並膨大成一顆葡萄，合起來就成了一串葡萄。這就是為什麼開花不良會直接減少收成。","What is the correct order of the stages of grape formation?":"葡萄形成各階段的正確順序是什麼？","Flowering, fruit set, véraison, ripening":"開花、著果、轉色期、成熟","Fruit set, flowering, ripening, véraison":"著果、開花、成熟、轉色期","Flowering, véraison, fruit set, ripening":"開花、轉色期、著果、成熟","Véraison, flowering, ripening and finally fruit set":"轉色期、開花、成熟，最後著果","First the flower, then the green grape (fruit set), then the colour change (véraison) that starts ripening.":"先是花，然後是綠色的葡萄（著果），接著是開啟成熟的顏色變化（轉色期）。","The vine flowers in spring, and the pollinated flower becomes a small, hard, green grape. In mid-summer véraison marks the start of ripening, which continues until harvest. Véraison cannot come before fruit set: without a grape there is nothing to change colour.":"葡萄樹在春天開花，授粉的花變成一顆又小又硬的綠色葡萄。盛夏時，轉色期標誌著成熟的開始，成熟一直持續到採收。轉色期不可能在著果之前：沒有葡萄，就沒有東西可以變色。","What colour do white grapes turn at véraison?":"白葡萄在轉色期會變成什麼顏色？","Golden":"金黃色","Dark green":"深綠色","Brown, like a raisin":"像葡萄乾一樣的褐色","At véraison grapes lose their green: white grapes turn golden, black grapes red and then purple.":"轉色期時葡萄褪去綠色：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄先變紅再變紫。","Véraison happens in mid-summer and marks the start of ripening. The red-then-purple change applies to black grapes, not white ones. A brown, shrivelled look only appears much later, if grapes stay on the vine until they turn into raisins.":"轉色期發生在盛夏，標誌著成熟的開始。先紅後紫的變化是黑葡萄的，不是白葡萄的。褐色、乾縮的外觀要晚得多才會出現，只有當葡萄留在樹上直到變成葡萄乾時才會這樣。","At the start of ripening, what is a grape like?":"成熟剛開始時，葡萄是什麼樣子？","Very acidic, with hardly any sugar and a herbaceous taste":"非常酸，幾乎沒有糖分，帶有草本味道","Sweet, low in acid, with tropical fruit aromas":"甜、低酸，帶有熱帶水果香氣","Soft and juicy, already showing its signature aromas":"柔軟多汁，已經展現出招牌香氣","High in sugar, but with tannins still unripe in the pulp":"糖分高，但果肉中的單寧仍未成熟","Before ripening, the grape is very acidic, low in sugar and has an unattractive herbaceous taste.":"成熟之前，葡萄非常酸、糖分低，還帶有不討喜的草本味道。","During ripening the grape swells with water and softens, acidity falls, sugar rises and herbaceous notes give way to the variety's signature aromas. Sweetness and tropical fruit therefore belong to a ripe grape, not the start of ripening. Tannins, meanwhile, are in the skin, not the pulp.":"成熟過程中，葡萄吸水膨大並變軟，酸度下降，糖分上升，草本氣息讓位給品種的招牌香氣。所以甜味和熱帶水果屬於成熟的葡萄，而不是成熟剛開始時。至於單寧，它存在於果皮，而不是果肉。","As a black grape ripens, how do its aromas change?":"黑葡萄成熟時，香氣如何變化？","From tropical fruit to green fruit":"從熱帶水果到綠色水果","From cooked fruit to fresh fruit":"從煮熟的水果到新鮮水果","From vanilla and coconut to crunchy red fruit":"從香草和椰子到爽脆的紅色水果","In black grapes, rising ripeness moves the flavours from fresh fruit towards cooked fruit.":"對黑葡萄來說，成熟度提高會讓風味從新鮮水果轉向煮熟的水果。","The green-to-stone-to-tropical sequence applies to some white grapes, and runs in that direction, not the reverse. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak, not from the grape. For black grapes, the marker is the move from fresh to cooked fruit.":"綠色水果到核果再到熱帶水果的順序適用於某些白葡萄，而且是這個方向，不是相反。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是來自葡萄。對黑葡萄來說，指標是從新鮮水果轉向煮熟的水果。","What do tannins contribute to a red wine?":"單寧為紅酒帶來什麼？","To its mouthfeel":"口感","To its red colour, which comes entirely from the tannins in the seeds":"紅色，完全來自葡萄籽中的單寧","To its sweetness":"甜味","To its alcohol level":"酒精濃度","Tannins from black grape skins give red wines their mouthfeel.":"來自黑葡萄果皮的單寧賦予紅酒口感。","Tannins are compounds in the skins of black grapes (and also in seeds and stems), and they ripen during the ripening period. Colour comes from skin pigments, not seeds. Sweetness and alcohol depend on sugar, not on tannin.":"單寧是存在於黑葡萄果皮（以及葡萄籽和果梗）中的化合物，會在成熟期間逐漸成熟。顏色來自果皮的色素，不是葡萄籽。甜味和酒精取決於糖分，與單寧無關。","Why does a grape left on the vine until it shrivels have more concentrated sugars and acids?":"為什麼留在樹上直到乾縮的葡萄，糖和酸會更濃縮？","Because the water in the grape evaporates":"因為葡萄中的水分蒸發了","Because a fungus pierces the skin":"因為真菌刺穿了果皮","Because the water freezes inside the grape":"因為葡萄裡的水結冰了","Because the vine keeps pumping sugar and acid into the grapes even after its leaves have fallen":"因為即使葉子掉光，葡萄樹仍持續把糖和酸送進葡萄","With a long hang time the water evaporates and the grape becomes a raisin, concentrating sugars and acids.":"長時間掛在樹上，水分蒸發，葡萄變成葡萄乾，糖和酸隨之濃縮。","This is raisining on the vine, which also brings dried-fruit aromas. The fungus that pierces the skin is Botrytis (noble rot) and freezing the water is how icewine is made: two other ways of concentrating sugar. A vine with no leaves can no longer make sugar by photosynthesis.":"這就是在樹上風乾成葡萄乾，同時也會帶來乾果香氣。刺穿果皮的真菌是貴腐菌（Botrytis），而讓水結冰是冰酒的釀造方式：這是另外兩種濃縮糖分的方法。沒有葉子的葡萄樹已經無法透過光合作用製造糖。","In the early stages of extra-ripeness, what happens to the grapes?":"在過熟的初期，葡萄會發生什麼？","They develop exaggerated ripe aromas and build up more sugar":"發展出誇張的成熟香氣，累積更多糖分","They lose sugar and regain herbaceous notes":"失去糖分，重新出現草本氣息","They shrivel at once and taste of dried fruit":"立刻乾縮，嚐起來有乾果味","They turn green and hard again, as just after fruit set":"重新變綠變硬，就像剛著果時一樣","Early extra-ripeness exaggerates ripe aromas and increases sugar; shrivelling only comes later.":"過熟初期會放大成熟香氣並提高糖分；乾縮要晚一點才會出現。","If grapes stay on the vine past the normal harvest, in dry and warm enough weather, they keep developing. Only after a longer period does water evaporate, the grapes shrivel and dried-fruit notes appear. Herbaceous notes belong to unripe grapes.":"如果葡萄在正常採收期之後仍留在樹上，而天氣夠乾燥、夠溫暖，它們會繼續發展。要再過較長一段時間，水分才會蒸發，葡萄乾縮，出現乾果氣息。草本氣息則屬於未成熟的葡萄。","Where in the grape are flavours most concentrated?":"葡萄的風味最集中在哪裡？","In the skin and just beneath it":"果皮及其正下方","In the seeds":"葡萄籽","In the stem holding the bunch":"支撐果串的果梗","At the centre of the pulp, far from the skin, where there is most water":"果肉中心，遠離果皮、水分最多的地方","The skin and the area immediately below it hold high levels of flavour.":"果皮及其正下方的區域含有大量風味物質。","The pulp also contains acids and flavours, but it is mostly water and sugar. Seeds and stems are known for tannins, which can turn bitter if handled roughly. This is why contact with the skins matters so much to a wine's flavour.":"果肉也含有酸和風味物質，但主要是水和糖。葡萄籽和果梗以單寧著稱，處理粗暴時可能變苦。這就是為什麼與果皮的接觸對葡萄酒的風味如此重要。","Which parts of the grape and bunch contain tannins?":"葡萄和果串的哪些部位含有單寧？","Skins, seeds and stems":"果皮、葡萄籽和果梗","Only the pulp":"只有果肉","Pulp and juice, but never the skin or seeds":"果肉和果汁，但絕不在果皮或葡萄籽中","Only the stems":"只有果梗","Tannins are in the skins, especially of black grapes, and at high levels in seeds and stems.":"單寧存在於果皮中（尤其是黑葡萄），在葡萄籽和果梗中的含量也很高。","The pulp is mainly water, sugar, acids and flavours, not tannin. Tannins from black skins give red wines their structure, while those from seeds and stems can make wine bitter if crushed roughly. That is why winemakers handle them gently.":"果肉主要是水、糖、酸和風味物質，不是單寧。黑葡萄果皮的單寧賦予紅酒結構，而葡萄籽和果梗的單寧若被粗暴壓碎，可能讓酒變苦。所以釀酒師會輕柔地處理它們。","Climate is the long-term average, weather is what happens day to day":"氣候是長期平均，天氣是每天發生的狀況","Climate changes every year, weather stays stable for decades":"氣候每年都在變，天氣則數十年保持穩定","Climate covers only rainfall, weather only temperature":"氣候只涵蓋降雨，天氣只涵蓋溫度","Climate refers to one vineyard, weather to a whole country":"氣候指的是一座葡萄園，天氣指的是整個國家","Climate is the long-term average pattern; weather is what actually happens each day.":"氣候是長期的平均模式；天氣是每天實際發生的狀況。","Climate describes the average levels of temperature, sunlight and rainfall a region can expect; it does not change from year to year, though it can shift over decades. Weather is what actually happens day to day: cool or hot vintages, frost, hail and sudden downpours are all matters of weather.":"氣候描述的是一個產區可預期的平均溫度、日照和降雨水準；它不會年年改變，但可能在數十年間轉變。天氣則是每天實際發生的事：涼爽或炎熱的年份、霜凍、冰雹和突如其來的大雨，都屬於天氣。","A region has an average growing season temperature of 15.5°C. How is its climate classified?":"某產區生長季的平均溫度為 15.5°C。它的氣候屬於哪一類？","An average growing season temperature of 16.5°C or below counts as cool.":"生長季平均溫度在 16.5°C 以下屬於涼爽氣候。","The three bands used are: cool, 16.5°C (62°F) or below; moderate, 16.5 to 18.5°C (62 to 65°F); warm, 18.5 to 21°C (65 to 70°F). At 15.5°C the region is below the 16.5°C threshold, so its climate is cool. Such a climate tends to give grapes with higher acidity and less-ripe flavours.":"使用的三個區間是：涼爽，16.5°C（62°F）以下；溫和，16.5 至 18.5°C（62 至 65°F）；溫暖，18.5 至 21°C（65 至 70°F）。15.5°C 低於 16.5°C 的門檻，所以這個產區屬於涼爽氣候。這樣的氣候往往讓葡萄酸度較高、風味較不成熟。","When does the growing season run in the southern hemisphere?":"南半球的生長季在什麼時候？","January to June":"1 月到 6 月","July to December":"7 月到 12 月","In the southern hemisphere the season runs October to April, the reverse of the north.":"南半球的生長季是 10 月到 4 月，與北半球相反。","Seasons are reversed between the two hemispheres. In the northern hemisphere the growing season runs from April to October; in the southern hemisphere from October to April. That is why the Australian harvest happens early in the calendar year, while California's comes towards the end.":"南北半球的季節相反。北半球的生長季從 4 月到 10 月；南半球則從 10 月到 4 月。這就是為什麼澳洲在年初採收，而加州的採收接近年底。","Which grape is given as an example of a variety that only ripens well in warm climates?":"哪個品種被舉例為只有在溫暖氣候才能好好成熟的品種？","Grenache can only grow and ripen successfully in warm climates.":"格那希只能在溫暖氣候中順利生長和成熟。","Temperature decides which varieties can grow in a region. Grenache is the example of a grape that needs a warm climate to ripen. Chardonnay is the opposite example: it grows well in a range of climates but develops different flavours depending on the heat available.":"溫度決定了一個產區能種哪些品種。格那希是需要溫暖氣候才能成熟的例子。夏多內則是相反的例子：它在各種氣候中都長得很好，但會依可得的熱量發展出不同的風味。","What is the most important factor influencing a wine region's climate?":"影響葡萄酒產區氣候最重要的因素是什麼？","Soil type":"土壤類型","Nearness to a river":"鄰近河流","Slope aspect":"坡向","Latitude is the main factor: the closer to the equator, the hotter.":"緯度是主要因素：越接近赤道越熱。","The closer a region is to the equator, the hotter it tends to be. That is why most vineyards lie between 30° and 50° north or south: outside this band it is usually too hot or too cold. Soil, rivers and aspect can then modify the climate of an area or a single vineyard.":"產區越接近赤道，往往越熱。這就是為什麼大多數葡萄園位於南北緯 30° 到 50° 之間：在這個範圍之外通常太熱或太冷。土壤、河流和坡向則可以調節一個地區或單一葡萄園的氣候。","Between which latitudes are most vineyards found?":"大多數葡萄園位於哪兩個緯度之間？","Between 30° and 50° north or south":"南北緯 30° 到 50° 之間","Between 10° and 30° north or south":"南北緯 10° 到 30° 之間","Between 40° and 60° north or south":"南北緯 40° 到 60° 之間","Between 0° and 20° north or south":"南北緯 0° 到 20° 之間","Nearly all vineyards lie between 30° and 50° latitude in both hemispheres.":"幾乎所有葡萄園都位於南北半球緯度 30° 到 50° 之間。","The band between 30° and 50° latitude, north and south of the equator, offers temperatures suited to vines. Closer to the equator it is usually too hot, and further away too cold, for vines to survive. Within the band, altitude, seas, mountains and aspect fine-tune the local climate.":"赤道南北緯度 30° 到 50° 之間的地帶，提供了適合葡萄樹的溫度。越接近赤道通常太熱，越遠離則太冷，葡萄樹難以存活。在這個地帶內，海拔、海洋、山脈和坡向會微調當地氣候。","Two vineyards are at the same latitude, but one is much higher. What should you expect of the higher vineyard?":"兩座葡萄園位於同一緯度，但其中一座海拔高得多。你可以預期海拔較高的葡萄園會怎樣？","A cooler climate":"氣候較涼爽","A warmer climate":"氣候較溫暖","The same climate":"氣候相同","More summer rain":"夏季雨量較多","Temperature drops with altitude, so the higher vineyard is cooler.":"溫度隨海拔升高而下降，所以海拔較高的葡萄園較涼爽。","At the same latitude, a higher vineyard always has a cooler climate. This slows ripening: grapes tend to keep more acidity and build up sugar more slowly. Altitude is therefore a way to make fresher wines even in regions that would be warm because of their latitude.":"在同一緯度上，海拔較高的葡萄園氣候一定較涼爽。這會減緩成熟：葡萄往往保留較多酸度，糖分累積也較慢。因此，即使在因緯度而偏溫暖的產區，海拔也是釀出較清爽葡萄酒的一種方式。","Why does a vineyard on a slope facing the equator produce riper grapes?":"為什麼面向赤道的坡地葡萄園能產出較成熟的葡萄？","It receives more heat and light":"它接收到更多熱量和光照","It receives more rain":"它接收到更多雨水","It has more nutrient-rich soils":"它的土壤養分更豐富","It is more exposed to fog":"它更容易受霧氣影響","A slope facing the equator gets more heat and light, so grapes ripen more.":"面向赤道的坡地接收到更多熱量和光照，所以葡萄更成熟。","Far from the equator, light and heat are scarce and ripening grapes is hard. Planting on a slope facing the equator increases the heat and light reaching the vines. The result is riper grapes than those from a vineyard on flat land or on a slope facing the other way.":"在遠離赤道的地方，光照和熱量都很稀少，葡萄很難成熟。種在面向赤道的坡地上，可以增加葡萄樹接收到的熱量和光照。結果是葡萄比平地或背向坡地的葡萄園更成熟。","What effect do cold ocean currents have on the vineyards of the Cape in South Africa?":"寒冷洋流對南非 Cape 產區的葡萄園有什麼影響？","They cool a warm climate":"為溫暖的氣候降溫","They warm a cool climate":"讓涼爽的氣候變暖","They increase summer rainfall":"增加夏季降雨","They encourage noble rot":"促進貴腐菌生長","Cold currents moderate the Cape's warm climate by cooling it.":"寒冷洋流讓 Cape 溫暖的氣候變得涼爽而溫和。","Warm regions close to the sea can benefit from a moderating influence. In the Cape's grape-growing areas, the climate is cooled by cold ocean currents. The opposite happens in northern Europe, where warm currents warm the vineyards. Breezes blowing in from cold seas also cool coastal areas.":"靠近海洋的溫暖產區可以受益於海洋的調節作用。在 Cape 的葡萄種植區，氣候受到寒冷洋流的冷卻。北歐則相反，溫暖的洋流讓葡萄園變暖。從寒冷海面吹來的微風也會讓沿海地區降溫。","In a cool region, how does a river near the vineyard help?":"在涼爽產區，葡萄園附近的河流有什麼幫助？","It gives warmth, protects from frost and extends ripening":"提供溫暖、防止霜害並延長成熟期","It cools the vineyard and lowers sugar levels":"讓葡萄園降溫並降低糖分","It blocks light and slows photosynthesis":"遮擋光線並減緩光合作用","It shelters the vineyard from cloud and rain":"為葡萄園遮擋雲層和雨水","Rivers hold warmth in autumn, protect against frost and extend the ripening period.":"河流在秋天保有溫暖，防止霜害並延長成熟期。","Rivers warm up and cool down more slowly than land, so in autumn they are warmer than the ground around them. In cool regions they provide warmth, help prevent frost and extend the period warm enough to ripen grapes. They also reflect sunlight. Sheltering vineyards from cloud and rain is the role of mountains, not rivers.":"河流升溫和降溫都比陸地慢，所以秋天時比周圍的土地溫暖。在涼爽產區，河流提供溫暖，有助於防止霜害，並延長足以讓葡萄成熟的溫暖期。河流也會反射陽光。為葡萄園遮擋雲層和雨水是山脈的作用，不是河流。","In which areas is fog an important cooling influence?":"霧氣在哪些地區是重要的降溫因素？","Coastal California and Chile":"加州和智利的沿海地區","Warm regions of Australia":"澳洲的溫暖產區","The Cape regions of South Africa":"南非的 Cape 產區","Northern European vineyards":"北歐的葡萄園","Fog forms at ground level and cools coastal California and Chile.":"霧氣在地面形成，讓加州和智利的沿海地區降溫。","Fog is water vapour that forms at ground level and cools the vineyard; it is a very important moderating influence in coastal California and Chile. In some warmer Australian regions, cloud cover matters instead by reducing sunlight, while at the Cape the key factor is cold ocean currents.":"霧是在地面形成的水氣，會讓葡萄園降溫；它在加州和智利沿海地區是非常重要的調節因素。在澳洲某些較溫暖的產區，重要的反而是減少日照的雲層，而在 Cape，關鍵因素是寒冷洋流。","How can stones on the soil surface help ripening?":"土壤表面的石頭如何幫助成熟？","They absorb heat and warm the vineyard":"吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖","They hold more water for the vine":"為葡萄樹保存更多水分","They add nutrients to the soil":"為土壤增添養分","They shelter the vines from wind":"為葡萄樹擋風","Stones absorb heat and make the vineyard warmer, which helps ripening.":"石頭吸收熱量讓葡萄園變暖，有助於成熟。","Soil supplies water and nutrients, but it can also affect vineyard temperature. When the surface is covered in stones, they absorb heat and make the vineyard warmer. That extra heat can help grapes ripen, which is especially useful where the climate struggles to deliver full ripeness.":"土壤提供水和養分，但也可能影響葡萄園的溫度。當地表覆蓋著石頭時，石頭會吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖。這些額外的熱量有助於葡萄成熟，在氣候難以讓葡萄完全成熟的地方特別有用。","What typically happens to grapes in a cooler-than-normal vintage?":"在比平常涼爽的年份，葡萄通常會怎樣？","Acidity too high and sugar too low":"酸度太高，糖分太低","Acidity too low and sugar too high":"酸度太低，糖分太高","Dried-fruit aromas and sunburn":"乾果香氣和日灼","Swollen grapes with diluted flavours":"葡萄膨脹，風味被稀釋","With little heat and light, grapes struggle to ripen and stay acidic and low in sugar.":"熱量和光照不足時，葡萄難以成熟，維持高酸低糖。","In a cool vintage temperatures are lower and sunlight less bright than usual, so the vine struggles to ripen its grapes. Acidity stays too high, sugar too low and the variety's signature aromas may not develop. Dried-fruit aromas and sunburn point instead to a very hot vintage.":"在涼爽的年份，溫度比平常低、陽光也不如平常強，葡萄樹難以讓葡萄成熟。酸度維持太高，糖分太低，品種的招牌香氣也可能發展不出來。乾果香氣和日灼則指向非常炎熱的年份。","Why can heavy rain just before harvest reduce grape quality?":"為什麼採收前的大雨會降低葡萄品質？","Grapes swell with water and flavours are diluted":"葡萄吸水膨脹，風味被稀釋","Grapes dry out and turn into raisins":"葡萄乾掉變成葡萄乾","The skins become too dark":"果皮變得太深色","The vine immediately goes dormant":"葡萄樹立刻進入休眠","Excess water in the soil makes the grapes swell, diluting their flavours.":"土壤中過多的水分讓葡萄膨脹，稀釋了風味。","Heavy rain causes two problems. The moisture helps fungal diseases spread, which can reduce both the quantity and quality of grapes. And if heavy rain falls close to harvest, the excess water in the soil makes the grapes swell and dilutes their flavours, so the wine may be less concentrated.":"大雨會造成兩個問題。濕氣助長真菌病害蔓延，可能同時降低葡萄的產量和品質。而如果大雨落在採收前不久，土壤中過多的水分會讓葡萄膨脹、稀釋風味，酒就可能比較不濃郁。","Why are spring frosts particularly dangerous for vines?":"為什麼春霜對葡萄樹特別危險？","They damage new growth and reduce the crop":"它會損害新生枝葉，減少收成","They shrivel grapes that are already ripe":"它會讓已經成熟的葡萄乾縮","They dilute the flavours of the grapes":"它會稀釋葡萄的風味","They cause sunburn on the skins":"它會讓果皮日灼","In spring, frost kills new shoots, so there will be fewer bunches.":"春天的霜凍會凍死新梢，所以果串會變少。","In spring the vine is producing shoots, leaves and flowers. A frost at this point can damage or kill the new growth, reducing the number of bunches the plant can carry that year. The result is a smaller crop. Hail also cuts yields, but by striking vines and grapes at any point in the season.":"春天葡萄樹正在長出新梢、葉子和花朵。這時的霜凍可能損害甚至凍死新生枝葉，減少植株當年能承載的果串數量。結果就是收成變少。冰雹也會降低產量，但它是在生長季的任何時候打傷葡萄樹和葡萄。","Which months does the growing season cover in the northern hemisphere?":"北半球的生長季涵蓋哪幾個月？","All year round, without a break":"全年無休","In the northern hemisphere the season runs April to October; in the southern, October to April.":"北半球的生長季是 4 月到 10 月；南半球是 10 月到 4 月。","The seasons are reversed between the hemispheres, and so is the growing season. October to April is the southern calendar, for example in Australia or Chile. The vine is dormant in winter, so it does not grow all year.":"南北半球的季節相反，生長季也是如此。10 月到 4 月是南半球的時間表，例如澳洲或智利。葡萄樹冬天休眠，所以不會全年生長。","A region has an average growing season temperature of 17.5°C. How is its climate classified?":"某產區生長季的平均溫度為 17.5°C。它的氣候屬於哪一類？","Too cold to ripen any grape variety":"太冷，任何葡萄品種都無法成熟","An average between 16.5°C and 18.5°C means a moderate climate.":"平均溫度介於 16.5°C 與 18.5°C 之間屬於溫和氣候。","Cool means 16.5°C or below, warm 18.5°C to 21°C. At 17.5°C the region sits in between. A moderate climate ripens many varieties, so the last option is wrong.":"涼爽是指 16.5°C 以下，溫暖是 18.5°C 至 21°C。17.5°C 的產區介於兩者之間。溫和氣候能讓許多品種成熟，所以最後一個選項是錯的。","Why is Chardonnay given as an example when discussing climate?":"討論氣候時，為什麼會以夏多內為例？","It grows well in different climates, but its flavours change with climate":"它在不同氣候中都長得好，但風味會隨氣候改變","It only ripens in warm climates":"它只在溫暖氣候中成熟","It tastes the same wherever it is grown":"無論種在哪裡，嚐起來都一樣","It can only be grown in cool climates, near rivers or the sea":"它只能種在涼爽氣候、靠近河流或海洋的地方","Chardonnay adapts to many climates, but develops different flavours depending on temperature.":"夏多內能適應多種氣候，但會依溫度發展出不同的風味。","Temperature decides both which varieties can grow and which flavours they develop. Grenache is the example of a variety that only ripens in warm climates. Chardonnay, by contrast, grows in cool, moderate and warm climates with different flavour profiles.":"溫度既決定哪些品種能種植，也決定它們發展出什麼風味。格那希是只在溫暖氣候中成熟的品種的例子。相反地，夏多內在涼爽、溫和和溫暖氣候中都能生長，風味特徵各不相同。","What effect do warm ocean currents have on the vineyards of northern Europe?":"溫暖洋流對北歐的葡萄園有什麼影響？","They warm them":"讓它們變暖","They cool them":"讓它們降溫","They bring fogs that encourage noble rot every vintage":"每個年份都帶來助長貴腐菌的霧氣","They have no effect":"沒有影響","In northern Europe, warm ocean currents have a warming influence on the climate.":"在北歐，溫暖洋流對氣候有增溫作用。","The sea moderates climate both ways. In South Africa's Cape, cold currents cool a warm climate; in northern Europe, warm currents help a cold one. The morning mists linked to noble rot come mainly from rivers in autumn.":"海洋對氣候的調節是雙向的。在南非的 Cape，寒冷洋流讓溫暖的氣候降溫；在北歐，溫暖洋流則幫助寒冷的氣候。與貴腐菌相關的晨霧主要來自秋天的河流。","How can mountains cool a warm vineyard lower down at night?":"山脈如何在夜間讓低處溫暖的葡萄園降溫？","Cold air flows down from the mountains to lower altitudes":"冷空氣從山上流向較低的海拔","They block warm ocean currents":"它們阻擋溫暖洋流","They shade the vineyard all night":"它們整晚為葡萄園遮蔭","They hold clouds over the vineyard and stop heat escaping":"它們把雲留在葡萄園上方，阻止熱量散失","At night cold mountain air moves downhill and cools vineyards where heat built up during the day.":"夜間，山上的冷空氣往下坡移動，讓白天累積熱量的葡萄園降溫。","Cool air, whether from the sea or mountains, moderates the climate. Shade means nothing at night, as the sun has already set. If anything, mountains shelter vineyards from cloud, rain and cold winds; they do not trap clouds over them.":"無論來自海洋還是山脈，涼爽的空氣都能調節氣候。遮蔭在夜間沒有意義，因為太陽已經下山了。山脈頂多是為葡萄園遮擋雲層、雨水和冷風，而不是把雲困在葡萄園上方。","A vineyard is sheltered by a mountain range. Which conditions is it most likely to enjoy?":"一座葡萄園受到山脈的屏障。它最可能享有哪些條件？","Sunny summers, dry autumns and a longer growing season":"陽光充足的夏天、乾燥的秋天和較長的生長季","More rain and more cloud":"更多雨水和雲層","Thick fog every summer morning":"每個夏日清晨都有濃霧","Constant cold winds that shorten ripening in autumn":"持續的冷風，縮短秋天的成熟期","Mountains act as a barrier to cloud, rain and cold winds, extending the season.":"山脈是阻擋雲、雨和冷風的屏障，能延長生長季。","Because they block cloud and rain, mountains bring sunny summers and dry autumns. Shelter from cold winds lets grapes ripen for longer, not shorter. Thick fogs are typical of some coastal areas, such as California and Chile.":"由於阻擋了雲和雨，山脈帶來陽光充足的夏天和乾燥的秋天。擋住冷風能讓葡萄成熟得更久，而不是更短。濃霧則是某些沿海地區的典型現象，例如加州和智利。","How can cloud slow down ripening in some warm Australian regions?":"在澳洲某些溫暖產區，雲層如何減緩成熟？","They block sunlight and slow photosynthesis":"它們遮擋陽光，減緩光合作用","They form at ground level and chill the roots":"它們在地面形成，讓根部受寒","They always bring hail, which reduces the crop":"它們總是帶來冰雹，減少收成","They raise humidity and encourage noble rot on the grapes every year":"它們提高濕度，每年都讓葡萄長出貴腐菌","Clouds form above ground and block the sun: less photosynthesis, slower ripening.":"雲在地面上方形成並遮住太陽：光合作用減少，成熟變慢。","This is an important moderating factor in some warm Australian regions. What forms at ground level is fog, not cloud. Noble rot needs morning mists followed by warm, dry afternoons instead.":"這是澳洲某些溫暖產區重要的調節因素。在地面形成的是霧，不是雲。貴腐菌需要的則是晨霧，加上溫暖乾燥的午後。","Which form of water vapour is essential for noble rot to develop?":"哪種形式的水氣對貴腐菌的發展不可或缺？","Autumn morning mists near rivers":"秋天清晨河流附近的薄霧","Low summer clouds that hide the sun for weeks":"連續數週遮住太陽的夏季低雲","Coastal Californian fog":"加州沿海的霧","Spring rain":"春雨","Mists rising from rivers on autumn mornings let the fungus develop.":"秋天早晨從河流升起的薄霧讓這種真菌得以發展。","Mist is a less dense form of fog. It must reach grapes that are already ripe, so in autumn, not spring. Coastal Californian fog mainly cools vineyards, while clouds block light and slow ripening.":"薄霧是比霧稀薄的形式。它必須接觸到已經成熟的葡萄，所以是在秋天，而不是春天。加州沿海的霧主要讓葡萄園降溫，而雲層則遮擋光線、減緩成熟。","Besides giving warmth in autumn, how else can a river help ripening far from the equator?":"在遠離赤道的地方，河流除了在秋天提供溫暖，還能以什麼方式幫助成熟？","It reflects sunlight onto the vines":"把陽光反射到葡萄樹上","It supplies nutrients to the leaves":"為葉片提供養分","It cools summers that are too hot":"讓過熱的夏天降溫","It prevents any mist from forming, so avoiding fungal disease":"阻止任何薄霧形成，從而避免真菌病害","The water's surface reflects light, which helps where sun and heat are scarce.":"水面反射光線，在陽光和熱量稀少的地方很有幫助。","Rivers warm up and cool down more slowly than land: in autumn they stay warmer, protect against frost and extend ripening. They do not feed the leaves, which take CO2 from the air. And river mists are exactly what encourages noble rot.":"河流升溫和降溫都比陸地慢：秋天時保持較溫暖，防止霜害並延長成熟期。它們不會餵養葉片，葉片是從空氣中吸收 CO2 的。而河流的薄霧正是助長貴腐菌的因素。","What is the soil's main role for the vine?":"土壤對葡萄樹的主要作用是什麼？","To supply water and nutrients":"提供水和養分","To supply carbon dioxide for photosynthesis":"為光合作用提供二氧化碳","To pollinate the flowers in spring":"在春天為花朵授粉","To protect the bunches from hail and birds during summer":"在夏天保護果串免受冰雹和鳥害","The soil must store enough water and nutrients to keep the vine healthy.":"土壤必須儲存足夠的水和養分，讓葡萄樹保持健康。","CO2 comes from the air through the leaves, not from the soil. Soil can also affect temperature: stones on the surface absorb heat and warm the vineyard. Against hail and birds, growers use nets, not soil.":"CO2 是透過葉片從空氣中取得的，不是來自土壤。土壤也可能影響溫度：地表的石頭吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖。對付冰雹和鳥類，種植者用的是網子，不是土壤。","A very hot, bright vintage: what risk do the grapes face?":"一個非常炎熱、陽光充足的年份：葡萄面臨什麼風險？","Untypical dried-fruit aromas and sunburn":"不典型的乾果香氣和日灼","Swollen grapes and diluted flavours":"葡萄膨脹，風味被稀釋","Strong herbaceous notes, as in grapes picked too early":"強烈的草本氣息，就像太早採收的葡萄","Excess heat and light can give untypical dried-fruit aromas and sunburn the grapes.":"過多的熱量和光照可能帶來不典型的乾果香氣，並讓葡萄日灼。","High acidity, little sugar and herbaceous notes are cool-vintage problems. Swollen grapes and diluted flavours come from heavy rain close to harvest. In extreme heat and drought, the vine may even shut down and fail to ripen its grapes.":"高酸、低糖和草本氣息是涼爽年份的問題。葡萄膨脹、風味稀釋則是採收前大雨造成的。在極端炎熱和乾旱下，葡萄樹甚至可能停止運作，無法讓葡萄成熟。","Why may grapes fail to ripen in a very hot summer with no rain?":"為什麼在非常炎熱又不下雨的夏天，葡萄可能無法成熟？","Short of water, the vine shuts down to protect itself":"缺水時，葡萄樹會停止運作以保護自己","The heat kills the yeasts on the skins and stops photosynthesis":"高溫殺死果皮上的酵母並中止光合作用","The grapes take up too much water from the roots":"葡萄從根部吸收了太多水","The leaves fall straight after flowering":"葉子在開花後立刻掉落","Heat increases the vine's need for water; without it, the vine shuts down and the grapes stop developing.":"高溫增加葡萄樹對水的需求；缺水時，葡萄樹停止運作，葡萄也停止發育。","High temperatures usually come with little rain, and in the worst cases the vine can die. Irrigation helps, but in these conditions there is often no water to use. Yeasts belong to fermentation in the winery, not ripening in the vineyard.":"高溫通常伴隨著少雨，最嚴重時葡萄樹可能死亡。灌溉有幫助，但在這種情況下往往無水可用。酵母屬於酒廠裡的發酵，不屬於葡萄園裡的成熟。","What causes drought?":"乾旱是什麼造成的？","Long periods of below-average rainfall, often made worse by heat":"長期降雨低於平均，常因高溫而更加嚴重","A single spring frost":"一次春霜","Too much irrigation":"過度灌溉","Coastal fog":"沿海的霧","Drought comes from prolonged low rainfall and worsens with above-average temperatures.":"乾旱來自長期的低降雨量，在溫度高於平均時會更嚴重。","In drought the vine cannot ripen its grapes and at worst it dies. Irrigation can help, but water is not always available. Frost damages new shoots and fog cools: neither causes drought.":"乾旱時葡萄樹無法讓葡萄成熟，最嚴重時會死亡。灌溉有幫助，但不一定有水可用。霜凍損害新梢，霧氣則帶來涼爽：兩者都不會造成乾旱。","What is the worst damage a heavy hailstorm can cause?":"一場猛烈的冰雹最嚴重會造成什麼損害？","Destroying the whole year's crop":"摧毀整年的收成","Slightly diluting the grapes' flavours":"輕微稀釋葡萄的風味","Starting noble rot on the ripe grapes":"讓成熟的葡萄開始長出貴腐菌","Delaying véraison by a few days with no effect on quality":"讓轉色期延後幾天，對品質沒有影響","Hail can badly damage vines and grapes, even wiping out the entire annual crop.":"冰雹可能嚴重損害葡萄樹和葡萄，甚至讓整年的收成化為烏有。","That is why, in some areas such as Argentina, growers stretch hail nets over the rows. Diluted flavours come from rain close to harvest. Noble rot needs morning mists and dry afternoons, not hail.":"所以在某些地區，例如阿根廷，種植者會在葡萄樹行上方架設防雹網。風味稀釋來自採收前的降雨。貴腐菌需要的是晨霧和乾燥的午後，而不是冰雹。","Why does a very wet season worry a grower even well before harvest?":"為什麼非常潮濕的季節，即使離採收還很久，也讓種植者擔心？","Moisture helps fungal diseases spread":"濕氣助長真菌病害蔓延","Rain stops photosynthesis for the whole summer":"下雨讓光合作用整個夏天都停止","Rain always increases the grapes' sugar":"下雨總是會提高葡萄的糖分","Rainwater stops the roots taking up any nutrients from the soil":"雨水讓根部無法從土壤吸收任何養分","High moisture helps fungi spread on leaves and grapes.":"高濕度助長真菌在葉片和葡萄上蔓延。","Fungal diseases reduce both the quality and the quantity of grapes. Close to harvest, rain also swells the grapes and dilutes flavours. Rain does not raise sugar; if anything, it dilutes it.":"真菌病害會同時降低葡萄的品質和產量。接近採收時，下雨還會讓葡萄膨脹、稀釋風味。下雨不會提高糖分；如果有影響，也是稀釋糖分。","Which statement about climate change and grape growing is correct?":"關於氣候變遷與葡萄種植，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Average temperatures are rising and extreme events are more frequent":"平均溫度正在上升，極端事件也更加頻繁","Climate changes completely from one year to the next":"氣候每年都會徹底改變","It only affects air temperatures, not ocean temperatures":"它只影響氣溫，不影響海洋溫度","No producers or industry bodies are yet taking action to adapt":"還沒有任何生產者或產業組織採取調適行動","Records show a sustained rise in air and ocean temperatures, with more droughts and floods.":"紀錄顯示氣溫和海洋溫度持續上升，乾旱和洪水也變多了。","Climate does not change from year to year, but it can shift over decades; it is weather that varies each year. A growing number of producers and industry bodies are already acting to adapt and mitigate. The rise affects both air and oceans.":"氣候不會年年改變，但可能在數十年間轉變；每年變化的是天氣。越來越多生產者和產業組織已經採取行動，進行調適和減緩。溫度上升同時影響空氣和海洋。","When are vines usually pruned?":"葡萄樹通常在什麼時候修剪？","In winter, while the vine is dormant":"冬天，葡萄樹休眠時","In spring, during flowering":"春天，開花期間","In summer, at véraison":"夏天，轉色期時","In autumn, just before harvest":"秋天，就在採收前","Pruning is done in winter, when the vine is dormant, to keep its shape.":"修剪在冬天葡萄樹休眠時進行，以維持樹形。","Training and pruning ensure a healthy, commercially viable crop each year. Pruning is generally done in winter, when the vine is dormant and not growing, and it keeps each vine in its required shape. In spring and summer the plant is busy growing and then ripening its grapes.":"整枝和修剪能確保每年都有健康、具商業價值的收成。修剪一般在冬天進行，這時葡萄樹休眠、不生長，修剪能讓每株葡萄樹維持所需的樹形。春天和夏天，植株正忙著生長和讓葡萄成熟。","What are most vines trained on?":"大多數葡萄樹以什麼來整枝？","Trellises":"棚架","Trees":"樹木","Stone walls":"石牆","Hail nets":"防雹網","Most vines are trained on trellises of posts and wires.":"大多數葡萄樹以立柱和鐵絲組成的棚架來整枝。","Training gives the vine its shape and, together with pruning, helps produce a regular, healthy crop. In the vast majority of cases vines are supported by trellises of posts and wires. Nets serve other purposes, such as protecting against hail or keeping birds away.":"整枝賦予葡萄樹樹形，並與修剪一起幫助產出穩定、健康的收成。絕大多數情況下，葡萄樹由立柱和鐵絲組成的棚架支撐。網子則有其他用途，例如防冰雹或驅趕鳥類。","Why do most growers now use irrigation sparingly?":"為什麼現在大多數種植者都節制地使用灌溉？","Water is increasingly limited and expensive":"水越來越有限，也越來越貴","Irrigation is banned in all regions":"所有產區都禁止灌溉","Water makes sugar levels rise too much":"水會讓糖分上升太多","Irrigation causes spring frosts":"灌溉會引發春霜","Water is an increasingly limited and expensive resource.":"水是越來越有限、越來越昂貴的資源。","In regions with little rain, irrigation is usually allowed, with methods ranging from flooding the field to watering individual vines. However, water has become an increasingly limited and expensive resource, so it is used sparingly. In a severe drought, there is often no water available for irrigation anyway.":"在雨量少的產區，灌溉通常是允許的，方法從漫灌整片田地到為單株葡萄樹澆水都有。不過，水已經成為越來越有限、越來越昂貴的資源，所以要節制使用。而在嚴重乾旱時，往往根本無水可供灌溉。","Which product is used to kill fungi in the vineyard?":"葡萄園裡用哪種產品殺死真菌？","Fungicide":"殺菌劑","Insecticide":"殺蟲劑","Herbicide":"除草劑","Fertiliser":"肥料","Fungicides kill fungi; insecticides and herbicides target insects and weeds.":"殺菌劑殺死真菌；殺蟲劑和除草劑分別針對昆蟲和雜草。","Fungi and insects are hard to control, and one solution is chemical sprays. Fungicides act against fungi, insecticides against insects and herbicides against weeds. Because some of these products can cause longer-term problems, many growers try to use them as little as possible.":"真菌和昆蟲很難控制，其中一個解決方法是噴灑化學藥劑。殺菌劑對付真菌，殺蟲劑對付昆蟲，除草劑對付雜草。由於有些產品可能造成長期問題，許多種植者盡量少用。","What does it mean if a vineyard is certified organic?":"葡萄園獲得有機認證代表什麼？","Grapes are grown without most chemicals":"種植葡萄時不使用大部分化學藥劑","No sprays of any kind are ever used":"完全不使用任何噴灑藥劑","Grapes are always picked by hand":"葡萄一律人工採收","The maximum yield is set by law":"最高產量由法律規定","Organic growing avoids most chemicals, though some sprays are still permitted.":"有機種植避免使用大部分化學藥劑，但仍允許部分噴灑藥劑。","A certified organic vineyard does without most chemicals. It is not a total ban, though: some sprays are still allowed to keep the worst fungal diseases under control. Organic status says nothing about harvesting method or yields, which depend on other choices or rules.":"獲得有機認證的葡萄園不使用大部分化學藥劑。但這並非全面禁止：仍允許部分噴灑藥劑，以控制最嚴重的真菌病害。有機身分與採收方式或產量無關，那取決於其他選擇或法規。","What effect can an excessively high yield have on the grapes?":"產量過高會對葡萄造成什麼影響？","Diluted flavours and less sugar":"風味被稀釋，糖分較少","More concentrated flavours and more sugar":"風味更濃縮，糖分更多","Dried-fruit and raisin aromas":"乾果和葡萄乾的香氣","With yields too high, grapes can have diluted flavours and lower sugar.":"產量太高時，葡萄可能風味稀釋、糖分較低。","Yield measures how much fruit is produced per unit of area, and in some regions it is capped by law. If a vine carries too many bunches, the grapes can be lower in sugar with diluted flavours. On the other hand, with too few bunches the crop becomes too small to be commercially viable.":"產量衡量的是每單位面積生產多少果實，在某些產區有法定上限。如果一株葡萄樹掛了太多果串，葡萄可能糖分較低、風味稀釋。反過來說，果串太少，收成就太小，不具商業價值。","A producer wants a fresh white with crisp acidity. Which harvest choice helps most?":"一位生產者想釀出酸度爽脆的清爽白酒。哪種採收選擇最有幫助？","Picking earlier in the ripening process":"在成熟過程中較早採收","Picking very late":"非常晚才採收","Waiting for the grapes to shrivel":"等葡萄乾縮","Waiting for noble rot":"等貴腐菌出現","Grapes picked early have more acidity, less sugar and less-ripe flavours.":"較早採收的葡萄酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟。","Harvest timing changes the balance of the grapes. Picked early, they have higher acidity, less sugar and less-ripe flavours, ideal for a fresh style. Picking late, waiting for shrivelling or for noble rot instead brings more sugar and riper or more concentrated flavours, typical of richer or sweet wines.":"採收時機會改變葡萄的平衡。較早採收的葡萄酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟，非常適合清爽的風格。相反地，晚採、等待乾縮或等待貴腐菌，則帶來更多糖分和更成熟或更濃縮的風味，是較豐潤或甜型葡萄酒的典型特徵。","Which statement about hand and machine harvesting is correct?":"關於人工採收和機器採收，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Machines cannot be used on steep slopes":"機器無法在陡坡上使用","Hand-picking always gives better wines":"人工採收總是釀出更好的酒","Machine picking always gives better wines":"機器採收總是釀出更好的酒","Machines are compulsory in organic vineyards":"有機葡萄園規定必須使用機器","Neither method is inherently better, but machines cannot work steep slopes.":"兩種方法本身沒有優劣之分，但機器無法在陡坡上作業。","Grapes can be picked by hand or by machine, and neither method is inherently better for wine quality. The choice usually depends on the style being made. There is one practical constraint, however: machine harvesters cannot work on steep slopes, where hand-picking is needed.":"葡萄可以用人工或機器採收，兩種方法本身對葡萄酒品質沒有優劣之分。選擇通常取決於要釀造的風格。不過有一個實際的限制：採收機無法在陡坡上作業，那裡需要人工採收。","How does the Botrytis fungus concentrate the sugar in a grape?":"貴腐菌如何濃縮葡萄中的糖分？","It makes tiny holes in the skin so water evaporates":"在果皮上造成微小的孔洞，讓水分蒸發","It turns the water in the grape into ice":"把葡萄裡的水變成冰","It adds sugar from its own growth":"藉由自身生長添加糖分","It blocks photosynthesis in the leaves":"阻斷葉片的光合作用","Botrytis pierces the skin, water evaporates, and sugars, acids and flavours concentrate.":"貴腐菌刺穿果皮，水分蒸發，糖、酸和風味隨之濃縮。","Noble rot is caused by the Botrytis fungus, which creates tiny holes in the skin. Water evaporates through these holes, concentrating acids, sugars and flavours. Turning water into ice is instead the mechanism behind the frozen grapes used for icewine. Grapes affected by noble rot nearly always go into sweet wines.":"貴腐是由貴腐菌（Botrytis）引起的，它會在果皮上造成微小的孔洞。水分從這些孔洞蒸發，使酸、糖和風味濃縮。把水變成冰則是用來釀造冰酒的冰凍葡萄的原理。受貴腐菌感染的葡萄幾乎都用來釀造甜酒。","Which weather conditions are ideal for beneficial noble rot?":"哪種天氣條件最適合有益的貴腐菌？","Damp misty mornings, then warm dry afternoons":"潮濕多霧的早晨，接著是溫暖乾燥的午後","Constant rain throughout autumn":"整個秋天持續下雨","Hot, dry days with no moisture at all":"炎熱乾燥、完全沒有濕氣的日子","Night frosts followed by cold days":"夜間霜凍，接著是寒冷的白天","Morning damp lets the fungus grow; warm, dry afternoons stop it destroying the grapes.":"早晨的濕氣讓真菌生長；溫暖乾燥的午後則阻止它毀掉葡萄。","Botrytis can easily destroy grapes, so it must act in a controlled way. First, the grapes must be ripe. Then damp, misty mornings, often from mists near rivers, allow the fungus to grow and spread, followed by warm, dry afternoons that limit its growth before it ruins the crop.":"貴腐菌很容易毀掉葡萄，所以它必須在受控的情況下作用。首先，葡萄必須已經成熟。接著，潮濕多霧的早晨（霧氣常來自河流附近）讓真菌生長蔓延，隨後溫暖乾燥的午後限制它的生長，以免毀掉收成。","Why are grapes for icewine pressed while still frozen?":"為什麼冰酒用的葡萄要在結冰狀態下壓榨？","The ice stays behind, leaving more concentrated juice":"冰留在壓榨機裡，留下更濃縮的果汁","The cold adds colour to the juice":"寒冷為果汁增添顏色","Freezing kills the noble rot on the grapes":"冰凍會殺死葡萄上的貴腐菌","Frozen grapes have more tannin":"結冰的葡萄單寧較多","Pressing frozen grapes leaves ice and skins behind, so the little juice is very concentrated.":"壓榨結冰的葡萄時，冰和果皮留在壓榨機裡，所以少量的果汁非常濃縮。","In frozen grapes much of the water has turned to ice. By pressing before they thaw, the ice crystals stay behind with the skins and only a small amount of unfrozen liquid runs off, very rich in acids, sugars and flavours. This is the basis of icewines: sweet, concentrated and with pure varietal character.":"在結冰的葡萄中，大部分的水已經變成冰。在解凍前壓榨，冰晶會和果皮一起留下，只有少量未結冰的液體流出，富含酸、糖和風味。這就是冰酒的基礎：甜美、濃縮，帶有純粹的品種特色。","What do extra-ripeness, noble rot and frozen grapes have in common?":"過熟、貴腐和冰凍葡萄有什麼共同點？","They concentrate sugar and are often used for sweet wines":"它們都會濃縮糖分，常用來釀造甜酒","They lower sugar and give dry, light wines":"它們會降低糖分，釀出不甜、輕盈的酒","They all need a warm climate with no fog":"它們都需要沒有霧氣的溫暖氣候","They mainly increase colour and tannin":"它們主要增加顏色和單寧","All three methods concentrate grape sugar, ideal for sweet wines.":"三種方法都會濃縮葡萄的糖分，非常適合釀造甜酒。","These are three different ways of getting very sweet grapes. With extra-ripeness, water slowly evaporates and the grapes shrivel; with noble rot, the fungus pierces the skin and water evaporates; with freezing, the water stays locked in ice during pressing. In every case sugars and acids are concentrated and the grapes suit sweet wines.":"這是取得非常甜的葡萄的三種不同方法。過熟時，水分緩慢蒸發，葡萄乾縮；貴腐時，真菌刺穿果皮，水分蒸發；冰凍時，水在壓榨過程中被鎖在冰裡。在每一種情況下，糖和酸都會濃縮，葡萄都適合釀造甜酒。","What is the main purpose of training and pruning vines?":"整枝和修剪葡萄樹的主要目的是什麼？","To get a healthy, commercially viable crop every year":"每年都獲得健康、具商業價值的收成","To make vineyards suitable only for hand harvesting":"讓葡萄園只適合人工採收","To push each vine's yield as high as possible, whatever the ripeness":"不管成熟度如何，盡可能提高每株葡萄樹的產量","To prevent winter dormancy":"防止冬季休眠","Training and pruning ensure a healthy, viable crop can be harvested successfully every year.":"整枝和修剪確保每年都能順利採收健康、具商業價值的收成。","Winter pruning keeps each vine in its required shape, and most vines are trained on trellises. An excessive yield dilutes flavour and sugar, so that is not the goal. Winter dormancy is natural and cannot be avoided.":"冬季修剪讓每株葡萄樹維持所需的樹形，而大多數葡萄樹以棚架整枝。過高的產量會稀釋風味和糖分，所以那不是目標。冬季休眠是自然現象，無法避免。","Which irrigation system can water each individual vine?":"哪一種灌溉系統可以為每一株葡萄樹單獨澆水？","Drip irrigation":"滴灌","Flooding the field":"漫灌整片田地","Digging a channel next to the vineyard to raise the river level":"在葡萄園旁挖渠道以抬高河水水位","A drip system delivers water directly to each vine.":"滴灌系統把水直接送到每一株葡萄樹。","Methods range from flooding the whole field to systems that measure water vine by vine. The latter are valuable because water is increasingly scarce and expensive. Fog cools a vineyard but is not an irrigation system.":"灌溉方法從漫灌整片田地，到逐株計量用水的系統都有。後者非常有價值，因為水越來越稀少、越來越昂貴。霧氣能讓葡萄園降溫，但它不是灌溉系統。","In which regions are growers normally allowed to irrigate?":"種植者通常在哪些產區被允許灌溉？","Where there is a lack of rainfall":"缺乏降雨的地方","Only in cool-climate regions":"只在涼爽氣候產區","Anywhere, without limit, even in very rainy areas":"任何地方都行，毫無限制，連多雨地區也一樣","Only in organic vineyards":"只在有機葡萄園","Irrigation is normally permitted in regions that lack rainfall.":"在缺乏降雨的產區，灌溉通常是允許的。","Irrigation makes up for a natural lack of water, typical of warm, dry areas rather than cool ones. Even where it is allowed, growers now use it sparingly because water is a limited resource. Organic rules are about chemicals, not water.":"灌溉是為了彌補天然的缺水，這是溫暖乾燥地區而非涼爽地區的典型問題。即使在允許灌溉的地方，種植者現在也節制使用，因為水是有限的資源。有機規範涉及的是化學藥劑，不是水。","A grower wants to control weeds with a chemical spray. What do they use?":"一位種植者想用化學噴劑控制雜草。他會用什麼？","A herbicide":"除草劑","A fungicide":"殺菌劑","An insecticide":"殺蟲劑","A fine mesh net stretched over the rows":"架在葡萄樹行上方的細網","Herbicides are used to control weeds.":"除草劑用來控制雜草。","Fungicides kill fungi and insecticides kill insects. Nets protect against birds, larger animals or hail, not weeds. Many growers try to limit these chemicals anyway, as they can cause longer-term problems.":"殺菌劑殺死真菌，殺蟲劑殺死昆蟲。網子防的是鳥類、較大的動物或冰雹，不是雜草。無論如何，許多種植者都盡量限制這些化學藥劑，因為它們可能造成長期問題。","How are grapes most easily protected from birds and larger animals?":"保護葡萄免受鳥類和較大動物侵害，最簡單的方法是什麼？","With nets and fences":"用網子和圍欄","With fungicides sprayed on the leaves":"在葉片上噴灑殺菌劑","With shorter pruning in summer":"夏天修剪得更短","By harvesting just after fruit set, before the grapes turn sweet":"在著果後、葡萄變甜之前就採收","Birds and animals are kept away with physical barriers such as nets and fences.":"用網子和圍欄等實體屏障讓鳥類和動物遠離。","Large pests are fairly easy to keep out; fungi and insects are much harder to control. Fungicides act on fungi, not birds. Harvesting right after fruit set would give hard, green, inedible grapes.":"大型害物相對容易阻擋；真菌和昆蟲則難控制得多。殺菌劑作用於真菌，不是鳥類。著果後立刻採收，得到的會是又硬又綠、無法食用的葡萄。","In some areas, such as Argentina, nets are stretched over the vines. What are they mainly for?":"在某些地區，例如阿根廷，葡萄樹上方會架設網子。它們主要用來做什麼？","Against hail":"防冰雹","Against spring frost":"防春霜","To hold fog over the vineyard":"把霧氣留在葡萄園上方","To stop the roots taking up too much water after summer storms":"防止根部在夏季暴雨後吸收太多水","Hail nets shield vines and bunches from hailstones.":"防雹網保護葡萄樹和果串免受冰雹打擊。","A violent hailstorm can destroy a whole crop, and a net is an effective physical barrier. A net does little against frost, as the cold gets through anyway. Nets have no effect on fog or roots.":"一場猛烈的冰雹可能摧毀整年的收成，而網子是有效的實體屏障。網子對霜凍幫助不大，因為寒冷照樣會穿透。網子對霧氣或根部都沒有影響。","Why do many growers try to limit their use of chemical sprays?":"為什麼許多種植者盡量限制使用化學噴劑？","They can cause longer-term problems in vineyards":"它們可能在葡萄園造成長期問題","They are banned in every wine region except outside the EU":"除了歐盟以外，所有葡萄酒產區都禁止使用","They make wine sweeter":"它們讓葡萄酒更甜","They have no effect on fungi or insects":"它們對真菌或昆蟲沒有作用","Some of these chemicals can cause longer-term problems in vineyards.":"其中一些化學藥劑可能在葡萄園造成長期問題。","Fungicides, insecticides and herbicides do work, which is why they are used. They are not banned everywhere; organic growing uses very few, but some sprays against the worst fungal diseases are still allowed. A wine's sweetness has nothing to do with them.":"殺菌劑、殺蟲劑和除草劑確實有效，所以才會被使用。它們並非到處都被禁止；有機種植用得很少，但仍允許部分對付最嚴重真菌病害的噴劑。葡萄酒的甜度與它們無關。","Which statement about a certified organic vineyard is correct?":"關於獲得有機認證的葡萄園，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Some sprays against the worst fungal diseases are still allowed":"仍允許部分對付最嚴重真菌病害的噴劑","No sprays of any kind are allowed":"不允許任何噴劑","Harvesting must be done by machine":"必須用機器採收","Irrigation is banned and vines must live on rainwater alone":"禁止灌溉，葡萄樹只能靠雨水生存","Organic growing avoids most chemicals, but some anti-fungal sprays remain permitted.":"有機種植避免使用大部分化學藥劑，但仍允許部分抗真菌噴劑。","'Organic' on a label means grapes grown without most chemicals, not with no treatment at all. The rules do not impose a harvesting method. Irrigation depends on lack of rainfall, not on organic status.":"酒標上的「有機」代表種植葡萄時不使用大部分化學藥劑，而不是完全不做任何處理。法規並未規定採收方式。灌溉與否取決於是否缺乏降雨，與有機身分無關。","Where do the fungi that attack vines grow, and what harm do they do?":"侵襲葡萄樹的真菌長在哪裡？會造成什麼危害？","On grapes and leaves; they reduce grape quality and quantity":"長在葡萄和葉片上；會降低葡萄的品質和產量","Only on the roots; they lower the wine's alcohol":"只長在根部；會降低葡萄酒的酒精濃度","Only on the trunk; they never touch the grapes":"只長在主幹上；從不接觸葡萄","In winery barrels; they add vanilla and coconut notes to the wine":"長在酒廠的橡木桶裡；為酒增添香草和椰子氣息","Fungi grow on grapes and leaves and can greatly reduce crop quality and quantity.":"真菌長在葡萄和葉片上，可能大幅降低收成的品質和產量。","Vines are vulnerable to many fungal diseases, sometimes with very serious damage. That is why fungicides are used, partly even in organic vineyards. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak, not a fungus.":"葡萄樹容易感染許多真菌病害，有時損害非常嚴重。這就是為什麼要使用殺菌劑，甚至有機葡萄園也部分使用。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是真菌。","What is the problem if a vine produces too few grapes?":"如果一株葡萄樹結的葡萄太少，會有什麼問題？","The crop is too small to be commercially viable":"收成太小，不具商業價值","The flavours become diluted":"風味變得稀釋","The grapes always have less sugar":"葡萄的糖分總是比較少","The wine automatically becomes a late harvest wine":"酒會自動變成晚收酒","With too low a yield, there is not enough fruit for the vineyard to pay its way.":"產量太低時，果實不夠多，葡萄園無法回本。","Growers look for a balance: too many grapes give diluted flavours and less sugar, too few do not pay. Dilution and low sugar are therefore the risks of excessive yields, not low ones. 'Late harvest' depends on picking date, not yield.":"種植者追求的是平衡：葡萄太多會稀釋風味、降低糖分，太少則不划算。所以稀釋和低糖是產量過高的風險，而不是產量過低。「晚收」取決於採收日期，與產量無關。","Which statement about yield is correct?":"關於產量，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","In some regions the maximum yield is set by law":"在某些產區，最高產量由法律規定","Yield measures the finished wine's alcohol":"產量衡量的是成品酒的酒精濃度","The higher the yield, the more concentrated the flavours":"產量越高，風味越濃縮","Yield depends only on climate and the grower cannot influence it in any way":"產量只取決於氣候，種植者完全無法影響","Yield is fruit produced per unit of area, and in some regions the law sets a maximum.":"產量是每單位面積生產的果實量，在某些產區法律訂有上限。","Excessive yields dilute flavours and lower sugar rather than concentrating them. Yield measures the amount of fruit, not alcohol. Pruning and vineyard management exist precisely to regulate the crop.":"過高的產量會稀釋風味、降低糖分，而不是讓它們濃縮。產量衡量的是果實的數量，不是酒精。修剪和葡萄園管理正是為了調節收成而存在。","A producer harvests later than usual. What kind of grapes should they expect?":"一位生產者比平常晚採收。他應該預期得到什麼樣的葡萄？","More sugar, less acidity and riper flavours":"糖分較多、酸度較低、風味較成熟","Less sugar, more acidity and greener flavours":"糖分較少、酸度較高、風味較青澀","The same sugar and acidity, but paler skins":"糖分和酸度相同，但果皮顏色較淺","More acidity and more unripe tannins":"酸度較高，未成熟的單寧較多","Picking later means higher sugar, lower acidity and riper flavours.":"較晚採收代表糖分較高、酸度較低、風味較成熟。","Harvest timing is a key style decision. More acidity, less sugar and less ripe flavours come from picking early. If grapes stay on the vine even longer, they shrivel and take on raisin notes.":"採收時機是關鍵的風格決定。酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟來自較早採收。如果葡萄在樹上留得更久，就會乾縮並帶有葡萄乾的氣息。","Between hand and machine harvesting, which gives better-quality wine?":"人工採收和機器採收，哪一種能釀出品質更好的酒？","Neither is fundamentally better":"兩者本質上沒有優劣之分","Always hand harvesting":"永遠是人工採收","Always machine harvesting":"永遠是機器採收","Machine on steep slopes, hand only on flat land":"陡坡用機器，平地才用人工","Neither method is fundamentally better: the choice mainly depends on the wine style.":"兩種方法本質上沒有優劣之分：選擇主要取決於葡萄酒的風格。","The practical limit is that machines cannot work on steep slopes, where hand picking is needed; the last option gets this backwards. Always linking hand picking with quality is a cliché, not a rule.":"實際的限制是機器無法在陡坡上作業，那裡需要人工採收；最後一個選項正好說反了。總是把人工採收和品質畫上等號只是刻板印象，不是規則。","Which condition is essential for Botrytis to be 'noble' rather than destructive?":"貴腐菌要成為「貴腐」而非破壞性的，哪個條件不可或缺？","It must grow on grapes that are already ripe":"它必須長在已經成熟的葡萄上","It must attack grapes just after fruit set":"它必須在著果後立刻侵襲葡萄","It must rain heavily every afternoon":"每天下午都必須下大雨","The grapes must freeze on the vine before the fungus appears":"葡萄必須在真菌出現之前就在樹上結冰","The fungus is only beneficial on ripe grapes, with the right weather.":"這種真菌只有在成熟的葡萄上、配合合適的天氣，才是有益的。","Botrytis can easily destroy grapes. It needs ripe grapes, then damp, misty mornings to grow and warm, dry afternoons to hold it back. Afternoon rain would let it run out of control; freezing relates to icewine instead.":"貴腐菌很容易毀掉葡萄。它需要成熟的葡萄，接著需要潮濕多霧的早晨讓它生長，以及溫暖乾燥的午後抑制它。午後下雨會讓它失控；結冰則與冰酒有關。","In the development of noble rot, what is the role of warm, dry afternoons?":"在貴腐菌的發展過程中，溫暖乾燥的午後扮演什麼角色？","To limit the fungus so it does not destroy the grapes":"抑制真菌，以免它毀掉葡萄","To start the fungus growing on the grapes":"讓真菌開始在葡萄上生長","To freeze the water in the grapes":"讓葡萄裡的水結冰","To add water to the grapes to dilute acidity before harvest":"在採收前為葡萄補水以稀釋酸度","Warm, dry afternoons slow the fungus and stop it ruining the grapes.":"溫暖乾燥的午後減緩真菌生長，阻止它毀掉葡萄。","Damp, misty mornings are what allow the fungus to grow and spread. Alternating the two creates noble rot, which evaporates water and concentrates sugars, acids and flavours. Freezing grapes is the icewine technique.":"讓真菌生長蔓延的是潮濕多霧的早晨。兩者交替就形成貴腐，使水分蒸發，糖、酸和風味濃縮。冰凍葡萄則是冰酒的技術。","What style of wine is usually made from grapes frozen on the vine (icewine)?":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄（冰酒）通常釀成什麼風格的酒？","Sweet, concentrated and with pure varietal character":"甜美、濃縮，帶有純粹的品種特色","Dry and light, with flavours diluted by the ice water":"不甜、輕盈，風味被冰水稀釋","A tannic red for long ageing":"適合長期陳年的高單寧紅酒","Sweet, with strong noble-rot and raisin notes":"甜，帶有強烈的貴腐和葡萄乾氣息","Pressing healthy frozen grapes gives a little juice rich in sugar, acid and pure flavours: sweet, concentrated wines.":"壓榨健康的結冰葡萄，能得到少量富含糖、酸和純粹風味的果汁：釀出甜美濃縮的酒。","For icewine, healthy grapes stay on the vine through autumn into winter, are picked frozen and pressed before they thaw. Ice and skins stay in the press, so there is no dilution. Noble-rot and raisin notes belong to other concentration methods.":"釀造冰酒時，健康的葡萄從秋天一直留在樹上到冬天，在結冰狀態下採收，並在解凍前壓榨。冰和果皮留在壓榨機裡，所以不會被稀釋。貴腐和葡萄乾氣息屬於其他的濃縮方法。","A legally defined vineyard area":"法律界定的葡萄園區域","A grape variety permitted in a region":"某產區允許使用的葡萄品種","A brand registered by a producer":"生產者註冊的品牌","A quality ranking of vintages":"年份的品質排名","A GI is a legally defined vineyard area, large or small.":"GI 是法律界定的葡萄園區域，可大可小。","A GI legally defines a vineyard area. It can be very large, up to a whole region or country, or very small, such as a single vineyard. GIs appear on labels worldwide because the place where grapes grow can influence wine style. Not every wine comes from a GI, but some statement of origin must always be given.":"GI（地理標示）在法律上界定一個葡萄園區域。它可以非常大，大到整個產區或國家，也可以非常小，例如單一葡萄園。世界各地的酒標上都有 GI，因為葡萄生長的地方會影響葡萄酒的風格。並非每一款酒都來自某個 GI，但一定要標示某種產地說明。","Why is an EU GI a more reliable guide to style than a GI outside the EU?":"為什麼歐盟的 GI 比歐盟以外的 GI 更能可靠地反映風格？","It has rules on permitted grapes and winemaking":"它對允許的品種和釀造方式有規定","It always covers larger areas":"它涵蓋的區域總是比較大","It always names the grape on the label":"它總是在酒標上標示品種","It bans the use of irrigation":"它禁止灌溉","In the EU each GI sets which grapes may be grown and how the wine is made.":"在歐盟，每個 GI 都規定可以種植哪些品種，以及酒要如何釀造。","Outside the EU, a GI mainly shows where the grapes were grown: growers plant what they like and rules are minimal, so styles vary widely. In the EU, each GI adds rules on permitted varieties and winemaking methods. That is why an EU GI tells you much more about the expected style, even without the grape name.":"在歐盟以外，GI 主要表示葡萄種植的地點：種植者想種什麼就種什麼，規定極少，所以風格差異很大。在歐盟，每個 GI 還加上允許品種和釀造方式的規定。這就是為什麼即使沒有標示品種，歐盟的 GI 也能告訴你更多關於預期風格的資訊。","Which description best fits a PDO compared with a PGI?":"與 PGI 相比，哪一項描述最符合 PDO？","Smaller area and stricter rules":"區域較小，規定較嚴格","Wider area and more flexible rules":"區域較廣，規定較彈性","No rules on which grapes to use":"對使用的品種沒有規定","Only inexpensive high-volume wines":"只有平價的大量生產酒款","PDOs usually cover small areas with tight rules; PGIs are wider and more flexible.":"PDO 通常涵蓋小區域、規定嚴格；PGI 則區域較廣、較有彈性。","PDOs generally cover relatively small areas with tight regulations and include many of Europe's most prestigious wines. PGIs cover much wider areas with less strict rules, giving more freedom over grapes and techniques. PGI wines range from inexpensive high-volume wines to outstanding, premium-priced ones, so they are not only simple wines.":"PDO（受保護原產地名稱）一般涵蓋相對較小的區域，規定嚴格，包括歐洲許多最負盛名的葡萄酒。PGI（受保護地理標示）涵蓋廣得多的區域，規定較寬鬆，在品種和技術上給予更多自由。PGI 葡萄酒從平價的大量生產酒款到價格高昂的傑出酒款都有，所以不只是簡單的酒。","Which French term indicates a PGI?":"哪一個法文術語代表 PGI？","In France PGI is Indication géographique protégée; AOC and AOP indicate PDO.":"在法國，PGI 是 Indication géographique protégée；AOC 和 AOP 代表 PDO。","France uses two terms for PDO: Appellation d'origine protégée (AOP) and the traditional Appellation d'origine contrôlée (AOC). For PGI it uses Indication géographique protégée (IGP). Vieilles vignes, on the other hand, means old vines and is not even a legally defined term.":"法國的 PDO 有兩個術語：Appellation d'origine protégée（AOP）和傳統的 Appellation d'origine contrôlée（AOC）。PGI 則使用 Indication géographique protégée（IGP）。另一方面，Vieilles vignes 的意思是老藤，甚至不是法律定義的術語。","Which Italian term corresponds to PGI?":"哪一個義大利文術語對應 PGI？","In Italy PGI is Indicazione Geografica Tipica (IGT); DOC and DOCG are PDO.":"在義大利，PGI 是 Indicazione Geografica Tipica（IGT）；DOC 和 DOCG 是 PDO。","Italy has two traditional terms for PDO: Denominazione di Origine Controllata (DOC) and Denominazione di Origine Controllata e Garantita (DOCG). For PGI it uses Indicazione Geografica Tipica (IGT). DOCa is a Spanish term, Denominación de Origen Calificada, which belongs to the PDO category.":"義大利的 PDO 有兩個傳統術語：Denominazione di Origine Controllata（DOC）和 Denominazione di Origine Controllata e Garantita（DOCG）。PGI 則使用 Indicazione Geografica Tipica（IGT）。DOCa 是西班牙術語 Denominación de Origen Calificada，屬於 PDO 類別。","Which Spanish term indicates a PGI?":"哪一個西班牙文術語代表 PGI？","In Spain PGI is Vino de la Tierra; DO and DOCa are PDO.":"在西班牙，PGI 是 Vino de la Tierra；DO 和 DOCa 是 PDO。","In Spain, PDO is expressed by Denominación de Origen (DO) and Denominación de Origen Calificada (DOCa), while PGI is called Vino de la Tierra. Landwein is also a PGI term, but it is German, not Spanish, so it is the trap to avoid here.":"在西班牙，PDO 以 Denominación de Origen（DO）和 Denominación de Origen Calificada（DOCa）表示，而 PGI 稱為 Vino de la Tierra。Landwein 也是 PGI 術語，但它是德文，不是西班牙文，所以這是要避開的陷阱。","In Germany, which term corresponds to PGI?":"在德國，哪一個術語對應 PGI？","Germany's PGI term is Landwein; Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein are PDO.":"德國的 PGI 術語是 Landwein；Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein 是 PDO。","In Germany there are two traditional terms for PDO, Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein, while PGI corresponds to Landwein. Eiswein is not an origin category at all: it is a grape-growing term meaning the grapes were left to freeze on the vine before harvest.":"德國的 PDO 有兩個傳統術語：Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein，而 PGI 對應 Landwein。Eiswein 根本不是產地類別：它是葡萄種植術語，意思是葡萄在採收前留在樹上結冰。","A label reads Appellation Chablis Contrôlée but names no grape. Which grape is the wine made from?":"一張酒標上寫著 Appellation Chablis Contrôlée，但沒有標示品種。這款酒是用哪個品種釀的？","Chablis rules require Chardonnay, even though it is not shown on the label.":"Chablis 的法規規定使用夏多內，即使酒標上沒有標示。","Chablis is a French GI, and Appellation Contrôlée is the traditional French term for PDO. The rules of this appellation require the wines to be made from Chardonnay. For European PDO wines the grape does not have to appear on the label, so knowing the rules of the area tells you what is in the bottle.":"Chablis 是法國的 GI，而 Appellation Contrôlée 是法國 PDO 的傳統術語。這個法定產區的法規要求以夏多內釀造。歐洲的 PDO 葡萄酒不必在酒標上標示品種，所以了解產區法規就能知道瓶中是什麼。","Why are wines from old vines often highly prized?":"為什麼老藤釀的酒常常備受珍視？","Fewer grapes, with more concentrated, complex aromas":"葡萄較少，香氣更濃縮、更複雜","Higher yields with fresher aromas":"產量較高，香氣更清新","The term legally guarantees a minimum age":"這個術語在法律上保證最低樹齡","They are always sweet wines from shrivelled grapes":"它們總是用乾縮葡萄釀的甜酒","Old vines produce smaller crops, often with more concentrated, complex fruit.":"老藤的收成較小，果實常常更濃縮、更複雜。","As vines age, they tend to produce fewer bunches. A smaller crop can give grapes with more concentrated and complex aromas, and so higher-quality wines. That is why such wines are often labelled Old Vine or vieilles vignes. However, the term is not legally defined, so it guarantees no minimum age and its use can be disputed.":"隨著樹齡增長，葡萄樹結的果串往往變少。較小的收成可能帶來香氣更濃縮、更複雜的葡萄，因而釀出品質更高的酒。這就是為什麼這類酒常標示 Old Vine 或 vieilles vignes。不過，這個術語沒有法律定義，所以不保證任何最低樹齡，其使用也可能引起爭議。","An Australian and a Californian wine are both labelled 2022. Which statement is correct?":"一款澳洲酒和一款加州酒都標示 2022。下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","The Australian wine is about six months older":"澳洲酒大約老六個月","The Californian wine is about six months older":"加州酒大約老六個月","They are exactly the same age":"兩者年齡完全相同","The Australian wine is about a year older":"澳洲酒大約老一年","The southern hemisphere harvest comes about six months before the northern one.":"南半球的採收比北半球早大約六個月。","The vintage is the year of harvest. In the southern hemisphere the growing season runs from October to April, so grapes are picked early in the year; in the northern hemisphere it runs from April to October, with harvest towards the end of the year. An Australian 2022 is therefore about half a year older than a Californian 2022.":"年份是採收的年份。南半球的生長季從 10 月到 4 月，所以葡萄在年初採收；北半球則從 4 月到 10 月，在接近年底時採收。因此，2022 年的澳洲酒比 2022 年的加州酒大約老半年。","What does the term Late Harvest on a label indicate?":"酒標上的 Late Harvest 代表什麼？","Grapes picked well after the normal time":"葡萄在正常時間之後很久才採收","Grapes affected by noble rot":"葡萄受到貴腐菌感染","Grapes frozen on the vine":"葡萄在樹上結冰","Grapes from vines at least 60 years old":"葡萄來自至少 60 年樹齡的葡萄樹","Late Harvest means grapes left on the vine and picked much later than usual.":"Late Harvest 是指葡萄留在樹上，比平常晚很多才採收。","Late Harvest wines are made from grapes left on the vine beyond the normal picking time. The grapes have riper flavours and more sugar, and the wines are fuller-bodied and more concentrated than those from grapes picked at the usual time. Noble rot and frozen grapes have their own terms: Botrytis/Noble Rot and icewine/Eiswein.":"Late Harvest（晚收）葡萄酒是用留在樹上超過正常採收時間的葡萄釀造的。這些葡萄風味更成熟、糖分更多，釀出的酒比正常時間採收的葡萄酒體更飽滿、更濃縮。貴腐和冰凍葡萄則有各自的術語：Botrytis/Noble Rot 以及 icewine/Eiswein。","Which statement about a wine labelled Late Harvest is correct?":"關於標示 Late Harvest 的酒，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet":"它可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜","It is always a sweet wine":"它一定是甜酒","It is always lighter than a normal wine":"它一定比一般的酒輕盈","It is always made from frozen grapes":"它一定是用冰凍葡萄釀的","Late Harvest wines are fuller and more concentrated, but their sweetness varies.":"Late Harvest 葡萄酒更飽滿、更濃縮，但甜度不一。","Late-picked grapes have more sugar and riper flavours, giving fuller-bodied, more concentrated wines. That does not mean the wine must be sweet: a Late Harvest wine can be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet. By contrast, grapes with noble rot nearly always go into sweet wines, and icewine uses frozen grapes, not just late-picked ones.":"晚採的葡萄糖分更多、風味更成熟，釀出酒體更飽滿、更濃縮的酒。但這不代表酒一定是甜的：Late Harvest 葡萄酒可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜。相對地，受貴腐菌感染的葡萄幾乎都用來釀甜酒，而冰酒用的是冰凍的葡萄，不只是晚採的葡萄。","Which statement about the size of a geographical indication (GI) is correct?":"關於地理標示（GI）的大小，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can range from a single vineyard to a whole country":"它可以從單一葡萄園到整個國家","It must always match one village":"它必須總是對應一個村莊","It can never exceed 100 hectares":"它絕不能超過 100 公頃","It always covers a whole administrative region, never a smaller area":"它總是涵蓋整個行政區，絕不會是較小的區域","A GI is a legally defined vineyard area, as large as a country or as small as one vineyard.":"GI 是法律界定的葡萄園區域，可以大如一個國家，也可以小如一座葡萄園。","GIs appear on labels because where grapes are grown influences the wine's style. There is no fixed size and no required link to administrative borders. For example, 'South Eastern Australia' is a very large GI, while others are tiny.":"酒標上出現 GI，是因為葡萄種植的地點會影響酒的風格。GI 沒有固定大小，也不必與行政邊界對應。例如「South Eastern Australia」是非常大的 GI，而其他有些則非常小。","A wine does not come from any GI. Which statement of origin must still appear on the label, where applicable?":"一款酒不來自任何 GI。酒標上仍必須標示哪一種產地說明（如適用）？","The country of origin":"原產國","The vineyard name":"葡萄園名稱","The age of the vines":"葡萄樹的樹齡","The exact harvest date and the names of the pickers":"確切的採收日期和採收者的姓名","Not every wine has a GI, but some statement of origin is required, such as the country.":"並非每一款酒都有 GI，但必須標示某種產地說明，例如國家。","A vineyard name is used only when the wine truly comes from it, and is often a GI itself. Vine age ('old vines') is optional and not legally defined. Exact dates and pickers' names do not appear on labels.":"葡萄園名稱只有在酒確實來自該葡萄園時才會使用，而且它本身常常就是一個 GI。樹齡（「老藤」）是選擇性的，沒有法律定義。確切日期和採收者姓名不會出現在酒標上。","A customer is looking at a wine from a non-EU GI and wants to predict its style. What is most useful to check on the label?":"一位顧客在看一款來自歐盟以外 GI 的酒，想預測它的風格。酒標上最值得查看的是什麼？","The grape variety":"葡萄品種","The GI name alone":"只看 GI 名稱","The colour of the capsule":"瓶封的顏色","The bottle size, which varies with the style of wine":"酒瓶容量，它會隨葡萄酒風格而不同","Outside the EU a GI only shows where the grapes grew, so the grape variety is the best clue.":"在歐盟以外，GI 只表示葡萄生長的地點，所以葡萄品種是最好的線索。","Outside the EU growers can plant whatever varieties they like, with few restrictions, so one place name can cover very different styles. That is why these wines are often varietally labelled. Capsule colour and bottle size tell you nothing reliable about style.":"在歐盟以外，種植者可以種任何想種的品種，限制很少，所以同一個地名可能涵蓋非常不同的風格。這就是為什麼這些酒常以品種標示。瓶封顏色和酒瓶容量都無法可靠地反映風格。","Which pair of Italian terms both indicate a PDO?":"下列哪一組義大利術語都代表 PDO？","IGT and DOC":"IGT 和 DOC","IGT and DOCG":"IGT 和 DOCG","IGT and table wine showing a region":"IGT 和標示產區的餐酒","In Italy DOC and DOCG are the traditional terms for PDO; IGT corresponds to PGI.":"在義大利，DOC 和 DOCG 是 PDO 的傳統術語；IGT 對應 PGI。","Each EU country uses its own traditional terms for the two categories. Any pair containing IGT mixes a PDO with a PGI. PDOs usually cover smaller areas with stricter rules.":"每個歐盟國家都用自己的傳統術語表示這兩個類別。任何包含 IGT 的組合都把 PDO 和 PGI 混在一起了。PDO 通常涵蓋較小的區域，規定較嚴格。","A Spanish label shows 'DOCa'. What does this tell you?":"一張西班牙酒標上寫著「DOCa」。這告訴你什麼？","That the wine is a PDO":"這款酒是 PDO","That the wine is a PGI":"這款酒是 PGI","That the wine is made from frozen grapes":"這款酒是用冰凍葡萄釀的","That the wine has no GI and comes from several countries":"這款酒沒有 GI，來自多個國家","In Spain, DO and DOCa are traditional terms for PDO.":"在西班牙，DO 和 DOCa 是 PDO 的傳統術語。","Spain's PGI term is Vino de la Tierra. DOCa (Denominación de Origen Calificada) belongs to the tier with smaller areas and tighter rules. It has nothing to do with frozen grapes, which is how icewine is made.":"西班牙的 PGI 術語是 Vino de la Tierra。DOCa（Denominación de Origen Calificada）屬於區域較小、規定較嚴格的等級。它與冰凍葡萄無關，冰凍葡萄是冰酒的釀法。","A German label says 'Prädikatswein'. Which EU category does the wine belong to?":"一張德國酒標上寫著「Prädikatswein」。這款酒屬於哪個歐盟類別？","Wine with no geographical indication":"沒有地理標示的葡萄酒","A category reserved for certified organic wines":"專屬於有機認證葡萄酒的類別","In Germany, Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein correspond to PDO; Landwein to PGI.":"在德國，Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein 對應 PDO；Landwein 對應 PGI。","Landwein is Germany's PGI term, with looser rules. Prädikatswein, like Qualitätswein, belongs to the higher tier. Organic is a separate certification, unrelated to the origin category.":"Landwein 是德國的 PGI 術語，規定較寬鬆。Prädikatswein 和 Qualitätswein 一樣屬於較高的等級。有機是另一種認證，與產地類別無關。","In France, what is the difference between AOC and AOP on a label?":"在法國，酒標上的 AOC 和 AOP 有什麼不同？","None: both are terms for the same PDO category":"沒有不同：兩者都是同一個 PDO 類別的術語","AOC is a PDO, AOP is a PGI":"AOC 是 PDO，AOP 是 PGI","AOP is used only for sweet wines":"AOP 只用於甜酒","AOC means organic, while AOP means a wine from old vines":"AOC 代表有機，而 AOP 代表老藤釀的酒","Appellation d'origine contrôlée and appellation d'origine protégée both indicate PDO.":"Appellation d'origine contrôlée 和 appellation d'origine protégée 都代表 PDO。","France's PGI term is Indication géographique protégée (IGP). AOC is the traditional term and is still widely seen, as in 'Appellation Chablis Contrôlée'. Neither term has anything to do with organic status, sweetness or vine age.":"法國的 PGI 術語是 Indication géographique protégée（IGP）。AOC 是傳統術語，至今仍很常見，例如「Appellation Chablis Contrôlée」。這兩個術語都與有機身分、甜度或樹齡無關。","Which of these terms does NOT indicate a PDO?":"下列哪一個術語不代表 PDO？","IGT is Italy's PGI term; the other three all indicate a PDO.":"IGT 是義大利的 PGI 術語；其他三個都代表 PDO。","DOCa (Spain), Qualitätswein (Germany) and AOC (France) all belong to the PDO tier. PGIs cover wider areas, with more freedom over grapes and techniques. That is why one producer's IGT wines can differ widely.":"DOCa（西班牙）、Qualitätswein（德國）和 AOC（法國）都屬於 PDO 等級。PGI 涵蓋較廣的區域，在品種和技術上有更多自由。這就是為什麼同一家生產者的 IGT 葡萄酒可能差異很大。","Which of these terms does NOT indicate a PGI?":"下列哪一個術語不代表 PGI？","DOC is an Italian PDO term; Landwein, Vino de la Tierra and IGP all indicate PGI.":"DOC 是義大利的 PDO 術語；Landwein、Vino de la Tierra 和 IGP 都代表 PGI。","Watch out for similar acronyms: Italy's DOC is a PDO, as is Spain's DO. The PGI terms are Landwein in Germany, Vino de la Tierra in Spain, IGP in France and IGT in Italy. Learning the table country by country avoids mix-ups.":"小心相似的縮寫：義大利的 DOC 是 PDO，西班牙的 DO 也是。PGI 術語在德國是 Landwein，在西班牙是 Vino de la Tierra，在法國是 IGP，在義大利是 IGT。逐國記住這張表就不會混淆。","Which statement about PGI wines is correct?":"關於 PGI 葡萄酒，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They range from cheap, high-volume wines to outstanding low-volume wines":"從便宜的大量生產酒款，到產量稀少的傑出酒款都有","They are always lower in quality than any PDO":"品質一定比任何 PDO 都低","They must be made from one grape only":"必須只用單一品種釀造","They have stricter rules than PDOs on grapes and winemaking":"在品種和釀造方面的規定比 PDO 更嚴格","PGIs' more flexible rules allow a very wide range of styles and quality levels.":"PGI 較彈性的規定容許非常廣泛的風格和品質等級。","PGIs cover wide areas with looser rules than PDOs, giving producers more freedom. Some use that freedom to make outstanding wines sold at a premium. Nothing requires a single grape variety.":"PGI 涵蓋廣大區域，規定比 PDO 寬鬆，給予生產者更多自由。有些生產者利用這份自由釀出以高價出售的傑出酒款。沒有任何規定要求使用單一品種。","Which statement about the term 'Old Vine' / vieilles vignes is correct?":"關於「Old Vine」／vieilles vignes 這個術語，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is not legally defined, so its use can be disputed":"它沒有法律定義，所以其使用可能引起爭議","It means vines at least 50 years old under EU law":"根據歐盟法律，它代表至少 50 年樹齡的葡萄樹","It may be used only on PDO wines":"它只能用在 PDO 葡萄酒上","It guarantees a sweet wine, because old vines give sweeter grapes":"它保證是甜酒，因為老藤結的葡萄比較甜","'Old vines' has no legal definition, so there can be disagreement over its use.":"「老藤」沒有法律定義，所以其使用可能有爭議。","Old vines give fewer grapes with more concentrated, complex flavours, hence their prestige. But no law sets a minimum age or limits the term to certain categories. It is about yield and concentration, not sweetness.":"老藤結的葡萄較少，風味更濃縮、更複雜，因此享有聲望。但沒有法律規定最低樹齡，也沒有把這個術語限制在特定類別。它關乎的是產量和濃縮度，而不是甜度。","What does the vintage on a label refer to?":"酒標上的年份指的是什麼？","The year the grapes were harvested":"葡萄採收的年份","The year the wine was bottled":"葡萄酒裝瓶的年份","The year the wine went on sale":"葡萄酒上市的年份","The year the vines that made the wine were planted":"釀酒的葡萄樹種植的年份","The vintage is the year of harvest.":"年份就是採收的年份。","Bottling and release can happen months or years after harvest. The vines' planting year is never shown as the vintage. Knowing the vintage helps you judge the wine's age and whether it is at its best.":"裝瓶和上市可能在採收後數月或數年才進行。葡萄樹的種植年份從不會標示為年份。了解年份有助於判斷酒的年齡，以及它是否處於最佳狀態。","Why is the vintage especially useful for expensive wines from prestigious regions with variable weather?":"對於來自天氣多變的知名產區的昂貴葡萄酒，為什麼年份特別有用？","Each year's weather can greatly affect grape quality":"每年的天氣可能大幅影響葡萄品質","It shows which grape was used":"它顯示使用了哪個品種","It reveals whether the wine is organic":"它透露這款酒是否有機","It proves the wine always has the same style, whatever the year's weather":"它證明無論當年天氣如何，酒的風格總是一樣","Where weather varies a lot year to year, the vintage helps predict style and quality.":"在天氣年年差異很大的地方，年份有助於預測風格和品質。","A cool or rainy year can produce a wine different from what you expect. Knowing it helps you decide if the price is justified and when to drink the wine. The last option says the opposite: variability is exactly why the vintage matters.":"涼爽或多雨的年份釀出的酒可能和你預期的不同。了解這一點有助於判斷價格是否合理，以及何時飲用。最後一個選項說的正好相反：正是因為多變，年份才重要。","A customer wants a dry white and points to an Australian bottle labelled 'Botrytis Semillon'. What should you tell them?":"一位顧客想要不甜的白酒，指著一瓶標示「Botrytis Semillon」的澳洲酒。你應該怎麼告訴他？","That it is almost certainly a sweet wine":"這幾乎可以肯定是一款甜酒","That it is a light, dry white":"這是一款輕盈、不甜的白酒","That it is a red, because Semillon is a black grape":"這是紅酒，因為榭密雍是黑葡萄","That it was ruined by a vineyard disease and should be avoided completely":"它被葡萄園的病害毀了，應該完全避開","Noble-rot grapes are highly concentrated in sugar and nearly always make sweet wines.":"貴腐葡萄的糖分高度濃縮，幾乎都用來釀甜酒。","Semillon is a white grape; outside the EU, varietal labelling is common. Here the Botrytis is beneficial: it is noble rot, which concentrates sugars and acids. For a dry white, suggest a different bottle.":"榭密雍是白葡萄；在歐盟以外，以品種標示很常見。這裡的貴腐菌是有益的：它就是貴腐，會濃縮糖和酸。想要不甜的白酒，就建議另一瓶吧。","What does 'Icewine' or 'Eiswein' on a label tell you about the harvest?":"酒標上的「Icewine」或「Eiswein」告訴你什麼採收資訊？","The grapes were left to freeze on the vine before picking":"葡萄在採收前留在樹上結冰","The grapes were frozen in the winery after harvest":"葡萄在採收後於酒廠冷凍","The wine is meant to be served over ice":"這款酒應該加冰塊飲用","The grapes were affected by noble rot in a very cold region":"葡萄在非常寒冷的產區受到貴腐菌感染","Icewine/Eiswein means grapes frozen naturally on the vine and pressed while still frozen.":"Icewine/Eiswein 是指葡萄在樹上自然結冰，並在結冰狀態下壓榨。","The ice stays in the press and the juice is rich in sugar and acid, usually for sweet wines. Freezing must happen in the vineyard, not the winery. Noble rot is a different concentration method, labelled as Botrytis or Noble Rot.":"冰留在壓榨機裡，果汁富含糖和酸，通常用來釀甜酒。結冰必須發生在葡萄園，而不是酒廠。貴腐是另一種濃縮方法，標示為 Botrytis 或 Noble Rot。","Compared with a wine from a normal harvest, what can you expect from a 'Late Harvest' wine of the same grape?":"與正常採收的酒相比，同一品種的「Late Harvest」葡萄酒可以預期有什麼不同？","More body and more concentration":"酒體更飽滿、更濃縮","Less alcohol and more acidity":"酒精較低、酸度較高","Greener, more herbaceous flavours":"風味更青澀、更有草本氣息","Exactly the same style, since only the bottling date matters":"風格完全相同，因為只有裝瓶日期才重要","Later-picked grapes are riper and sweeter, giving fuller-bodied, more concentrated wines.":"較晚採收的葡萄更成熟、更甜，釀出酒體更飽滿、更濃縮的酒。","Late harvest brings riper flavours and more sugar, not green notes. The wine can still be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet. Lower alcohol and higher acidity are typical of grapes picked early.":"晚收帶來更成熟的風味和更多糖分，而不是青澀的氣息。這款酒仍然可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜。酒精較低、酸度較高是早採葡萄的典型特徵。","Which microorganisms carry out alcoholic fermentation?":"哪一種微生物進行酒精發酵？","Bacteria":"細菌","Moulds":"黴菌","Yeast feed on the sugars in the juice and turn them into alcohol.":"酵母以果汁中的糖為食，把糖轉化為酒精。","Alcoholic fermentation is the one process common to all wines, and it is carried out by yeast. Bacteria, on the other hand, are responsible for malolactic conversion, which happens afterwards and lowers acidity. Moulds and enzymes are not what produce the alcohol: mixing them up with yeast is a common exam mistake.":"酒精發酵是所有葡萄酒共有的唯一過程，由酵母進行。相對地，細菌負責乳酸轉化，它發生在之後並降低酸度。製造酒精的不是黴菌或酵素：把它們和酵母搞混是考試中常見的錯誤。","Apart from alcohol, what do yeast produce during fermentation?":"除了酒精，酵母在發酵過程中還產生什麼？","Carbon dioxide and heat":"二氧化碳和熱","Oxygen and acidity":"氧氣和酸","Sugar and water":"糖和水","Fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, CO2 and heat.":"發酵把糖轉化為酒精、CO2 和熱。","As they consume sugar, yeast release alcohol, carbon dioxide and heat. For still wines the CO2 usually escapes into the air, while the heat must be controlled because temperature affects style. Colour and tannin are not made by yeast: they are extracted from the skins of black grapes, and the heat of fermentation helps that extraction.":"酵母消耗糖時，會釋放酒精、二氧化碳和熱。釀造靜態酒時，CO2 通常散逸到空氣中，而熱必須加以控制，因為溫度會影響風格。顏色和單寧不是酵母製造的：它們是從黑葡萄的果皮萃取出來的，發酵的熱有助於萃取。","What mainly determines the alcohol level of a dry wine?":"主要是什麼決定了不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度？","The amount of sugar in the grapes":"葡萄中的糖量","The type of vessel used":"使用的容器類型","The length of storage":"儲存的時間長短","The amount of tannin in the skins":"果皮中的單寧量","The more sugar in the grapes, the more alcohol the yeast can make.":"葡萄中的糖越多，酵母能產生的酒精就越多。","In a dry wine the yeast use up all the available sugar, so the final alcohol depends on how much sugar there was at the start, in other words on grape ripeness. That is why warm-climate wines tend to be higher in alcohol. Vessels, storage time and tannins affect other aspects of style, but not how much alcohol is produced.":"在不甜的葡萄酒中，酵母會把所有可用的糖消耗殆盡，所以最終的酒精濃度取決於一開始有多少糖，也就是葡萄的成熟度。這就是為什麼溫暖氣候的葡萄酒酒精濃度往往較高。容器、儲存時間和單寧會影響風格的其他方面，但不影響產生多少酒精。","What is the typical alcohol range of most dry wines?":"大多數不甜葡萄酒的典型酒精濃度範圍是多少？","About 11.5–16% abv":"約 11.5–16% abv","About 5–9% abv":"約 5–9% abv","About 15–20% abv":"約 15–20% abv","About 18–22% abv":"約 18–22% abv","Most dry wines sit between about 11.5% and 16% abv.":"大多數不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度約在 11.5% 到 16% abv 之間。","The alcohol level of dry wines depends on grape sugar and usually falls between 11.5% and 16% abv. The 15–20% abv range belongs to fortified wines, where alcohol is added to stop fermentation. Very low levels, under 10%, are not typical of dry wines, because they suggest that not all the sugar has been converted.":"不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度取決於葡萄的糖分，通常介於 11.5% 到 16% abv 之間。15–20% abv 的範圍屬於加烈酒，它們是添加酒精來中止發酵的。低於 10% 的極低酒精濃度不是不甜葡萄酒的典型特徵，因為這表示並非所有的糖都被轉化了。","In white winemaking, when does pressing usually take place?":"釀造白酒時，壓榨通常在什麼時候進行？","Before alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之前","After alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之後","During oak maturation":"橡木桶熟成期間","Just before bottling":"就在裝瓶前","For whites, grapes are crushed and pressed before fermenting, without skins.":"釀造白酒時，葡萄在發酵前破皮和壓榨，不帶果皮發酵。","The typical order for a white is crushing, pressing, fermentation, storage or maturation, packaging. The juice ferments apart from the skins, which are usually discarded, because colour and tannin are not wanted. For reds it is the opposite: pressing comes after fermentation, because the skins must stay in contact with the fermenting juice.":"白酒的典型順序是破皮、壓榨、發酵、儲存或熟成、包裝。果汁與果皮分開發酵，果皮通常被丟棄，因為不需要顏色和單寧。紅酒則相反：壓榨在發酵之後，因為果皮必須與發酵中的果汁保持接觸。","What is the typical order for a dry red wine?":"不甜紅酒的典型順序是什麼？","Draining, crushing, fermentation, pressing":"排汁、破皮、發酵、壓榨","In reds the skins ferment with the juice; draining and pressing come afterwards.":"釀造紅酒時，果皮與果汁一起發酵；排汁和壓榨在之後進行。","A red must be made from black grapes, and the skins must stay in the juice during fermentation to give colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is finished is the wine drained off the skins, and the wine left in them is recovered by pressing. Storage or maturation and finally packaging follow.":"紅酒必須用黑葡萄釀造，而且發酵期間果皮必須留在果汁中，以帶來顏色和單寧。只有在發酵結束後，才把酒從果皮中排出，留在果皮中的酒則透過壓榨回收。接著是儲存或熟成，最後是包裝。","Why can white wine be made from black grapes?":"為什麼可以用黑葡萄釀造白酒？","The colour is found only in the skin":"顏色只存在於果皮中","The colour disappears during fermentation":"顏色在發酵過程中消失","The colour is found only in the seeds":"顏色只存在於葡萄籽中","The colour is removed by oak":"顏色被橡木桶去除","Black grape pulp is clear, so gentle pressing keeps the juice colourless.":"黑葡萄的果肉是透明的，所以輕柔壓榨能讓果汁保持無色。","In black grapes the coloured pigments are found only in the skin, not the pulp. If the grapes are pressed very gently, the juice comes out almost colourless and, fermented away from the skins, makes a white wine. For a red, by contrast, the skins must take part in fermentation precisely to release their colour.":"黑葡萄的色素只存在於果皮，不在果肉。如果非常輕柔地壓榨葡萄，流出的果汁幾乎無色，與果皮分開發酵後就成了白酒。相反地，釀造紅酒時，果皮必須參與發酵，正是為了釋放顏色。","In the short maceration method for rosé, when are the skins removed?":"以短時間浸皮法釀造粉紅酒時，果皮在什麼時候移除？","After several weeks of fermentation":"發酵數週之後","Only at bottling":"直到裝瓶時","The skins stay in contact for just a few hours, enough for a light colour.":"果皮只接觸幾個小時，足以帶來淡淡的顏色。","With short maceration, black grapes are used and the process starts like a red, but the fermenting juice is drained off the skins after a few hours. The brief contact gives a pink colour and little tannin. Fermentation then continues without the skins, at the cooler temperatures used for whites, and rosés rarely see oak.":"短時間浸皮法使用黑葡萄，一開始像釀紅酒一樣，但幾個小時後就把發酵中的果汁從果皮中排出。短暫的接觸帶來粉紅色和少量單寧。之後發酵在沒有果皮的情況下繼續進行，溫度與白酒一樣較低，而粉紅酒很少經過橡木桶。","Which rosé method is not permitted in many parts of Europe?":"哪一種粉紅酒釀法在歐洲許多地方不被允許？","Blending red wine with white wine":"把紅酒和白酒混合","Short maceration of black grapes":"黑葡萄短時間浸皮","Fermenting at low temperature":"低溫發酵","Using stainless steel tanks":"使用不鏽鋼槽","Rosé made by blending red and white is banned in many European regions.":"把紅酒和白酒混合釀成的粉紅酒，在歐洲許多產區是禁止的。","The two most common rosé methods are short maceration and blending. In blending, a red wine is mixed with a white wine to achieve the pink colour. It is a simple technique, but it is not permitted in many parts of Europe. Short maceration, by contrast, is allowed and widely used.":"最常見的兩種粉紅酒釀法是短時間浸皮法和混合法。混合法是把紅酒和白酒混合，得到粉紅色。這是一種簡單的技術，但在歐洲許多地方不被允許。相反地，短時間浸皮法是允許的，而且廣泛使用。","Why are red wines fermented at higher temperatures than whites?":"為什麼紅酒的發酵溫度比白酒高？","To extract colour and tannin from the skins":"為了從果皮萃取顏色和單寧","To preserve delicate fruity aromas":"為了保留細緻的果香","To increase the wine's acidity":"為了提高酒的酸度","To stop the yeast early":"為了提早讓酵母停止作用","Heat helps extract colour and tannin from the skins.":"熱有助於從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。","Reds ferment at roughly 20–32°C, whites at 12–22°C. The higher temperatures allow reds to extract colour and tannin from the skins, which are essential to their style. Whites, which ferment without skins, benefit instead from cooler temperatures, which bring out fruity aromas.":"紅酒的發酵溫度約為 20–32°C，白酒則為 12–22°C。較高的溫度讓紅酒能從果皮萃取顏色和單寧，這對紅酒的風格不可或缺。不帶果皮發酵的白酒，則受益於較低的溫度，能帶出果香。","Which temperature range is typical for fermenting white wines?":"白酒典型的發酵溫度範圍是多少？","12–22°C (54–72°F)":"12–22°C（54–72°F）","20–32°C (68–90°F)":"20–32°C（68–90°F）","2–8°C (36–46°F)":"2–8°C（36–46°F）","30–40°C (86–104°F)":"30–40°C（86–104°F）","Whites ferment at 12–22°C, cooler than reds.":"白酒在 12–22°C 發酵，比紅酒低。","Whites ferment at roughly 12–22°C. At the cooler end of that range, fermentation can produce pronounced fruity aromas, prized in many fresh whites. The 20–32°C range belongs to reds, which need heat to extract colour and tannin. Short-maceration rosés, once drained, ferment at temperatures similar to whites.":"白酒的發酵溫度約為 12–22°C。在這個範圍的低溫端發酵，可以產生濃郁的果香，這在許多清爽的白酒中備受珍視。20–32°C 的範圍屬於紅酒，紅酒需要熱來萃取顏色和單寧。短時間浸皮的粉紅酒在排汁後，以類似白酒的溫度發酵。","A white wine fermented at a very cool temperature is most likely to show...":"一款在非常低溫下發酵的白酒，最可能表現出……","Pronounced fruity aromas":"濃郁的果香","High tannin":"高單寧","Nut and caramel aromas":"堅果和焦糖香氣","A deep amber colour":"深琥珀色","Cool white fermentations can produce pronounced fruity aromas.":"低溫發酵的白酒可以產生濃郁的果香。","At the cool end of the white range, around 12°C, fermentation can bring out pronounced fruity aromas. Nut and caramel come from contact with oxygen during barrel maturation, while an amber colour is a sign of age. High tannin does not apply to whites, which ferment without their skins.":"在白酒溫度範圍的低溫端，約 12°C 左右，發酵可以帶出濃郁的果香。堅果和焦糖來自橡木桶熟成期間與氧氣的接觸，而琥珀色則是陳年的跡象。高單寧不適用於白酒，因為白酒不帶果皮發酵。","What is the \"cap\" in red winemaking?":"紅酒釀造中的「酒帽」是什麼？","The layer of skins that floats to the top":"浮到頂部的果皮層","The layer of dead yeast at the bottom":"底部的死酵母層","The lid used to close the vessel":"用來封住容器的蓋子","The CO2 foam on top of the wine":"酒液表面的 CO2 泡沫","The skins float and form a thick layer called the cap.":"果皮浮起，形成一層稱為酒帽的厚層。","During red fermentation the skins rise and form the cap. Left undisturbed it gives up little colour and tannin, so it must be mixed often with the liquid by punching down or pumping over. The layer of dead yeast at the bottom, on the other hand, is called the lees and mostly matters in white winemaking.":"紅酒發酵期間，果皮上浮形成酒帽。如果不加處理，酒帽釋放的顏色和單寧很少，所以必須經常透過壓帽或淋汁讓它與液體混合。另一方面，底部的死酵母層稱為酒渣，主要在白酒釀造中發揮作用。","In which technique is liquid from the bottom of the vessel sprayed over the cap?":"哪一種技術是把容器底部的液體噴淋到酒帽上？","In pumping over, liquid is pumped through a hose and sprayed over the cap.":"淋汁是用管子抽取液體，噴淋到酒帽上。","Pumping over and punching down both mix skins and liquid to extract colour and tannin. In pumping over, liquid is drawn from the bottom of the vessel and sprayed over the cap; in punching down, a plunger pushes the cap down into the liquid. Draining and pressing take place once fermentation has finished.":"淋汁和壓帽都是讓果皮與液體混合，以萃取顏色和單寧。淋汁是從容器底部抽取液體，噴淋到酒帽上；壓帽則是用壓棒把酒帽壓入液體中。排汁和壓榨在發酵結束後進行。","In a cool vintage, why might a winemaker increase the sugar in the juice?":"在涼爽的年份，釀酒師為什麼可能提高果汁中的糖分？","To avoid a wine low in alcohol and body":"避免酒的酒精和酒體不足","To make the wine sweet":"讓酒變甜","To lower the acidity":"降低酸度","To extract more tannin":"萃取更多單寧","More sugar to ferment means more alcohol and more body.":"可發酵的糖越多，酒精和酒體就越多。","In cool climates or vintages the grapes may not ripen fully and may lack sugar, giving a wine low in alcohol and lacking body. Raising the sugar in the juice gives the yeast more to convert, so the finished wine has more alcohol. The added sugar is fermented, so the wine stays dry.":"在涼爽的氣候或年份，葡萄可能無法完全成熟、糖分不足，釀出的酒酒精低、酒體單薄。提高果汁中的糖分，讓酵母有更多可轉化的糖，成品酒的酒精就更高。添加的糖會被發酵掉，所以酒仍然是不甜的。","In a warm climate, which adjustment is most likely?":"在溫暖氣候中，最可能進行哪一種調整？","Adding acid":"加酸","Neutralising acid":"中和酸","Adding sugar":"加糖","Adding tannin":"添加單寧","In warm climates acidity drops sharply, leaving the wine unbalanced.":"在溫暖氣候中，酸度會大幅下降，讓酒失去平衡。","During ripening in a warm climate, grape acidity can fall very low. A wine with too little acidity would be unbalanced, so the winemaker may add acid in the winery. Neutralising acid and raising sugar are, by contrast, typical adjustments for cool climates, where grapes ripen with more acid and less sugar.":"在溫暖氣候中成熟時，葡萄的酸度可能降得非常低。酸度太低的酒會失去平衡，所以釀酒師可能在酒廠中加酸。相反地，中和酸和提高糖分是涼爽氣候的典型調整，因為那裡的葡萄成熟時酸較多、糖較少。","How does Tokaji Aszú get its sweetness?":"Tokaji Aszú 的甜味是怎麼來的？","From grapes with concentrated sugars":"來自糖分濃縮的葡萄","By adding alcohol":"添加酒精","By filtering out the yeast":"把酵母過濾掉","By adding juice to a dry wine":"在不甜的酒中加入果汁","The sugar is so concentrated that the yeast cannot consume it all.":"糖分濃縮到酵母無法全部消耗。","Tokaji Aszú from Hungary is made from grapes with highly concentrated sugars. When the juice is that sugary, the yeast cannot ferment it all, and fermentation stops with residual sugar left over. Adding alcohol is typical of Port, and filtering out yeast of White Zinfandel.":"匈牙利的 Tokaji Aszú 是用糖分高度濃縮的葡萄釀造的。當果汁這麼甜時，酵母無法把糖全部發酵完，發酵停止時就留下殘糖。添加酒精是 Port 的典型做法，過濾酵母則是 White Zinfandel 的做法。","Which sweet wine is made by removing the yeast with very fine filters?":"哪一種甜酒是用非常細的過濾器去除酵母釀成的？","Californian White Zinfandel uses filters that catch the yeast.":"加州的 White Zinfandel 使用能攔住酵母的過濾器。","Removing yeast from fermenting juice requires extremely sophisticated filters with holes small enough to catch them. Without yeast, fermentation stops and residual sugar remains: this is how White Zinfandel from California is made. Port is made by adding alcohol, while Tokaji Aszú and icewine start from grapes with concentrated sugars.":"要從發酵中的果汁去除酵母，需要極為精密、孔洞小到能攔住酵母的過濾器。沒有了酵母，發酵就停止，留下殘糖：加州的 White Zinfandel 就是這樣釀成的。Port 是添加酒精釀成的，而 Tokaji Aszú 和冰酒則是從糖分濃縮的葡萄開始。","Why is a fortified wine such as Port in no danger of fermenting again?":"為什麼像 Port 這樣的加烈酒沒有再次發酵的風險？","Alcohol at 15–20% abv kills the yeast":"15–20% abv 的酒精會殺死酵母","All the sugar has been used up":"所有的糖都已經用完了","The wine is filtered several times":"酒經過多次過濾","The wine is kept at a low temperature":"酒保存在低溫下","The added alcohol takes the wine to a level that kills yeast.":"添加的酒精讓酒達到足以殺死酵母的濃度。","Fortification adds alcohol to the fermenting juice, raising it to 15–20% abv. At this level the yeast die before they have used all the sugar, which stays in the wine as sweetness. The high alcohol also stops fermentation from restarting later, which is why Port is stable even though it is sweet.":"加烈是在發酵中的果汁裡添加酒精，把濃度提高到 15–20% abv。在這個濃度下，酵母在用完所有糖之前就死亡了，剩下的糖以甜味的形式留在酒中。高酒精也能防止日後重新發酵，這就是為什麼 Port 雖然是甜的，卻很穩定。","What is the main advantage of adding sweetness to a dry wine?":"在不甜的酒中添加甜味，主要的好處是什麼？","Precise control of the sweetness level":"精準控制甜度","A much higher alcohol level":"酒精濃度大幅提高","Softer tannins":"單寧更柔和","More intense oak flavours":"橡木桶風味更濃郁","Adding sweetness after fermentation lets the final sugar be set exactly.":"在發酵後添加甜味，可以準確設定最終的糖分。","This technique is widely used for red, white and rosé wines precisely because the winemaker can control sweetness accurately. The added sugar always comes from grapes: unfermented juice, very sweet concentrated juice, or a sweet wine blended with the dry one. It does not affect tannins or oak flavours.":"這項技術廣泛用於紅酒、白酒和粉紅酒，正是因為釀酒師可以精準控制甜度。添加的糖一定來自葡萄：未發酵的葡萄汁、非常甜的濃縮葡萄汁，或與不甜的酒混合的甜酒。它不會影響單寧或橡木桶風味。","What does crushing involve?":"破皮是指什麼？","Splitting the skins to release some of the juice":"把果皮弄破，釋放出一部分果汁","Squeezing the grapes to extract as much liquid as possible":"擠壓葡萄，盡可能取出最多液體","Separating the wine from the lees after fermentation":"發酵後把酒和酒渣分開","Pushing the cap of skins into the liquid with a plunger during red fermentation":"紅酒發酵期間用壓棒把果皮形成的酒帽壓入液體","Crushing means splitting the grape skins so some juice comes out.":"破皮是把葡萄果皮弄破，讓一部分果汁流出。","Squeezing hard is pressing, done in a press. Pushing the cap into the liquid is punching down, used for reds. Crushing is the first step for both white and red wines.":"用力擠壓是壓榨，在壓榨機中進行。把酒帽壓入液體是壓帽，用於紅酒。破皮是白酒和紅酒共同的第一步。","Which statement about pressing is correct?":"關於壓榨，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can take place before or after fermentation":"它可以在發酵之前或之後進行","It always happens after fermentation":"它總是在發酵之後進行","It always happens before crushing":"它總是在破皮之前進行","It is only used for sweet wines from frozen or noble-rot grapes":"它只用於以冰凍或貴腐葡萄釀造的甜酒","White wines are pressed before fermentation, red wines after it.":"白酒在發酵前壓榨，紅酒在發酵後壓榨。","Pressing squeezes crushed grapes to get out as much liquid as possible. For whites it separates juice from skins before fermentation; for reds it recovers the wine left in the skins after draining. It always follows crushing, never precedes it.":"壓榨是擠壓破皮後的葡萄，盡可能取出最多液體。對白酒來說，它在發酵前把果汁與果皮分開；對紅酒來說，它在排汁後回收留在果皮中的酒。壓榨總是在破皮之後，從不在之前。","When making a still wine, what happens to the carbon dioxide produced by the yeast?":"釀造靜態酒時，酵母產生的二氧化碳會怎樣？","It escapes into the atmosphere":"散逸到大氣中","It stays dissolved and makes the wine fizzy":"保持溶解，讓酒有氣泡","It turns into alcohol":"轉化為酒精","It is reabsorbed by the skins and deepens a red wine's colour":"被果皮重新吸收，加深紅酒的顏色","For still wines, fermentation CO2 is allowed to escape into the air.":"釀造靜態酒時，發酵產生的 CO2 會散逸到空氣中。","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol, CO2 and heat; CO2 is a product, it does not become alcohol. If it were trapped the wine would be fizzy. Red colour comes from the skins, helped by fermentation heat, not from CO2.":"酵母把糖轉化為酒精、CO2 和熱；CO2 是產物，不會變成酒精。如果把它封住，酒就會有氣泡。紅酒的顏色來自果皮，並藉助發酵的熱，而不是來自 CO2。","When does alcoholic fermentation usually stop naturally?":"酒精發酵通常在什麼時候自然停止？","When the yeast have eaten all the sugar":"當酵母把糖全部吃完時","After exactly one week":"剛好一週之後","When the wine reaches 5% abv":"當酒達到 5% abv 時","When the winemaker adds concentrated grape sugar to block the yeast":"當釀酒師加入濃縮葡萄糖來阻止酵母時","Fermentation typically ends on its own once no sugar is left, giving a dry wine.":"發酵通常在沒有糖剩下時自行結束，得到不甜的酒。","The final strength depends on the starting sugar: most dry wines are 11.5–16% abv. There is no fixed duration. Sweet wines use other techniques, such as highly concentrated grapes, filtration or adding alcohol.":"最終的酒精濃度取決於起始糖分：大多數不甜葡萄酒為 11.5–16% abv。發酵沒有固定的時間長度。甜酒則使用其他技術，例如高度濃縮的葡萄、過濾或添加酒精。","For most wines, how long is the storage period before bottling, and with what effect?":"對大多數葡萄酒來說，裝瓶前的儲存期有多長？效果如何？","Less than a year, with flavours changing little if at all":"不到一年，風味幾乎沒有變化","Several years in oak, with strong tertiary development":"在橡木桶中數年，發展出強烈的三級香氣","A few days, during which the wine gets sweeter":"幾天，期間酒會變甜","At least ten years in bottle, because every wine improves with time":"至少在瓶中十年，因為每一款酒都會隨時間變好","Most wine is stored for under a year, sometimes only months, and changes very little.":"大多數葡萄酒儲存不到一年，有時只有幾個月，變化非常小。","Only some wines are kept for long; this is called maturation, with flavours moving from primary to tertiary. Most wines do not improve in bottle and are best drunk young. Storage adds no sugar.":"只有部分葡萄酒會長期存放；這稱為熟成，風味從一級香氣轉向三級香氣。大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好，最好趁年輕飲用。儲存不會增加糖分。","What happens to a wine during extended maturation?":"長時間熟成期間，葡萄酒會發生什麼？","Flavours move from primary to tertiary and tannins become more integrated":"風味從一級轉向三級，單寧變得更融合","The wine regains the flavours of fresh grape juice":"酒重新獲得新鮮葡萄汁的風味","The alcohol rises by a few degrees":"酒精上升幾度","Tannins get harsher and red wines keep getting deeper in colour":"單寧變得更粗糙，紅酒的顏色越來越深","Maturation brings tertiary flavours and makes structure, such as tannin, more integrated.":"熟成帶來三級風味，並讓單寧等結構更融合。","Maturation usually takes place in oak, which can also add secondary flavours. Fruit loses freshness and never returns to fresh juice character. Tannins soften and red colour tends to fade; alcohol does not rise.":"熟成通常在橡木桶中進行，橡木桶也可能增添二級風味。果味失去新鮮感，再也不會回到新鮮果汁的特徵。單寧變柔和，紅酒的顏色傾向變淡；酒精不會上升。","What is still the most popular form of wine packaging?":"至今最受歡迎的葡萄酒包裝形式是什麼？","The glass bottle":"玻璃瓶","Bag-in-box":"盒中袋","The plastic bottle":"塑膠瓶","The carton brick, now used more than any other container":"紙盒包裝，現在比任何其他容器都更常用","Glass bottles remain the most widely used wine packaging.":"玻璃瓶仍然是使用最廣泛的葡萄酒包裝。","Bag-in-box, plastic bottles and cartons are real alternatives, but less common than glass. Packaging is the last step, after storage or maturation.":"盒中袋、塑膠瓶和紙盒都是實際可行的替代方案，但不如玻璃瓶普遍。包裝是最後一步，在儲存或熟成之後。","Which two conditions are needed to make a red wine?":"釀造紅酒需要哪兩個條件？","Black grapes, with the skins in the fermentation":"黑葡萄，且果皮參與發酵","Black grapes, pressed before fermentation":"黑葡萄，且在發酵前壓榨","Any grapes, and ageing in new oak":"任何葡萄，並在新橡木桶中陳年","White and black grapes mixed and fermented very cool":"白葡萄和黑葡萄混合，在非常低溫下發酵","Red wine comes from black grapes fermented with their skins, which give colour and tannin.":"紅酒來自與果皮一起發酵的黑葡萄，果皮帶來顏色和單寧。","Pressing black grapes before fermentation gives a white or nearly white wine, because the colour stays in the skins. Oak does not make wine red. Reds ferment warmer, 20–32°C, precisely to extract more.":"在發酵前壓榨黑葡萄，會得到白酒或近乎白色的酒，因為顏色留在果皮中。橡木桶不會讓酒變紅。紅酒在較高的溫度（20–32°C）下發酵，正是為了萃取更多。","In punching down, how are the skins mixed with the liquid?":"壓帽時，果皮是怎麼與液體混合的？","A plunger pushes the cap down into the liquid":"用壓棒把酒帽壓入液體","Liquid from the bottom is pumped up and sprayed over the cap":"把底部的液體抽上來噴淋到酒帽上","The skins are filtered out":"把果皮過濾掉","Alcohol is added to make the skins sink to the bottom of the tank":"加入酒精讓果皮沉到槽底","Punching down uses a plunger to push the cap of skins into the liquid.":"壓帽是用壓棒把果皮形成的酒帽壓入液體中。","Pumping liquid from the bottom over the cap is pumping over, the other common technique. Both extract colour and tannin from the skins. Adding alcohol is fortification, which stops fermentation.":"把底部的液體抽上來淋在酒帽上是淋汁，另一種常見的技術。兩者都是從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。添加酒精是加烈，會中止發酵。","Why must the cap of skins be mixed often during red fermentation?":"為什麼紅酒發酵期間必須經常混合果皮形成的酒帽？","Left undisturbed on top, it gives up little colour and tannin":"如果放著不動浮在上面，它釋放的顏色和單寧很少","To cool the must down to 12°C":"為了把葡萄汁冷卻到 12°C","To remove all tannin from the wine":"為了去除酒中所有的單寧","To release the alcohol faster, which would otherwise stay trapped in the skins":"為了更快釋放原本會困在果皮中的酒精","Skins float to form the cap; without mixing, extraction stays poor.":"果皮浮起形成酒帽；不加混合，萃取效果就很差。","Fermentation heat helps extraction, but is not enough on its own. That is why winemakers punch down or pump over frequently and thoroughly. Low temperatures such as 12°C suit whites, not reds.":"發酵的熱有助於萃取，但光靠它還不夠。這就是為什麼釀酒師會頻繁而徹底地壓帽或淋汁。12°C 這樣的低溫適合白酒，不適合紅酒。","In red winemaking, why are the skins pressed after draining?":"釀造紅酒時，為什麼要在排汁後壓榨果皮？","To recover the wine left in the skins":"為了回收留在果皮中的酒","To start the alcoholic fermentation":"為了開始酒精發酵","To make a rosé":"為了釀造粉紅酒","To add the sugar left in the skins and make the wine sweeter":"為了加入果皮中殘留的糖，讓酒更甜","After fermentation the wine is drained off, then the press extracts what remains in the skins.":"發酵後先把酒排出，再用壓榨機取出留在果皮中的部分。","The red order is crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing, storage, packaging. By then fermentation is over and the sugar has been used up. Rosé is made by separating the juice from the skins after only a few hours.":"紅酒的順序是破皮、發酵、排汁、壓榨、儲存、包裝。到這時發酵已經結束，糖也已經用完了。粉紅酒則是在短短幾小時後就把果汁與果皮分開。","In a short-maceration rosé, at what temperature does fermentation continue once the skins are removed?":"以短時間浸皮法釀造粉紅酒時，移除果皮後，發酵在什麼溫度下繼續？","At temperatures similar to white wines":"與白酒類似的溫度","At red-wine temperatures, up to 32°C":"紅酒的溫度，最高 32°C","Below freezing, as for icewine":"冰點以下，就像冰酒","It doesn't: fermentation always stops when the skins come out":"不會繼續：果皮一取出，發酵就停止","Once drained, rosé ferments like a white, at cooler temperatures.":"排汁後，粉紅酒像白酒一樣在較低溫度下發酵。","Fermentation starts as for a red, but the liquid is drained off the skins after a few hours and carries on without them. There is no more need to extract colour and tannin, so cooler temperatures are used. Rosés are rarely matured in oak.":"發酵一開始像紅酒，但幾小時後把液體從果皮中排出，接著在沒有果皮的情況下繼續發酵。這時已經不需要萃取顏色和單寧，所以使用較低的溫度。粉紅酒很少在橡木桶中熟成。","Which statement about maturing rosé wines is correct?":"關於粉紅酒的熟成，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They are rarely stored or matured in oak":"它們很少在橡木桶中儲存或熟成","They are always matured in new barriques":"它們總是在新的小型橡木桶中熟成","They must age for at least five years":"它們必須陳年至少五年","They stay on the skins for months during maturation to deepen the colour":"熟成期間它們與果皮接觸數月，以加深顏色","Rosés usually skip oak, which keeps their flavours fresh and fruity.":"粉紅酒通常不經橡木桶，這能讓風味保持清新果香。","The rosé style relies on fresh fruit, which oak flavours would mask. Skin contact lasts only a few hours; months of maceration would make a red. There is no minimum ageing requirement for rosé.":"粉紅酒的風格仰賴新鮮果味，橡木桶的風味會掩蓋它。果皮接觸只持續幾個小時；浸皮數月就會變成紅酒了。粉紅酒沒有最低陳年要求。","In white winemaking, what usually happens to the grape skins?":"釀造白酒時，葡萄果皮通常會怎樣？","They are removed at pressing, before fermentation":"在發酵前的壓榨階段被移除","They ferment with the juice for several days":"與果汁一起發酵數天","They are added back after fermentation for tannin":"在發酵後重新加入以增添單寧","They are kept throughout maturation, forming a cap on top of the wine":"在整個熟成期間保留，在酒液表面形成酒帽","For whites, grapes are crushed and pressed before fermentation and the skins are usually discarded.":"釀造白酒時，葡萄在發酵前破皮和壓榨，果皮通常被丟棄。","The white order is crushing, pressing, fermentation, storage, packaging. A cap of skins and long extraction belong to red winemaking. That is why white wines have very little tannin.":"白酒的順序是破皮、壓榨、發酵、儲存、包裝。果皮形成的酒帽和長時間萃取屬於紅酒釀造。這就是為什麼白酒的單寧非常少。","What is residual sugar?":"什麼是殘糖？","Sugar added to the juice before fermentation":"發酵前加入果汁中的糖","Sugar that settles at the bottom of the bottle":"沉澱在酒瓶底部的糖","Sugar left in the stems and seeds after pressing":"壓榨後殘留在果梗和葡萄籽中的糖","It is the sugar not converted into alcohol that remains in the finished wine.":"殘糖是沒有被轉化為酒精、留在成品酒中的糖。","Off-dry wines have a little, sweet wines can have a great deal. Sugar added before fermentation raises alcohol and is normally fermented away. Bottle deposit is typical of aged reds, not sugar.":"微甜的酒有一點殘糖，甜酒則可能有非常多。發酵前加入的糖會提高酒精，通常會被發酵掉。瓶中沉澱物是陳年紅酒的典型特徵，不是糖。","Why does juice from raisined, botrytised or frozen grapes often give a sweet wine without intervention?":"為什麼用風乾、貴腐或冰凍葡萄的果汁，常常不需干預就能釀出甜酒？","There is so much sugar that the yeast cannot eat it all":"糖多到酵母無法全部吃完","These juices contain no yeast":"這些果汁不含酵母","Alcohol is always added to stop fermentation":"總是會添加酒精來中止發酵","Very high acidity turns the alcohol already made back into sugar":"非常高的酸度把已經產生的酒精變回糖","With such concentrated sugar, fermentation stops by itself, leaving residual sugar.":"糖分如此濃縮，發酵會自行停止，留下殘糖。","Hungary's Tokaji Aszú is an example of this method. Adding alcohol is a different technique, fortification, used for example in Port. Yeast are present; they simply stop before finishing the sugar.":"匈牙利的 Tokaji Aszú 就是這種方法的例子。添加酒精是另一種技術，稱為加烈，例如用於 Port。酵母是存在的；它們只是在吃完糖之前就停止了。","Which of these is NOT one of the ways of adding sweetness to a dry wine?":"下列哪一項不是為不甜的酒添加甜味的方法之一？","Adding cane sugar syrup":"加入蔗糖糖漿","Adding unfermented grape juice":"加入未發酵的葡萄汁","Adding concentrated grape juice":"加入濃縮葡萄汁","Blending the dry wine with a sweet wine":"把不甜的酒與甜酒混合","The added sweetness comes from grapes: juice, concentrated juice or a sweet wine.":"添加的甜味來自葡萄：葡萄汁、濃縮葡萄汁或甜酒。","This technique is widely used because it allows precise control of sweetness, for reds, whites and rosés. The three valid options all use grape sugars. Cane sugar is not among the methods described.":"這項技術使用廣泛，因為它能精準控制紅酒、白酒和粉紅酒的甜度。三個有效的選項都使用葡萄的糖。蔗糖不在所述的方法之中。","In a cool vintage the grapes are too acidic. What can the winemaker do?":"在涼爽的年份，葡萄太酸。釀酒師可以怎麼做？","Neutralise some of the acid":"中和一部分的酸","Add more acid":"加入更多酸","Ferment at 32°C":"在 32°C 下發酵","Add fresh grape juice after bottling to dilute the acidity":"在裝瓶後加入新鮮葡萄汁來稀釋酸度","In cool conditions some acid can be neutralised so the wine is not unbalanced by acidity.":"在涼爽的條件下，可以中和一部分的酸，以免酸度讓酒失去平衡。","Adding acid is the typical correction in warm climates, where acidity falls too low. In cool conditions the winemaker may also raise the sugar in the juice for more alcohol and body. Adjustments are made during winemaking, not after bottling.":"加酸是溫暖氣候的典型調整，那裡的酸度會降得太低。在涼爽的條件下，釀酒師也可能提高果汁中的糖分，以獲得更多酒精和酒體。調整是在釀造過程中進行的，不是在裝瓶後。","Why must the winemaker monitor fermentation temperature?":"為什麼釀酒師必須監控發酵溫度？","Fermentation creates heat, and the temperature must suit the style":"發酵會產生熱，而溫度必須符合想要的風格","Otherwise the wine turns sparkling":"否則酒會變成氣泡酒","To decide which vintage goes on the label":"為了決定酒標上要標示哪個年份","Because the law requires the same temperature for all wines, white or red":"因為法律規定所有葡萄酒，無論白酒或紅酒，都要用相同的溫度","Fermentation warms the juice, so it must be kept within the right range for the intended wine.":"發酵會讓果汁升溫，所以必須把溫度保持在適合目標酒款的範圍內。","Wineries today have technology to chill or warm a fermentation. Reds and whites have different ranges, 20–32°C versus 12–22°C, so there is no single temperature. The vintage depends only on the harvest year.":"現今的酒廠擁有可以為發酵降溫或加溫的技術。紅酒和白酒的溫度範圍不同，分別是 20–32°C 和 12–22°C，所以沒有單一的溫度。年份只取決於採收年。","A tank of red wine is fermenting at 28°C. What would a winemaker think?":"一槽紅酒正在 28°C 下發酵。釀酒師會怎麼想？","It is a normal temperature for a red":"這是紅酒的正常溫度","Too hot: reds ferment between 12 and 22°C":"太熱了：紅酒應在 12 到 22°C 之間發酵","Too cold to extract any colour":"太冷了，無法萃取任何顏色","It is the typical temperature for a rosé already drained off its skins":"這是已經排汁的粉紅酒的典型溫度","Reds usually ferment at 20–32°C, so 28°C is well within range.":"紅酒通常在 20–32°C 發酵，所以 28°C 完全在範圍內。","Higher temperatures help extract colour and tannin from the skins. The 12–22°C range is for whites, and for rosé after draining. At 28°C extraction is helped, not prevented.":"較高的溫度有助於從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。12–22°C 的範圍適用於白酒，以及排汁後的粉紅酒。在 28°C 下，萃取是受到幫助，而不是被阻礙。","What is today the most common way of killing the yeast to leave sugar in the wine?":"現今殺死酵母、把糖留在酒中最常見的方法是什麼？","Adding alcohol to the fermenting juice":"在發酵中的果汁裡添加酒精","Chilling the wine to 12°C":"把酒冷卻到 12°C","Mixing the cap of skins often during fermentation":"在發酵期間經常混合果皮形成的酒帽","Fortification raises alcohol to 15–20% abv, which kills the yeast.":"加烈把酒精提高到 15–20% abv，從而殺死酵母。","There are several ways to kill yeast, but adding alcohol is the most widely used today. 12°C is a normal white fermentation temperature and does not stop yeast. Acid adjusts balance, and mixing the cap is for extraction.":"殺死酵母的方法有好幾種，但添加酒精是現今使用最廣泛的。12°C 是白酒的正常發酵溫度，不會讓酵母停止。酸用來調整平衡，混合酒帽則是為了萃取。","Why would a winemaker choose stainless steel for a fresh, fruity white?":"為什麼釀酒師會為清爽果香的白酒選擇不鏽鋼槽？","It is inert and can be airtight":"它是惰性的，而且可以密封","It adds vanilla flavours":"它會增添香草風味","It lets oxygen in":"它會讓氧氣進入","It softens tannins":"它會讓單寧變柔和","Steel adds no flavour and can keep oxygen out, preserving the fruit.":"不鏽鋼不會增添風味，還能隔絕氧氣，保留果味。","Stainless steel and concrete are inert materials: they give no flavour to the wine. They can also be made airtight, stopping oxygen from changing the flavours. For a white where the aim is fresh, primary fruit, they are the ideal choice. Vanilla, oxygen contact and softer tannins are, by contrast, typical effects of oak barrels.":"不鏽鋼和混凝土是惰性材質：它們不會為酒增添任何風味。它們也可以做成密封的，防止氧氣改變風味。對於追求新鮮一級果味的白酒來說，它們是理想的選擇。相反地，香草、與氧氣接觸和更柔和的單寧，是橡木桶的典型效果。","Which pair of vessel materials is considered inert?":"下列哪一組容器材質被視為惰性的？","Stainless steel and concrete":"不鏽鋼和混凝土","New oak and old oak":"新橡木桶和舊橡木桶","Oak and concrete":"橡木和混凝土","Stainless steel and oak":"不鏽鋼和橡木","Stainless steel and concrete add no flavour to the wine.":"不鏽鋼和混凝土不會為酒增添風味。","Winery vessels divide into inert and oak. Stainless steel and concrete are inert: they can be used for fermentation and storage without changing the flavours. Oak, new or old, is not inert: even an old barrel, which gives little flavour, still lets oxygen in and makes the wine evolve during maturation.":"酒廠的容器分為惰性容器和橡木容器。不鏽鋼和混凝土是惰性的：可以用來發酵和儲存而不改變風味。橡木無論新舊都不是惰性的：即使是幾乎不帶風味的舊桶，仍然會讓氧氣進入，使酒在熟成期間演變。","What are the two ways an oak barrel influences wine style?":"橡木桶影響葡萄酒風格的兩種方式是什麼？","Adding flavour and allowing oxygen contact":"增添風味，以及讓酒與氧氣接觸","Raising alcohol and acidity":"提高酒精和酸度","Adding sugar and tannin":"增添糖分和單寧","Filtering the wine and clarifying it":"過濾並澄清酒液","Oak gives its own flavours and, not being airtight, lets oxygen in.":"橡木桶會帶來自身的風味，而且因為不密封，會讓氧氣進入。","Barrels are watertight but not airtight. They therefore work in two ways: they add flavours such as vanilla, coconut or spice directly, especially when new, and they let a little oxygen interact with the wine, developing caramel and nut notes and softening red wine tannins. They do not raise alcohol, acidity or sugar.":"橡木桶不漏水，但並不密封。因此它以兩種方式發揮作用：直接增添香草、椰子或香料等風味，尤其是新桶；以及讓少量氧氣與酒相互作用，發展出焦糖和堅果氣息，並讓紅酒的單寧變柔和。它們不會提高酒精、酸度或糖分。","Which flavours are typical of a new oak barrel?":"哪些風味是新橡木桶的典型特徵？","Vanilla, coconut, charred wood, spice":"香草、椰子、炭烤木頭、香料","Biscuit, bread, toast crust":"餅乾、麵包、烤麵包皮","Butter, cream, yoghurt":"奶油、鮮奶油、優格","Fig, prune, wet leaves":"無花果、黑李乾、濕葉子","New oak gives lots of flavour: vanilla, coconut, charred wood and spice.":"新橡木桶帶來大量風味：香草、椰子、炭烤木頭和香料。","A barrel that has never been used still has all its flavour potential and can give a lot: vanilla, coconut, charred wood and spice. Biscuit and bread notes come instead from lees contact, buttery notes from malolactic conversion, while fig, prune and wet leaves are tertiary flavours of reds aged in bottle.":"從未使用過的橡木桶仍保有全部的風味潛力，能帶來很多風味：香草、椰子、炭烤木頭和香料。餅乾和麵包的氣息則來自與酒渣接觸，奶油氣息來自乳酸轉化，而無花果、黑李乾和濕葉子是瓶中陳年紅酒的三級風味。","After how many uses does a barrel have very little flavour left to give?":"橡木桶使用幾次之後，就幾乎沒有風味可以給了？","After two or three uses":"使用兩到三次之後","After a single use":"只使用一次之後","Never, oak always gives flavour":"永遠不會，橡木總是會帶來風味","After two or three uses a barrel is old oak, with little flavour left.":"使用兩到三次之後，橡木桶就成了舊桶，幾乎沒有風味可以給了。","Every time a barrel is filled it gives up some of its flavour. From the second use it already gives less than a new barrel, and after two or three uses it has very little left: this is called old oak. Such barrels are still useful when the aim is the effect of oxygen without strong oak character.":"每次裝酒，橡木桶都會釋出一部分風味。從第二次使用起，它給的風味就已經比新桶少，使用兩到三次之後就幾乎所剩無幾：這稱為舊桶。當目標是氧氣的效果、而不要強烈的橡木特徵時，這樣的桶仍然很有用。","What determines a barrel's toast level?":"什麼決定了橡木桶的烘烤程度？","How long and how hot the staves are heated":"桶板加熱的時間長短和溫度高低","The age of the oak trees":"橡樹的樹齡","How many times the barrel has been used":"橡木桶使用過的次數","The temperature of the cellar":"酒窖的溫度","Staves are heated over flame: time and heat set the toast level.":"桶板在火上加熱：時間和熱度決定烘烤程度。","To make a barrel, the oak staves are heated over an open flame and bent into shape. The longer and hotter the heating, the higher the toast level. Toasting changes the flavours the wood gives to the wine and can produce sweet-spice and charred-wood notes.":"製作橡木桶時，橡木桶板在明火上加熱並彎曲成形。加熱時間越長、溫度越高，烘烤程度就越高。烘烤會改變木頭為酒帶來的風味，可能產生甜香料和炭烤木頭的氣息。","Why do oxygen-related changes happen faster in small barrels?":"為什麼在小型橡木桶中，與氧氣相關的變化發生得比較快？","More of the wine is in contact with the wood":"有更多的酒與木頭接觸","Small barrels are always made of newer oak":"小型橡木桶總是用較新的橡木製成","Small barrels are airtight":"小型橡木桶是密封的","Small barrels are more heavily toasted":"小型橡木桶烘烤得比較重","In small barrels a greater share of the wine touches the wood.":"在小型橡木桶中，有較大比例的酒接觸到木頭。","In a small barrel the ratio of wood surface to wine volume is higher, so more of the wine is in contact with the barrel. Interactions with oxygen, such as the development of caramel and nut flavours and the softening of tannins, therefore happen faster. Large oak vessels are rarely used to give oak flavour.":"在小型橡木桶中，木頭表面積與酒液體積的比例較高，所以有更多的酒與桶接觸。因此，與氧氣的相互作用，例如焦糖和堅果風味的發展以及單寧的柔化，發生得更快。大型橡木容器很少用來增添橡木風味。","Which flavours can develop from oxygen during barrel maturation?":"橡木桶熟成期間，氧氣會發展出哪些風味？","Caramel, dried fruit, hazelnut":"焦糖、果乾、榛果","Citrus, green apple, flowers":"柑橘、青蘋果、花香","Butter and cream":"奶油和鮮奶油","Bread and biscuit":"麵包和餅乾","Oxygen entering the barrel develops caramel, dried fruit and nut notes.":"進入橡木桶的氧氣會發展出焦糖、果乾和堅果氣息。","Barrels are not airtight: during maturation a little oxygen gets in and interacts with the wine, encouraging caramel, dried fruit and nut flavours such as hazelnut, almond and walnut. Citrus and green apple are primary grape flavours; butter comes from malolactic conversion; bread and biscuit from lees contact.":"橡木桶並不密封：熟成期間少量氧氣進入並與酒相互作用，促進焦糖、果乾以及榛果、杏仁和核桃等堅果風味。柑橘和青蘋果是葡萄的一級風味；奶油來自乳酸轉化；麵包和餅乾來自與酒渣接觸。","How can oak flavour be given to an inexpensive wine?":"如何為平價的葡萄酒增添橡木風味？","With staves or chips in an inert vessel":"在惰性容器中加入橡木條或橡木片","With long lees contact":"長時間與酒渣接觸","Through malolactic conversion":"透過乳酸轉化","With large old oak vessels":"使用大型舊橡木容器","Staves and chips cost far less than barrels and still give oak flavour.":"橡木條和橡木片比橡木桶便宜得多，仍然能帶來橡木風味。","Oak barrels are expensive. For cheaper wines, oak staves or chips can be added to wine stored in an inert vessel, giving oak flavour at a lower cost. Large old oak vessels rarely add oak flavour, while lees and malolactic conversion give bread and buttery notes respectively, not oak.":"橡木桶很昂貴。對於較便宜的葡萄酒，可以在儲存於惰性容器中的酒裡加入橡木條或橡木片，以較低的成本帶來橡木風味。大型舊橡木容器很少增添橡木風味，而酒渣和乳酸轉化分別帶來麵包和奶油氣息，不是橡木風味。","Which microorganism carries out malolactic conversion?":"哪一種微生物進行乳酸轉化？","Moulds from the oak":"來自橡木的黴菌","Malolactic conversion is carried out by bacteria, not yeast.":"乳酸轉化是由細菌進行的，不是酵母。","Malolactic conversion takes place after alcoholic fermentation and is the work of bacteria. Yeast are responsible for alcoholic fermentation, while botrytis is a fungus that acts in the vineyard, concentrating grape sugars. The bacteria's activity lowers the wine's acidity and can add buttery flavours.":"乳酸轉化發生在酒精發酵之後，是細菌的作用。酵母負責酒精發酵，而貴腐菌是在葡萄園中作用、濃縮葡萄糖分的真菌。細菌的活動會降低酒的酸度，並可能增添奶油風味。","What are the effects of malolactic conversion?":"乳酸轉化有什麼效果？","Lower acidity and possible buttery flavours":"降低酸度，可能帶來奶油風味","Higher acidity and citrus flavours":"提高酸度，帶來柑橘風味","More alcohol and more body":"更多酒精和更飽滿的酒體","More tannin and deeper colour":"更多單寧和更深的顏色","The bacteria lower acidity and can give buttery flavours.":"細菌會降低酸度，並可能帶來奶油風味。","The bacteria's activity during malolactic conversion lowers the wine's acidity and can add buttery flavours, giving a softer style. It does not produce alcohol, which comes only from yeast in alcoholic fermentation, nor does it add tannin or colour, which come from the skins. That is why it is avoided when a lively, fresh white is wanted.":"乳酸轉化期間細菌的活動會降低酒的酸度，並可能增添奶油風味，讓風格更柔和。它不會產生酒精，酒精只來自酒精發酵中的酵母；也不會增添單寧或顏色，那些來自果皮。這就是為什麼想要活潑清爽的白酒時會避免它。","For which grape is malolactic conversion usually prevented?":"對哪一個品種通常會阻止乳酸轉化？","For aromatic grapes like Riesling, acidity and fruit are kept intact.":"對於麗絲玲這類芳香品種，會完整保留酸度和果味。","In whites, malolactic conversion is a choice. For aromatic varieties like Riesling it is usually prevented, because it would lower acidity and add buttery notes that would mask the fruit. Certain styles of Chardonnay, on the other hand, benefit from it. In reds such as Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir it nearly always takes place.":"對白酒來說，乳酸轉化是一種選擇。對於麗絲玲這類芳香品種，通常會阻止它，因為它會降低酸度，並增添掩蓋果味的奶油氣息。另一方面，某些風格的夏多內則受益於它。在卡本內蘇維濃和黑皮諾等紅酒中，它幾乎總是會發生。","What are lees?":"什麼是酒渣？","Dead yeast cells that settle at the bottom":"沉到底部的死酵母細胞","Skins floating on the surface":"浮在表面的果皮","Oak chips added to the wine":"加入酒中的橡木片","The deposit in aged red wines":"陳年紅酒中的沉澱物","After fermentation the yeast die and form a layer at the bottom.":"發酵結束後，酵母死亡並在底部形成一層。","When alcoholic fermentation ends, the yeast die and fall to the bottom of the vessel, forming a layer of dead cells: the lees. Floating skins form the cap in red winemaking instead, and the deposit that appears in reds aged in bottle is a different phenomenon, linked to maturation.":"酒精發酵結束時，酵母死亡並落到容器底部，形成一層死細胞：這就是酒渣。浮起的果皮則是在紅酒釀造中形成酒帽，而瓶中陳年紅酒出現的沉澱物是另一種與熟成相關的現象。","What effect does stirring the lees have on a white wine?":"攪動酒渣對白酒有什麼效果？","More body and bread and biscuit flavours":"更飽滿的酒體，以及麵包和餅乾風味","More acidity and citrus flavours":"更高的酸度和柑橘風味","More tannin and colour":"更多單寧和顏色","Less alcohol and less body":"酒精更低，酒體更輕","Lees contact adds body and bread and biscuit notes.":"與酒渣接觸會增添酒體以及麵包和餅乾氣息。","If the winemaker keeps a white in contact with its lees, they can be stirred through the wine during maturation. This increases the wine's body and adds flavours such as biscuit and bread. It does not raise acidity or tannin, nor lower alcohol. It is a typical choice for rich whites, often combined with malolactic conversion or oak.":"如果釀酒師讓白酒與酒渣保持接觸，就可以在熟成期間把酒渣攪入酒中。這會增加酒體，並增添餅乾和麵包等風味。它不會提高酸度或單寧，也不會降低酒精。這是豐潤型白酒的典型選擇，常與乳酸轉化或橡木桶結合。","Why are different wines blended each year for a branded wine?":"為什麼品牌酒每年都要混調不同的酒？","To keep the style consistent":"為了保持風格一致","To avoid malolactic conversion":"為了避免乳酸轉化","To make the wine clearer":"為了讓酒更清澈","Consumers expect a branded wine to taste the same every year.":"消費者期待品牌酒每年喝起來都一樣。","Each vintage gives different wines because of climate and weather. For a branded wine, though, consumers expect the same taste year after year. The winemaker therefore blends different wines to rebuild the same profile. Blending also serves to create complexity, but its purpose is not to raise alcohol or clarify the wine.":"由於氣候和天氣，每個年份的酒都不同。但對於品牌酒，消費者期待年年都是同樣的味道。因此釀酒師會混調不同的酒，重建相同的風味特徵。混調也用來創造複雜度，但它的目的不是提高酒精或澄清酒液。","Which kind of blending aims mainly at complexity?":"哪一種混調主要是為了複雜度？","Combining wines from different grapes, sites or techniques":"結合來自不同品種、園地或技術的酒","Combining dry wine and grape juice":"結合不甜的酒和葡萄汁","Combining red and white wine":"結合紅酒和白酒","Combining wine and spirit":"結合葡萄酒和烈酒","Different components make the wine more complex than its parts.":"不同的組成讓酒比各部分更複雜。","By blending wines from different grape varieties, vineyard locations or techniques, the winemaker creates a wine more complex than its individual components. Combining dry wine with juice is used for sweetening, combining red and white is a rosé method, and adding spirit is fortification.":"透過混調來自不同葡萄品種、葡萄園位置或技術的酒，釀酒師能創造出比各個組成更複雜的酒。結合不甜的酒和葡萄汁是為了增甜，結合紅酒和白酒是粉紅酒的釀法，加入烈酒則是加烈。","Why do some winemakers choose not to filter their wine?":"為什麼有些釀酒師選擇不過濾他們的酒？","They feel it can strip the wine's character":"他們認為過濾可能剝奪酒的個性","It makes the wine more alcoholic":"過濾會讓酒的酒精更高","It adds oak flavours":"過濾會增添橡木風味","It increases the wine's acidity":"過濾會提高酒的酸度","Some believe filtration can take something away from the wine's character.":"有些人認為過濾可能奪走酒的部分個性。","Most consumers want a perfectly clear wine, and filtration helps achieve that. Some winemakers, however, feel these techniques can take something away from the wine's character and prefer not to use them. Their wine may therefore look less than perfectly clear in the glass. Filtration does not affect alcohol, oak or acidity.":"大多數消費者想要完全清澈的酒，而過濾有助於達到這一點。不過，有些釀酒師認為這些技術可能奪走酒的部分個性，因此寧可不用。他們的酒在杯中可能看起來不那麼完全清澈。過濾不會影響酒精、橡木或酸度。","How does a white wine's colour change with age?":"白酒的顏色如何隨年齡變化？","Lemon → gold → amber, deeper":"檸檬色 → 金黃色 → 琥珀色，越來越深","Gold → lemon → green, paler":"金黃色 → 檸檬色 → 綠色，越來越淺","Amber → gold → lemon, paler":"琥珀色 → 金黃色 → 檸檬色，越來越淺","Lemon → pink → garnet":"檸檬色 → 粉紅色 → 石榴紅","Whites go from lemon to gold to amber and deepen in colour.":"白酒從檸檬色變成金黃色再到琥珀色，顏色加深。","Over time, the colour of whites moves from lemon to gold and finally amber, also becoming deeper. This is the opposite of reds, which tend to get paler with age, moving from ruby to garnet, tawny and brown. Alongside the colour change, tertiary flavours such as dried apricot, honey, nut and spice appear.":"隨著時間推移，白酒的顏色從檸檬色轉為金黃色，最後成為琥珀色，同時也變得更深。這與紅酒相反，紅酒隨著陳年往往變淡，從寶石紅轉為石榴紅、茶褐色和褐色。伴隨顏色變化，還會出現杏桃乾、蜂蜜、堅果和香料等三級風味。","Which set of flavours signals a red wine that has aged in bottle?":"哪一組風味表示紅酒經過瓶中陳年？","Fig, prune, meat, wet leaves":"無花果、黑李乾、肉、濕葉子","Strawberry, raspberry, fresh cherry":"草莓、覆盆子、新鮮櫻桃","Butter, bread, biscuit":"奶油、麵包、餅乾","Fig, prune, meat and wet leaves are tertiary flavours of reds.":"無花果、黑李乾、肉和濕葉子是紅酒的三級風味。","With bottle age, the fresh fruit of reds gives way to dried fruit and complex notes: fig, prune, meat and wet leaves, as well as mushroom and leather. Strawberry and fresh cherry are primary flavours of a young wine; vanilla and coconut come from new oak; butter, bread and biscuit from malolactic conversion and lees.":"經過瓶中陳年，紅酒的新鮮果味讓位給果乾和複雜的氣息：無花果、黑李乾、肉和濕葉子，還有蘑菇和皮革。草莓和新鮮櫻桃是年輕酒款的一級風味；香草和椰子來自新橡木桶；奶油、麵包和餅乾則來自乳酸轉化和酒渣。","Which feature matters most for a wine to improve in bottle?":"一款酒要在瓶中變好，哪個特徵最重要？","Enough concentration of flavour":"足夠的風味濃縮度","A low alcohol level":"低酒精濃度","Low acidity":"低酸度","A plastic closure":"塑膠瓶塞","Above all, the wine needs enough flavour concentration to evolve well.":"最重要的是，酒需要足夠的風味濃縮度才能好好演變。","Most wines do not improve in bottle: their fruit fades and vegetal notes appear. Wines for ageing often have high acidity, plenty of sugar if sweet and plenty of tannin if red, components that preserve them. Above all, though, they need enough concentration of flavour to evolve positively and gain complexity.":"大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好：果味會消退，出現植物性氣息。適合陳年的酒往往酸度高，若是甜酒則糖分多，若是紅酒則單寧多，這些成分能保存酒。但最重要的是，它們需要足夠的風味濃縮度，才能正向演變並增添複雜度。","Which statement about oak barrels is correct?":"關於橡木桶，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They are watertight but not airtight":"不漏水但不密封","They are airtight like steel tanks":"像不鏽鋼槽一樣密封","They let both air and wine through":"空氣和酒都會透過","They are inert and give no flavour to the wine, like concrete":"像混凝土一樣是惰性的，不會為酒增添風味","Wood holds the wine in but lets some oxygen in during maturation.":"木頭能留住酒液，但熟成期間會讓一些氧氣進入。","This oxygen contact is exactly what develops caramel, dried fruit and nut notes and softens tannins. Steel and concrete, by contrast, are inert and can be made airtight. Oak is not inert: especially when new, it adds flavour.":"正是這種與氧氣的接觸發展出焦糖、果乾和堅果氣息，並讓單寧變柔和。相反地，不鏽鋼和混凝土是惰性的，而且可以做成密封的。橡木不是惰性的：尤其是新桶，會增添風味。","A winemaker wants a wine to mature with some oxygen contact but without picking up oak flavour. Which vessel fits best?":"一位釀酒師希望酒在熟成時與一些氧氣接觸，但不沾染橡木風味。哪一種容器最合適？","A large, old oak vessel":"大型舊橡木容器","A small, new, heavily toasted barrel":"重度烘烤的小型新橡木桶","A sealed stainless steel tank":"密封的不鏽鋼槽","A sealed concrete tank with new oak chips added":"加入新橡木片的密封混凝土槽","Large old oak vessels allow oxygen exchange but give very little oak flavour.":"大型舊橡木容器允許氧氣交換，但帶來的橡木風味非常少。","Large vessels are rarely used to add oak flavour, and after two or three uses the wood has little left to give. A small new barrel would add lots of oak. A sealed steel tank keeps oxygen out, and chips are used precisely to add oak flavour.":"大型容器很少用來增添橡木風味，而木頭使用兩到三次之後也所剩無幾。小型新橡木桶會增添大量橡木風味。密封的不鏽鋼槽會隔絕氧氣，而橡木片正是用來增添橡木風味的。","What effect does oxygen entering the barrel have on a red wine's tannins?":"進入橡木桶的氧氣對紅酒的單寧有什麼影響？","It softens them":"讓單寧變柔和","It makes them harsher and bitter":"讓單寧變粗糙苦澀","It removes them completely":"把單寧完全去除","None, because oxygen only affects white wines":"沒有影響，因為氧氣只影響白酒","Slow oxygen contact helps soften red wine tannins.":"緩慢的氧氣接觸有助於柔化紅酒的單寧。","These changes are faster in small barrels, where more of the wine touches the wood. Tannins soften but do not disappear. Oxygen affects whites and reds alike, developing notes such as caramel and dried fruit.":"在小型橡木桶中，這些變化更快，因為有更多的酒接觸到木頭。單寧會變柔和，但不會消失。氧氣對白酒和紅酒都有影響，會發展出焦糖和果乾等氣息。","Which aromas are linked in particular to the toast level of a barrel?":"哪些香氣特別與橡木桶的烘烤程度有關？","Sweet spice and charred wood":"甜香料和炭烤木頭","Fresh citrus and crisp green apple":"清新的柑橘和爽脆的青蘋果","Heating the staves over a flame gives sweet-spice and charred-wood notes.":"在火上加熱桶板會帶來甜香料和炭烤木頭的氣息。","Butter and cream come from malolactic conversion, bread and biscuit from lees contact. Citrus and green apple are primary grape aromas. The length and heat of toasting decide how strong it is.":"奶油和鮮奶油來自乳酸轉化，麵包和餅乾來自與酒渣接觸。柑橘和青蘋果是葡萄的一級香氣。烘烤的時間長短和溫度高低決定了烘烤的強度。","Which statement about concrete vessels is correct?":"關於混凝土容器，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They are inert and can be used for fermentation and storage":"它們是惰性的，可用於發酵和儲存","They give vanilla and coconut flavours":"它們帶來香草和椰子風味","They are used only for storage, never for fermentation":"它們只用於儲存，從不用於發酵","They always let in lots of oxygen, more than a small oak barrel":"它們總是讓大量氧氣進入，比小型橡木桶還多","Like steel, concrete is inert, adds no flavour and is used for both fermentation and storage.":"和不鏽鋼一樣，混凝土是惰性的，不會增添風味，可同時用於發酵和儲存。","Concrete vessels can also be made airtight, stopping oxygen from changing the flavours. Vanilla and coconut are typical of new oak. It is oak, not concrete, that lets some oxygen in.":"混凝土容器也可以做成密封的，防止氧氣改變風味。香草和椰子是新橡木桶的典型特徵。讓一些氧氣進入的是橡木，不是混凝土。","When does malolactic conversion take place?":"乳酸轉化在什麼時候發生？","After the alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之後","In the vineyard, during véraison":"在葡萄園中，轉色期間","At the same time as alcoholic fermentation, by the same yeast":"與酒精發酵同時，由同樣的酵母進行","Malolactic conversion follows alcoholic fermentation and is carried out by bacteria, not yeast.":"乳酸轉化在酒精發酵之後，由細菌而不是酵母進行。","It is a winery step that lowers acidity and may add buttery notes. It has nothing to do with the vineyard. The last option mixes up the two microorganisms: yeast for alcohol, bacteria for malolactic.":"這是在酒廠中進行的步驟，會降低酸度，並可能增添奶油氣息。它與葡萄園無關。最後一個選項把兩種微生物搞混了：酵母負責酒精，細菌負責乳酸轉化。","Which statement about malolactic conversion in red wines is correct?":"關於紅酒中的乳酸轉化，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It nearly always happens and buttery notes are barely noticeable":"它幾乎總是會發生，奶油氣息幾乎察覺不到","It is nearly always prevented":"它幾乎總是被阻止","It makes reds more acidic":"它讓紅酒更酸","It always gives reds a strong buttery aroma, far more than in whites":"它總是讓紅酒帶有強烈的奶油香氣，比白酒明顯得多","In reds, malolactic conversion is almost routine and buttery notes are not really noticeable.":"在紅酒中，乳酸轉化幾乎是例行步驟，奶油氣息並不明顯。","The real choice is for whites: winemakers can block it to keep acidity, as for Riesling, or seek it for some Chardonnay styles. It always lowers acidity, never raises it. Buttery notes are more obvious in some whites.":"真正需要選擇的是白酒：釀酒師可以阻止它以保留酸度，例如麗絲玲；也可以為某些夏多內風格刻意進行。它總是降低酸度，從不提高。奶油氣息在某些白酒中更明顯。","For which white grape can malolactic conversion benefit certain styles?":"乳酸轉化對哪一個白葡萄品種的某些風格有益？","None: in whites, malolactic is always a fault":"沒有：在白酒中，乳酸轉化總是缺陷","Any aromatic grape, because butter lifts floral aromas":"任何芳香品種，因為奶油會提升花香","Some Chardonnay styles benefit from malolactic conversion and its buttery notes.":"某些夏多內風格受益於乳酸轉化及其奶油氣息。","For aromatic grapes such as Riesling it is usually prevented, to keep acidity and aromatic purity. It is not a fault but a style choice. Buttery notes would mask floral aromas, not lift them.":"對於麗絲玲這類芳香品種，通常會阻止乳酸轉化，以保留酸度和純淨的香氣。它不是缺陷，而是一種風格選擇。奶油氣息會掩蓋花香，而不是提升花香。","A white wine smells of butter and cream. Which winemaking step best explains this?":"一款白酒聞起來有奶油和鮮奶油的氣味。哪一個釀造步驟最能解釋這一點？","A very cool fermentation":"非常低溫的發酵","Maturation in sealed steel":"在密封的不鏽鋼槽中熟成","A very early harvest to keep all the grapes' natural acidity":"非常早採收，以保留葡萄所有的天然酸度","Butter and cream are secondary aromas typical of malolactic conversion.":"奶油和鮮奶油是乳酸轉化典型的二級香氣。","Cheese can also be a malolactic aroma. A cool fermentation mainly gives fruity notes, and sealed steel adds nothing. An early harvest brings acidity and less ripe flavours, not dairy notes.":"乳酪也可能是乳酸轉化的香氣。低溫發酵主要帶來果香，密封的不鏽鋼槽則什麼也不增添。早採帶來酸度和較不成熟的風味，而不是乳製品氣息。","A white wine has more body than usual and bread and biscuit notes, but no oak. Which winery choice is most likely?":"一款白酒的酒體比平常飽滿，帶有麵包和餅乾氣息，但沒有橡木味。最可能是哪一種酒廠選擇？","Maturation on stirred lees":"在攪動的酒渣上熟成","Blocked malolactic conversion":"阻止乳酸轉化","Fermentation at red-wine temperature":"以紅酒的溫度發酵","Adding toasted oak chips to a steel tank":"在不鏽鋼槽中加入烘烤過的橡木片","Stirring the lees adds body and bread and biscuit flavours.":"攪動酒渣會增添酒體以及麵包和餅乾風味。","Lees are dead yeast cells that settle after fermentation; keeping wine on them is a typical white-wine choice. Oak chips would give oak flavours, which are absent here. Blocking malolactic keeps acidity but adds neither body nor bready notes.":"酒渣是發酵後沉澱的死酵母細胞；讓酒留在酒渣上是白酒的典型選擇。橡木片會帶來橡木風味，而這裡並沒有。阻止乳酸轉化能保留酸度，但不會增添酒體或麵包氣息。","At what point in winemaking can blending take place?":"混調可以在釀造過程的哪個時間點進行？","At many different stages of the process":"在過程中的許多不同階段","Only in the vineyard, before harvest":"只在葡萄園中，採收之前","Only after bottling":"只在裝瓶之後","Only on the day of crushing, never after fermentation starts":"只在破皮當天，發酵開始後就不行","Blending can happen at many stages of winemaking.":"混調可以在釀造的許多階段進行。","Blending defines and maintains a wine's style, for consistency or complexity. Wines from different grapes, sites or techniques can be combined. Once bottled, a wine is no longer blended.":"混調界定並維持酒的風格，以求一致或增添複雜度。可以結合來自不同品種、園地或技術的酒。酒一旦裝瓶，就不再混調。","A customer notices their wine is slightly hazy. The producer states it is unfiltered. What is the best reply?":"一位顧客發現他的酒有點混濁。生產者聲明這款酒未經過濾。最好的回答是什麼？","It is the producer's choice, to avoid stripping the wine's character":"這是生產者的選擇，為了避免剝奪酒的個性","The wine has definitely gone off":"這瓶酒肯定已經壞了","It shows a failed malolactic conversion":"這表示乳酸轉化失敗","The wine has clearly been aged in over-toasted new barrels":"這瓶酒顯然是在烘烤過度的新橡木桶中陳年的","Skipping filtration means accepting a less than perfectly clear wine to keep its character.":"不過濾，就是為了保留酒的個性而接受酒不那麼完全清澈。","Most customers expect perfectly clear wine, and filtration helps achieve this. Some producers, however, feel it takes something away from the wine. A slight haze in an unfiltered wine is not a fault in itself.":"大多數顧客期待完全清澈的酒，而過濾有助於做到這一點。不過，有些生產者認為過濾會奪走酒的某些東西。未過濾的酒略顯混濁，本身並不是缺陷。","What happens to most wines if they are kept in bottle for a long time?":"大多數葡萄酒如果在瓶中存放很久，會發生什麼？","Fruit fades and vegetal notes appear":"果味消退，出現植物性氣息","They always improve and gain complexity":"它們總是會變好，增添複雜度","They become sweeter":"它們會變甜","They stay exactly the same for decades as long as the bottle stays closed":"只要瓶子不開，它們數十年都會保持原樣","Most wines do not improve in bottle: fruit fades and is replaced by vegetal notes.":"大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好：果味消退，被植物性氣息取代。","Only some wines, with the right features, develop positively over years or decades. For the rest, the vintage helps you tell whether they are still at their best. In bottle, wine neither gets sweeter nor stays unchanged.":"只有部分具備合適特徵的酒，會在數年或數十年間正向發展。至於其他的酒，年份能幫你判斷它們是否仍處於最佳狀態。在瓶中，酒既不會變甜，也不會保持不變。","Which feature does NOT help a wine keep and improve in bottle?":"下列哪一個特徵無助於酒在瓶中保存並變好？","Very low acidity":"非常低的酸度","High tannin, in a red":"高單寧（紅酒）","High residual sugar, in a sweet wine":"高殘糖（甜酒）","Enough concentration of flavour to develop positively":"足以正向發展的風味濃縮度","High acidity, sugar or tannin preserve a wine; low acidity does not help.":"高酸度、糖分或單寧能保存酒；低酸度則沒有幫助。","Wines for ageing often have high acidity and, depending on style, high residual sugar or tannin. Above all, they need enough flavour concentration to evolve into complexity. A low-acid wine tends to fade early instead.":"適合陳年的酒往往酸度高，並依風格有高殘糖或高單寧。最重要的是，它們需要足夠的風味濃縮度，才能演變出複雜度。低酸的酒反而往往很早就衰退。","In a wine that matures well in bottle, how do fresh fruit flavours evolve?":"在一款能在瓶中好好熟成的酒裡，新鮮果味會如何演變？","They turn to dried fruit, with notes such as mushroom and leather":"轉變為果乾，帶有蘑菇和皮革等氣息","They become fresher tropical fruit":"變成更新鮮的熱帶水果","They stay exactly the same":"保持完全不變","They turn into vanilla and coconut thanks to the cork":"多虧軟木塞而變成香草和椰子","With age, fresh fruit becomes dried fruit and complex notes such as mushroom and leather develop.":"隨著陳年，新鮮果味變成果乾，並發展出蘑菇和皮革等複雜氣息。","These are tertiary aromas, linked to ageing. Vanilla and coconut are secondary aromas from new oak, not the cork. Fruit loses freshness over time, so it does not become fresher.":"這些是與陳年相關的三級香氣。香草和椰子是來自新橡木桶的二級香氣，不是來自軟木塞。果味會隨時間失去新鮮感，所以不會變得更新鮮。","Which tertiary aromas can a white wine develop with bottle age?":"白酒經過瓶中陳年會發展出哪些三級香氣？","Dried apricot, honey, nuts and spice":"杏桃乾、蜂蜜、堅果和香料","Fresh strawberry and raspberry":"新鮮草莓和覆盆子","Cut grass and green apple":"青草和青蘋果","Green pepper, tomato leaf and asparagus, ever more intense":"青椒、番茄葉和蘆筍，越來越濃","With age a white can develop dried apricot, honey, nut and spice.":"隨著陳年，白酒可能發展出杏桃乾、蜂蜜、堅果和香料。","Grass, green apple and herbaceous notes are primary aromas, typical of young wines or less ripe grapes. Fresh red fruit is primary and mostly linked to reds. With age, white wine colour also moves from lemon to gold to amber.":"青草、青蘋果和草本氣息是一級香氣，是年輕酒款或較不成熟葡萄的典型特徵。新鮮紅色水果是一級香氣，主要與紅酒有關。隨著陳年，白酒的顏色也會從檸檬色轉為金黃色再到琥珀色。","With bottle age, how does colour intensity change in white and red wines?":"經過瓶中陳年，白酒和紅酒的顏色深淺如何變化？","Whites get deeper, reds get paler":"白酒變深，紅酒變淡","Both get paler":"兩者都變淡","Whites get paler, reds get deeper":"白酒變淡，紅酒變深","Neither changes in intensity; only the hue changes":"兩者的深淺都不變；只有色調改變","Whites deepen (lemon to gold to amber), while reds tend to lose intensity.":"白酒顏色加深（檸檬色到金黃色到琥珀色），而紅酒往往失去深度。","In reds, the hue moves from ruby to garnet to tawny and finally brown, with ever less intensity. In whites, by contrast, the colour deepens. So both hue and intensity change.":"紅酒的色調從寶石紅轉為石榴紅、茶褐色，最後是褐色，深度越來越淺。相反地，白酒的顏色會加深。所以色調和深淺都會改變。","What is the correct order of colours as a red wine ages?":"紅酒陳年時，顏色的正確順序是什麼？","Ruby, garnet, tawny, brown":"寶石紅、石榴紅、茶褐色、褐色","Purple, ruby, lemon, gold":"紫色、寶石紅、檸檬色、金黃色","Brown, tawny, garnet, ruby":"褐色、茶褐色、石榴紅、寶石紅","Garnet, ruby, purple and finally deep black after many years":"石榴紅、寶石紅、紫色，多年後最終變成深黑色","A red moves from ruby to garnet, then tawny and finally brown.":"紅酒從寶石紅轉為石榴紅，接著是茶褐色，最後是褐色。","The second option mixes red and white colours: lemon and gold are white-wine hues. The third gives the reverse order. With age, red colour gets paler, not darker.":"第二個選項把紅酒和白酒的顏色混在一起了：檸檬色和金黃色是白酒的色調。第三個選項的順序正好相反。隨著陳年，紅酒的顏色會變淡，而不是變深。","An old bottle of red has thrown a lot of deposit. What is usually done before serving it?":"一瓶老紅酒產生了大量沉澱物。侍酒前通常會怎麼做？","It is decanted":"換瓶","The bottle is shaken well":"用力搖晃酒瓶","Water is added to dilute the deposit":"加水稀釋沉澱物","It is sent back to the producer, since deposit always means a fault":"退回給生產者，因為沉澱物一定代表有缺陷","If there is a lot of deposit, the wine is normally decanted off it.":"如果沉澱物很多，通常會換瓶，把酒與沉澱物分開。","Deposit often forms in reds that mature in bottle; it is normal, not a fault. Shaking would stir it back into the wine. Decanting lets you pour the clear wine and leave the sediment in the bottle.":"在瓶中熟成的紅酒常會形成沉澱物；這是正常的，不是缺陷。搖晃會把沉澱物重新攪入酒中。換瓶可以倒出清澈的酒，把沉澱物留在瓶中。","A wine has spent a long time maturing in barrel with oxygen contact. Which tertiary aromas are most likely?":"一款酒在橡木桶中與氧氣接觸、熟成了很長時間。最可能出現哪些三級香氣？","Coffee and caramel":"咖啡和焦糖","Fresh flowers and citrus":"新鮮花香和柑橘","Green apple and gooseberry, typical of a very young wine":"青蘋果和醋栗，非常年輕酒款的典型特徵","Oxidative ageing, for example in barrel, brings notes such as coffee and caramel.":"氧化陳年，例如在橡木桶中，會帶來咖啡和焦糖等氣息。","Petrol, honey and mushroom are typical of ageing protected from oxygen, such as in bottle. Flowers, citrus, green apple and gooseberry are primary aromas of young wines. In both kinds of ageing, fruit loses freshness.":"汽油、蜂蜜和蘑菇是隔絕氧氣陳年（例如在瓶中）的典型特徵。花香、柑橘、青蘋果和醋栗是年輕酒款的一級香氣。在兩種陳年方式中，果味都會失去新鮮感。","A winemaker wants only a light touch of oak in a white. Which barrel suits best?":"一位釀酒師只想讓白酒帶一點輕微的橡木味。哪一種橡木桶最合適？","A barrel that has already been used several times":"已經使用過多次的橡木桶","A new barrique":"新的小型橡木桶","A heavily toasted new barrique":"重度烘烤的新小型橡木桶","A small new barrel with toasted oak chips added too":"小型新橡木桶，另外再加入烘烤過的橡木片","A used barrel gives less flavour than a new one; after two or three uses it gives very little.":"用過的橡木桶給的風味比新桶少；使用兩到三次之後就非常少了。","New barrels give lots of vanilla, coconut, charred wood and spice, even more when heavily toasted. Adding chips would increase the effect, not reduce it. For a light touch, old oak is the logical choice.":"新橡木桶會帶來大量香草、椰子、炭烤木頭和香料，重度烘烤時更多。加入橡木片會增強效果，而不是減弱。要輕微的橡木味，舊桶是合理的選擇。","Which profile is typical of a cool-climate Chardonnay?":"哪一種風味特徵是涼爽氣候夏多內的典型特徵？","High acidity, apple, lemon, wet stones":"高酸度、蘋果、檸檬、濕石頭","Medium acidity, pineapple, banana, full body":"中等酸度、鳳梨、香蕉、酒體飽滿","Low acidity, peach, melon, full body":"低酸度、桃子、哈密瓜、酒體飽滿","Medium acidity, mango, honey, ginger":"中等酸度、芒果、蜂蜜、薑","Cool weather slows ripening, so grapes keep acidity and show green fruit and citrus.":"涼爽的天氣減緩成熟，所以葡萄保留酸度，展現綠色水果和柑橘。","In a cool climate Chardonnay ripens slowly and does not build much sugar. The result is a wine with high acidity, light to medium body and aromas of green fruit (apple, pear), lemon and wet stones. Pineapple and banana instead point to a warm climate, where acidity drops to medium and the body becomes full.":"在涼爽氣候中，夏多內成熟緩慢，累積的糖分不多。結果是一款酸度高、酒體輕盈至中等、帶有綠色水果（蘋果、梨）、檸檬和濕石頭香氣的酒。鳳梨和香蕉則指向溫暖氣候，那裡的酸度降到中等，酒體變得飽滿。","Which flavours typify a warm-climate Chardonnay?":"哪些風味是溫暖氣候夏多內的典型特徵？","Apple, pear and wet stones":"蘋果、梨和濕石頭","Grass, green pepper and asparagus":"青草、青椒和蘆筍","Rose, lychee and apricot":"玫瑰、荔枝和杏桃","Heat ripens the grapes fully, so stone fruit and tropical fruit dominate.":"熱量讓葡萄完全成熟，所以核果和熱帶水果佔主導。","In warm climates Chardonnay gains more sugar and loses acid. The wine is full-bodied with medium acidity and ripe aromas of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple and banana. Apple and wet stones belong to cool climates; grass and asparagus suggest Sauvignon Blanc; rose and lychee suggest Gewurztraminer.":"在溫暖氣候中，夏多內累積更多糖分、失去酸度。酒的酒體飽滿、酸度中等，帶有桃子和鳳梨、香蕉等熱帶水果的成熟香氣。蘋果和濕石頭屬於涼爽氣候；青草和蘆筍讓人想到白蘇維濃；玫瑰和荔枝則讓人想到格烏茲塔明那。","Why are many warm-climate Chardonnays acidified?":"為什麼許多溫暖氣候的夏多內要加酸？","To balance their high alcohol and body":"為了平衡它們的高酒精和飽滿酒體","To add butter and cream flavours":"為了增添奶油和鮮奶油風味","To protect the wine against frost":"為了保護酒免受霜害","To reduce the amount of alcohol":"為了降低酒精含量","Warm-climate grapes lack acid; adding it balances full-bodied, alcoholic wines.":"溫暖氣候的葡萄缺酸；加酸能平衡酒體飽滿、酒精高的酒。","In heat the grapes ripen fully, build sugar (hence alcohol) and lose acid. The wine could taste heavy and flat. Acidification, adding acid in the winery, is therefore common to restore freshness and balance. It does not add dairy notes, which come from malolactic conversion, and it does not lower alcohol.":"在高溫下，葡萄完全成熟，累積糖分（因此酒精也高）並失去酸度。酒可能嚐起來沉重而平淡。因此常會在酒廠中加酸，以恢復清新感和平衡。加酸不會增添乳製品氣息，那來自乳酸轉化；也不會降低酒精。","Which technique adds butter and cream flavours to Chardonnay?":"哪一種技術為夏多內增添奶油和鮮奶油風味？","Lees contact":"與酒渣接觸","Stainless steel fermentation":"不鏽鋼槽發酵","Malolactic conversion softens acidity and brings dairy notes of butter and cream.":"乳酸轉化讓酸度變柔和，帶來奶油和鮮奶油的乳製品氣息。","Malolactic conversion turns harsh acids into softer ones and leaves dairy aromas of butter and cream. Lees contact instead gives body and bread or biscuit notes, while stainless steel is an inert vessel that adds no flavour. Acidification raises acidity and brings no dairy character.":"乳酸轉化把尖銳的酸轉化為較柔和的酸，並留下奶油和鮮奶油的乳製品香氣。與酒渣接觸則帶來酒體以及麵包或餅乾氣息，而不鏽鋼槽是不增添任何風味的惰性容器。加酸會提高酸度，不會帶來乳製品特徵。","What does lees contact during maturation add to Chardonnay?":"熟成期間與酒渣接觸會為夏多內增添什麼？","Body and bread and biscuit notes":"酒體以及麵包和餅乾氣息","Higher acidity and lemon notes":"更高的酸度和檸檬氣息","Hazelnut and mushroom notes":"榛果和蘑菇氣息","Lees enrich the wine with more body and bread and biscuit aromas.":"酒渣讓酒更豐富，帶來更飽滿的酒體以及麵包和餅乾香氣。","Keeping the wine on its lees during maturation increases the feeling of body and adds secondary aromas of bread and biscuit. Vanilla and coconut come from oak; hazelnut and mushroom are tertiary aromas that appear as the best wines age in bottle. Lees do not raise acidity.":"熟成期間讓酒留在酒渣上，會增加酒體感，並增添麵包和餅乾的二級香氣。香草和椰子來自橡木桶；榛果和蘑菇是最好的酒在瓶中陳年時出現的三級香氣。酒渣不會提高酸度。","Why do inexpensive Chardonnay brands often use oak chips or staves?":"為什麼平價的夏多內品牌常使用橡木片或橡木條？","They cost less than new barrels":"它們比新橡木桶便宜","They give the wine more acidity":"它們讓酒的酸度更高","They allow long bottle ageing":"它們讓酒能長期瓶中陳年","They prevent malolactic conversion":"它們能阻止乳酸轉化","Chips and staves give oak flavours far more cheaply than new barrels.":"橡木片和橡木條帶來橡木風味，成本比新橡木桶低得多。","New oak barrels are expensive. To give high-volume wines vanilla, smoke or coconut flavours at a low price, many producers soak chips or staves in the wine. It is a cost choice, common for example in Pays d'Oc IGP and California Central Valley brands; it does nothing for acidity or longevity.":"新橡木桶很昂貴。為了以低價讓大量生產的酒帶有香草、煙燻或椰子風味，許多生產者會把橡木片或橡木條浸泡在酒中。這是成本上的選擇，例如在 Pays d'Oc IGP 和 California Central Valley 的品牌中很常見；它對酸度或陳年潛力毫無幫助。","What does the term unoaked on a Chardonnay label tell you?":"夏多內酒標上的 unoaked 告訴你什麼？","The wine has had no oak treatment":"這款酒沒有經過任何橡木處理","The wine was made from late-picked grapes":"這款酒用晚採的葡萄釀造","The wine is blended with Semillon":"這款酒混調了榭密雍","The wine has been acidified":"這款酒經過加酸","Unoaked or unwooded tells consumers no oak was used.":"Unoaked 或 unwooded 告訴消費者沒有使用橡木。","Some producers want a pure-fruited Chardonnay: they use inert vessels and sometimes avoid malolactic conversion and lees. To tell buyers, they may print unoaked or unwooded on the label. The term says nothing about harvest timing, blending or acidification. It is a simple way to guide people looking for a fresh, fruit-led style.":"有些生產者想要果味純淨的夏多內：他們使用惰性容器，有時也避免乳酸轉化和酒渣接觸。為了告知買家，他們可能在酒標上印上 unoaked 或 unwooded。這個術語與採收時機、混調或加酸無關。這是為尋找清爽、以果味為主風格的人提供指引的簡單方式。","Which tertiary flavours do fine Chardonnays develop with bottle age?":"優質夏多內經過瓶中陳年會發展出哪些三級風味？","Hazelnut and mushroom":"榛果和蘑菇","Smoke and vanilla":"煙燻和香草","With years in bottle, tertiary notes of hazelnut and mushroom appear.":"在瓶中多年後，會出現榛果和蘑菇的三級氣息。","Very good or outstanding Chardonnays can evolve for years, and the best Burgundies for decades, developing tertiary aromas of hazelnut and mushroom. Butter and cream (malolactic), smoke and vanilla (oak) and bread and biscuit (lees) are secondary aromas linked to winery choices.":"非常好或傑出的夏多內可以演變多年，最好的布根地白酒甚至可達數十年，發展出榛果和蘑菇的三級香氣。奶油和鮮奶油（乳酸轉化）、煙燻和香草（橡木桶）以及麵包和餅乾（酒渣）都是與酒廠選擇相關的二級香氣。","Which Burgundy appellation gives cool-climate, light to medium-bodied wines that almost never show oak?":"哪一個布根地法定產區出產涼爽氣候、酒體輕盈至中等、幾乎從不帶橡木味的酒？","Chablis producers ferment in inert vessels to keep the delicate cool-climate fruit.":"Chablis 的生產者使用惰性容器發酵，以保留涼爽氣候細緻的果味。","Chablis is the coolest part of Burgundy: dry wines, high acidity, apple, lemon and wet stones. With very few exceptions no oak is detectable, as producers prefer inert vessels. Meursault, Puligny-Montrachet and Pouilly-Fuissé, by contrast, often use barrels to add body and complexity.":"Chablis 是布根地最涼爽的地區：不甜的酒、高酸度、蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭。除了極少數例外，喝不出橡木味，因為生產者偏好惰性容器。相反地，Meursault、Puligny-Montrachet 和 Pouilly-Fuissé 則常使用橡木桶來增添酒體和複雜度。","Which weather hazard is a key concern that can limit Chablis production?":"哪一種天氣災害是可能限制 Chablis 產量的主要隱憂？","Frost":"霜凍","Drought":"乾旱","Excessive heat":"過熱","Morning fog":"晨霧","In this cool region, frost can cut the crop from year to year.":"在這個涼爽產區，霜凍可能年年削減收成。","Chablis lies at the northern tip of Burgundy and has a cool climate. That is why frost is a constant worry: it can damage the vines and limit how much wine is made each year. Drought and excessive heat are problems of warmer areas; fog is a cooling factor elsewhere, for example in Los Carneros.":"Chablis 位於布根地的最北端，屬於涼爽氣候。這就是為什麼霜凍是持續的隱憂：它可能損害葡萄樹，限制每年的產量。乾旱和過熱是較溫暖地區的問題；霧則是其他地方的降溫因素，例如 Los Carneros。","Why do Chablis Premier Cru and Grand Cru vineyards give more complex wines?":"為什麼 Chablis Premier Cru 和 Grand Cru 的葡萄園能釀出更複雜的酒？","South/south-west slopes: more sun, riper grapes":"朝南／西南的坡地：日照更多，葡萄更成熟","They are always made in new barrels":"它們總是在新橡木桶中釀造","They lie on flat land, safe from frost":"它們位於平地，不受霜害","They are irrigated to raise yields":"它們經過灌溉以提高產量","Slope aspect increases sunshine, hence ripeness, flavour and complexity.":"坡向增加了日照，因而提升成熟度、風味和複雜度。","In a cool climate like Chablis every bit of sun matters. The best vineyards, labelled Premier Cru or Grand Cru, usually sit on hillsides facing south or south-west. This aspect increases sun exposure, so grapes ripen better and wines are more flavourful and complex. New oak, by contrast, is an exception in Chablis.":"在像 Chablis 這樣的涼爽氣候中，每一點陽光都很重要。最好的葡萄園，標示為 Premier Cru 或 Grand Cru，通常位於朝南或西南的山坡上。這樣的坡向增加了日照，所以葡萄成熟得更好，酒的風味更豐富、更複雜。相反地，新橡木桶在 Chablis 是例外。","What style is a Chardonnay labelled Bourgogne AOC usually?":"標示 Bourgogne AOC 的夏多內通常是什麼風格？","Simple, high acidity, apple and lemon":"簡單、高酸度、蘋果和檸檬","Full, tropical, lots of new oak":"飽滿、熱帶水果、大量新橡木桶","Sweet, from late-harvested grapes":"甜，用晚收葡萄釀造","Complex, hazelnut and mushroom":"複雜、榛果和蘑菇","It is the regional appellation: grapes from anywhere in Burgundy, simple fresh wines.":"這是地區級法定產區：葡萄可來自布根地任何地方，酒款簡單清爽。","Bourgogne AOC is the regional level: grapes can come from anywhere in Burgundy. These wines are generally simple, with high acidity and apple and lemon aromas. The more complex styles with hazelnut and mushroom come from the premier cru and grand cru sites of villages such as Meursault or Puligny-Montrachet.":"Bourgogne AOC 是地區級：葡萄可以來自布根地任何地方。這些酒一般很簡單，酸度高，帶有蘋果和檸檬香氣。帶有榛果和蘑菇的較複雜風格，來自 Meursault 或 Puligny-Montrachet 等村莊的 premier cru 和 grand cru 園地。","In which part of the Côte d'Or is Chardonnay production focused?":"Côte d'Or 的夏多內生產集中在哪個部分？","Côte de Beaune, south of Beaune":"Côte de Beaune，Beaune 以南","The Mâconnais, in the far south":"最南端的 Mâconnais","Chablis, in the north":"北部的 Chablis","The plains along the Rhône":"隆河沿岸的平原","Côte d'Or Chardonnay is focused south of Beaune, in the Côte de Beaune.":"Côte d'Or 的夏多內集中在 Beaune 以南的 Côte de Beaune。","The Côte d'Or has a moderate climate and gives fuller, riper Chardonnay than Chablis. White wine production is focused south of the town of Beaune, in the Côte de Beaune, home to famous villages such as Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet. Chablis and the Mâconnais are part of Burgundy but not of the Côte d'Or.":"Côte d'Or 屬於溫和氣候，釀出的夏多內比 Chablis 更飽滿、更成熟。白酒生產集中在 Beaune 鎮以南的 Côte de Beaune，這裡有 Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 等著名村莊。Chablis 和 Mâconnais 屬於布根地，但不屬於 Côte d'Or。","Which two Côte de Beaune villages are famous for outstanding Chardonnay?":"Côte de Beaune 的哪兩個村莊以傑出的夏多內聞名？","Mâcon and Pouilly-Fuissé":"Mâcon 和 Pouilly-Fuissé","Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé":"Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé","Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet are the great Chardonnay villages of the Côte de Beaune.":"Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 是 Côte de Beaune 偉大的夏多內村莊。","Meursault AOC and Puligny-Montrachet AOC produce very good to outstanding Chardonnay, barrel fermented and/or matured and aged on lees. Mâcon and Pouilly-Fuissé are in the Mâconnais; Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé are Loire Sauvignon Blanc appellations; Graves and Pessac-Léognan are in Bordeaux.":"Meursault AOC 和 Puligny-Montrachet AOC 出產非常好到傑出的夏多內，在橡木桶中發酵和／或熟成，並在酒渣上陳年。Mâcon 和 Pouilly-Fuissé 位於 Mâconnais；Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 是羅亞爾河的白蘇維濃法定產區；Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 則位於波爾多。","A simple, fruity, mostly unoaked wine with lemon, peach and melon most likely comes from which appellation?":"一款簡單、果香豐富、大多未經橡木桶、帶有檸檬、桃子和哈密瓜的酒，最可能來自哪個法定產區？","The Mâconnais makes fruity, mostly unoaked Chardonnay labelled Mâcon AOC.":"Mâconnais 出產果香豐富、大多未經橡木桶的夏多內，標示為 Mâcon AOC。","In the Mâconnais, the southernmost part of Burgundy, Chardonnay gives fruity wines with simple lemon, peach and melon flavours, rarely oaked. Meursault relies on barrels and lees; Chablis Grand Cru is crisper and stonier; Pessac-Léognan is a Bordeaux white from Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon.":"在布根地最南端的 Mâconnais，夏多內釀出果香豐富的酒，帶有簡單的檸檬、桃子和哈密瓜風味，很少經過橡木桶。Meursault 仰賴橡木桶和酒渣；Chablis Grand Cru 更爽脆、礦石感更強；Pessac-Léognan 則是以白蘇維濃和榭密雍釀造的波爾多白酒。","What makes Pouilly-Fuissé wines higher in quality than Mâcon AOC?":"是什麼讓 Pouilly-Fuissé 的酒品質高於 Mâcon AOC？","Steep east/south-east slopes and more concentrated fruit":"朝東／東南的陡坡，以及更濃縮的果實","A cooler climate, the same as Chablis":"更涼爽的氣候，與 Chablis 相同","The exclusive use of inert vessels":"只使用惰性容器","Higher yields thanks to irrigation":"灌溉帶來更高的產量","Steep, well-exposed slopes give concentrated grapes, often enhanced by barrel use.":"日照良好的陡坡帶來濃縮的葡萄，常再藉由橡木桶加以提升。","Around the village of Pouilly-Fuissé, vineyards lie on steep slopes facing east and south-east. They give wines with concentrated stone and tropical fruit, often barrel fermented and/or matured for extra body and complexity. Simpler Mâcon AOC is largely unoaked. Both are found in the Mâconnais, in southern Burgundy.":"在 Pouilly-Fuissé 村周圍，葡萄園位於朝東和東南的陡坡上。這裡的酒帶有濃縮的核果和熱帶水果風味，常在橡木桶中發酵和／或熟成，以增添酒體和複雜度。較簡單的 Mâcon AOC 大多未經橡木桶。兩者都位於布根地南部的 Mâconnais。","Under which label is most Chardonnay from Languedoc-Roussillon sold?":"Languedoc-Roussillon 的夏多內大多以什麼標示出售？","The region is home to Pays d'Oc IGP, used for most of its Chardonnay.":"這個地區有 Pays d'Oc IGP，大部分的夏多內都用這個標示。","Languedoc-Roussillon, on the Mediterranean coast, makes several AOC wines, but most of its Chardonnay is labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. The warm climate gives large volumes of ripe, fruity wine with peach, pineapple and banana. Bourgogne, Touraine and Alsace are appellations of other French regions.":"位於地中海沿岸的 Languedoc-Roussillon 出產數種 AOC 葡萄酒，但大部分的夏多內都標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。溫暖的氣候帶來大量成熟、果香豐富的酒，帶有桃子、鳳梨和香蕉。Bourgogne、Touraine 和 Alsace 則是法國其他地區的法定產區。","Why does California's Central Valley produce high-volume Chardonnay with medium acidity?":"為什麼加州的 Central Valley 出產酸度中等的大量生產夏多內？","It is very hot, dry, irrigated and cut off from the sea":"它非常炎熱、乾燥、經過灌溉，並與海洋隔絕","It is cooled by fog from San Pablo Bay":"它受到 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣降溫","It has high-altitude vineyards with long seasons":"它有生長季很長的高海拔葡萄園","It is exposed to cool Pacific breezes":"它受到涼爽的太平洋微風吹拂","Mountains block sea influence; heat and irrigation give high yields and moderate acidity.":"山脈阻擋了海洋的影響；高溫和灌溉帶來高產量和中等酸度。","The Central Valley is cut off from the ocean by mountains, so it is very hot and dry. Irrigation allows high yields, ideal for high-volume brands labelled California. Grapes ripen fully: peach and pineapple, medium acidity and body, any oak from chips or staves. Fog and breezes instead cool coastal areas such as Los Carneros and Sonoma.":"Central Valley 被山脈與海洋隔開，所以非常炎熱乾燥。灌溉讓產量很高，非常適合標示 California 的大量生產品牌。葡萄完全成熟：桃子和鳳梨、中等酸度和酒體，若有橡木味則來自橡木片或橡木條。霧氣和微風則讓 Los Carneros 和 Sonoma 等沿海地區降溫。","Which Californian area is cooled by morning fogs from San Pablo Bay?":"加州哪個地區受到 San Pablo Bay 晨霧的降溫？","Northern Napa Valley":"Napa Valley 北部","Bay fogs cool Los Carneros, helping the grapes keep their acidity.":"海灣的霧氣讓 Los Carneros 降溫，幫助葡萄保留酸度。","In northern California, Los Carneros receives morning fogs from San Pablo Bay. This cooling slows ripening, so the grapes keep acidity while building complex flavours. Napa Valley warms up further north, the Central Valley is hot and cut off from the sea, and Santa Barbara County is cooled by breezes funnelled through valleys.":"在北加州，Los Carneros 受到來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧影響。這種降溫減緩成熟，讓葡萄在發展複雜風味的同時保留酸度。Napa Valley 越往北越溫暖，Central Valley 炎熱且與海洋隔絕，而 Santa Barbara County 則受到經由山谷導入的微風降溫。","Which Californian region is known for full-bodied, tropical Chardonnay with vanilla and spice from new oak?":"加州哪個產區以酒體飽滿、帶熱帶水果和新橡木桶香草與香料的夏多內聞名？","Napa Valley grows warmer and sunnier to the north: ripe, oaky wines.":"Napa Valley 越往北越溫暖、陽光越充足：成熟、帶橡木味的酒。","Moving north up Napa Valley the climate becomes warmer and sunnier. Grapes ripen fully and give full-bodied Chardonnay with pronounced tropical fruit plus vanilla and spice from new oak. Los Carneros and Sonoma are cooler thanks to fog and breezes; moderate Oregon is known for high acidity.":"沿著 Napa Valley 往北，氣候變得更溫暖、陽光更充足。葡萄完全成熟，釀出酒體飽滿的夏多內，帶有濃郁的熱帶水果，以及新橡木桶的香草和香料。Los Carneros 和 Sonoma 因為霧氣和微風而較涼爽；氣候溫和的奧勒岡則以高酸度著稱。","What cools the vineyards of Santa Barbara County?":"是什麼讓 Santa Barbara County 的葡萄園降溫？","Sea breezes funnelled inland by lateral valleys":"由橫向山谷導入內陸的海風","The altitude of inland hills":"內陸丘陵的海拔","Ocean currents from the south":"來自南方的洋流","Fogs from San Pablo Bay":"來自 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣","Valleys open to the sea channel cool breezes inland.":"向海洋開口的山谷把涼爽的微風導入內陸。","Santa Barbara County, on California's Central Coast, gets cool sea breezes funnelled inland by lateral valleys. Styles range from wines like the Côte de Beaune to more tropical versions with higher alcohol and more new oak. San Pablo Bay fogs relate to Los Carneros; altitude cools Adelaide Hills, for example.":"位於加州中部海岸的 Santa Barbara County，受到由橫向山谷導入內陸的涼爽海風吹拂。風格從類似 Côte de Beaune 的酒，到酒精更高、新橡木桶更多的熱帶水果風格都有。San Pablo Bay 的霧氣與 Los Carneros 有關；海拔則讓例如 Adelaide Hills 降溫。","What can a Chardonnay labelled South Eastern Australia indicate?":"標示 South Eastern Australia 的夏多內可能代表什麼？","A high-volume wine from a very broad area":"來自非常廣大區域的大量生產酒款","A single-vineyard wine from high altitude":"來自高海拔的單一葡萄園酒款","A wine from one cool coastal zone":"來自單一涼爽沿海地帶的酒","A sweet wine from late-picked grapes":"用晚採葡萄釀的甜酒","The label covers a huge area, often using warm, irrigated inland fruit.":"這個標示涵蓋廣大的區域，常使用溫暖、經灌溉的內陸果實。","South Eastern Australia allows grapes from a vast area, often warm, irrigated inland vineyards. These high-volume Chardonnays are sometimes blended with other varieties such as Semillon, or with wines from cooler sites; blending helps achieve better balance. Cooler regions such as Adelaide Hills or Yarra Valley give finer wines instead.":"South Eastern Australia 允許使用來自廣大區域的葡萄，常是溫暖、經灌溉的內陸葡萄園。這些大量生產的夏多內有時會與榭密雍等其他品種混調，或與較涼爽園地的酒混調；混調有助於取得更好的平衡。Adelaide Hills 或 Yarra Valley 等較涼爽的產區則出產較精緻的酒。","What cools the Australian region of Adelaide Hills?":"是什麼讓澳洲的 Adelaide Hills 產區降溫？","Morning fogs":"晨霧","Heavy irrigation":"大量灌溉","Adelaide Hills is cooled by altitude; Yarra Valley by ocean currents.":"Adelaide Hills 因海拔而涼爽；Yarra Valley 則因洋流而涼爽。","Adelaide Hills in South Australia owes its coolness to altitude, while Yarra Valley in Victoria is cooled by ocean currents from the south. Both enjoy long seasons, giving Chardonnay with ripe peach, sometimes tropical fruit, medium to high acidity and well-balanced oak.":"南澳的 Adelaide Hills 因海拔而涼爽，而維多利亞的 Yarra Valley 則受到來自南方的洋流降溫。兩者都享有很長的生長季，釀出帶有成熟桃子、有時帶熱帶水果、酸度中等至高、橡木味平衡良好的夏多內。","Which moderate New Zealand region gives full-bodied Chardonnay balanced by high acidity?":"紐西蘭哪個氣候溫和的產區出產以高酸度平衡飽滿酒體的夏多內？","In Hawke's Bay Chardonnay is the most planted white: full, crisp, stone-fruited wines.":"在 Hawke's Bay，夏多內是種植最多的白葡萄：飽滿、爽脆、帶核果風味的酒。","Hawke's Bay, on the east coast of the North Island, has a moderate climate and Chardonnay is its most planted white grape. It gives full-bodied wines balanced by high acidity, with pronounced stone fruit. Marlborough is cooler, with subtle oak; Margaret River is Australian and Walker Bay South African.":"位於北島東岸的 Hawke's Bay 屬於溫和氣候，夏多內是當地種植最多的白葡萄品種。它釀出酒體飽滿、以高酸度平衡、帶有濃郁核果風味的酒。Marlborough 較涼爽，橡木味細緻；Margaret River 在澳洲，Walker Bay 則在南非。","Why does Casablanca Valley make refreshing Chardonnay despite Chile's warmth?":"儘管智利很溫暖，為什麼 Casablanca Valley 能釀出清爽的夏多內？","Pacific breezes and fogs slow ripening":"太平洋的微風和霧氣減緩成熟","The vineyards are heavily irrigated":"葡萄園大量灌溉","The grapes are picked very late":"葡萄非常晚才採收","Mountains block the sea's influence":"山脈阻擋了海洋的影響","The ocean cools the valley: slow ripening, preserved acidity, lemon and peach.":"海洋讓山谷降溫：成熟緩慢、保留酸度、檸檬和桃子。","Casablanca Valley is a coastal region exposed to Pacific sea breezes and morning fogs. This cooling slows ripening and gives refreshing Chardonnay with lemon and peach and varying levels of oak. The larger, warmer Central Valley covers every level, from cheap brands to altitude-moderated wines.":"Casablanca Valley 是受到太平洋海風和晨霧影響的沿海產區。這種降溫減緩成熟，釀出帶有檸檬和桃子、橡木程度不一的清爽夏多內。較大、較溫暖的 Central Valley 則涵蓋各個等級，從便宜的品牌到受海拔調節的酒款都有。","Which South African region, among the country's coolest, is known for very good Chardonnay?":"南非哪個產區是全國最涼爽的地區之一，以非常好的夏多內聞名？","Inland Western Cape":"西開普內陸","Walker Bay is cooled by strong southerly sea breezes: high acidity and ripe fruit.":"Walker Bay 受到強勁的南方海風降溫：高酸度和成熟果味。","Coastal Walker Bay is among South Africa's coolest areas thanks to strong sea breezes from the south. It makes very good Chardonnay with high acidity, peach, pineapple and oak. The hot inland Western Cape vineyards mostly supply high-volume brands, sometimes blended with Chenin Blanc.":"沿海的 Walker Bay 因為來自南方的強勁海風，成為南非最涼爽的地區之一。這裡出產非常好的夏多內，帶有高酸度、桃子、鳳梨和橡木味。炎熱的西開普內陸葡萄園則主要供應大量生產的品牌，有時與白梢楠混調。","Why is Chardonnay considered such a versatile grape?":"為什麼夏多內被視為如此多才多藝的品種？","It makes outstanding wines in cool, moderate and warm climates":"它在涼爽、溫和和溫暖氣候中都能釀出傑出的酒","It withstands winter cold better than any other white grape variety":"它比任何其他白葡萄品種都更耐冬季寒冷","It is used mainly for sweet botrytised wines":"它主要用來釀造貴腐甜酒","Its aromas are so neutral that they never change with climate":"它的香氣非常中性，從不隨氣候改變","Chardonnay reaches outstanding quality in all three climate types, in different styles.":"夏多內在三種氣候類型中都能達到傑出品質，風格各不相同。","From light, crisp cool-climate wines to full, tropical warm-climate ones, Chardonnay covers a huge range, from high-volume brands to wines that evolve for years. It is not known for cold-hardiness (that is Riesling) or for botrytised sweet wines. Its primary aromas actually change a great deal with climate.":"從涼爽氣候輕盈爽脆的酒，到溫暖氣候飽滿帶熱帶水果的酒，夏多內涵蓋非常廣的範圍，從大量生產的品牌到可以演變多年的酒款都有。它不以耐寒著稱（那是麗絲玲），也不以貴腐甜酒著稱。它的一級香氣其實會隨氣候大幅改變。","Which profile fits a moderate-climate Chardonnay?":"哪一種風味特徵符合溫和氣候的夏多內？","Medium to high acidity, medium to full body, lemon, peach, melon":"酸度中等至高、酒體中等至飽滿、檸檬、桃子、哈密瓜","High acidity, light body, green apple, pear and wet stones":"高酸度、酒體輕盈、青蘋果、梨和濕石頭","Medium acidity, full body, very ripe pineapple and banana":"中等酸度、酒體飽滿、非常成熟的鳳梨和香蕉","Low acidity, light body, floral and cut-grass notes":"低酸度、酒體輕盈、花香和青草氣息","In a moderate climate Chardonnay sits in the middle: lemon and peach, sometimes melon, with medium to high acidity.":"在溫和氣候中，夏多內居於中間：檸檬和桃子，有時帶哈密瓜，酸度中等至高。","A moderate climate gives riper fruit than a cool one but keeps more freshness than a warm one. Apple, pear and wet stones with a light body point to a cool climate; pineapple and banana with medium acidity point to a warm one. Grassy notes with low acidity do not describe Chardonnay.":"溫和氣候帶來比涼爽氣候更成熟的果味，但比溫暖氣候保留更多清新感。蘋果、梨和濕石頭配上輕盈酒體指向涼爽氣候；鳳梨和香蕉配上中等酸度則指向溫暖氣候。低酸帶青草氣息並不是在描述夏多內。","Besides butter aromas, what else does malolactic conversion do to a Chardonnay?":"除了奶油香氣，乳酸轉化對夏多內還有什麼作用？","It softens harsh acids":"讓尖銳的酸變柔和","It raises the alcohol level and the wine's warming sensation":"提高酒精濃度和酒的溫熱感","It adds vanilla and coconut notes":"增添香草和椰子氣息","It makes the wine sweeter":"讓酒更甜","Malolactic conversion turns sharp acids into softer ones.":"乳酸轉化把尖銳的酸轉化為較柔和的酸。","Malolactic conversion has two effects: dairy notes (butter, cream) and softer acidity. It produces no alcohol and adds no sugar. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, not from malolactic conversion.":"乳酸轉化有兩種效果：乳製品氣息（奶油、鮮奶油）和更柔和的酸度。它不會產生酒精，也不會增加糖分。香草和椰子來自橡木桶，不是乳酸轉化。","Which flavours suggest that a Chardonnay was fermented or matured in oak?":"哪些風味表示夏多內曾在橡木桶中發酵或熟成？","Smoke, vanilla, coconut":"煙燻、香草、椰子","Butter, cream and a softer texture":"奶油、鮮奶油和更柔和的質地","Apple, lemon and wet stones":"蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭","Oak brings body and flavours of smoke, vanilla and coconut.":"橡木桶帶來酒體以及煙燻、香草和椰子風味。","Each technique leaves its own signature: oak = smoke, vanilla, coconut; malolactic = butter and cream; lees = bread and biscuit. Apple, lemon and wet stones are primary grape aromas from a cool climate, not from wood.":"每種技術都留下自己的特徵：橡木桶 = 煙燻、香草、椰子；乳酸轉化 = 奶油和鮮奶油；酒渣 = 麵包和餅乾。蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭是涼爽氣候葡萄的一級香氣，不是來自木頭。","Why do not all Chardonnays benefit from malolactic, lees and oak?":"為什麼不是所有的夏多內都受益於乳酸轉化、酒渣和橡木桶？","Strong secondary flavours can swamp a delicately flavoured wine":"強烈的二級風味可能淹沒風味細緻的酒","European law forbids them for wines with a protected origin":"歐洲法律禁止受保護產地的酒使用它們","They make the wine unstable and cause it to referment in bottle":"它們讓酒不穩定，導致在瓶中再次發酵","They always lower quality":"它們總是會降低品質","Only wines with enough fruit intensity can carry these secondary flavours.":"只有果味強度足夠的酒，才承載得了這些二級風味。","These techniques are all optional: on a light wine they can hide the fruit, while in an intense wine they add complexity. They are not banned by law (Meursault uses oak and lees) and do not automatically lower quality. They do not cause refermentation in bottle.":"這些技術都是選擇性的：用在輕盈的酒上可能掩蓋果味，用在濃郁的酒上則能增添複雜度。法律並未禁止它們（Meursault 就使用橡木桶和酒渣），它們也不會自動降低品質。它們不會導致瓶中再次發酵。","A producer wants a pure-fruited Chardonnay with no secondary flavours. What will they most likely do?":"一位生產者想要果味純淨、沒有二級風味的夏多內。他最可能怎麼做？","Use inert vessels and avoid malolactic and lees contact":"使用惰性容器，避免乳酸轉化和酒渣接觸","Ferment in new barrels and leave the wine on its lees for a long time":"在新橡木桶中發酵，並讓酒長時間留在酒渣上","Add oak chips":"加入橡木片","Encourage full malolactic conversion to highlight freshness":"促進完全的乳酸轉化以突顯清新感","Inert vessels with no malolactic or lees contact keep only primary fruit aromas.":"使用惰性容器、不做乳酸轉化也不接觸酒渣，就只保留一級果香。","Steel or concrete give no flavour; avoiding malolactic and lees keeps out butter, cream, bread and biscuit. New barrels and chips add oak flavours instead. Malolactic does not highlight freshness: it softens acidity and adds dairy notes.":"不鏽鋼或混凝土不會帶來風味；避免乳酸轉化和酒渣，就不會有奶油、鮮奶油、麵包和餅乾。新橡木桶和橡木片則會增添橡木風味。乳酸轉化不會突顯清新感：它會讓酸度變柔和並增添乳製品氣息。","What is the order of Burgundy's areas, from north to south?":"布根地各地區由北到南的順序是什麼？","Chablis is in the cool north, the Côte d'Or in the moderate middle, the Mâconnais in the south.":"Chablis 位於涼爽的北部，Côte d'Or 位於溫和的中部，Mâconnais 位於南部。","Going south the climate warms: this is why Chablis is the coolest and crispest, the Côte d'Or gives fuller wines and the Mâconnais fruity, simple ones, with Pouilly-Fuissé as the exception. The other orders put Chablis or the Mâconnais in the wrong place.":"越往南氣候越溫暖：這就是為什麼 Chablis 最涼爽、最爽脆，Côte d'Or 的酒更飽滿，而 Mâconnais 的酒果香豐富、簡單，Pouilly-Fuissé 則是例外。其他順序都把 Chablis 或 Mâconnais 放錯了位置。","Compared with a Chablis, what does a Côte d'Or Chardonnay usually show?":"與 Chablis 相比，Côte d'Or 的夏多內通常表現出什麼？","More body and riper fruit, such as peach and melon":"更飽滿的酒體和更成熟的果味，例如桃子和哈密瓜","More acidity and stronger wet-stone notes":"更高的酸度和更強烈的濕石頭氣息","Less alcohol and more noticeable residual sugar":"酒精更低，殘糖更明顯","Grass and asparagus aromas":"青草和蘆筍香氣","The Côte d'Or's moderate climate ripens grapes further than cool Chablis.":"Côte d'Or 的溫和氣候讓葡萄比涼爽的 Chablis 更成熟。","Chablis is cool: light to medium body, apple, lemon and wet stones with high acidity. In the Côte d'Or the moderate climate gives more body and fruit such as peach and melon. Both are dry; grass and asparagus belong to Sauvignon Blanc.":"Chablis 很涼爽：酒體輕盈至中等，蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭，酸度高。在 Côte d'Or，溫和的氣候帶來更飽滿的酒體和桃子、哈密瓜等果味。兩者都是不甜的；青草和蘆筍屬於白蘇維濃。","How do producers in Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet add complexity and body?":"Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 的生產者如何增添複雜度和酒體？","By fermenting or maturing in oak barrels and ageing on the lees":"在橡木桶中發酵或熟成，並在酒渣上陳年","By late-harvesting grapes affected by noble rot":"晚採受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","By adding unfermented grape juice before bottling":"在裝瓶前加入未發酵的葡萄汁","With oak chips":"用橡木片","In the Côte de Beaune, barrels and lees give body and complexity to the great Chardonnays.":"在 Côte de Beaune，橡木桶和酒渣為偉大的夏多內帶來酒體和複雜度。","These villages make top-level dry whites worked in oak barrels and on their lees. They are not sweet wines, so neither noble rot nor added juice is used. Chips are a cheap shortcut typical of high-volume wines, not of Côte de Beaune crus.":"這些村莊出產頂級的不甜白酒，在橡木桶中並在酒渣上釀製。它們不是甜酒，所以既不用貴腐菌，也不加葡萄汁。橡木片是大量生產酒款典型的便宜捷徑，不是 Côte de Beaune 特級酒款的做法。","A label reads 'Bourgogne' and 'Chardonnay'. Where can the grapes come from?":"一張酒標上寫著「Bourgogne」和「Chardonnay」。葡萄可以來自哪裡？","From anywhere in Burgundy":"布根地的任何地方","Only from Côte de Beaune premier cru vineyards":"只能來自 Côte de Beaune 的 premier cru 葡萄園","Only from the village of Chablis":"只能來自 Chablis 村","From any region of France, because it is a protected geographical indication":"法國任何地區，因為它是受保護地理標示","Bourgogne AOC is the regional appellation covering the whole of Burgundy.":"Bourgogne AOC 是涵蓋整個布根地的地區級法定產區。","As the broadest appellation, Bourgogne AOC allows grapes from the whole region to be combined: that is why the wine is usually simple, with apple, lemon and high acidity. Premier cru and Chablis have their own, narrower appellations. It is not a nationwide PGI: it stays within Burgundy.":"作為範圍最廣的法定產區，Bourgogne AOC 允許結合來自整個地區的葡萄：這就是為什麼這種酒通常很簡單，帶有蘋果、檸檬和高酸度。Premier cru 和 Chablis 有各自範圍更小的法定產區。它不是全國性的 PGI：範圍仍在布根地之內。","A customer asks for a Pouilly-Fuissé. What wine are they asking for?":"一位顧客要一瓶 Pouilly-Fuissé。他要的是什麼酒？","A Mâconnais Chardonnay, often oak-matured":"Mâconnais 的夏多內，常經橡木桶熟成","A Loire Sauvignon Blanc, dry and herbaceous":"羅亞爾河的白蘇維濃，不甜且帶草本氣息","A Pinot Noir from the Côte de Nuits":"Côte de Nuits 的黑皮諾","A sweet Chenin Blanc made from grapes affected by noble rot":"以受貴腐菌感染的葡萄釀造的甜型白梢楠","Pouilly-Fuissé is a Chardonnay white from the Mâconnais in southern Burgundy.":"Pouilly-Fuissé 是來自布根地南部 Mâconnais 的夏多內白酒。","The name is easily confused with Pouilly-Fumé, which is a Loire Sauvignon Blanc. Pouilly-Fuissé comes from steep east- and south-east-facing slopes, with concentrated fruit and often barrel treatment. It is neither a red nor a sweet wine.":"這個名字很容易和 Pouilly-Fumé 混淆，後者是羅亞爾河的白蘇維濃。Pouilly-Fuissé 來自朝東和東南的陡坡，果味濃縮，常經過橡木桶處理。它既不是紅酒，也不是甜酒。","An inexpensive Central Valley Chardonnay says only 'California' and tastes slightly of vanilla. What can you infer?":"一款平價的 Central Valley 夏多內只標示「California」，嚐起來略帶香草味。你可以推斷什麼？","High-volume grapes; the vanilla probably comes from oak chips or staves":"大量生產的葡萄；香草味可能來自橡木片或橡木條","Grapes from a coastal Sonoma vineyard, matured in new barrels":"來自 Sonoma 沿海葡萄園的葡萄，在新橡木桶中熟成","A Los Carneros wine":"一款 Los Carneros 的酒","A wine fermented in barrel on its lees":"一款在橡木桶中帶酒渣發酵的酒","Without a more specific GI, Central Valley grapes are sold as 'California'; any oak usually comes from chips or staves.":"沒有更具體的 GI 時，Central Valley 的葡萄以「California」出售；若有橡木味，通常來自橡木片或橡木條。","The Central Valley is hot, dry and irrigated, with high yields destined for high-volume brands. In an inexpensive wine, oak flavours almost always come from chips or staves, which cost less than barrels. Sonoma or Los Carneros would appear on the label as more specific GIs.":"Central Valley 炎熱、乾燥、經過灌溉，產量很高，用於大量生產的品牌。在平價的酒中，橡木風味幾乎總是來自比橡木桶便宜的橡木片或橡木條。Sonoma 或 Los Carneros 會作為更具體的 GI 出現在酒標上。","What changes in Napa Valley as you go further north?":"在 Napa Valley 越往北走，會有什麼變化？","It becomes warmer and sunnier":"變得更溫暖、陽光更充足","It becomes cooler thanks to the bay fogs":"因為海灣的霧氣而變得更涼爽","It becomes rainier and suits only sparkling base wines":"變得更多雨，只適合氣泡酒的基酒","It becomes higher and windier":"變得更高、風更大","Further north, Napa Valley gets further from the bay and becomes warmer and sunnier.":"越往北，Napa Valley 離海灣越遠，變得更溫暖、陽光更充足。","The rising warmth explains the typical style: full-bodied Chardonnays with pronounced tropical fruit and vanilla and spice from new oak. San Pablo Bay fogs cool the south, towards Los Carneros, not the north. Altitude and rain are not the factors involved.":"溫度上升解釋了典型的風格：酒體飽滿的夏多內，帶有濃郁的熱帶水果，以及新橡木桶的香草和香料。San Pablo Bay 的霧氣讓南部（往 Los Carneros 方向）降溫，而不是北部。海拔和雨水都不是相關因素。","What effect do Pacific breezes have on Chardonnay from Sonoma's coastal vineyards?":"太平洋微風對 Sonoma 沿海葡萄園的夏多內有什麼影響？","Grapes keep their acidity while developing complex flavours":"葡萄在發展複雜風味的同時保留酸度","Grapes ripen faster and build more sugar and alcohol":"葡萄成熟得更快，累積更多糖分和酒精","Grapes are more often affected by noble rot":"葡萄更常受到貴腐菌感染","The wine becomes more tannic":"酒變得更有單寧感","Cooling slows ripening: acidity is kept and flavours become more complex.":"降溫減緩成熟：保留酸度，風味變得更複雜。","Coastal influences temper California's heat and allow slow, balanced ripening. Faster ripening would be the effect of a warmer climate, not a cooler one. Noble rot is not part of these dry wines, and a white does not become tannic.":"沿海的影響緩和了加州的高溫，讓葡萄緩慢而均衡地成熟。成熟加快是較溫暖氣候的效果，而不是較涼爽氣候的。貴腐菌與這些不甜的酒無關，白酒也不會變得有單寧感。","What range of styles does Santa Barbara County Chardonnay offer?":"Santa Barbara County 的夏多內提供哪些風格範圍？","From Côte de Beaune-like wines to tropical styles with more new oak":"從類似 Côte de Beaune 的酒，到新橡木桶更多的熱帶水果風格","Only light, unoaked wines similar to Chablis":"只有類似 Chablis、輕盈且未經橡木桶的酒","Mainly sweet late-harvest wines":"主要是甜型晚收酒","Only high-volume wines sold under the simple California label":"只有以簡單的 California 標示出售的大量生產酒款","In Santa Barbara, styles run from Burgundian-style Chardonnay to more tropical, higher-alcohol, oakier wines.":"在 Santa Barbara，風格從布根地式的夏多內，到熱帶水果更多、酒精更高、橡木味更重的酒都有。","Sea breezes funnelled by lateral valleys allow elegant wines close to the Côte de Beaune, while other producers aim for tropical fruit, higher alcohol and pronounced new oak. The area is known for quality, not for bulk or sweet wines.":"由橫向山谷導入的海風讓這裡能釀出接近 Côte de Beaune 的優雅酒款，而其他生產者則追求熱帶水果、更高的酒精和濃郁的新橡木桶風味。這個地區以品質著稱，而不是大量生產酒或甜酒。","Which description fits Oregon Chardonnay?":"哪一項描述符合奧勒岡的夏多內？","High acidity, lemon to melon; small production compared with California":"高酸度、從檸檬到哈密瓜；與加州相比產量很小","Low acidity, very ripe banana and pineapple":"低酸度、非常成熟的香蕉和鳳梨","Sweet style, with noble rot":"甜型風格，帶有貴腐","Large volumes from hot, irrigated inland vineyards, sold as brands":"來自炎熱、經灌溉的內陸葡萄園的大量酒款，以品牌出售","Oregon's moderate climate gives fresh Chardonnays with lemon and melon notes.":"奧勒岡的溫和氣候帶來帶有檸檬和哈密瓜氣息的清爽夏多內。","Oregon has a generally moderate climate: its Chardonnay has refreshing high acidity and flavours from citrus to light tropical notes. Production is small compared with California. Bulk wines from hot inland vineyards describe California's Central Valley, not Oregon.":"奧勒岡整體屬於溫和氣候：它的夏多內有令人清爽的高酸度，風味從柑橘到淡淡的熱帶水果氣息。與加州相比，產量很小。來自炎熱內陸葡萄園的大量生產酒款描述的是加州的 Central Valley，不是奧勒岡。","Why are some 'South Eastern Australia' Chardonnays blended with Semillon or with wine from cooler vineyards?":"為什麼有些「South Eastern Australia」夏多內會與榭密雍或較涼爽葡萄園的酒混調？","To achieve better balance":"為了取得更好的平衡","Because Australian law requires at least two grapes in every branded wine":"因為澳洲法律規定每款品牌酒至少要用兩個品種","To make them fit for long ageing":"為了讓它們適合長期陳年","Grapes from warm, irrigated inland vineyards benefit from blending that rebalances the wine.":"來自溫暖、經灌溉的內陸葡萄園的葡萄，受益於能重新平衡酒款的混調。","The South Eastern Australia GI covers a vast area; much of the fruit comes from warm inland zones. Adding Semillon or cooler-site wine helps balance, for example between acidity and body. There is no blending requirement, these wines are not made for long ageing, and Semillon brings no oak notes.":"South Eastern Australia 這個 GI 涵蓋廣大的區域；大部分的果實來自溫暖的內陸地帶。加入榭密雍或較涼爽園地的酒，有助於取得平衡，例如在酸度和酒體之間。並沒有混調的規定，這些酒也不是為長期陳年而釀的，而榭密雍不會帶來橡木氣息。","Which Australian region owes its cooler climate to ocean currents from the south rather than to altitude?":"澳洲哪個產區的涼爽氣候來自南方的洋流，而不是海拔？","Yarra Valley, in Victoria, is cooled by ocean currents from the south.":"維多利亞的 Yarra Valley 受到來自南方的洋流降溫。","Adelaide Hills, Clare Valley and Eden Valley are all in South Australia and owe their coolness mainly to altitude. Yarra Valley is moderated by the ocean instead. Both influences lengthen the season and give Chardonnays with peach and medium to high acidity.":"Adelaide Hills、Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley 都位於南澳，主要因海拔而涼爽。Yarra Valley 則受到海洋的調節。兩種影響都能延長生長季，釀出帶有桃子、酸度中等至高的夏多內。","Which statement about Margaret River is correct?":"關於 Margaret River，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Warm climate moderated by sea breezes; small volumes, consistent quality":"受海風調節的溫暖氣候；產量小，品質穩定","It is the main source of irrigated South Eastern Australia brands":"它是經灌溉的 South Eastern Australia 品牌的主要來源","It lies in the state of Victoria":"它位於維多利亞州","It has a cold climate, cooled by altitude":"它屬於寒冷氣候，因海拔而涼爽","Margaret River, in Western Australia, is warm but sea-cooled, with limited production and high quality.":"西澳的 Margaret River 很溫暖但受海洋降溫，產量有限、品質很高。","Sea breezes slow ripening and give medium- to full-bodied Chardonnays with peach and pineapple. The region is in Western Australia, not Victoria, and is not about altitude or bulk wine: it produces far less than South Eastern Australia.":"海風減緩成熟，釀出酒體中等至飽滿、帶有桃子和鳳梨的夏多內。這個產區位於西澳，不是維多利亞，與海拔或大量生產酒款無關：它的產量遠少於 South Eastern Australia。","Which profile fits a Marlborough Chardonnay?":"哪一種風味特徵符合 Marlborough 的夏多內？","Ripe lemon, peach, melon, high acidity, subtle oak":"成熟的檸檬、桃子、哈密瓜，高酸度，細緻的橡木味","Banana and pineapple, medium acidity, strong new-oak vanilla and a very full body":"香蕉和鳳梨，中等酸度，強烈的新橡木桶香草味，酒體非常飽滿","Sweet, with honey and dried apricot":"甜，帶有蜂蜜和杏桃乾","Marlborough is cool but sunny: ripe fruit with high natural acidity.":"Marlborough 涼爽但陽光充足：成熟的果味配上高天然酸度。","In the north-east of the South Island, Marlborough has sea breezes and plentiful rain: its Chardonnay is very good, fresh, with light oak. Strong vanilla and medium acidity describe warm styles; grass and asparagus are typical of its Sauvignon Blanc, not its Chardonnay.":"位於南島東北部的 Marlborough 有海風和充沛的雨水：它的夏多內非常好、清爽，橡木味輕盈。強烈的香草味和中等酸度描述的是溫暖風格；青草和蘆筍是它的白蘇維濃的典型特徵，不是夏多內。","In Chile, where do the outstanding Chardonnays of the Central Valley come from?":"在智利，Central Valley 傑出的夏多內來自哪裡？","From vineyards moderated by altitude":"來自受海拔調節的葡萄園","From the hottest, flattest irrigated valley-floor vineyards":"來自最炎熱、最平坦、經灌溉的谷底葡萄園","From grapes affected by noble rot":"來自受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","From vineyards on the Argentine border":"來自阿根廷邊境的葡萄園","In the warm Central Valley, the best Chardonnays come from vineyards cooled by altitude.":"在溫暖的 Central Valley，最好的夏多內來自因海拔而涼爽的葡萄園。","The Central Valley is larger and warmer than Casablanca Valley and produces everything from cheap brands to outstanding wines. Altitude tempers the heat and allows quality wines. The hot, irrigated valley floor mainly gives volume; noble rot and the Argentine border are irrelevant.":"Central Valley 比 Casablanca Valley 更大、更溫暖，出產從便宜品牌到傑出酒款的各種酒。海拔緩和了高溫，讓優質酒款成為可能。炎熱、經灌溉的谷底主要帶來產量；貴腐菌和阿根廷邊境都無關。","In the hot inland vineyards of the Western Cape, which grape is Chardonnay sometimes blended with?":"在西開普炎熱的內陸葡萄園，夏多內有時會與哪個品種混調？","Pinotage, the country's signature black grape":"皮諾塔吉，這個國家的招牌黑葡萄","For high-volume brands, Western Cape Chardonnay is sometimes blended with Chenin Blanc.":"用於大量生產的品牌時，西開普的夏多內有時會與白梢楠混調。","The hot inland vineyards of the Western Cape mainly supply branded wines, and Chenin Blanc is South Africa's most planted white grape. Pinot Noir and Pinotage are black grapes, not used in such a white; Riesling is not the partner mentioned.":"西開普炎熱的內陸葡萄園主要供應品牌酒，而白梢楠是南非種植最多的白葡萄品種。黑皮諾和皮諾塔吉是黑葡萄，不會用在這樣的白酒中；麗絲玲也不是所提到的搭檔。","Why has Chardonnay suffered from a poor image in many markets?":"為什麼夏多內在許多市場的形象不佳？","Because of its link with the heavy oak of the 1980s and 1990s":"因為它與 1980 和 1990 年代的濃重橡木味有關","Because it was linked to low-quality sweet wines such as Liebfraumilch":"因為它與 Liebfraumilch 等低品質甜酒有關","Because its herbaceous aromas are tiring":"因為它的草本香氣令人厭倦","Because it never ages":"因為它從不陳年","The very oaky style of those decades shaped the grape's image.":"那幾十年橡木味極重的風格塑造了這個品種的形象。","Today the aim is not to hide the fruit under wood, but Chardonnay is still more likely to show oak than Pinot Grigio or Sauvignon Blanc. Liebfraumilch harmed Riesling; worries about herbaceous aromas concern Sauvignon Blanc. Great Chardonnays can age for decades.":"現在的目標不是用木頭掩蓋果味，但夏多內仍比灰皮諾或白蘇維濃更可能帶有橡木味。Liebfraumilch 傷害的是麗絲玲；對草本香氣的顧慮涉及的是白蘇維濃。偉大的夏多內可以陳年數十年。","Which two factors have helped Chablis stay steadily popular?":"哪兩個因素幫助 Chablis 保持穩定的人氣？","Unoaked style and labelling by region, not by grape":"未經橡木桶的風格，以及以產區而非品種標示","Low prices and large volumes from irrigated vineyards":"低價格和來自灌溉葡萄園的大量產量","Strong new oak and very ripe tropical fruit":"強烈的新橡木桶味和非常成熟的熱帶水果","Noticeable residual sugar and low alcohol, designed for broad appeal":"明顯的殘糖和低酒精，為了廣泛的吸引力而設計","Chablis is unoaked and labelled by region, which separates it from Chardonnay's 'oaky' image.":"Chablis 未經橡木桶且以產區標示，讓它與夏多內「橡木味重」的形象區隔開來。","Many consumers link Chardonnay with heavy oak; Chablis avoids both problems, being fresh and unoaked and often not naming the grape at all. It is not a bulk wine from irrigated vineyards, nor tropical or sweet.":"許多消費者把夏多內與濃重的橡木味聯想在一起；Chablis 避開了這兩個問題，它清爽、未經橡木桶，而且常常根本不標示品種。它不是來自灌溉葡萄園的大量生產酒款，也不是熱帶水果風格或甜酒。","Which of these is NOT a secondary flavour in Chardonnay?":"下列哪一項不是夏多內的二級風味？","Hazelnut":"榛果","Butter":"奶油","Biscuit":"餅乾","Hazelnut is a tertiary flavour that develops with bottle age.":"榛果是隨瓶中陳年發展出的三級風味。","Secondary flavours come from the winery: butter from malolactic, biscuit from lees, vanilla from oak. Hazelnut and mushroom instead appear in quality Chardonnays after years in bottle, so they are tertiary.":"二級風味來自酒廠：奶油來自乳酸轉化，餅乾來自酒渣，香草來自橡木桶。榛果和蘑菇則是優質夏多內在瓶中多年後才出現的，所以是三級風味。","Which aromas are the hallmark of Sauvignon Blanc?":"哪些香氣是白蘇維濃的招牌特徵？","Grass, green bell pepper, asparagus":"青草、青椒、蘆筍","Rose, lychee, apricot":"玫瑰、荔枝、杏桃","Butter, cream, vanilla":"奶油、鮮奶油、香草","Pear, ginger, honey":"梨、薑、蜂蜜","Sauvignon Blanc is known for pronounced herbaceous aromas.":"白蘇維濃以濃郁的草本香氣著稱。","Sauvignon Blanc is an aromatic grape whose wines are recognised by herbaceous notes: grass, green bell pepper and asparagus. Rose and lychee point to Gewurztraminer; butter, cream and vanilla are winemaking aromas typical of many Chardonnays; pear, ginger and honey suggest Pinot Gris, especially with age.":"白蘇維濃是芳香型品種，它的酒以草本氣息辨識：青草、青椒和蘆筍。玫瑰和荔枝指向格烏茲塔明那；奶油、鮮奶油和香草是許多夏多內典型的釀造香氣；梨、薑和蜂蜜則讓人想到灰皮諾，尤其是陳年後。","In which climates does Sauvignon Blanc perform best?":"白蘇維濃在哪些氣候中表現最好？","Cool and moderate":"涼爽和溫和","Hot and dry":"炎熱乾燥","Only warm and irrigated":"只在溫暖且經灌溉的地方","Hot and humid":"炎熱潮濕","Coolness preserves the grape's high acidity and herbaceous aromas.":"涼爽能保留這個品種的高酸度和草本香氣。","Sauvignon Blanc grows best in cool and moderate climates, where it keeps the high acidity and herbaceous aromas that make it recognisable. In areas that are too warm it loses freshness, which is why in Languedoc the best wines come from high sites and in California growers seek cooler areas or pick early.":"白蘇維濃在涼爽和溫和氣候中生長得最好，在那裡能保留讓它容易辨識的高酸度和草本香氣。在太溫暖的地區，它會失去清新感，這就是為什麼在 Languedoc 最好的酒來自高海拔園地，而在加州種植者會尋找較涼爽的地區或提早採收。","Riper Sauvignon Blanc grapes give which flavours?":"較成熟的白蘇維濃葡萄會帶來哪些風味？","Peach and passion fruit":"桃子和百香果","Green apple and gooseberry":"青蘋果和醋栗","Grapefruit and wet stones":"葡萄柚和濕石頭","With more ripeness the fruit moves from green and citrus to peach and tropical.":"成熟度越高，果味就從綠色水果和柑橘轉向桃子和熱帶水果。","Sauvignon Blanc's fruit depends on ripeness. Less ripe grapes give apple, gooseberry, grapefruit and wet stones; riper grapes bring stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as passion fruit. Hazelnut and mushroom are tertiary aromas typical of aged Chardonnay.":"白蘇維濃的果味取決於成熟度。較不成熟的葡萄帶來蘋果、醋栗、葡萄柚和濕石頭；較成熟的葡萄則帶來桃子等核果和百香果等熱帶水果。榛果和蘑菇是陳年夏多內典型的三級香氣。","Why is single-varietal Sauvignon Blanc usually made in inert vessels?":"為什麼單一品種的白蘇維濃通常在惰性容器中釀造？","New oak would mask its herbaceous aromas":"新橡木桶會掩蓋它的草本香氣","To increase body and alcohol":"為了增加酒體和酒精","To encourage long ageing":"為了促進長期陳年","Because the law bans oak":"因為法律禁止使用橡木桶","Its distinctive herbaceous aromas are easily overwhelmed by new oak.":"它獨特的草本香氣很容易被新橡木桶壓過。","Sauvignon Blanc's appeal lies in its herbaceous and fruity aromas. New oak flavours would easily mask them, so single-varietal wines are mostly made in stainless steel or other inert vessels. Oak is not banned: when used, labels often show terms such as barrel aged.":"白蘇維濃的魅力在於它的草本和果香。新橡木桶的風味很容易掩蓋這些香氣，所以單一品種的酒大多在不鏽鋼槽或其他惰性容器中釀造。橡木桶並沒有被禁止：使用時，酒標上常會出現 barrel aged 等術語。","What happens to many Sauvignon Blancs after a couple of years in bottle?":"許多白蘇維濃在瓶中放了一兩年後會怎樣？","They lose freshness and turn vegetal":"失去清新感，變得有植物味","They develop hazelnut and mushroom":"發展出榛果和蘑菇","They become sweeter and more tropical":"變得更甜、更有熱帶水果味","They gain butter and cream notes":"增添奶油和鮮奶油氣息","It is best young; with time the fresh aromas fade.":"它最好趁年輕喝；隨著時間，清新的香氣會消退。","Most Sauvignon Blanc is meant to be drunk young. Even outstanding wines can lose their fresh aromas within a couple of years of the vintage and develop unattractive vegetal notes. Exceptions include some Semillon blends, such as the best Graves and Pessac-Léognan, which age to develop honey and nutty notes.":"大多數白蘇維濃都是要趁年輕喝的。即使是傑出的酒款，也可能在年份後一兩年內失去清新的香氣，發展出不討喜的植物性氣息。例外包括一些與榭密雍混調的酒，例如最好的 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan，它們陳年後會發展出蜂蜜和堅果氣息。","Which grape is Sauvignon Blanc often blended with?":"白蘇維濃常與哪個品種混調？","Semillon":"榭密雍","Semillon is the classic partner, adding body and ageing ability.":"榭密雍是經典的搭檔，增添酒體和陳年能力。","Sauvignon Blanc is mainly a single-varietal wine, but when blended its typical partner is Semillon: in Bordeaux (Bordeaux AOC, Graves, Pessac-Léognan) and in Australia (Margaret River, Adelaide Hills). Semillon adds body and helps the wine age. Sauvignon, for its part, brings acidity and herbaceous aromas to the blend.":"白蘇維濃主要以單一品種釀造，但混調時典型的搭檔是榭密雍：在波爾多（Bordeaux AOC、Graves、Pessac-Léognan）和澳洲（Margaret River、Adelaide Hills）都是如此。榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。白蘇維濃則為混調帶來酸度和草本香氣。","In which two Loire appellations is Sauvignon Blanc the only permitted white grape?":"在哪兩個羅亞爾河法定產區，白蘇維濃是唯一允許的白葡萄品種？","Touraine and Vouvray":"Touraine 和 Vouvray","Chablis and Pouilly-Fuissé":"Chablis 和 Pouilly-Fuissé","Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé, facing across the Loire, allow only Sauvignon Blanc for whites.":"隔著羅亞爾河相望的 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé，白酒只允許使用白蘇維濃。","Sancerre AOC and Pouilly-Fumé AOC face each other across the Loire in a cool climate. For whites only Sauvignon Blanc is allowed: dry wines with high acidity, green apple, grass, asparagus and sometimes wet stones. Graves and Pessac-Léognan are in Bordeaux; Chablis and Pouilly-Fuissé are Burgundy Chardonnay appellations.":"Sancerre AOC 和 Pouilly-Fumé AOC 在涼爽氣候中隔著羅亞爾河相望。白酒只允許使用白蘇維濃：不甜、高酸度，帶有青蘋果、青草、蘆筍，有時還有濕石頭。Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 位於波爾多；Chablis 和 Pouilly-Fuissé 是布根地的夏多內法定產區。","Which profile best describes a white Sancerre?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述 Sancerre 白酒？","Dry, high acidity, green apple, grass, asparagus":"不甜、高酸度、青蘋果、青草、蘆筍","Full, low acidity, rose and lychee":"飽滿、低酸度、玫瑰和荔枝","Full, new oak, pineapple and vanilla":"飽滿、新橡木桶、鳳梨和香草","Off-dry, peach, mango and ginger":"微甜、桃子、芒果和薑","The cool Loire climate gives dry, crisp wines with green fruit and herbaceous notes.":"羅亞爾河的涼爽氣候帶來不甜、爽脆、帶有綠色水果和草本氣息的酒。","Sancerre is a cool Loire appellation dedicated, for whites, to Sauvignon Blanc. The cool climate preserves high acidity and leaves green fruit such as apple, herbaceous grass and asparagus notes and sometimes wet stones. Rose and lychee indicate Gewurztraminer; mango and ginger an Alsace Pinot Gris.":"Sancerre 是羅亞爾河的涼爽法定產區，白酒專門使用白蘇維濃。涼爽的氣候保留了高酸度，留下蘋果等綠色水果、青草和蘆筍等草本氣息，有時還有濕石頭。玫瑰和荔枝表示格烏茲塔明那；芒果和薑則表示阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾。","What style does Touraine AOC Sauvignon Blanc usually offer?":"Touraine AOC 的白蘇維濃通常是什麼風格？","Fruity and inexpensive":"果香豐富且價格平實","Concentrated, oaked, built to age":"濃縮、經橡木桶、適合陳年","Sweet, from very ripe grapes":"甜，用非常成熟的葡萄釀造","Full, blended with Semillon":"飽滿，與榭密雍混調","Touraine covers a wide area west of Sancerre: fruity, affordable wines.":"Touraine 涵蓋 Sancerre 以西的廣大區域：果香豐富、價格親民的酒。","Touraine AOC grapes come from the wide Touraine sub-region, west of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé. The wines are typically fruity and inexpensive. The concentrated, oak-matured, age-worthy style belongs instead to the best Graves and Pessac-Léognan, where Sauvignon is blended with Semillon.":"Touraine AOC 的葡萄來自廣大的 Touraine 子產區，位於 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 以西。這些酒通常果香豐富、價格平實。濃縮、經橡木桶熟成、適合陳年的風格，則屬於最好的 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan，那裡的白蘇維濃會與榭密雍混調。","What role does Semillon play in Graves and Pessac-Léognan whites?":"榭密雍在 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 白酒中扮演什麼角色？","It adds body and helps the wine age":"增添酒體並幫助酒陳年","It adds acidity and herbaceous notes":"增添酸度和草本氣息","It adds floral rose aromas":"增添玫瑰花香","It lowers alcohol and body":"降低酒精和酒體","Semillon fills out Sauvignon: more body and longer life.":"榭密雍讓白蘇維濃更豐滿：酒體更飽滿，壽命更長。","Graves AOC and Pessac-Léognan AOC make whites more concentrated and complex than simple Bordeaux AOC, usually blending Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon. Sauvignon brings acidity and herbaceous aromas; Semillon adds body and helps the wine age. The best are oak-matured and develop honey and nutty notes in bottle.":"Graves AOC 和 Pessac-Léognan AOC 出產比簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 更濃縮、更複雜的白酒，通常混調白蘇維濃和榭密雍。白蘇維濃帶來酸度和草本香氣；榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。最好的酒款經橡木桶熟成，在瓶中會發展出蜂蜜和堅果氣息。","Which flavours do the best Pessac-Léognan whites develop in bottle?":"最好的 Pessac-Léognan 白酒在瓶中會發展出哪些風味？","Honey and nuts":"蜂蜜和堅果","Grass and asparagus":"青草和蘆筍","Lychee and rose":"荔枝和玫瑰","Banana and pineapple":"香蕉和鳳梨","Oak-matured blends evolve towards complex honey and nutty notes.":"經橡木桶熟成的混調酒會朝複雜的蜂蜜和堅果氣息演變。","Very good or outstanding Graves and Pessac-Léognan whites, Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blends often matured in oak, can age in bottle. Over time they develop complex aromas of honey and nuts. Grass and asparagus are primary aromas of young Sauvignon; lychee and rose belong to Gewurztraminer.":"非常好或傑出的 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 白酒，是常經橡木桶熟成的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調，可以在瓶中陳年。隨著時間，它們會發展出蜂蜜和堅果的複雜香氣。青草和蘆筍是年輕白蘇維濃的一級香氣；荔枝和玫瑰則屬於格烏茲塔明那。","Where do Languedoc-Roussillon's best Sauvignon Blancs come from?":"Languedoc-Roussillon 最好的白蘇維濃來自哪裡？","From areas cooled by altitude":"來自因海拔而涼爽的地區","From the hottest coastal plains":"來自最炎熱的沿海平原","From irrigated, high-yield vineyards":"來自經灌溉的高產量葡萄園","From very late-harvested grapes":"來自非常晚採收的葡萄","Much of the region is too warm; altitude provides the coolness needed.":"這個地區大部分都太溫暖；海拔提供了所需的涼爽。","Languedoc-Roussillon is mostly too warm for a cool-loving grape like Sauvignon Blanc. The best wines therefore come from areas cooled by altitude: dry, high in acidity, with passion fruit and herbaceous grass notes, usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. The tropical fruit reflects the region's generally warm climate.":"對白蘇維濃這種喜愛涼爽的品種來說，Languedoc-Roussillon 大部分地方都太溫暖了。因此最好的酒來自因海拔而涼爽的地區：不甜、酸度高，帶有百香果和青草等草本氣息，通常標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。熱帶水果反映了這個地區整體溫暖的氣候。","Why do Marlborough Sauvignon Blancs show such a broad range of fruit flavours?":"為什麼 Marlborough 的白蘇維濃展現如此廣泛的果味？","Blending across sites and ripeness levels":"混調來自不同園地和成熟度的葡萄","Long ageing in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","Systematic blending with Chardonnay":"有系統地與夏多內混調","Late harvest of raisined grapes":"晚收風乾的葡萄","Combining sites and ripeness brings grapefruit, peach and passion fruit together.":"結合不同園地和成熟度，讓葡萄柚、桃子和百香果匯聚一堂。","In Marlborough many Sauvignon Blancs are made by blending grapes from different sites or picked at different ripeness levels. Grapefruit (less ripe) then sits alongside peach and passion fruit (riper), with intense green pepper and asparagus. The result is a more pronounced style than the Loire's.":"在 Marlborough，許多白蘇維濃是混調來自不同園地或在不同成熟度採收的葡萄釀成的。葡萄柚（較不成熟）與桃子和百香果（較成熟）並存，再加上濃烈的青椒和蘆筍。結果是比羅亞爾河更鮮明的風格。","A Sauvignon Blanc with grapefruit, passion fruit and intense green pepper most likely comes from?":"一款帶有葡萄柚、百香果和濃烈青椒味的白蘇維濃，最可能來自哪裡？","Marlborough gives the most pronounced style: tropical fruit and intense herbaceous notes.":"Marlborough 的風格最鮮明：熱帶水果加上濃烈的草本氣息。","Marlborough's classic style combines a broad range of fruit, from grapefruit to passion fruit, with very pronounced green pepper and asparagus. Pessac-Léognan is more complex and often oaked; Touraine is fruity but simple; Elgin, South Africa's coolest region, leans to green apple and wet stones.":"Marlborough 的經典風格結合了從葡萄柚到百香果的廣泛果味，以及非常鮮明的青椒和蘆筍。Pessac-Léognan 更複雜，常經橡木桶；Touraine 果香豐富但簡單；南非最涼爽的產區 Elgin 則偏向青蘋果和濕石頭。","How are some Marlborough producers experimenting beyond the classic style?":"有些 Marlborough 的生產者如何在經典風格之外進行嘗試？","Cooler sites, or a little oak and lees":"使用較涼爽的園地，或加入少許橡木桶和酒渣","Fermenting on skins like a red":"像紅酒一樣帶皮發酵","Stopping fermentation for a sweet wine":"中止發酵以釀造甜酒","Blending with Gewurztraminer":"與格烏茲塔明那混調","Some seek a Loire-like style from cool sites; others add complexity with oak or lees.":"有些人從涼爽園地追求類似羅亞爾河的風格；其他人則用橡木桶或酒渣增添複雜度。","Experimentation is increasingly common in Marlborough. Some producers choose grapes from cooler sites for wines similar to the Loire; others use small amounts of oak or lees contact to add complexity and body. The aim is to offer variety to drinkers who might tire of intense herbaceous aromas.":"在 Marlborough，各種嘗試越來越普遍。有些生產者選用較涼爽園地的葡萄，釀出類似羅亞爾河的酒；其他人則使用少量橡木桶或酒渣接觸，增添複雜度和酒體。目的是為可能對濃烈草本香氣感到厭倦的飲酒者提供多樣選擇。","In which Australian region is Sauvignon Blanc the most widely planted grape?":"在澳洲哪個產區，白蘇維濃是種植最廣泛的品種？","Altitude-cooled Adelaide Hills has Sauvignon Blanc as its leading grape.":"因海拔而涼爽的 Adelaide Hills，以白蘇維濃為主要品種。","In Adelaide Hills, South Australia, altitude cools the vineyards and Sauvignon Blanc is the most planted variety. Wines are generally fresh and fruity, from citrus to tropical fruit; some are blended with Semillon for more body and ageing potential. Margaret River is known mainly for Sauvignon-Semillon blends.":"在南澳的 Adelaide Hills，海拔讓葡萄園保持涼爽，白蘇維濃是種植最多的品種。酒款一般清爽、果香豐富，從柑橘到熱帶水果都有；有些會與榭密雍混調，以增添酒體和陳年潛力。Margaret River 則主要以白蘇維濃與榭密雍的混調著稱。","What Sauvignon Blanc style is Margaret River known for?":"Margaret River 以哪一種白蘇維濃風格聞名？","Semillon blends, concentrated and herbaceous":"與榭密雍混調，濃縮且帶草本氣息","Sweet late-harvest wines":"甜型晚收酒","Light, cheap single-varietals":"輕盈、便宜的單一品種酒","Chardonnay blends in new oak":"在新橡木桶中與夏多內混調","In Margaret River Sauvignon is often blended with Semillon, with concentrated herbaceous aromas.":"在 Margaret River，白蘇維濃常與榭密雍混調，帶有濃縮的草本香氣。","Margaret River in Western Australia has built a reputation for Sauvignon Blanc, most often blended with Semillon. These wines show concentrated herbaceous aromas such as grass, and some are made in contact with oak. They are neither sweet wines nor simple cheap ones.":"西澳的 Margaret River 以白蘇維濃建立了名聲，大多與榭密雍混調。這些酒展現青草等濃縮的草本香氣，有些會與橡木接觸釀造。它們既不是甜酒，也不是簡單的便宜酒。","Why is Casablanca Valley known for very good Sauvignon Blanc?":"為什麼 Casablanca Valley 以非常好的白蘇維濃聞名？","It is cooled by sea breezes and morning fog":"它受到海風和晨霧降溫","It is cooled by Andean altitude":"它受到安地斯山脈的海拔降溫","It is Chile's warmest area":"它是智利最溫暖的地區","It always uses new oak":"它總是使用新橡木桶","Pacific breezes and fog keep freshness and acidity.":"太平洋的微風和霧氣保留了清新感和酸度。","Casablanca Valley is a coastal Chilean region cooled both by sea breezes and by Pacific morning fogs. These conditions suit Sauvignon Blanc's fresh, herbaceous style. The larger Central Valley produces wines at every level, from cheap brands to very good examples.":"Casablanca Valley 是智利的沿海產區，同時受到海風和太平洋晨霧的降溫。這樣的條件適合白蘇維濃清爽、帶草本氣息的風格。較大的 Central Valley 則出產各個等級的酒，從便宜品牌到非常好的酒款都有。","Why is South African Sauvignon Blanc concentrated in coastal regions?":"為什麼南非的白蘇維濃集中在沿海產區？","Inland vineyards are generally too warm":"內陸葡萄園一般太溫暖","Inland is too cold and frosty":"內陸太冷、容易結霜","The law bans the grape inland":"法律禁止在內陸種植這個品種","Only the coast has suitable soils":"只有沿海有合適的土壤","Sauvignon likes coolness; the coast offers breezes the hot interior lacks.":"白蘇維濃喜歡涼爽；沿海有炎熱內陸所缺乏的微風。","In South Africa inland vineyards are generally too warm for Sauvignon Blanc, which needs coolness to keep its acidity and herbaceous aromas. Plantings are therefore concentrated on the coast: Constantia is cooled by Southern Ocean breezes, while Elgin owes its coolness to altitude.":"在南非，內陸葡萄園對白蘇維濃來說一般太溫暖，而這個品種需要涼爽才能保留酸度和草本香氣。因此種植集中在沿海：Constantia 受到南冰洋微風的降溫，而 Elgin 則因海拔而涼爽。","Which South African region, south of Cape Town, is cooled by Southern Ocean breezes?":"南非哪個位於開普敦以南的產區受到南冰洋微風的降溫？","Constantia, south of Cape Town, gives fresh, tropical and herbaceous Sauvignon.":"開普敦以南的 Constantia 出產清爽、帶熱帶水果和草本氣息的白蘇維濃。","Constantia lies south of Cape Town and is cooled by Southern Ocean breezes. It produces refreshing Sauvignon Blanc with ripe tropical fruit and herbaceous aromas. Elgin is cooled by altitude instead; Walker Bay is mainly noted here for Chardonnay. As elsewhere in the country, the coast is preferred to the hot interior.":"Constantia 位於開普敦以南，受到南冰洋微風的降溫。這裡出產令人清爽的白蘇維濃，帶有成熟的熱帶水果和草本香氣。Elgin 則是因海拔而涼爽；Walker Bay 在這裡主要以夏多內著稱。和這個國家其他地方一樣，人們偏好沿海而非炎熱的內陸。","Which region is often cited as South Africa's coolest wine region?":"哪個產區常被稱為南非最涼爽的葡萄酒產區？","Small, altitude-cooled Elgin gives Sauvignon with green apple and wet stones.":"小巧、因海拔而涼爽的 Elgin，出產帶有青蘋果和濕石頭的白蘇維濃。","Elgin is a small region cooled by altitude and often cited as South Africa's coolest wine area. Its Sauvignon Blancs typically show green fruit such as apple and sometimes wet stones, signs of a cool climate. Casablanca Valley is Chilean; the inland Western Cape is hot.":"Elgin 是因海拔而涼爽的小產區，常被稱為南非最涼爽的葡萄酒產區。它的白蘇維濃通常展現蘋果等綠色水果，有時還有濕石頭，這是涼爽氣候的跡象。Casablanca Valley 在智利；西開普內陸則很炎熱。","How is a fresh, herbaceous Sauvignon Blanc achieved in California?":"在加州，如何釀出清爽、帶草本氣息的白蘇維濃？","Cooler sites and early picking":"較涼爽的園地和提早採收","Late picking for more ripeness":"晚採以提高成熟度","Irrigation and very high yields":"灌溉和非常高的產量","Long maturation in new oak":"在新橡木桶中長時間熟成","Heat must be offset: cool sites and early harvest keep acidity and aromas.":"必須抵消高溫：涼爽園地和提早採收能保留酸度和香氣。","California is mostly too warm for the fresh, herbaceous style typical of France and New Zealand. The finest grapes therefore come from cooler areas and may be picked early to retain acidity and herbaceous aromas. Very good examples come from cooler parts of Napa Valley, sometimes oaked for body and smoky notes.":"對於法國和紐西蘭典型的清爽草本風格來說，加州大部分地方都太溫暖了。因此最好的葡萄來自較涼爽的地區，並可能提早採收以保留酸度和草本香氣。非常好的酒款來自 Napa Valley 較涼爽的地方，有時會經橡木桶以增添酒體和煙燻氣息。","What does oak add to some Napa Valley Sauvignon Blancs?":"橡木桶為某些 Napa Valley 的白蘇維濃增添什麼？","Body and smoky flavour":"酒體和煙燻風味","Acidity and herbaceous notes":"酸度和草本氣息","Floral rose aromas":"玫瑰花香","Residual sweetness":"殘留的甜味","Oak contact adds body and a smoky touch.":"與橡木接觸會增添酒體和一絲煙燻味。","Cooler parts of Napa Valley make very good Sauvignon Blanc, sometimes in contact with oak. The wood adds body and flavours such as smoke. Acidity and herbaceous notes come from the cool climate and early picking, not from oak; residual sugar plays no part.":"Napa Valley 較涼爽的地方出產非常好的白蘇維濃，有時會與橡木接觸。木頭增添酒體和煙燻等風味。酸度和草本氣息來自涼爽氣候和提早採收，不是來自橡木桶；殘糖則毫無作用。","Which label term often signals a Sauvignon Blanc that has seen oak?":"哪一個酒標術語常表示白蘇維濃經過橡木桶？","Since it is usually unoaked, oak use is flagged by terms such as barrel aged.":"由於它通常不經橡木桶，使用橡木桶時會以 barrel aged 等術語標示。","Most Sauvignon Blanc is made without oak so as not to mask its herbaceous aromas. When oak has been used, producers often say so with terms like barrel aged. Unwooded means the opposite; Vendanges tardives means late harvest in Alsace; Grand Cru is a vineyard term.":"大多數白蘇維濃不使用橡木桶，以免掩蓋它的草本香氣。使用橡木桶時，生產者常以 barrel aged 等術語說明。Unwooded 的意思正好相反；Vendanges tardives 在阿爾薩斯是晚收的意思；Grand Cru 則是葡萄園術語。","What style is a simple white Bordeaux AOC based on Sauvignon Blanc usually?":"以白蘇維濃為主的簡單 Bordeaux AOC 白酒通常是什麼風格？","Fresh, grass and green apple":"清爽、青草和青蘋果","Full, honey and nuts":"飽滿、蜂蜜和堅果","Sweet, from extra-ripe grapes":"甜，用過熟的葡萄釀造","Full, rose and lychee":"飽滿、玫瑰和荔枝","Simple Bordeaux AOC offers fresh grass and green apple aromas.":"簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 帶有清新的青草和青蘋果香氣。","In Bordeaux, Sauvignon Blanc covers many styles. Simple Bordeaux AOC has fresh grass and green apple aromas and may be single-varietal or blended with Semillon. Honey and nutty notes belong instead to the best aged Graves and Pessac-Léognan, which are more concentrated and often oak-matured.":"在波爾多，白蘇維濃涵蓋許多風格。簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 帶有清新的青草和青蘋果香氣，可能是單一品種，也可能與榭密雍混調。蜂蜜和堅果氣息則屬於最好的陳年 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan，它們更濃縮，常經橡木桶熟成。","Which flavours do less ripe grapes give to Sauvignon Blanc?":"較不成熟的葡萄為白蘇維濃帶來哪些風味？","Apple, gooseberry, grapefruit, wet stones":"蘋果、醋栗、葡萄柚、濕石頭","Peach, passion fruit and other very ripe tropical fruit":"桃子、百香果和其他非常成熟的熱帶水果","Strawberry, raspberry and red cherry":"草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃","Honey and dried fruit":"蜂蜜和果乾","Less ripe grapes give green fruit, citrus and wet stones.":"較不成熟的葡萄帶來綠色水果、柑橘和濕石頭。","Sauvignon Blanc runs from green fruit (apple, gooseberry), grapefruit and wet stones to peach and passion fruit when the grapes are riper. Red fruits belong to Pinot Noir; honey and dried fruit are tertiary or sweet-wine notes.":"白蘇維濃的風味範圍從綠色水果（蘋果、醋栗）、葡萄柚和濕石頭，到葡萄較成熟時的桃子和百香果。紅色水果屬於黑皮諾；蜂蜜和果乾則是三級香氣或甜酒的氣息。","Which structure is typical of a Sauvignon Blanc?":"哪一種結構是白蘇維濃的典型特徵？","Dry, light to medium body, high acidity":"不甜、酒體輕盈至中等、高酸度","Off-dry, full body, low acidity and high alcohol":"微甜、酒體飽滿、低酸度和高酒精","Dry, full body, medium acidity":"不甜、酒體飽滿、中等酸度","Sweet, full body, high acidity":"甜、酒體飽滿、高酸度","Sauvignon Blanc is usually dry, light to medium-bodied and very fresh.":"白蘇維濃通常不甜、酒體輕盈至中等，非常清爽。","Refreshing high acidity is its hallmark, together with herbaceous aromas. Full body and medium acidity describe a warm-climate Chardonnay instead. Sweet wines exist in blends with Semillon, but the typical Sauvignon Blanc style is dry.":"令人清爽的高酸度是它的招牌特徵，再加上草本香氣。酒體飽滿和中等酸度描述的則是溫暖氣候的夏多內。與榭密雍混調的甜酒是存在的，但白蘇維濃的典型風格是不甜的。","How can complexity be added to a Sauvignon Blanc without using oak?":"如何在不使用橡木桶的情況下為白蘇維濃增添複雜度？","By blending grapes from different sites at different ripeness levels":"混調來自不同園地、不同成熟度的葡萄","By leaving the grapes on the vine until they freeze":"把葡萄留在樹上直到結冰","By macerating the juice for a long time with black grape skins":"讓果汁與黑葡萄果皮長時間浸泡","Combining riper and less ripe grapes layers green, citrus and tropical flavours.":"結合較成熟和較不成熟的葡萄，能疊加綠色水果、柑橘和熱帶水果風味。","Sauvignon Blanc changes a lot with ripeness: blending different sites adds layers of flavour. Leaving grapes to freeze is for sweet wines, maceration with black skins would make a rosé or red, and chips are still oak.":"白蘇維濃的風味隨成熟度變化很大：混調不同園地能增添風味層次。讓葡萄結冰是釀甜酒的方法，與黑葡萄果皮浸泡會釀成粉紅酒或紅酒，而橡木片仍然是橡木。","Where are Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé in relation to each other?":"Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 彼此的相對位置如何？","Facing each other across the Loire River":"隔著羅亞爾河相望","One in the Loire and the other in Bordeaux":"一個在羅亞爾河，另一個在波爾多","Both in the Mâconnais, in southern Burgundy":"兩者都在布根地南部的 Mâconnais","Both near the Loire estuary, close to the Atlantic":"兩者都在靠近大西洋的羅亞爾河河口附近","Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé face each other across the Loire.":"Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 隔著羅亞爾河相望。","These neighbouring appellations share a cool climate and the same grape, Sauvignon Blanc, for dry, crisp wines. Pouilly-Fuissé, with its similar name, is in the Mâconnais. Touraine lies to the west, but neither appellation is near the Atlantic.":"這兩個相鄰的法定產區有相同的涼爽氣候和同一個品種——白蘇維濃，釀出不甜、爽脆的酒。名字相似的 Pouilly-Fuissé 則位於 Mâconnais。Touraine 位於西邊，但這兩個法定產區都不靠近大西洋。","A label reads 'Pouilly-Fumé'. Which grape is the wine made from?":"一張酒標上寫著「Pouilly-Fumé」。這款酒是用哪個品種釀的？","Mâconnais Chardonnay":"Mâconnais 的夏多內","A barrel-aged Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blend":"經橡木桶陳年的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調","In Pouilly-Fumé, Sauvignon Blanc is the only white grape allowed.":"在 Pouilly-Fumé，白蘇維濃是唯一允許的白葡萄品種。","Many European appellations do not name the grape, so you need to know the rules. Pouilly-Fumé is a Loire white made only from Sauvignon Blanc. Chardonnay is Pouilly-Fuissé; the Semillon blend is typical of Graves and Pessac-Léognan.":"許多歐洲法定產區不標示品種，所以你需要了解法規。Pouilly-Fumé 是只用白蘇維濃釀造的羅亞爾河白酒。夏多內是 Pouilly-Fuissé；與榭密雍的混調則是 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 的典型特徵。","Where do the grapes for a Touraine AOC Sauvignon Blanc come from?":"Touraine AOC 白蘇維濃的葡萄來自哪裡？","From the wider Touraine area, west of Sancerre":"來自 Sancerre 以西更廣大的 Touraine 地區","Only from the steepest slopes of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé":"只來自 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 最陡的坡地","From high-altitude Languedoc-Roussillon vineyards":"來自 Languedoc-Roussillon 的高海拔葡萄園","From the Graves area":"來自 Graves 地區","Touraine AOC covers a broad Loire sub-region west of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé.":"Touraine AOC 涵蓋 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 以西廣大的羅亞爾河子產區。","As a broader area, Touraine gives fruity, inexpensive Sauvignons, less sought after than Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé. High southern vineyards give Pays d'Oc IGP, and Graves is in Bordeaux.":"作為較廣大的區域，Touraine 出產果香豐富、價格平實的白蘇維濃，不如 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 搶手。南部的高海拔葡萄園出產 Pays d'Oc IGP，而 Graves 位於波爾多。","What can a simple white labelled Bordeaux AOC contain?":"標示 Bordeaux AOC 的簡單白酒可以包含什麼？","Sauvignon Blanc alone, or Sauvignon Blanc with Semillon":"只有白蘇維濃，或白蘇維濃加榭密雍","Only Chardonnay":"只有夏多內","A blend that must contain at least half Riesling":"必須含有至少一半麗絲玲的混調","Only botrytised Semillon, always sweet":"只有貴腐榭密雍，一定是甜的","White Bordeaux AOC can be a pure Sauvignon or a blend with Semillon.":"Bordeaux AOC 白酒可以是純白蘇維濃，也可以與榭密雍混調。","Simple white Bordeaux AOC is fresh, with grass and green apple, from Sauvignon alone or with Semillon. Chardonnay and Riesling are not Bordeaux grapes. Botrytised Semillon is typical of Sauternes, a different appellation.":"簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 白酒很清爽，帶有青草和青蘋果，以白蘇維濃單獨或與榭密雍一起釀造。夏多內和麗絲玲不是波爾多的品種。貴腐榭密雍是 Sauternes 的典型特徵，那是另一個法定產區。","Compared with a simple white Bordeaux AOC, what are Graves and Pessac-Léognan whites like?":"與簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 白酒相比，Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 白酒是什麼樣子？","More concentrated and complex":"更濃縮、更複雜","Lighter and meant to be drunk within months of the harvest":"更輕盈，要在採收後幾個月內喝掉","Always sweet":"一定是甜的","Made only in steel, with no Semillon and no oak at all":"只在不鏽鋼槽中釀造，完全沒有榭密雍也沒有橡木桶","Graves and Pessac-Léognan give more concentrated, complex whites, often oak-matured.":"Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 出產更濃縮、更複雜的白酒，常經橡木桶熟成。","They are usually Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blends; the best see oak and develop honey and nuts in bottle. They are not wines for immediate drinking, not sweet by definition, and Semillon is often part of them.":"它們通常是白蘇維濃與榭密雍的混調；最好的酒款經過橡木桶，在瓶中會發展出蜂蜜和堅果。它們不是要立刻喝的酒，按定義也不是甜酒，而且常常含有榭密雍。","Which profile does a typical Pays d'Oc IGP Sauvignon Blanc have?":"典型的 Pays d'Oc IGP 白蘇維濃有什麼風味特徵？","Dry, high acidity, passion fruit and grass":"不甜、高酸度、百香果和青草","Sweet, with honey and apricot":"甜，帶有蜂蜜和杏桃","Full body and low acidity, with strong vanilla and coconut":"酒體飽滿、低酸度，帶有強烈的香草和椰子","Light red":"淡紅酒","The higher, cooler parts of southern France give a dry, fresh, tropical and grassy Sauvignon.":"法國南部較高、較涼爽的地方出產不甜、清爽、帶熱帶水果和青草的白蘇維濃。","Much of Languedoc-Roussillon is too warm for this grape, but altitude keeps the acidity. The result combines passion fruit with grassy notes. It is neither a sweet wine nor a fat, oaky white.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 大部分地方對這個品種來說太溫暖，但海拔能保留酸度。結果結合了百香果和青草氣息。它既不是甜酒，也不是肥厚、橡木味重的白酒。","Where is the Marlborough region?":"Marlborough 產區在哪裡？","In the north-east of New Zealand's South Island":"在紐西蘭南島的東北部","On the east coast of New Zealand's North Island":"在紐西蘭北島的東岸","In Western Australia":"在西澳","In the south of the South Island, ringed by mountains":"在南島南部，四周群山環繞","Marlborough lies in the north-eastern part of the South Island.":"Marlborough 位於南島的東北部。","It is a cool region now closely linked with Sauvignon Blanc. The North Island's east coast is Hawke's Bay; the mountainous south of the South Island is Central Otago; Margaret River is in Western Australia.":"這是一個涼爽產區，現在與白蘇維濃密不可分。北島東岸是 Hawke's Bay；南島多山的南部是 Central Otago；Margaret River 則在西澳。","What generally distinguishes a Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc from a Loire one?":"一般來說，Marlborough 的白蘇維濃與羅亞爾河的有什麼不同？","More pronounced characteristics":"特徵更鮮明","Much lower acidity and a heavier body":"酸度低得多，酒體更厚重","Compulsory maturation in new oak for at least a year":"規定必須在新橡木桶中熟成至少一年","Strong wet-stone notes":"強烈的濕石頭氣息","Marlborough Sauvignon is usually more intense and aromatic than Loire Sauvignon.":"Marlborough 的白蘇維濃通常比羅亞爾河的更濃烈、更芳香。","Marlborough shows grapefruit, peach, passion fruit and very marked green pepper. Both styles have high acidity. Wet stones are more typical of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé, and there is no oak requirement.":"Marlborough 展現葡萄柚、桃子、百香果和非常明顯的青椒。兩種風格都有高酸度。濕石頭更是 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 的典型特徵，也沒有橡木桶的規定。","A Marlborough producer wants a Sauvignon closer in style to Sancerre. What will they do?":"一位 Marlborough 的生產者想要風格更接近 Sancerre 的白蘇維濃。他會怎麼做？","Use grapes from cooler vineyard sites":"使用較涼爽葡萄園的葡萄","Pick riper grapes to boost tropical fruit":"採收更成熟的葡萄以增強熱帶水果","Ferment in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中發酵","Add unfermented juice to leave some sweetness":"加入未發酵的葡萄汁以保留一些甜味","Cooler sites give less tropical fruit, closer to the Loire style.":"較涼爽的園地帶來較少的熱帶水果，更接近羅亞爾河的風格。","Sancerre is dry, with green apple, grass and sometimes wet stones. Riper grapes would go the opposite way, new oak would hide the herbaceous aromas, and residual sugar does not match the dry Loire style.":"Sancerre 不甜，帶有青蘋果、青草，有時還有濕石頭。較成熟的葡萄會往相反方向走，新橡木桶會掩蓋草本香氣，而殘糖也不符合羅亞爾河不甜的風格。","Which statement about Adelaide Hills Sauvignon Blanc is correct?":"關於 Adelaide Hills 的白蘇維濃，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Most are fresh and fruity, from citrus to tropical fruit":"大多清爽、果香豐富，從柑橘到熱帶水果都有","Almost all are sweet, from late-harvested grapes":"幾乎都是用晚收葡萄釀的甜酒","They come from hot, irrigated inland plains":"它們來自炎熱、經灌溉的內陸平原","They are never blended with Semillon":"它們從不與榭密雍混調","Cooled by altitude, Adelaide Hills gives fresh Sauvignons with fruit from citrus to tropical.":"因海拔而涼爽的 Adelaide Hills，出產果味從柑橘到熱帶水果的清爽白蘇維濃。","Sauvignon Blanc is the area's most planted grape. Some wines are blended with Semillon for more body and ageing potential, so 'never' is wrong. They are not sweet and do not come from hot plains.":"白蘇維濃是這個地區種植最多的品種。有些酒會與榭密雍混調以增添酒體和陳年潛力，所以「從不」是錯的。它們不是甜酒，也不是來自炎熱的平原。","Why do some Adelaide Hills producers add Semillon to Sauvignon Blanc?":"為什麼有些 Adelaide Hills 的生產者會在白蘇維濃中加入榭密雍？","For more body and greater ageing potential":"為了更飽滿的酒體和更強的陳年潛力","To boost green-pepper aromas":"為了增強青椒香氣","To lower the alcohol level":"為了降低酒精濃度","To give the wine a pink tint that looks better on the shelf":"為了讓酒帶點粉紅色調，在貨架上更好看","Semillon adds body and helps the wine age.":"榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。","Semillon plays the same role as in Bordeaux: it makes the wine fuller and longer-lived. It does not strengthen the herbaceous aromas, which come from Sauvignon, and it does not lower alcohol. It is a white grape, so it gives no pink colour.":"榭密雍扮演的角色和在波爾多一樣：讓酒更飽滿、壽命更長。它不會增強來自白蘇維濃的草本香氣，也不會降低酒精。它是白葡萄，所以不會帶來粉紅色。","A Margaret River Sauvignon Blanc–Semillon blend: what should you expect?":"一款 Margaret River 的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調：你應該預期什麼？","Concentrated grassy aromas; sometimes oak contact":"濃縮的青草香氣；有時與橡木接觸","A sweet botrytised wine with honey, apricot and caramel":"帶有蜂蜜、杏桃和焦糖的貴腐甜酒","A neutral, light wine from very early-picked grapes":"用非常早採的葡萄釀造的中性輕盈酒款","Red fruit and soft tannins":"紅色水果和柔和的單寧","Margaret River is known for Sauvignon–Semillon blends with concentrated grassy notes, sometimes with oak contact.":"Margaret River 以帶有濃縮青草氣息的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調著稱，有時與橡木接觸。","These dry blends show intense grassiness and, in some cases, a touch of oak. Sweet botrytised wine is typical of Sauternes; neutral early-picked Semillon describes Hunter Valley. Red fruit and tannins point to a red.":"這些不甜的混調展現濃烈的青草味，有些還帶一絲橡木味。貴腐甜酒是 Sauternes 的典型特徵；中性的早採榭密雍描述的是 Hunter Valley。紅色水果和單寧則指向紅酒。","What range of quality does Chile's Central Valley Sauvignon Blanc offer?":"智利 Central Valley 的白蘇維濃提供什麼樣的品質範圍？","From inexpensive high-volume brands to very good examples":"從平價的大量生產品牌到非常好的酒款","Only very expensive wines from tiny plots":"只有來自極小地塊、非常昂貴的酒","Only sweet wines":"只有甜酒","None: the area is too cold to ripen Sauvignon Blanc":"沒有：這個地區太冷，白蘇維濃無法成熟","The large Central Valley makes Sauvignon at every level, from brands to very good wines.":"廣大的 Central Valley 出產各個等級的白蘇維濃，從品牌酒到非常好的酒款都有。","The Central Valley is larger and warmer than coastal Casablanca Valley, known for very good quality. Its size is exactly what explains the range of levels. It is not too cold (it is warm) and does not specialise in sweet wines.":"Central Valley 比以非常好的品質著稱的沿海 Casablanca Valley 更大、更溫暖。正是它的面積解釋了等級的多樣。它並不太冷（它很溫暖），也不專門生產甜酒。","What style of Sauvignon Blanc does Constantia produce?":"Constantia 出產什麼風格的白蘇維濃？","Refreshing, with ripe tropical fruit and herbaceous notes":"令人清爽，帶有成熟的熱帶水果和草本氣息","Neutral, with apple and wet stones":"中性，帶有蘋果和濕石頭","Sweet and botrytised, made for long cellaring":"甜型貴腐酒，適合長期窖藏","Heavily oaked, with vanilla":"橡木味很重，帶有香草","Southern Ocean breezes cool Constantia: fresh, tropical and herbaceous Sauvignon.":"南冰洋的微風讓 Constantia 降溫：清爽、帶熱帶水果和草本氣息的白蘇維濃。","Constantia, south of Cape Town, combines ripe tropical fruit and herbaceous notes in refreshing wines. Apple and wet stones are more typical of cooler Elgin. It is neither a sweet nor a heavily oaked style.":"開普敦以南的 Constantia，在令人清爽的酒中結合了成熟的熱帶水果和草本氣息。蘋果和濕石頭更是較涼爽的 Elgin 的典型特徵。它既不是甜型風格，也不是橡木味很重的風格。","A South African Sauvignon Blanc tastes of green apple and wet stones. Which area does it most likely come from?":"一款南非白蘇維濃嚐起來有青蘋果和濕石頭。它最可能來自哪個地區？","The hot inland vineyards of the Western Cape":"西開普炎熱的內陸葡萄園","Elgin, cooled by altitude, gives Sauvignons with green apple and sometimes wet stones.":"因海拔而涼爽的 Elgin，出產帶有青蘋果、有時帶濕石頭的白蘇維濃。","Elgin is often cited as South Africa's coolest region, hence the green fruit. Constantia gives a more tropical style; inland vineyards are generally too warm for Sauvignon. Stellenbosch is known mainly for reds.":"Elgin 常被稱為南非最涼爽的產區，因此有綠色水果。Constantia 的風格更具熱帶水果味；內陸葡萄園對白蘇維濃來說一般太溫暖。Stellenbosch 則主要以紅酒著稱。","What cools Elgin, compared with Constantia?":"與 Constantia 相比，是什麼讓 Elgin 涼爽？","Altitude; Constantia is cooled by sea breezes":"海拔；Constantia 則因海風而涼爽","Morning fog from a bay; Constantia by altitude":"來自海灣的晨霧；Constantia 則因海拔而涼爽","A mountain range that blocks rain; Constantia by a cold current":"阻擋雨水的山脈；Constantia 則因寒冷洋流而涼爽","Nothing: both are warm":"沒有：兩者都很溫暖","Elgin is cool because of altitude, Constantia because of Southern Ocean breezes.":"Elgin 因海拔而涼爽，Constantia 則因南冰洋的微風而涼爽。","Two nearby areas, two different influences: altitude makes Elgin the coolest and gives green fruit; the sea cools Constantia, which keeps more tropical fruit. Both are coastal and cool, not warm like the interior.":"兩個相鄰的地區，兩種不同的影響：海拔讓 Elgin 成為最涼爽的地區，帶來綠色水果；海洋讓 Constantia 降溫，保留較多熱帶水果。兩者都是涼爽的沿海地區，不像內陸那樣溫暖。","Why does much of California struggle to make the classic fresh, herbaceous Sauvignon?":"為什麼加州大部分地區難以釀出經典的清爽草本風格白蘇維濃？","The climate is mostly too warm":"氣候大多太溫暖","The climate is too cold and wet":"氣候太冷太濕","The law forbids single-varietal Sauvignon Blanc":"法律禁止單一品種的白蘇維濃","Chalky soils stop the grapes from developing herbaceous aromas":"白堊土讓葡萄無法發展出草本香氣","Heat strips acidity and herbaceous aromas, so cooler areas and early picking are needed.":"高溫會奪走酸度和草本香氣，所以需要較涼爽的地區和提早採收。","Sauvignon Blanc prefers cool and moderate climates. In California the best come from the cooler areas, such as parts of Napa Valley, with early picking. Cold, legal bans or soils are not the causes.":"白蘇維濃偏好涼爽和溫和的氣候。在加州，最好的酒來自較涼爽的地區，例如 Napa Valley 的部分地方，並提早採收。寒冷、法律禁令或土壤都不是原因。","Why are some Sauvignon Blanc producers experimenting beyond the classic style?":"為什麼有些白蘇維濃生產者會在經典風格之外進行嘗試？","They fear consumers may tire of intense herbaceous aromas":"他們擔心消費者可能對濃烈的草本香氣感到厭倦","The grape has become unpopular and sales are collapsing everywhere":"這個品種已經不受歡迎，各地銷量都在崩跌","New laws require oak":"新法律規定必須使用橡木桶","The climate has become too cold":"氣候變得太冷","The style is so recognisable that some producers look for points of difference to keep it interesting.":"這種風格太容易辨識，有些生產者尋找差異點來保持新鮮感。","Sauvignon Blanc is very popular today, almost like a trusted brand: that is exactly why some fear fatigue. Sales are not collapsing and oak is not compulsory; using wood or lees is a choice.":"白蘇維濃現在非常受歡迎，幾乎像一個值得信賴的品牌：正是因此有人擔心消費者會厭倦。銷量並沒有崩跌，橡木桶也不是強制的；使用木桶或酒渣是一種選擇。","A customer opens a simple, unoaked Sauvignon Blanc from four years ago. What will they most likely find?":"一位顧客打開一瓶四年前的簡單、未經橡木桶的白蘇維濃。他最可能發現什麼？","Faded fresh aromas and unattractive vegetal notes":"清新香氣已經消退，出現不討喜的植物性氣息","Complex honey, hazelnut and dried-fruit notes, like a great aged white":"複雜的蜂蜜、榛果和果乾氣息，就像偉大的陳年白酒","More fresh tropical fruit":"更多新鮮的熱帶水果","Forest-floor and mushroom aromas":"森林地表和蘑菇香氣","Sauvignon Blanc is for drinking young: after a couple of years it loses freshness and turns vegetal.":"白蘇維濃要趁年輕喝：一兩年後就會失去清新感，變得有植物味。","Only some oaked Semillon blends from Graves or Pessac-Léognan develop honey and nuts. A simple, unoaked Sauvignon instead loses its fresh aromas. Fruit does not increase with time, and forest floor and mushroom are typical of reds such as aged Pinot Noir.":"只有一些來自 Graves 或 Pessac-Léognan、經橡木桶的榭密雍混調會發展出蜂蜜和堅果。簡單、未經橡木桶的白蘇維濃反而會失去清新的香氣。果味不會隨時間增加，而森林地表和蘑菇是陳年黑皮諾等紅酒的典型特徵。","Which of these regions is NOT known for South African Sauvignon Blanc?":"下列哪一個產區不以南非白蘇維濃著稱？","The coastal areas near Cape Town":"開普敦附近的沿海地區","Casablanca Valley is in Chile, not South Africa.":"Casablanca Valley 在智利，不在南非。","Casablanca Valley is also known for very good Sauvignon Blanc, but it is a Chilean coastal area cooled by Pacific breezes and fog. In South Africa, Sauvignon is concentrated on the coast: Constantia, south of Cape Town, and Elgin.":"Casablanca Valley 也以非常好的白蘇維濃著稱，但它是智利的沿海地區，受到太平洋微風和霧氣的降溫。在南非，白蘇維濃集中在沿海：開普敦以南的 Constantia 以及 Elgin。","Two Sauvignon Blancs: one with green apple, grass and wet stones, the other with grapefruit, passion fruit and intense green pepper. Which origins are most likely?":"兩款白蘇維濃：一款帶有青蘋果、青草和濕石頭，另一款帶有葡萄柚、百香果和濃烈的青椒。最可能的產地是什麼？","The first Sancerre, the second Marlborough":"第一款是 Sancerre，第二款是 Marlborough","The first Marlborough, the second Sancerre":"第一款是 Marlborough，第二款是 Sancerre","Both Pessac-Léognan, but from different vintages and oak regimes":"兩款都是 Pessac-Léognan，但年份和橡木桶處理不同","The first Constantia, the second Touraine":"第一款是 Constantia，第二款是 Touraine","The restrained wet-stone style is Loire; the explosive tropical, green-pepper style is Marlborough.":"內斂、帶濕石頭的風格是羅亞爾河；熱帶水果和青椒奔放的風格是 Marlborough。","Sancerre is cool: green apple, grass, asparagus and sometimes wet stones. Marlborough blends grapes from different sites and ripeness levels, with grapefruit, peach, passion fruit and pronounced green pepper. Constantia is tropical and Touraine fruity and simple, so the last pairing does not fit.":"Sancerre 很涼爽：青蘋果、青草、蘆筍，有時還有濕石頭。Marlborough 混調來自不同園地和成熟度的葡萄，帶有葡萄柚、桃子、百香果和鮮明的青椒。Constantia 帶熱帶水果味，Touraine 果香豐富但簡單，所以最後一個組合不符合。","A label reads 'Pessac-Léognan blanc'. Which grapes does it most likely contain?":"一張酒標上寫著「Pessac-Léognan blanc」。它最可能含有哪些品種？","Chardonnay and Pinot Gris":"夏多內和灰皮諾","Only Sauvignon Blanc, by law, as in Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé":"依法只能用白蘇維濃，就像 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé","Riesling and Chenin Blanc":"麗絲玲和白梢楠","Pessac-Léognan whites are usually Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blends.":"Pessac-Léognan 白酒通常是白蘇維濃與榭密雍的混調。","As in Graves, Semillon adds body and longevity to Sauvignon and the best wines see oak. The Sauvignon-only rule applies to Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé, not Bordeaux. Chardonnay, Pinot Gris, Riesling and Chenin are not grapes of this area.":"和 Graves 一樣，榭密雍為白蘇維濃增添酒體和陳年潛力，最好的酒款會經過橡木桶。只能用白蘇維濃的規定適用於 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé，不適用於波爾多。夏多內、灰皮諾、麗絲玲和白梢楠都不是這個地區的品種。","Which statement about Sauvignon Blanc is FALSE?":"關於白蘇維濃，下列哪一項敘述是錯誤的？","It performs best in warm climates":"它在溫暖氣候中表現最好","It is considered a French variety":"它被視為法國品種","It is usually made without oak":"它通常不使用橡木桶","It is usually best young, while still fresh and highly aromatic":"它通常最好趁年輕喝，那時仍清爽且香氣濃郁","Sauvignon Blanc performs best in cool and moderate climates, not warm ones.":"白蘇維濃在涼爽和溫和氣候中表現最好，而不是溫暖氣候。","Heat strips Sauvignon of acidity and herbaceous aromas: in warm areas it needs altitude, breezes or early picking. The other statements are true: it is considered French, is now grown worldwide, is mostly unoaked and is best drunk young.":"高溫會奪走白蘇維濃的酸度和草本香氣：在溫暖地區，它需要海拔、微風或提早採收。其他敘述都是正確的：它被視為法國品種，現在種植於世界各地，大多不經橡木桶，最好趁年輕喝。","Which climate does Riesling prefer?":"麗絲玲偏好哪種氣候？","Cool to moderate":"涼爽至溫和","Moderate to hot":"溫和至炎熱","Riesling is a cold-hardy grape that prefers cool to moderate climates.":"麗絲玲是耐寒的品種，偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候。","Riesling copes well with cold and prefers cool to moderate climates, where the grapes ripen slowly and keep their high natural acidity. It does best in cool, dry, sunny regions such as the Mosel, Rheingau, Alsace or Australia's higher-altitude Clare and Eden Valleys. A hot climate would cost it freshness and aromatic finesse.":"麗絲玲很能耐寒，偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候，在那裡葡萄成熟緩慢，保留高天然酸度。它在涼爽、乾燥、陽光充足的產區表現最好，例如 Mosel、Rheingau、阿爾薩斯，或澳洲海拔較高的 Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley。炎熱的氣候會讓它失去清新感和細緻的香氣。","Why can Riesling make outstanding wines at every sweetness level?":"為什麼麗絲玲在每一種甜度都能釀出傑出的酒？","High natural acidity and susceptibility to botrytis":"高天然酸度，以及容易感染貴腐菌","Thick skins and high tannins":"厚果皮和高單寧","Low acidity and high alcohol":"低酸度和高酒精","Fast ripening and high yields":"成熟快速和高產量","Acidity balances sweetness, and botrytis concentrates grapes for sweet styles.":"酸度平衡甜度，而貴腐菌為甜型風格濃縮葡萄。","Riesling has high natural acidity that persists even when the grapes are very ripe. That acidity keeps dry wines fresh and balances the sugar in sweet wines perfectly. The grape is also susceptible to botrytis, which concentrates sugars, acidity and flavours and allows great sweet wines such as Beerenauslese and Trockenbeerenauslese.":"麗絲玲有高天然酸度，即使葡萄非常成熟時依然存在。這種酸度讓不甜的酒保持清爽，也完美平衡甜酒中的糖分。這個品種也容易感染貴腐菌，貴腐菌會濃縮糖分、酸度和風味，造就 Beerenauslese 和 Trockenbeerenauslese 等偉大的甜酒。","Which aromas do just-ripe Riesling grapes usually give?":"剛成熟的麗絲玲葡萄通常帶來哪些香氣？","Green apple, lemon, lime, blossom":"青蘋果、檸檬、萊姆、花香","Mango, pineapple, dried apricot":"芒果、鳳梨、杏桃乾","Honey, petrol, dried fruit":"蜂蜜、汽油、果乾","Just-ripe grapes give green fruit, citrus and blossom.":"剛成熟的葡萄帶來綠色水果、柑橘和花香。","Riesling's aromas follow ripeness. With just-ripe grapes, green fruit such as apple and pear, citrus such as lemon and lime, and floral notes dominate. With extra-ripe grapes, peach, apricot, mango, pineapple and sometimes dried fruit appear. Honey and petrol, by contrast, are tertiary aromas that come with bottle age.":"麗絲玲的香氣隨成熟度變化。葡萄剛成熟時，以蘋果和梨等綠色水果、檸檬和萊姆等柑橘以及花香為主。葡萄過熟時，會出現桃子、杏桃、芒果、鳳梨，有時還有果乾。相反地，蜂蜜和汽油是瓶中陳年後才出現的三級香氣。","Which aromas point to a Riesling made from extra-ripe grapes?":"哪些香氣表示麗絲玲是用過熟的葡萄釀造的？","Peach, apricot, mango, pineapple":"桃子、杏桃、芒果、鳳梨","Green apple, pear, lemon":"青蘋果、梨、檸檬","Grass, green pepper, gooseberry":"青草、青椒、醋栗","Forest floor, mushroom, earth":"森林地表、蘑菇、泥土","Extra-ripe grapes bring stone and tropical fruit, sometimes dried fruit.":"過熟的葡萄帶來核果和熱帶水果，有時還有果乾。","When Riesling is picked extra-ripe, its aromas shift from green fruit and citrus to stone fruit (peach, apricot) and tropical fruit (mango, pineapple). In the most extreme cases, dried-fruit notes such as dried apricot appear too. These aromas are typical of Spätlese, Auslese and concentrated sweet styles.":"麗絲玲在過熟時採收，香氣會從綠色水果和柑橘轉向核果（桃子、杏桃）和熱帶水果（芒果、鳳梨）。在最極端的情況下，也會出現杏桃乾等果乾氣息。這些香氣是 Spätlese、Auslese 和濃縮甜型風格的典型特徵。","Why is Riesling suited to late harvesting?":"為什麼麗絲玲適合晚收？","It keeps its acidity and builds sugar slowly":"它能保留酸度，糖分累積緩慢","Its thick skins resist autumn rain":"它的厚果皮能抵抗秋雨","It loses acidity quickly late in the season":"它在季末會迅速失去酸度","It ripens very early in summer":"它在夏天很早就成熟","Riesling stays acidic while sugar and flavour build slowly, given a dry, sunny autumn.":"麗絲玲保持酸度，糖分和風味緩慢累積，前提是秋天乾燥晴朗。","Riesling builds sugar and flavour slowly without losing its acidity. In regions with dry, sunny autumns, the grapes can therefore hang on the vine for a long time and concentrate. The result is richer, often sweet wines that stay fresh thanks to their acidity. A grape that lost acidity quickly would give heavy, unbalanced sweet wines instead.":"麗絲玲緩慢累積糖分和風味，卻不會失去酸度。因此在秋天乾燥晴朗的產區，葡萄可以在樹上掛很久並濃縮。結果是更豐潤、常常是甜的酒，因為酸度而保持清爽。迅速失去酸度的品種，則會釀出沉重、失衡的甜酒。","Unfermented grape juice added to the wine":"加入酒中的未發酵葡萄汁","Yeast added to restart fermentation":"加入酵母以重新啟動發酵","Wine aged in wooden barrels":"在木桶中陳年的酒","Süssreserve is unfermented juice used to sweeten off-dry or medium Riesling.":"Süssreserve 是用來為微甜或半甜麗絲玲增甜的未發酵葡萄汁。","Off-dry and medium Riesling styles can be made in two ways. The first is to stop fermentation by removing the yeasts, which leaves sugar and lower alcohol. The second is to add a small amount of unfermented grape juice, called Süssreserve, to a dry wine, bringing sweetness and fresh grape flavour.":"微甜和半甜的麗絲玲風格可以用兩種方式釀造。第一種是去除酵母以中止發酵，留下糖分，酒精也較低。第二種是在不甜的酒中加入少量未發酵的葡萄汁，稱為 Süssreserve，帶來甜味和新鮮的葡萄風味。","What happens when a Riesling fermentation is stopped by removing the yeasts?":"以去除酵母的方式中止麗絲玲的發酵，會發生什麼？","Residual sugar remains and alcohol is lower":"留下殘糖，酒精較低","The wine becomes dry and higher in alcohol":"酒變得不甜，酒精較高","Acidity falls and the colour darkens":"酸度下降，顏色變深","The wine develops honey and petrol notes":"酒發展出蜂蜜和汽油氣息","Without yeasts, some sugar is never turned into alcohol: sweeter, lower-alcohol wine.":"沒有酵母，部分糖分永遠不會轉化為酒精：酒更甜、酒精更低。","During fermentation, yeasts turn the sugar in the juice into alcohol. If they are removed before they finish, some sugar stays in the wine as residual sugar and the alcohol level remains lower. This is one of the methods used to make off-dry and medium Rieslings, alongside adding Süssreserve.":"發酵期間，酵母把果汁中的糖轉化為酒精。如果在它們完成之前就被去除，部分糖分會以殘糖的形式留在酒中，酒精濃度也較低。這是釀造微甜和半甜麗絲玲的方法之一，另一種是加入 Süssreserve。","Why does fermentation stop naturally in the sweetest Riesling styles?":"為什麼在最甜的麗絲玲風格中，發酵會自然停止？","The juice is too sugary for the yeasts":"果汁對酵母來說太甜了","Alcohol is added during fermentation":"發酵期間加入了酒精","It is fermented in new oak barrels":"在新橡木桶中發酵","Süssreserve is added to the juice":"在果汁中加入 Süssreserve","With extra-ripe grapes, sugar is so high that yeasts cannot ferment it all.":"用過熟的葡萄時，糖分高到酵母無法全部發酵。","The sweetest Riesling styles come from extra-ripe grapes, often concentrated by late harvesting, botrytis or freezing. The juice contains so much sugar that yeasts cannot convert it all into alcohol, and fermentation stops on its own. The wines therefore stay sweet and low in alcohol, balanced by high acidity.":"最甜的麗絲玲風格來自過熟的葡萄，常經由晚收、貴腐或冰凍而濃縮。果汁含有大量的糖，酵母無法把它全部轉化為酒精，發酵就自行停止。因此這些酒保持甜美、酒精低，並以高酸度平衡。","Why is Riesling usually fermented in stainless steel?":"為什麼麗絲玲通常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵？","To preserve its floral aromas":"為了保留它的花香","To add vanilla and smoke notes":"為了增添香草和煙燻氣息","To soften the tannins":"為了讓單寧變柔和","To encourage oxidation":"為了促進氧化","Inert vessels add no flavour and protect Riesling's aromatic character.":"惰性容器不會增添風味，能保護麗絲玲的芳香特色。","Riesling is an aromatic grape whose appeal lies in its fruit and floral aromas. That is why inert vessels such as stainless steel are used: they add no oak flavours and protect the fruit. Vanilla and smoke notes would come from oak, and as a white wine, Riesling has no significant tannins to soften.":"麗絲玲是芳香型品種，魅力在於果香和花香。這就是為什麼使用不鏽鋼槽等惰性容器：它們不會增添橡木風味，能保護果味。香草和煙燻氣息會來自橡木桶，而麗絲玲作為白酒，沒有明顯的單寧需要柔化。","Which tertiary aromas does a fine aged Riesling develop?":"優質的陳年麗絲玲會發展出哪些三級香氣？","Honey and petrol":"蜂蜜和汽油","Earth and meat":"泥土和肉","Vanilla and coffee":"香草和咖啡","With age, Riesling develops honey and petrol while acidity keeps it fresh.":"隨著陳年，麗絲玲發展出蜂蜜和汽油，而酸度讓它保持清爽。","The finest Rieslings can age for years or decades. Over time they develop complex tertiary aromas of honey and petrol, while high acidity keeps them fresh. Forest floor and mushroom are typical of aged Pinot Noir, earth and meat of old-vine Zinfandel, and vanilla and coffee come from oak.":"最優質的麗絲玲可以陳年數年甚至數十年。隨著時間，它們會發展出蜂蜜和汽油的複雜三級香氣，而高酸度讓它們保持清爽。森林地表和蘑菇是陳年黑皮諾的典型特徵，泥土和肉是老藤金芬黛的典型特徵，香草和咖啡則來自橡木桶。","Which style is typical of a Mosel Riesling?":"哪一種風格是 Mosel 麗絲玲的典型特徵？","Light body, medium sweetness, very high acidity":"酒體輕盈、半甜、酸度非常高","Full body, dry, low acidity":"酒體飽滿、不甜、低酸度","Medium body, dry, new-oak notes":"酒體中等、不甜、帶新橡木桶氣息","Full body, sweet, low acidity":"酒體飽滿、甜、低酸度","Its northerly latitude makes Mosel Riesling light, with sweetness balancing very high acidity.":"偏北的緯度讓 Mosel 麗絲玲輕盈，以甜度平衡非常高的酸度。","The Mosel is one of Germany's most northerly wine regions. The cool climate gives grapes with very high acidity and wines lighter in body than those from further south. To balance that acidity, many Mosel Rieslings have medium sweetness. The Rheingau and Pfalz, warmer and sunnier, give drier, fuller-bodied wines instead.":"Mosel 是德國最北的葡萄酒產區之一。涼爽的氣候讓葡萄酸度非常高，酒體也比更南方的酒輕盈。為了平衡這樣的酸度，許多 Mosel 麗絲玲是半甜的。更溫暖、陽光更充足的 Rheingau 和 Pfalz 則出產更不甜、酒體更飽滿的酒。","What helps grapes ripen in the best Mosel vineyards?":"在 Mosel 最好的葡萄園中，是什麼幫助葡萄成熟？","Steep south-facing slopes, stony soils and light reflected off the river":"朝南的陡坡、多石的土壤和河面反射的光線","Flat valley floors and deep clay soils":"平坦的谷底和深厚的黏土","Morning fogs and ocean breezes":"晨霧和海風","High altitude and warm nights":"高海拔和溫暖的夜晚","Southerly aspect, heat-holding stones and river-reflected light all aid ripening.":"朝南的坡向、能保溫的石頭和河面反射的光線都有助於成熟。","In the cool Mosel, every source of warmth counts. The best vineyards are planted on very steep south- or south-west-facing slopes along the river. The aspect increases the sunlight received, the stony soils aid ripening, and the river reflects sunlight back onto the vines. This lets the grapes ripen despite the northerly latitude.":"在涼爽的 Mosel，每一點熱源都很重要。最好的葡萄園種在沿河、朝南或西南的非常陡峭的坡地上。坡向增加了接收的日照，多石的土壤有助於成熟，而河流把陽光反射回葡萄樹上。這讓葡萄儘管緯度偏北也能成熟。","How do Rheingau Rieslings differ from Mosel Rieslings?":"Rheingau 的麗絲玲與 Mosel 的麗絲玲有什麼不同？","They are drier and fuller-bodied":"更不甜，酒體更飽滿","They are sweeter and lighter":"更甜、更輕盈","They are more tannic and new-oaked":"單寧更多，經新橡木桶","They are always made from frozen grapes":"總是用冰凍的葡萄釀造","South-facing slopes on the Rhine's north bank give drier, fuller Rieslings than the Mosel.":"萊茵河北岸的朝南坡地，釀出比 Mosel 更不甜、更飽滿的麗絲玲。","In the Rheingau, vineyards lie on steep south-facing slopes on the north bank of the Rhine to make the most of sun and warmth. The grapes ripen more fully, and the wines are generally drier and fuller-bodied than in the Mosel, where the more northerly climate gives light Rieslings, often with medium sweetness.":"在 Rheingau，葡萄園位於萊茵河北岸朝南的陡坡上，以充分利用陽光和熱量。葡萄成熟得更充分，酒一般比 Mosel 更不甜、酒體更飽滿；Mosel 較偏北的氣候則帶來輕盈、常常是半甜的麗絲玲。","Which German region, sheltered by mountains to the west, is seen as a climatic extension of Alsace?":"德國哪個產區西邊受山脈屏障，被視為阿爾薩斯氣候的延伸？","The Pfalz, near the French border, is dry and sunny like Alsace and makes dry Rieslings.":"靠近法國邊境的 Pfalz 像阿爾薩斯一樣乾燥晴朗，出產不甜的麗絲玲。","The Pfalz lies towards the French border and is sheltered by mountains to the west, giving it a dry, sunny climate. It is therefore seen almost as a climatic extension of Alsace, and its wines are similar in style: a typical Pfalz Riesling is dry and medium-bodied. The Mosel and Rheingau are other German regions, while Clare Valley is in Australia.":"Pfalz 位於靠近法國邊境的地方，西邊受山脈屏障，氣候乾燥晴朗。因此它幾乎被視為阿爾薩斯氣候的延伸，酒的風格也相似：典型的 Pfalz 麗絲玲不甜、酒體中等。Mosel 和 Rheingau 是德國的其他產區，而 Clare Valley 在澳洲。","Why is Alsace one of the driest and sunniest wine regions in France?":"為什麼阿爾薩斯是法國最乾燥、陽光最充足的葡萄酒產區之一？","The Vosges shelter it from rainy westerly winds":"孚日山脈為它擋住多雨的西風","Rhine fogs trap the heat":"萊茵河的霧氣留住了熱量","It lies at a very southerly latitude":"它位於非常偏南的緯度","It receives warm Mediterranean breezes":"它受到溫暖的地中海微風吹拂","Alsace lies east of the Vosges, which block rain-bearing westerly winds.":"阿爾薩斯位於孚日山脈以東，山脈阻擋了帶雨的西風。","Alsace AOC lies east of the Vosges Mountains. These mountains stop the moist winds coming from the west, so the region gets little rain and plenty of sun. The best vineyards are on east- or south-east-facing slopes for the morning sun, and dry autumns extend ripening, giving dry, intense Rieslings.":"Alsace AOC 位於孚日山脈以東。這些山脈擋住了從西方吹來的潮濕氣流，所以這個地區雨量少、陽光充足。最好的葡萄園位於朝東或東南的坡地上，以接收早晨的陽光，而乾燥的秋天延長了成熟期，釀出不甜、濃郁的麗絲玲。","Which description fits a typical Alsace Riesling?":"哪一項描述符合典型的阿爾薩斯麗絲玲？","Dry, pronounced, medium body, high acidity":"不甜、香氣濃郁、酒體中等、高酸度","Light, medium sweetness, low alcohol":"輕盈、半甜、低酒精","Sweet, amber, with caramel notes":"甜、琥珀色、帶焦糖氣息","Dry, neutral, low acidity":"不甜、中性、低酸度","Alsace Riesling is dry, with ripe citrus and stone fruit, medium body and high acidity.":"阿爾薩斯麗絲玲不甜，帶有成熟的柑橘和核果，酒體中等，酸度高。","Alsace's dry, sunny climate brings the grapes to good ripeness. A typical Alsace Riesling is therefore dry, with pronounced aromas and flavours of ripe citrus and stone fruit, medium body and high acidity. The best come from grand cru vineyards. The light, medium-sweet style is more typical of the Mosel.":"阿爾薩斯乾燥晴朗的氣候讓葡萄達到良好的成熟度。因此典型的阿爾薩斯麗絲玲不甜，帶有成熟柑橘和核果的濃郁香氣和風味，酒體中等，酸度高。最好的酒來自 grand cru 葡萄園。輕盈半甜的風格則更是 Mosel 的典型特徵。","What does Vendanges Tardives on an Alsace Riesling label indicate?":"阿爾薩斯麗絲玲酒標上的 Vendanges Tardives 代表什麼？","A sweeter style from late-harvested grapes":"用晚收葡萄釀的較甜風格","A wine from a grand cru vineyard":"來自 grand cru 葡萄園的酒","A dry wine aged in new oak":"在新橡木桶中陳年的不甜酒","A wine from grapes frozen on the vine":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的酒","Vendanges Tardives means late harvest: riper grapes and a sweeter wine.":"Vendanges Tardives 是晚收的意思：葡萄更成熟，酒更甜。","Alongside dry Rieslings, Alsace also makes sweeter styles. These come from leaving the grapes on the vine for longer, taking advantage of dry autumns so sugars and flavours concentrate. Such wines are labelled Vendanges Tardives. Wines from grapes frozen on the vine are German Eiswein instead.":"除了不甜的麗絲玲，阿爾薩斯也出產較甜的風格。這些酒來自讓葡萄在樹上留得更久，利用乾燥的秋天讓糖分和風味濃縮。這樣的酒標示為 Vendanges Tardives。用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的酒，則是德國的 Eiswein。","Why do Eden Valley and Clare Valley have moderate climates, unlike nearby Barossa Valley?":"為什麼 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley 屬於溫和氣候，而不像鄰近的 Barossa Valley？","Because of their higher altitude":"因為它們海拔較高","Because of Pacific fogs":"因為太平洋的霧氣","Because of a ring of mountains":"因為一圈環繞的山脈","Because of light reflected off rivers":"因為河面反射的光線","Altitude cools Eden and Clare Valleys, suiting dry, fresh Riesling.":"海拔讓 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley 保持涼爽，適合不甜、清爽的麗絲玲。","Australia's premium Riesling is centred on South Australia's Eden Valley and Clare Valley. These valleys sit higher than the nearby warm Barossa Valley, and the altitude lowers temperatures, creating a moderate climate. They produce refreshing dry Rieslings with pronounced aromas of lime, lemon and sometimes petrol.":"澳洲的頂級麗絲玲集中在南澳的 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley。這些山谷比鄰近溫暖的 Barossa Valley 海拔更高，海拔降低了溫度，形成溫和氣候。它們出產令人清爽的不甜麗絲玲，帶有萊姆、檸檬，有時還有汽油的濃郁香氣。","A dry, refreshing Riesling with pronounced lime, lemon and a hint of petrol most likely comes from:":"一款不甜、清爽、帶有濃郁萊姆、檸檬和一絲汽油味的麗絲玲，最可能來自：","Mosel, medium-sweet style":"Mosel，半甜風格","Alsace, Vendanges Tardives":"阿爾薩斯，Vendanges Tardives","Germany, Eiswein":"德國，Eiswein","Lime, lemon and petrol in a dry Riesling are typical of Clare and Eden Valleys.":"不甜麗絲玲中的萊姆、檸檬和汽油，是 Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley 的典型特徵。","Australia's Clare and Eden Valleys, kept moderate by altitude, produce dry, refreshing Rieslings with pronounced lime and lemon and sometimes petrol. The other options are sweeter styles: the Mosel often gives medium-sweet wines, Alsace Vendanges Tardives is sweeter, and Eiswein is a sweet wine from frozen grapes.":"澳洲的 Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley 因海拔而保持溫和，出產不甜、清爽、帶有濃郁萊姆和檸檬、有時還有汽油的麗絲玲。其他選項都是較甜的風格：Mosel 常出產半甜的酒，阿爾薩斯的 Vendanges Tardives 更甜，而 Eiswein 是用冰凍葡萄釀的甜酒。","Why is Riesling often misunderstood by consumers?":"為什麼麗絲玲常被消費者誤解？","It is linked with Liebfraumilch, a low-quality sweet wine":"它與低品質的甜酒 Liebfraumilch 有關","It is confused with a black grape":"它被誤認為黑葡萄","People think it cannot age":"人們以為它無法陳年","People believe it is always oaked":"人們以為它總是經過橡木桶","Its German roots tie it to Liebfraumilch, a simple sweetened style now out of fashion.":"它的德國淵源讓它與 Liebfraumilch 連在一起，那是一種現已過時的簡單加甜風格。","Many consumers wrongly link Riesling with Liebfraumilch, a low-quality sweetened German wine that has fallen out of fashion. In fact Riesling makes high-quality wines from dry to sweet, and enthusiasts value it for its versatility, flavour intensity and ability to age. It is these premium wines that keep driving Riesling sales worldwide.":"許多消費者誤把麗絲玲與 Liebfraumilch 聯想在一起，那是一種已經過時的低品質加甜德國酒。事實上，麗絲玲能釀出從不甜到甜的高品質酒款，愛好者珍視它的多才多藝、風味強度和陳年能力。正是這些頂級酒款持續推動麗絲玲在全球的銷售。","What does it mean that Riesling is a 'cold-hardy' grape?":"麗絲玲是「耐寒」品種，這是什麼意思？","It copes well with cold, so it thrives in cool climates":"它很能耐寒，所以在涼爽氣候中生長茁壯","It must be fermented at very low temperatures":"它必須在非常低的溫度下發酵","It can only be grown where grapes freeze on the vine every year":"它只能種在葡萄每年都會在樹上結冰的地方","It must be served ice-cold":"它必須冰鎮後飲用","Cold-hardiness lets Riesling thrive in cool climates such as Germany.":"耐寒讓麗絲玲能在德國等涼爽氣候中生長茁壯。","The term is about the vine, not the winery or service. Riesling prefers cool to moderate climates; grapes freezing on the vine matter only for Eiswein, which is not made every year.":"這個術語說的是葡萄樹，不是酒廠或侍酒。麗絲玲偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候；葡萄在樹上結冰只與 Eiswein 有關，而 Eiswein 並不是每年都能釀。","Which of these does NOT concentrate sugars and flavours in Riesling grapes?":"下列哪一項不會濃縮麗絲玲葡萄的糖分和風味？","Adding Süssreserve":"加入 Süssreserve","Late harvesting":"晚收","Noble rot (botrytis)":"貴腐（貴腐菌）","Grapes freezing naturally on the vine, as for Eiswein":"葡萄在樹上自然結冰，如 Eiswein","Süssreserve is juice added to the wine: it sweetens but does not concentrate the grapes.":"Süssreserve 是加入酒中的果汁：它能增甜，但不會濃縮葡萄。","Late harvest, botrytis and freezing act on the grapes in the vineyard, concentrating sugar, acidity and flavour. Süssreserve is added after fermentation and is a way to make off-dry or medium wines, not a form of concentration.":"晚收、貴腐和冰凍都是在葡萄園中作用於葡萄，濃縮糖分、酸度和風味。Süssreserve 是在發酵後加入的，是釀造微甜或半甜酒的方法，不是一種濃縮方式。","Which autumn conditions does Riesling need for a successful late harvest?":"麗絲玲需要什麼樣的秋天條件才能成功晚收？","Dry, sunny autumns":"乾燥晴朗的秋天","Wet, warm autumns":"潮濕溫暖的秋天","Early September frosts that stop ripening early":"九月初的霜凍，讓成熟提早結束","Frequent hail":"頻繁的冰雹","A dry, sunny autumn keeps grapes healthy on the vine and lets them keep ripening slowly.":"乾燥晴朗的秋天讓葡萄在樹上保持健康，並繼續緩慢成熟。","Riesling builds sugar and flavour slowly while keeping its acidity: it is ideal for late harvesting, but only if the weather stays dry and sunny. Rain encourages unwanted rot, hail damages the grapes, and an early frost cuts ripening short.":"麗絲玲緩慢累積糖分和風味，同時保留酸度：它非常適合晚收，但前提是天氣保持乾燥晴朗。下雨會助長不受歡迎的腐爛，冰雹會損傷葡萄，而早來的霜凍會讓成熟提早中斷。","Its high natural acidity balances the sweetness":"它的高天然酸度平衡了甜度","The grape's tannins offset the sugar":"葡萄的單寧抵消了糖分","Its very high alcohol masks the sugar and warms the finish":"它非常高的酒精掩蓋了糖分，讓餘韻溫熱","New-oak ageing dries it out":"新橡木桶陳年讓它變乾","Riesling's high acidity is perfect for balancing high sugar levels.":"麗絲玲的高酸度非常適合平衡高糖分。","Acidity brings freshness and keeps sweet wines lively even after years. Riesling is a white without notable tannin; the sweetest examples often have low alcohol, and it is usually made in steel, not new oak.":"酸度帶來清新感，讓甜酒即使過了多年依然活潑。麗絲玲是沒有明顯單寧的白酒；最甜的酒款常常酒精很低，而且它通常在不鏽鋼槽而不是新橡木桶中釀造。","What keeps a fine Riesling tasting fresh after decades in bottle?":"是什麼讓優質麗絲玲在瓶中數十年後依然嚐起來清爽？","Its high natural acidity":"它的高天然酸度","Time in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中的時間","Carbon dioxide added at bottling":"裝瓶時加入的二氧化碳","High alcohol, acting as a natural preservative for many years":"高酒精，多年來作為天然防腐劑","High acidity keeps the wine lively while it develops honey and petrol.":"高酸度讓酒在發展出蜂蜜和汽油的同時保持活潑。","In Riesling, acidity is the key to longevity: the wine stays fresh as tertiary notes appear. It is usually made in inert vessels without new oak; alcohol is not the factor involved, and carbon dioxide has nothing to do with ageing.":"在麗絲玲中，酸度是長壽的關鍵：酒在三級氣息出現的同時保持清爽。它通常在惰性容器中釀造，不使用新橡木桶；酒精不是相關因素，二氧化碳也與陳年無關。","Why are Mosel Rieslings usually light-bodied?":"為什麼 Mosel 麗絲玲通常酒體輕盈？","Because of the very northerly latitude":"因為緯度非常偏北","Because they are always cut with water or juice, as German law requires":"因為德國法律規定一定要摻水或果汁","Because yields are very high":"因為產量非常高","Because of very fertile soils":"因為土壤非常肥沃","Mosel is among Germany's most northerly regions: grapes ripen less and wines are lighter.":"Mosel 是德國最北的產區之一：葡萄成熟度較低，酒也較輕盈。","Further north means less warmth and therefore less sugar and alcohol: that is why Mosel Riesling is lighter than wines from more southerly regions. There is no required blending, and the best vineyards are on steep, stony slopes, not fertile soils.":"越往北熱量越少，因此糖分和酒精也越少：這就是為什麼 Mosel 麗絲玲比更南方產區的酒輕盈。沒有規定要摻混，而最好的葡萄園位於多石的陡坡上，不是肥沃的土壤。","Why do many Mosel Rieslings have medium sweetness?":"為什麼許多 Mosel 麗絲玲是半甜的？","To balance very high acidity":"為了平衡非常高的酸度","To hide very harsh tannins":"為了掩蓋非常粗糙的單寧","Because the law bans dry Riesling in this region":"因為法律禁止這個產區釀造不甜的麗絲玲","To raise the alcohol and give more body and warmth":"為了提高酒精，帶來更多酒體和溫熱感","In the cool Mosel, residual sugar balances very high acidity.":"在涼爽的 Mosel，殘糖平衡了非常高的酸度。","The cool climate gives very acidic wines; a little sugar brings harmony. Riesling is not tannic, no law bans the dry style, and residual sugar does not raise alcohol: on the contrary, unfermented sugar means less alcohol.":"涼爽的氣候帶來非常酸的酒；一點糖分能帶來和諧。麗絲玲沒有單寧感，沒有法律禁止不甜風格，而殘糖也不會提高酒精：相反地，未發酵的糖代表酒精更少。","Why are the Rheingau's vineyards on the north bank of the Rhine?":"為什麼 Rheingau 的葡萄園位於萊茵河北岸？","So the slopes face south and get more sun and warmth":"讓坡地朝南，獲得更多陽光和熱量","To shield the vines from strong sun":"為葡萄樹遮擋強烈的陽光","Because the south bank is legally reserved for black grapes":"因為南岸依法保留給黑葡萄","To encourage fog and rot":"為了促進霧氣和腐爛","On the river's north bank, steep slopes face south and maximise light and warmth.":"在河的北岸，陡坡朝南，能最大化光照和熱量。","In a cool climate like Germany's, aspect is decisive: a south-facing slope ripens grapes better. This is why Rheingau Rieslings are drier and fuller than Mosel ones. The other options make no sense where the problem is a lack of warmth.":"在德國這樣的涼爽氣候中，坡向具有決定性：朝南的坡地讓葡萄成熟得更好。這就是為什麼 Rheingau 的麗絲玲比 Mosel 的更不甜、更飽滿。在問題是熱量不足的地方，其他選項都說不通。","A dry, medium-bodied Riesling from a German region near the French border most likely comes from:":"一款來自德國靠近法國邊境產區、不甜且酒體中等的麗絲玲，最可能來自：","Pfalz, towards the French border, gives dry, medium-bodied Rieslings.":"靠近法國邊境的 Pfalz 出產不甜、酒體中等的麗絲玲。","Pfalz is sheltered by mountains to the west, dry and sunny, and its wines resemble those of Alsace. Mosel gives lighter wines, often with medium sweetness; the Rheingau is not near France. Clare Valley is in Australia.":"Pfalz 西邊受山脈屏障，乾燥晴朗，它的酒與阿爾薩斯的相似。Mosel 的酒較輕盈，常常是半甜的；Rheingau 並不靠近法國。Clare Valley 則在澳洲。","Why are many German label terms based on grape ripeness?":"為什麼許多德國酒標術語是以葡萄成熟度為基礎？","The cool climate makes the desired ripeness hard to reach":"涼爽的氣候讓葡萄難以達到想要的成熟度","Because naming the grape on the label is banned in Germany":"因為德國禁止在酒標上標示品種","Because grapes always ripen too fast":"因為葡萄總是成熟得太快","Because all German wines are sweet":"因為所有德國酒都是甜的","In a cool climate ripeness is precious, so the categories measure sugar in the grapes at harvest.":"在涼爽氣候中成熟度很珍貴，所以這些類別衡量的是採收時葡萄的糖分。","German growers often struggle to reach their desired ripeness, so the system rewards higher sugar levels. The grape can appear on the label (e.g. Riesling Kabinett), grapes do not ripen too fast, and many German wines are dry.":"德國種植者常常難以達到想要的成熟度，所以這個體系獎勵更高的糖分。品種可以出現在酒標上（例如 Riesling Kabinett），葡萄不會成熟得太快，而且許多德國酒是不甜的。","Which style is typical of a German Landwein?":"哪一種風格是德國 Landwein 的典型特徵？","Light-bodied, dry to off-dry":"酒體輕盈，不甜至微甜","Very sweet, from botrytised grapes":"非常甜，用貴腐葡萄釀造","Full-bodied, high in alcohol and long aged in new barrels":"酒體飽滿、酒精高，在新橡木桶中長期陳年","Landwein, Germany's PGI, is usually light and dry to off-dry.":"Landwein 是德國的 PGI，通常輕盈，不甜至微甜。","Landwein requires less ripeness than Qualitätswein, so it gives lighter wines. Very sweet botrytised wines belong to the top Prädikat levels such as BA and TBA. Full body and new oak do not describe this category.":"Landwein 要求的成熟度比 Qualitätswein 低，所以釀出的酒較輕盈。非常甜的貴腐酒屬於 BA 和 TBA 等最高的 Prädikat 等級。飽滿的酒體和新橡木桶並不符合這個類別。","What does a Qualitätswein require compared with a Landwein?":"與 Landwein 相比，Qualitätswein 有什麼要求？","One of 13 winegrowing areas and riper grapes":"來自 13 個葡萄酒產區之一，且葡萄更成熟","Botrytis-affected grapes":"受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","Grapes frozen on the vine, picked at night below zero":"在樹上結冰、於零度以下夜間採收的葡萄","A single grand cru vineyard":"單一 grand cru 葡萄園","Qualitätswein comes from one of the 13 areas, such as Mosel or Rheingau, with a higher minimum ripeness than Landwein.":"Qualitätswein 來自 13 個產區之一，例如 Mosel 或 Rheingau，最低成熟度要求比 Landwein 高。","The result is usually more intense, fuller wines than Landwein. Botrytis and frozen grapes concern Prädikat levels such as BA, TBA and Eiswein; grand cru is a Burgundy and Alsace concept, not part of this German category.":"結果通常是比 Landwein 更濃郁、更飽滿的酒。貴腐和冰凍葡萄涉及的是 BA、TBA 和 Eiswein 等 Prädikat 等級；grand cru 是布根地和阿爾薩斯的概念，不屬於這個德國類別。","Two Mosel Rieslings from the same producer: a Kabinett and a Spätlese. What should you expect from the Spätlese?":"同一家生產者的兩款 Mosel 麗絲玲：一款 Kabinett 和一款 Spätlese。你應該對 Spätlese 有什麼預期？","More concentrated flavours and more body, with ripe citrus and peach":"風味更濃縮、酒體更飽滿，帶有成熟的柑橘和桃子","A lighter, more delicate wine with green apple and blossom":"更輕盈、更細緻的酒，帶有青蘋果和花香","Dried apricot, mango and honey from botrytis":"來自貴腐菌的杏桃乾、芒果和蜂蜜","Fine bubbles":"細緻的氣泡","Spätlese ('late harvest') comes from riper grapes than Kabinett: more concentration and body.":"Spätlese（「晚收」）來自比 Kabinett 更成熟的葡萄：更濃縮、酒體更飽滿。","Kabinett is the lightest Prädikat, with green apple, lime and blossom. Spätlese adds ripe citrus and a touch of peach. Botrytis, mango and dried fruit describe higher levels such as Beerenauslese; bubbles are irrelevant.":"Kabinett 是最輕盈的 Prädikat，帶有青蘋果、萊姆和花香。Spätlese 增添了成熟的柑橘和一絲桃子。貴腐菌、芒果和果乾描述的是 Beerenauslese 等更高的等級；氣泡則無關。","Which statement about Riesling Eiswein is correct?":"關於麗絲玲 Eiswein，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It cannot be made every year":"它無法每年都釀造","Botrytis is essential to make it":"釀造它必須有貴腐菌","It has high yields and low prices, because picking is quick and mechanised":"它產量高、價格低，因為採收快速且機械化","It is a dry, high-alcohol wine":"它是不甜、高酒精的酒","The weather for Eiswein, grapes frozen on the vine, does not occur every year.":"讓葡萄在樹上結冰以釀造 Eiswein 的天氣，並不是每年都會出現。","Eiswein has vibrant peach, apricot, mango and pineapple aromas, and botrytis plays no part. It is labour-intensive with tiny yields, hence expensive. It is sweet and naturally low in alcohol, because yeast cannot ferment so much sugar.":"Eiswein 帶有鮮明的桃子、杏桃、芒果和鳳梨香氣，貴腐菌不參與其中。它耗費大量人力、產量極少，因此價格昂貴。它是甜的，天然酒精低，因為酵母無法發酵這麼多的糖。","Which pair of Prädikat levels requires the same minimum sugar at harvest?":"哪一組 Prädikat 等級要求相同的採收最低糖分？","Beerenauslese and Eiswein":"Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein","Kabinett and Spätlese":"Kabinett 和 Spätlese","Auslese and Trockenbeerenauslese":"Auslese 和 Trockenbeerenauslese","Spätlese and Beerenauslese":"Spätlese 和 Beerenauslese","Beerenauslese and Eiswein are the one exception to the rising order: they share the same minimum sugar.":"Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein 是遞增順序中唯一的例外：它們的最低糖分相同。","The six Prädikat levels rise by minimum sugar: Kabinett, Spätlese, Auslese, then Beerenauslese and Eiswein at the same level, and finally Trockenbeerenauslese. The other pairs have different levels.":"六個 Prädikat 等級依最低糖分遞增：Kabinett、Spätlese、Auslese，接著是同一等級的 Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein，最後是 Trockenbeerenauslese。其他組合的等級都不同。","Which statement about Australian Riesling is correct?":"關於澳洲麗絲玲，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It has been grown since the early 19th century; the best come from Eden and Clare Valley":"從 19 世紀初就開始種植；最好的來自 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley","It was only introduced in the 2000s":"直到 2000 年代才引進","It is made mostly in a sweet style in the warm Barossa Valley":"主要在溫暖的 Barossa Valley 釀成甜型風格","It is almost always aged in new oak":"幾乎總是在新橡木桶中陳年","Australia has grown Riesling since the early 1800s; premium Riesling centres on Eden Valley and Clare Valley.":"澳洲從 1800 年代初就種植麗絲玲；頂級麗絲玲集中在 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley。","These two South Australian valleys are moderated by altitude and give dry Rieslings with lime and lemon. Nearby Barossa Valley is warm and not the centre of Riesling, and the typical style is dry. As almost everywhere, Riesling is made without new oak.":"這兩個南澳的山谷受海拔調節，出產帶有萊姆和檸檬的不甜麗絲玲。鄰近的 Barossa Valley 很溫暖，不是麗絲玲的中心，而典型的風格是不甜的。和幾乎所有地方一樣，麗絲玲不使用新橡木桶釀造。","In Alsace, where are the best Riesling vineyards usually located?":"在阿爾薩斯，最好的麗絲玲葡萄園通常位於哪裡？","On Vosges foothills facing east or south-east":"孚日山脈山麓朝東或東南的坡地","On the fertile, deep alluvial plain of the Rhine":"萊茵河肥沃深厚的沖積平原","On the western side of the Vosges":"孚日山脈的西側","On the banks of the Mosel":"Mosel 河畔","The best vineyards are in the Vosges foothills, facing east or south-east for morning sun.":"最好的葡萄園位於孚日山脈山麓，朝東或東南以接收早晨的陽光。","Alsace lies east of the Vosges, which shelter it from rain; east-facing slopes catch the morning sun, and dry autumns extend ripening. The western side is rainy and outside Alsace; the plain gives less rich wines; the Mosel is in Germany.":"阿爾薩斯位於孚日山脈以東，山脈為它擋住雨水；朝東的坡地接收早晨的陽光，乾燥的秋天延長了成熟期。西側多雨，而且不屬於阿爾薩斯；平原出產的酒不那麼豐富；Mosel 則在德國。","Compared with a typical Mosel Riesling, an Alsace Riesling is usually:":"與典型的 Mosel 麗絲玲相比，阿爾薩斯麗絲玲通常：","Drier and fuller-bodied":"更不甜，酒體更飽滿","Sweeter and lighter":"更甜、更輕盈","More tannic, deeper in colour and marked by new oak":"單寧更多、顏色更深，帶有明顯的新橡木桶味","Lightly sparkling":"微帶氣泡","Dry, sunny Alsace gives dry, medium-bodied Rieslings; Mosel gives light wines, often medium-sweet.":"乾燥晴朗的阿爾薩斯出產不甜、酒體中等的麗絲玲；Mosel 出產輕盈、常常半甜的酒。","Shelter from the Vosges makes Alsace one of France's driest, sunniest areas: riper grapes, dry wines with ripe citrus and stone fruit. The Mosel, further north, is cooler. Both Rieslings are usually made without new oak.":"孚日山脈的屏障讓阿爾薩斯成為法國最乾燥、陽光最充足的地區之一：葡萄更成熟，酒不甜，帶有成熟的柑橘和核果。更北的 Mosel 則較涼爽。兩地的麗絲玲通常都不使用新橡木桶。","Where do the finest Alsace Rieslings come from, in appellation terms?":"就法定產區而言，最優質的阿爾薩斯麗絲玲來自哪裡？","From individual grand cru vineyards":"來自個別的 grand cru 葡萄園","From region-wide blends sold as Alsace AOC":"來自以 Alsace AOC 出售的全區混調","From irrigated plain vineyards":"來自經灌溉的平原葡萄園","From vineyards classified as Prädikatswein, as in Germany":"來自像德國一樣分級為 Prädikatswein 的葡萄園","In Alsace, the best Rieslings come from grand cru vineyards.":"在阿爾薩斯，最好的麗絲玲來自 grand cru 葡萄園。","Alsace grands crus are specific sites on the Vosges foothills, and Riesling is among the permitted grapes. Alsace AOC is the regional appellation; Prädikatswein is a German term, not an Alsace one.":"阿爾薩斯的 grand cru 是孚日山脈山麓上的特定園地，麗絲玲是允許的品種之一。Alsace AOC 是地區級法定產區；Prädikatswein 是德國術語，不是阿爾薩斯的。","Where does Riesling find ideal conditions to reach its potential?":"麗絲玲在哪裡能找到發揮潛力的理想條件？","In cool, dry areas sunny enough for slow ripening":"在涼爽、乾燥、陽光足以讓葡萄緩慢成熟的地區","In hot, humid areas where it ripens fast":"在炎熱潮濕、讓它快速成熟的地區","In very rainy areas where grey rot strikes every year":"在每年都會發生灰黴病的非常多雨地區","Only on irrigated plains":"只在經灌溉的平原","Riesling likes cool, dry, sunny areas where sugars and flavours develop slowly.":"麗絲玲喜歡涼爽、乾燥、晴朗的地區，在那裡糖分和風味緩慢發展。","Slow ripening keeps acidity and builds intense flavours, which is why regions like the Mosel, Alsace and Clare Valley give great Rieslings. Humid heat speeds things up and encourages disease, constant rain brings unwanted rot, and irrigated plains suit volume wines.":"緩慢成熟能保留酸度並累積濃郁的風味，這就是為什麼 Mosel、阿爾薩斯和 Clare Valley 等產區能釀出偉大的麗絲玲。濕熱會加快成熟並助長病害，持續下雨帶來不受歡迎的腐爛，而經灌溉的平原適合大量生產的酒。","What drives Riesling sales around the world today?":"今天是什麼推動了麗絲玲在全球的銷售？","Premium-quality wines":"頂級品質的酒款","Cheap sweet Liebfraumilch-style wines":"便宜的 Liebfraumilch 式甜酒","New-oak Rieslings with vanilla and coconut":"帶有香草和椰子的新橡木桶麗絲玲","High-volume sparkling Rieslings":"大量生產的氣泡麗絲玲","Enthusiasts value Riesling's versatility, intensity and ageing ability: premium wines drive its sales.":"愛好者珍視麗絲玲的多才多藝、濃郁度和陳年能力：頂級酒款推動了它的銷售。","Liebfraumilch harmed Riesling's image and has gone out of fashion. Today quality is what supports the grape. New oak is not typical of Riesling, and sparkling wine is not the style named as the sales driver.":"Liebfraumilch 傷害了麗絲玲的形象，而且已經過時。今天支撐這個品種的是品質。新橡木桶不是麗絲玲的典型特徵，氣泡酒也不是被點名推動銷售的風格。","What is the relationship between Pinot Grigio and Pinot Gris?":"Pinot Grigio 和 Pinot Gris 是什麼關係？","They are the same grape with two names":"它們是同一個品種的兩個名字","They are two different related grapes":"它們是兩個不同但相關的品種","Pinot Gris is a red-skinned version":"Pinot Gris 是紅皮的版本","Pinot Grigio is a cross of Pinot Gris":"Pinot Grigio 是 Pinot Gris 的雜交種","Grigio is the Italian and Gris the French name for one white grape.":"Grigio 是義大利文名稱，Gris 是法文名稱，指的是同一個白葡萄品種。","Pinot Grigio and Pinot Gris are the same white variety: the first is the Italian name, the second the French. Any difference in the glass comes not from the name but from vineyard choices, above all yield and harvest timing. Outside Europe the two names are used to hint at style.":"Pinot Grigio 和 Pinot Gris 是同一個白葡萄品種（灰皮諾）：前者是義大利文名稱，後者是法文名稱。杯中的任何差異並非來自名稱，而是來自葡萄園的選擇，尤其是產量和採收時機。在歐洲以外，這兩個名稱被用來暗示風格。","Which vineyard choices produce the light Pinot Grigio style?":"哪些葡萄園選擇會造就輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 風格？","High yields and early harvest":"高產量和提早採收","Low yields and late harvest":"低產量和晚採","Low yields and dried grapes":"低產量和風乾葡萄","High yields and late harvest":"高產量和晚採","Large crops picked early keep acidity and make a light, simple wine.":"早採的大量收成保留酸度，釀出輕盈簡單的酒。","The most common style comes from high yields and early picking, which preserves acidity. The wine is dry and light with medium to high acidity and simple pear and lemon flavours. Controlled yields and later picking give the opposite style: full-bodied, with more sugar and complexity and medium acidity.":"最常見的風格來自高產量和提早採收，這能保留酸度。酒不甜、輕盈，酸度中等至高，帶有簡單的梨和檸檬風味。控制產量並較晚採收則帶來相反的風格：酒體飽滿，糖分和複雜度更高，酸度中等。","Which flavours characterise a light Pinot Grigio?":"哪些風味是輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 的特徵？","Simple pear and lemon":"簡單的梨和檸檬","Mango, banana and ginger":"芒果、香蕉和薑","Green pepper and asparagus":"青椒和蘆筍","The light style shows simple pear and lemon flavours.":"輕盈的風格展現簡單的梨和檸檬風味。","Light Pinot Grigio, from high yields and early picking, is dry and fresh with simple pear and lemon flavours. Mango, banana and ginger point to the rich, ripe style, as in Alsace. Green pepper and asparagus are typical of Sauvignon Blanc; rose and lychee of Gewurztraminer.":"來自高產量和提早採收的輕盈 Pinot Grigio，不甜、清爽，帶有簡單的梨和檸檬風味。芒果、香蕉和薑指向豐潤成熟的風格，例如阿爾薩斯。青椒和蘆筍是白蘇維濃的典型特徵；玫瑰和荔枝則是格烏茲塔明那的。","Why do late-picked Pinot Gris grapes give a fuller wine?":"為什麼晚採的灰皮諾葡萄能釀出更飽滿的酒？","They have more sugar and more complex flavours":"它們糖分更多、風味更複雜","They have more acid and less sugar":"它們酸更多、糖更少","They always ferment in new oak":"它們總是在新橡木桶中發酵","They come from higher yields":"它們來自更高的產量","More ripeness means more sugar (alcohol, body), less acid and richer flavours.":"成熟度越高，糖分越多（酒精、酒體）、酸越少、風味越豐富。","With controlled yields and delayed harvest the grapes ripen further: they gain sugar, lose acid and build complex flavours. The result is a powerful, full-bodied wine with medium acidity and pronounced lemon, peach, mango and banana. Pinot Gris is usually made in inert vessels, not new oak.":"控制產量並延後採收，葡萄會更成熟：糖分增加、酸度下降，並累積複雜的風味。結果是一款強勁、酒體飽滿、酸度中等的酒，帶有濃郁的檸檬、桃子、芒果和香蕉。灰皮諾通常在惰性容器而不是新橡木桶中釀造。","Why is Pinot Grigio/Gris usually fermented in inert vessels?":"為什麼灰皮諾通常在惰性容器中發酵？","To preserve its fruity flavours":"為了保留它的果味","To raise acidity":"為了提高酸度","To make a sweet wine":"為了釀造甜酒","Inert vessels add no flavour and protect the grape's fruit.":"惰性容器不會增添風味，能保護這個品種的果味。","Pinot Grigio/Gris is usually fermented in inert vessels such as stainless steel, which add no flavour and keep the fruit intact. Oak would add vanilla, which is not the aim. Any sweetness comes from stopping fermentation, not from the type of vessel.":"灰皮諾通常在不鏽鋼槽等惰性容器中發酵，這些容器不會增添風味，能完整保留果味。橡木桶會增添香草味，那不是目標。任何甜味都來自中止發酵，與容器類型無關。","How do some producers make off-dry or medium Pinot Gris?":"有些生產者如何釀造微甜或半甜的灰皮諾？","They stop fermentation by removing the yeast":"去除酵母以中止發酵","They add acid during winemaking":"在釀造過程中加酸","They use oak chips":"使用橡木片","They pick very early":"非常早就採收","Removing the yeast leaves some sugar in the wine as sweetness.":"去除酵母會在酒中留下部分糖分作為甜味。","The light Italian style is almost always fermented dry. Producers of the riper, fuller style sometimes stop fermentation by removing the yeast: sugar not yet turned into alcohol stays in the wine, making it off-dry or medium. Acidification and oak do not create sweetness.":"輕盈的義大利風格幾乎都發酵至不甜。較成熟、較飽滿風格的生產者有時會去除酵母以中止發酵：尚未轉化為酒精的糖留在酒中，讓酒成為微甜或半甜。加酸和橡木桶都不會帶來甜味。","Which notes can concentrated, full-bodied Pinot Gris develop in bottle?":"濃縮、酒體飽滿的灰皮諾在瓶中會發展出哪些氣息？","Ginger and honey":"薑和蜂蜜","Smoke and coconut":"煙燻和椰子","With age, rich Pinot Gris evolves towards ginger and honey.":"隨著陳年，豐潤的灰皮諾會朝薑和蜂蜜演變。","Light Pinot Grigio styles should be drunk young, as their simple flavours fade fast. More concentrated, full-bodied examples, such as those from Alsace, can instead evolve in bottle and develop ginger and honey. Butter and cream come from malolactic conversion; smoke and coconut from oak.":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 風格要趁年輕喝，因為它們簡單的風味很快就會消退。相反地，更濃縮、酒體飽滿的酒款，例如阿爾薩斯的，可以在瓶中演變，發展出薑和蜂蜜。奶油和鮮奶油來自乳酸轉化；煙燻和椰子來自橡木桶。","Under which labels is much Veneto Pinot Grigio sold?":"許多威尼托的 Pinot Grigio 以什麼標示出售？","delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT":"delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT","Veneto Pinot Grigio is sold as delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT.":"威尼托的 Pinot Grigio 以 delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT 出售。","Much Italian Pinot Grigio comes from the Veneto in the north-east and is labelled delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT. These are simple, light, unoaked wines, inexpensive because they are made in high volumes. Alsace Grand Cru and Pays d'Oc IGP are French; Friuli-Venezia Giulia is noted for a more complex style.":"許多義大利 Pinot Grigio 來自東北部的威尼托，標示為 delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT。這些是簡單、輕盈、未經橡木桶的酒，因為大量生產而價格平實。Alsace Grand Cru 和 Pays d'Oc IGP 是法國的；Friuli-Venezia Giulia 則以較複雜的風格著稱。","What is the typical quality of high-volume Veneto Pinot Grigio?":"大量生產的威尼托 Pinot Grigio 典型品質如何？","Acceptable to good, short finish":"可接受至良好，餘韻短","Outstanding, very long finish":"傑出，餘韻非常長","Very good, built for long ageing":"非常好，適合長期陳年","Poor, always faulty":"欠佳，總是有缺陷","High volume and low price: simple wines, short finish, acceptable or good quality.":"產量大、價格低：簡單的酒，餘韻短，品質可接受或良好。","High-volume Veneto Pinot Grigio is inexpensive, simple and light. It usually has a short finish and acceptable to good quality. It is not made for ageing, as its simple flavours fade quickly. A more complex style is found in Friuli-Venezia Giulia.":"大量生產的威尼托 Pinot Grigio 價格平實、簡單而輕盈。它通常餘韻短，品質可接受至良好。它不是為陳年而釀的，因為簡單的風味很快就會消退。較複雜的風格可以在 Friuli-Venezia Giulia 找到。","Which Italian region is known for a more complex, fuller-bodied Pinot Grigio?":"義大利哪個地區以較複雜、酒體較飽滿的 Pinot Grigio 聞名？","In Italy's north-eastern corner, Friuli gives a fuller, more complex Pinot Grigio.":"在義大利東北角，Friuli 出產更飽滿、更複雜的 Pinot Grigio。","Most Italian Pinot Grigio is simple and light, often from the Veneto. A more complex, fuller-bodied style is found in Friuli-Venezia Giulia, in northern Italy's eastern corner. It shows how the same grape can deliver more intensity through different choices.":"大多數義大利 Pinot Grigio 簡單而輕盈，常來自威尼托。較複雜、酒體較飽滿的風格則可以在北義東角的 Friuli-Venezia Giulia 找到。這顯示同一個品種如何透過不同的選擇展現更多濃郁度。","How is Pinot Gris usually harvested in Alsace?":"在阿爾薩斯，灰皮諾通常如何採收？","Late, when grapes are extra-ripe":"晚採，在葡萄過熟時","Early, to keep high acidity":"早採，以保留高酸度","With very high yields and irrigation":"以非常高的產量並灌溉","After the grapes have frozen":"在葡萄結冰之後","Alsace picks late: more sugar, medium acidity and complex flavours.":"阿爾薩斯晚採：糖分更多、酸度中等、風味複雜。","In Alsace AOC, Pinot Gris is usually picked later in the season when the grapes are extra-ripe. By then acidity is medium and the grapes have more sugar and flavour complexity. The wines, dry to medium, have medium to full body with pronounced peach and mango.":"在 Alsace AOC，灰皮諾通常在季末葡萄過熟時才採收。這時酸度中等，葡萄的糖分和風味複雜度都更高。這些酒從不甜到半甜，酒體中等至飽滿，帶有濃郁的桃子和芒果。","A full-bodied white with medium acidity, pronounced peach and mango and slight sweetness is most likely?":"一款酒體飽滿、酸度中等、帶有濃郁桃子和芒果、略帶甜味的白酒，最可能是什麼？","An Alsace Pinot Gris":"阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾","A delle Venezie Pinot Grigio":"delle Venezie 的 Pinot Grigio","A Sancerre":"Sancerre","Extra-ripe grapes and sometimes stopped fermentation: the Alsace style.":"過熟的葡萄，有時還中止發酵：這是阿爾薩斯的風格。","Alsace Pinot Gris comes from extra-ripe grapes: medium to full body, medium acidity, pronounced peach and mango and sweetness from dry to medium. Delle Venezie Pinot Grigio is light and dry with pear and lemon; Sancerre and Chablis are crisp whites with high acidity.":"阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾來自過熟的葡萄：酒體中等至飽滿、酸度中等、濃郁的桃子和芒果，甜度從不甜到半甜。delle Venezie 的 Pinot Grigio 輕盈不甜，帶有梨和檸檬；Sancerre 和 Chablis 則是高酸度的爽脆白酒。","Where are Alsace's best Pinot Gris vineyards?":"阿爾薩斯最好的灰皮諾葡萄園在哪裡？","In grand cru sites on the Vosges slopes":"在孚日山脈坡地上的 grand cru 園地","On the plains along the Rhine":"在萊茵河沿岸的平原","In cool north-facing valleys":"在涼爽、朝北的山谷","On sea-cooled coasts":"在受海洋降溫的海岸","Grand cru sites on steep east/south-east slopes get more sun.":"位於朝東／東南陡坡的 grand cru 園地能獲得更多陽光。","The best Alsace Pinot Gris comes from grand cru vineyards, mostly on the steep foothills of the Vosges facing east and south-east. These sites get more sunlight and give riper-tasting, fuller wines than vineyards on the flatter plains. These wines can also develop honey and ginger in bottle.":"最好的阿爾薩斯灰皮諾來自 grand cru 葡萄園，大多位於孚日山脈朝東和東南的陡峭山麓。這些園地接收更多日照，釀出的酒比較平坦的平原葡萄園嚐起來更成熟、更飽滿。這些酒在瓶中也能發展出蜂蜜和薑。","What does Vendanges tardives (VT) mean on an Alsace label?":"阿爾薩斯酒標上的 Vendanges tardives（VT）是什麼意思？","A medium to sweet wine from extra-ripe grapes":"用過熟葡萄釀的半甜至甜型酒","A dry wine from early-picked grapes":"用早採葡萄釀的不甜酒","A wine aged long in oak":"在橡木桶中長時間陳年的酒","A wine from a single grand cru":"來自單一 grand cru 的酒","It means late harvest: extra-ripe grapes for medium to sweet wines.":"它是晚收的意思：用過熟的葡萄釀造半甜至甜型的酒。","Vendanges tardives means late harvest. In Alsace it usually denotes a medium to sweet wine made from extra-ripe grapes. Pinot Gris, Riesling and Gewurztraminer can carry it, in both Alsace and Alsace Grand Cru. It says nothing about oak or a single vineyard.":"Vendanges tardives 是晚收的意思。在阿爾薩斯，它通常代表用過熟葡萄釀造的半甜至甜型酒。灰皮諾、麗絲玲和格烏茲塔明那都可以使用這個標示，在 Alsace 和 Alsace Grand Cru 皆然。它與橡木桶或單一葡萄園無關。","Outside Italy and France, what does the name Pinot Gris suggest compared with Pinot Grigio?":"在義大利和法國以外，與 Pinot Grigio 相比，Pinot Gris 這個名稱暗示什麼？","More body and complexity":"更多酒體和複雜度","More acidity and lightness":"更多酸度、更輕盈","An always sweet wine":"一定是甜酒","Pinot Grigio suggests light and crisp; Pinot Gris fuller and more complex.":"Pinot Grigio 暗示輕盈爽脆；Pinot Gris 則暗示更飽滿、更複雜。","In many regions outside Europe, producers use the name as a style hint. Pinot Grigio recalls the Italian style, crisper and lighter; Pinot Gris recalls Alsace, with more body and complexity. The name implies neither bubbles nor guaranteed sweetness. It is a useful clue when choosing a bottle.":"在歐洲以外的許多產區，生產者把名稱當作風格提示。Pinot Grigio 讓人想到較爽脆、較輕盈的義大利風格；Pinot Gris 讓人想到阿爾薩斯，酒體更飽滿、更複雜。名稱既不暗示氣泡，也不保證甜度。挑選酒款時，這是很有用的線索。","A wine is labelled 'Pinot Gris'. Which language does this grape name come from?":"一款酒標示為「Pinot Gris」。這個品種名稱來自哪一種語言？","Italian":"義大利文","German":"德文","Pinot Gris is the French name; Pinot Grigio is the Italian name of the same grape.":"Pinot Gris 是法文名稱；Pinot Grigio 是同一個品種的義大利文名稱。","The two names refer to a single grape. In Alsace it is Pinot Gris; in Veneto and Friuli, Pinot Grigio. Outside Europe, the chosen name often hints at the style.":"這兩個名稱指的是同一個品種。在阿爾薩斯稱為 Pinot Gris；在威尼托和 Friuli 稱為 Pinot Grigio。在歐洲以外，選用的名稱常暗示風格。","In which climates is Pinot Grigio/Pinot Gris mainly grown?":"灰皮諾主要種植在哪些氣候中？","Cool or moderate":"涼爽或溫和","Only warm":"只在溫暖氣候","Very hot and dry, with constant irrigation all season":"非常炎熱乾燥，整季持續灌溉","Tropical":"熱帶","Pinot Grigio/Gris grows mainly in cool or moderate climates.":"灰皮諾主要種植在涼爽或溫和的氣候中。","Its classic areas, north-east Italy and Alsace, are cool or moderate. There, vineyard choices (yields and picking date) decide whether the wine is light and fresh or rich and ripe. Warm or tropical climates are not its typical home.":"它的經典產區——義大利東北部和阿爾薩斯——都屬於涼爽或溫和氣候。在那裡，葡萄園的選擇（產量和採收日期）決定了酒是輕盈清爽，還是豐潤成熟。溫暖或熱帶氣候並不是它典型的家。","What mainly determines the two very different styles of Pinot Grigio/Gris?":"主要是什麼決定了灰皮諾兩種截然不同的風格？","Grape-growing and harvesting choices":"葡萄種植和採收的選擇","Whether or not new barrels are used":"是否使用新橡木桶","The length of skin maceration, which also adds colour and tannin":"浸皮時間長短，它也會增添顏色和單寧","Yields and picking date decide whether the wine will be light or rich.":"產量和採收日期決定了酒會輕盈還是豐潤。","High yields and early picking give the light style; controlled yields and delayed picking give the full style. In the winery it is usually made in inert vessels, so oak is not the key factor; maceration and Süssreserve are not the choices involved.":"高產量和提早採收帶來輕盈的風格；控制產量和延後採收帶來飽滿的風格。在酒廠中，它通常在惰性容器中釀造，所以橡木桶不是關鍵因素；浸皮和 Süssreserve 也不是相關的選擇。","What happens to acidity when Pinot Gris picking is delayed?":"灰皮諾延後採收時，酸度會怎樣？","It falls while sugar rises":"酸度下降，糖分上升","It rises along with sugar, making the wine sharper and lighter":"隨糖分一起上升，讓酒更尖酸、更輕盈","It stays the same":"保持不變","It disappears completely":"完全消失","Riper grapes have more sugar and less acidity: hence the medium acidity of the rich style.":"較成熟的葡萄糖分更多、酸度更低：所以豐潤風格的酸度是中等的。","As grapes ripen, acidity falls and sugar and flavour build. The light, early-picked style has medium to high acidity; the rich, late-picked style has medium acidity. Acidity does not vanish and does not rise with ripeness.":"隨著葡萄成熟，酸度下降，糖分和風味累積。輕盈、早採的風格酸度中等至高；豐潤、晚採的風格酸度中等。酸度不會消失，也不會隨成熟度上升。","Which of these is NOT typical of the full, ripe style of young Pinot Gris?":"下列哪一項不是年輕灰皮諾飽滿成熟風格的典型特徵？","Peach":"桃子","Mango and banana":"芒果和香蕉","Grass and green pepper belong to Sauvignon Blanc, not ripe Pinot Gris.":"青草和青椒屬於白蘇維濃，不是成熟的灰皮諾。","The full style has pronounced lemon, stone fruit (peach) and tropical fruit (mango, banana). Herbaceous notes are Sauvignon Blanc's signature. Ginger and honey only come with bottle age.":"飽滿的風格帶有濃郁的檸檬、核果（桃子）和熱帶水果（芒果、香蕉）。草本氣息是白蘇維濃的招牌特徵。薑和蜂蜜只有在瓶中陳年後才會出現。","How is light Italian Pinot Grigio usually fermented?":"輕盈的義大利 Pinot Grigio 通常如何發酵？","Almost always to dryness":"幾乎總是發酵至不甜","Stopped early to leave medium sweetness":"提早中止以保留半甜","In new barrels with long lees ageing and full malolactic":"在新橡木桶中，長時間酒渣陳年並完全乳酸轉化","With sweet juice added after fermentation":"在發酵後加入甜的葡萄汁","The light Italian style is almost always dry.":"輕盈的義大利風格幾乎總是不甜的。","Light Pinot Grigio is fermented dry in inert vessels to keep its simple pear and lemon fruit. Stopping fermentation to keep sweetness is a choice some producers of the rich style make. New oak and added juice are not part of this style.":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 在惰性容器中發酵至不甜，以保留簡單的梨和檸檬果味。中止發酵以保留甜味，是部分豐潤風格生產者的選擇。新橡木桶和添加葡萄汁都不屬於這種風格。","A customer wants to keep a light, inexpensive Pinot Grigio for five years. What should you advise?":"一位顧客想把一瓶輕盈、平價的 Pinot Grigio 存放五年。你應該怎麼建議？","Drink it young: its simple flavours fade quickly":"趁年輕喝：它簡單的風味很快就會消退","Wait, as it will develop ginger and honey":"等一等，它會發展出薑和蜂蜜","Store it upright near a heat source to speed up its development":"直立存放在熱源附近，以加速它的發展","Wait at least ten years":"至少等十年","Light Pinot Grigio is best drunk fresh and young.":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 最好趁新鮮年輕時喝。","Ginger and honey only appear in full, concentrated versions such as the best Alsace Pinot Gris. A light style quickly loses its pear and lemon flavours. Heat damages any wine.":"薑和蜂蜜只出現在飽滿濃縮的版本中，例如最好的阿爾薩斯灰皮諾。輕盈的風格很快就會失去梨和檸檬風味。高溫會損害任何葡萄酒。","Why is most Veneto Pinot Grigio inexpensive?":"為什麼大多數威尼托 Pinot Grigio 價格平實？","Because it is made in high volumes":"因為它是大量生產的","Because the grapes are picked late":"因為葡萄是晚採的","Because it is aged for a long time in used barrels from other regions":"因為它在來自其他產區的舊橡木桶中長時間陳年","Because it comes from grand cru vineyards":"因為它來自 grand cru 葡萄園","The Veneto's large volumes keep prices low.":"威尼托的大量生產讓價格保持低廉。","The Veneto, in north-east Italy, makes huge quantities of simple, unoaked, light Pinot Grigio sold as delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT. Late harvesting and grands crus belong to the richer Alsace style, not to these wines.":"義大利東北部的威尼托生產大量簡單、未經橡木桶、輕盈的 Pinot Grigio，以 delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT 出售。晚採和 grand cru 屬於較豐潤的阿爾薩斯風格，不屬於這些酒。","Where is Friuli-Venezia Giulia?":"Friuli-Venezia Giulia 在哪裡？","In Italy's north-eastern corner":"在義大利東北角","In southern France, along the Mediterranean coast":"在法國南部的地中海沿岸","In southern Italy":"在義大利南部","In north-west Italy":"在義大利西北部","Friuli-Venezia Giulia lies in Italy's far north-east, next to the Veneto.":"Friuli-Venezia Giulia 位於義大利的最東北部，緊鄰威尼托。","Here you find a more complex, fuller-bodied Pinot Grigio than the Italian average. Southern and north-west Italy are not the areas named for this grape, and Mediterranean France is Languedoc-Roussillon.":"在這裡可以找到比義大利平均水準更複雜、酒體更飽滿的 Pinot Grigio。義大利南部和西北部不是以這個品種著稱的地區，而地中海沿岸的法國是 Languedoc-Roussillon。","An Alsace Pinot Gris can be dry or medium-sweet. What does this depend on?":"阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾可以是不甜或半甜。這取決於什麼？","On the winemaker's preference":"取決於釀酒師的偏好","On a rule requiring sweet wines in grands crus":"取決於 grand cru 必須是甜酒的規定","On the age of the vines":"取決於葡萄樹的樹齡","On the bottle type, as the Alsace flute is legally reserved for sweet wines":"取決於酒瓶類型，因為阿爾薩斯長笛瓶依法保留給甜酒","In Alsace, Pinot Gris ranges from dry to medium depending on the winemaker's preference.":"在阿爾薩斯，灰皮諾依釀酒師的偏好，從不甜到半甜都有。","Alsace grapes are picked very ripe: the producer decides whether to ferment to dryness or keep some sugar. This is why a sweetness indication on the label is useful. No rule requires sweetness in grands crus and the bottle shape does not show it.":"阿爾薩斯的葡萄在非常成熟時採收：生產者決定要發酵至不甜還是保留一些糖分。這就是為什麼酒標上的甜度標示很有用。沒有規定要求 grand cru 必須是甜的，瓶型也不會顯示甜度。","From the 2021 vintage, what must an Alsace AOC label show?":"從 2021 年份起，Alsace AOC 的酒標必須標示什麼？","The sweetness level, on a standard scale":"依標準刻度標示的甜度","The name of the single vineyard":"單一葡萄園的名稱","The percentage of new oak used":"使用新橡木桶的比例","The Prädikat level reached by the grapes at harvest":"葡萄採收時達到的 Prädikat 等級","Since 2021, Alsace wines must show their sweetness on a standardised scale.":"從 2021 年起，阿爾薩斯葡萄酒必須以標準化刻度標示甜度。","Because the same grape can be dry or medium, the indication helps consumers. Alsace wines usually also name the grape. A vineyard name appears on grands crus but is not required for all; Prädikat is a German system.":"由於同一個品種可能是不甜或半甜，這個標示有助於消費者。阿爾薩斯葡萄酒通常也會標示品種。葡萄園名稱會出現在 grand cru 上，但並非所有酒都必須標示；Prädikat 是德國的體系。","Which of these is NOT a typical grand cru grape in Alsace?":"下列哪一個不是阿爾薩斯典型的 grand cru 品種？","Pinot Gris, Riesling and Gewurztraminer are typical Alsace grand cru grapes; Chardonnay is not.":"灰皮諾、麗絲玲和格烏茲塔明那是阿爾薩斯典型的 grand cru 品種；夏多內不是。","Alsace grands crus are on steep east/south-east-facing Vosges slopes and give riper, fuller wines. The same three grapes can also be labelled Vendanges tardives. Chardonnay is Burgundy's great white, not Alsace's.":"阿爾薩斯的 grand cru 位於孚日山脈朝東／東南的陡坡上，出產更成熟、更飽滿的酒。這三個品種也可以標示 Vendanges tardives。夏多內是布根地的偉大白葡萄，不是阿爾薩斯的。","What trend does the recent success of light Pinot Grigio show?":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 近年的成功顯示了什麼趨勢？","A move away from heavy, oaky whites":"遠離厚重、橡木味重的白酒","A return to sweet whites":"回歸甜白酒","Growing interest in whites for long bottle ageing":"對適合長期瓶中陳年的白酒越來越感興趣","A preference for red wines":"偏好紅酒","The boom in simple Pinot Grigio shows consumers moving away from heavy, oaky styles.":"簡單 Pinot Grigio 的熱潮顯示消費者正遠離厚重、橡木味重的風格。","Light, dry, unoaked Pinot Grigio is exported in huge quantities from the Veneto. It is neither sweet nor for long ageing, so the other trends do not explain its success.":"輕盈、不甜、未經橡木桶的 Pinot Grigio 從威尼托大量出口。它既不甜，也不適合長期陳年，所以其他趨勢都無法解釋它的成功。","What kind of food do the riper styles of Pinot Gris pair well with?":"較成熟風格的灰皮諾適合搭配什麼樣的食物？","Strongly flavoured food":"風味濃郁的食物","Only very delicate dishes":"只適合非常清淡的菜餚","Only chocolate desserts":"只適合巧克力甜點","With no food: they are sipping wines, too rich for the table":"不適合搭餐：它們是單喝的酒，太豐潤不適合上桌","Riper Pinot Gris styles have the intensity and complexity to stand up to strongly flavoured food.":"較成熟風格的灰皮諾有足夠的濃郁度和複雜度，能撐得住風味濃郁的食物。","Full body and pronounced flavours make these wines good partners for bold flavours, where a light wine would be overwhelmed. They are not limited to delicate dishes, are not aimed at chocolate, and work well at the table.":"飽滿的酒體和濃郁的風味讓這些酒成為重口味的好搭檔，而輕盈的酒會被壓過。它們不只限於清淡的菜餚，不是針對巧克力，搭餐表現也很好。","Outside Italy and France, a producer calls their wine 'Pinot Grigio'. Which style does this suggest?":"在義大利和法國以外，一位生產者把他的酒稱為「Pinot Grigio」。這暗示什麼風格？","Lighter-bodied with higher acidity":"酒體較輕盈，酸度較高","Fuller, more complex and sometimes medium-sweet, on the Alsace model":"更飽滿、更複雜，有時半甜，以阿爾薩斯為範本","Aged in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中陳年","A light red wine":"淡紅酒","The name Pinot Grigio points to the Italian style: light and fresh.":"Pinot Grigio 這個名稱指向義大利風格：輕盈清爽。","Elsewhere, the name is a signal: Pinot Grigio for a higher-acid, lighter style, Pinot Gris for a fuller, more complex wine. Neither name indicates new oak, and it is always a white wine.":"在其他地方，名稱是一種訊號：Pinot Grigio 代表酸度較高、較輕盈的風格，Pinot Gris 代表更飽滿、更複雜的酒。兩個名稱都不表示新橡木桶，而且它永遠是白酒。","What does Pinot Grigio/Gris clearly demonstrate, according to wine experts?":"根據葡萄酒專家的說法，灰皮諾清楚地展示了什麼？","How yields and ripeness shape style, quality and price":"產量和成熟度如何塑造風格、品質和價格","That new oak always improves white wines":"新橡木桶總是能提升白酒","That soil is the only factor that matters":"土壤是唯一重要的因素","That picking date has no effect at all on the final wine style":"採收日期對最終的酒款風格完全沒有影響","The same grape gives light, cheap wines or rich, complex ones depending on yields and ripeness.":"同一個品種依產量和成熟度，能釀出輕盈便宜的酒，也能釀出豐潤複雜的酒。","High yields and early picking give the Veneto's volume Pinot Grigio; controlled yields and late picking give Alsace Pinot Gris, richer and pricier. Oak is not central for this grape, and picking date is precisely the deciding factor.":"高產量和提早採收帶來威尼托大量生產的 Pinot Grigio；控制產量和晚採帶來更豐潤、價格更高的阿爾薩斯 Pinot Gris。橡木桶對這個品種並非核心，而採收日期正是決定性的因素。","What climate does Pinot Noir need to produce good-quality grapes?":"黑皮諾需要什麼氣候才能產出優質的葡萄？","Pinot Noir needs a cool to moderate climate to keep its fresh fruit.":"黑皮諾需要涼爽至溫和的氣候，才能保留新鮮的果味。","Pinot Noir is a delicate, thin-skinned grape. In a cool to moderate climate it ripens slowly and keeps fresh red fruit and high acidity. If the climate is too warm, the fruit tastes cooked and the wines can become overly alcoholic. That is why the best regions, from Burgundy to Central Otago, are cool or have influences that temper the heat.":"黑皮諾是嬌貴、果皮薄的品種。在涼爽至溫和的氣候中，它成熟緩慢，保留新鮮的紅色水果和高酸度。如果氣候太溫暖，果味會嚐起來像煮過，酒也可能酒精過高。這就是為什麼最好的產區，從布根地到 Central Otago，都很涼爽，或有緩和高溫的影響因素。","What happens to Pinot Noir grown in a climate that is too warm?":"種在過於溫暖氣候中的黑皮諾會怎樣？","It loses fresh fruit and tastes cooked":"失去新鮮果味，嚐起來像煮過","It becomes more tannic and darker":"變得更有單寧感、顏色更深","It develops grassy, green notes":"發展出青草、青澀的氣息","It gains acidity and freshness":"增加酸度和清新感","Too much heat strips Pinot Noir of its fresh aromas and gives cooked flavours.":"過多的熱量會奪走黑皮諾的新鮮香氣，帶來煮過的風味。","Pinot Noir performs best in cool or moderate climates. When it is too warm, its delicate strawberry, raspberry and cherry aromas turn cooked and unattractive. Planting in over-warm sites has also brought overly alcoholic wines to market that lack the typical fruit needed for balance. It is a clear example of why matching grape and climate matters.":"黑皮諾在涼爽或溫和氣候中表現最好。太溫暖時，它細緻的草莓、覆盆子和櫻桃香氣會變得像煮過一樣，不討喜。種在過於溫暖的園地，也讓市場上出現酒精過高、缺乏平衡所需典型果味的酒。這清楚說明了為什麼品種與氣候的搭配很重要。","Which structure is typical of Pinot Noir?":"哪一種結構是黑皮諾的典型特徵？","High acidity, low to medium tannins":"高酸度，單寧低至中等","Low acidity, high tannins":"低酸度，高單寧","Medium acidity, high tannins":"中等酸度，高單寧","Low acidity, low tannins":"低酸度，低單寧","Pinot Noir pairs high acidity with gentle, low to medium tannins.":"黑皮諾結合了高酸度和柔和、低至中等的單寧。","Pinot Noir has thin skins and gives wines that are pale to medium in colour. On the palate acidity is high while tannins stay low to medium. This combination makes it fresh and easy-drinking, enjoyable even without food. Reds with lots of tannin and little acidity have a very different profile and are not typical of this grape.":"黑皮諾果皮薄，釀出的酒顏色淺至中等。口中酸度高，而單寧保持低至中等。這樣的組合讓它清爽易飲，即使不搭餐也很好喝。單寧多而酸度少的紅酒風味特徵截然不同，不是這個品種的典型特徵。","Blackcurrant, blackberry, black plum":"黑醋栗、黑莓、黑李","Green apple, lemon, pear":"青蘋果、檸檬、梨","Prune, raisin, fig":"黑李乾、葡萄乾、無花果","Pinot Noir is a red-fruit grape: strawberry, raspberry and red cherry.":"黑皮諾是紅色水果品種：草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃。","Pinot Noir's main aromas are red fruits: strawberry, raspberry and red cherry. Depending on ripeness, the fruit can be crisp and fresh or riper and cooked. Black fruits such as blackcurrant and blackberry belong to other grapes, while dried fruits like prune and raisin point to over-ripe grapes, a trait linked more with Zinfandel.":"黑皮諾的主要香氣是紅色水果：草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃。依成熟度不同，果味可以爽脆新鮮，也可以更成熟、像煮過。黑醋栗和黑莓等黑色水果屬於其他品種，而黑李乾和葡萄乾等果乾則指向過熟的葡萄，這個特徵更常與金芬黛連結。","Why are older or larger barrels often used for Pinot Noir?":"為什麼黑皮諾常使用較舊或較大的橡木桶？","They give less flavour and do not swamp the delicate fruit":"它們給的風味較少，不會淹沒細緻的果味","They add more tannin to a wine that is too light":"它們為太輕盈的酒增添更多單寧","They make the colour darker and deeper":"它們讓顏色更深更濃","They give strong vanilla and coconut aromas":"它們帶來強烈的香草和椰子香氣","Small new oak barrels can overwhelm Pinot Noir's delicate fruit.":"小型新橡木桶可能壓過黑皮諾細緻的果味。","Pinot Noir has delicate red-fruit aromas. Small new barrels give a lot of flavour and can mask them. Older or larger barrels give less flavour, so the oak stays in the background. In the best wines you notice only subtle smoke, clove and vanilla notes sitting in balance with the fruit.":"黑皮諾有細緻的紅色水果香氣。小型新橡木桶帶來大量風味，可能掩蓋這些香氣。較舊或較大的橡木桶給的風味較少，讓橡木退居幕後。在最好的酒中，你只會察覺到與果味平衡的細微煙燻、丁香和香草氣息。","Which tertiary aromas does a fine aged Pinot Noir develop?":"優質的陳年黑皮諾會發展出哪些三級香氣？","With age, Pinot Noir develops tertiary notes of forest floor and mushroom.":"隨著陳年，黑皮諾會發展出森林地表和蘑菇的三級氣息。","Most Pinot Noir is drunk young, but very good and outstanding examples evolve in bottle. Over the years the fresh fruit gives way to tertiary aromas of forest floor and mushroom. Honey and petrol, by contrast, are typical of aged Riesling, while fresh strawberry and raspberry are primary aromas of a young wine.":"大多數黑皮諾都是趁年輕喝，但非常好和傑出的酒款會在瓶中演變。多年後，新鮮的果味讓位給森林地表和蘑菇的三級香氣。相反地，蜂蜜和汽油是陳年麗絲玲的典型特徵，而新鮮的草莓和覆盆子是年輕酒款的一級香氣。","In which type of wine is Pinot Noir most notably blended?":"黑皮諾最常在哪一種酒中被混調？","In sparkling wines such as Champagne":"在 Champagne 等氣泡酒中","In red Bourgogne AOC":"在 Bourgogne AOC 紅酒中","In Côte de Nuits Grand Cru wines":"在 Côte de Nuits Grand Cru 酒款中","In Central Otago reds":"在 Central Otago 紅酒中","Pinot Noir is usually a single-varietal wine; the main exception is sparkling wine like Champagne.":"黑皮諾通常以單一品種釀造；主要的例外是 Champagne 這樣的氣泡酒。","Most still wines made from Pinot Noir are single-varietal, in Burgundy and elsewhere. The best-known exception is sparkling wine, such as Champagne, where Pinot Noir is blended with other grapes. Bourgogne AOC, Grand Cru wines and Central Otago reds are all still Pinot Noir wines, generally made from the grape alone.":"以黑皮諾釀造的靜態酒，無論在布根地或其他地方，大多是單一品種。最知名的例外是氣泡酒，例如 Champagne，其中黑皮諾會與其他品種混調。Bourgogne AOC、Grand Cru 酒款和 Central Otago 紅酒都是黑皮諾靜態酒，一般只用這個品種釀造。","Which statement about Pinot Noir in the vineyard is correct?":"關於葡萄園中的黑皮諾，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is prone to rot and disease":"它容易腐爛和感染病害","It has thick, tough skins":"它的果皮厚而堅韌","It performs best in hot climates":"它在炎熱氣候中表現最好","It is very easy to grow":"它非常容易種植","Pinot Noir is prone to rot and disease, so poor vintages yield little good fruit.":"黑皮諾容易腐爛和感染病害，所以在不佳的年份很少有好的果實。","Pinot Noir is seen as a difficult grape. It has thin skins, needs a cool to moderate climate and is prone to rot and disease. In poor vintages it can be hard to produce even small amounts of quality fruit. This fragility, together with strong demand, helps explain the high prices of its best wines.":"黑皮諾被視為難種的品種。它果皮薄，需要涼爽至溫和的氣候，而且容易腐爛和感染病害。在不佳的年份，連生產少量優質果實都可能很困難。這種脆弱性加上強勁的需求，有助於解釋它最好的酒款為何價格高昂。","In Burgundy, where are the best Pinot Noir vineyards usually located?":"在布根地，最好的黑皮諾葡萄園通常位於哪裡？","On south- and south-east-facing slopes":"朝南和東南的坡地","On north-facing slopes":"朝北的坡地","On flat valley floors":"平坦的谷底","On west-facing slopes":"朝西的坡地","South- and south-east-facing slopes get extra sun and give concentrated wines.":"朝南和東南的坡地獲得額外的陽光，釀出濃縮的酒。","Burgundy's climate runs from cool to moderate, so every bit of sunshine counts. Slopes facing south and south-east receive more light and warmth, helping the grapes ripen. These sites give the most concentrated, complex and age-worthy wines, including the premiers crus and grands crus. Valley floors and north-facing slopes are less favourable.":"布根地的氣候從涼爽到溫和，所以每一點陽光都很重要。朝南和東南的坡地接收更多光照和熱量，幫助葡萄成熟。這些園地出產最濃縮、最複雜、最適合陳年的酒，包括 premier cru 和 grand cru。谷底和朝北的坡地則較不理想。","What is the northern half of the Côte d'Or called?":"Côte d'Or 的北半部叫什麼？","The Côte d'Or splits into the Côte de Nuits in the north and Côte de Beaune in the south.":"Côte d'Or 分為北部的 Côte de Nuits 和南部的 Côte de Beaune。","Burgundy's most celebrated vineyards lie in the Côte d'Or, which is split into two halves. The northern half is the Côte de Nuits, home to villages such as Gevrey-Chambertin and Nuits-Saint-Georges. The southern half is the Côte de Beaune, with villages such as Beaune and Pommard. The Mâconnais and Chablis are other parts of Burgundy, outside the Côte d'Or.":"布根地最著名的葡萄園位於 Côte d'Or，它分為兩半。北半部是 Côte de Nuits，有 Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 等村莊。南半部是 Côte de Beaune，有 Beaune 和 Pommard 等村莊。Mâconnais 和 Chablis 是布根地的其他地區，位於 Côte d'Or 之外。","Which of these Pinot Noir village appellations is in the Côte de Beaune?":"下列哪一個黑皮諾村莊級法定產區位於 Côte de Beaune？","Pommard, like Beaune, is a village in the Côte de Beaune.":"Pommard 和 Beaune 一樣，是 Côte de Beaune 的村莊。","The most famous Pinot Noir villages are in the Côte d'Or. In its southern half, the Côte de Beaune, Beaune and Pommard stand out. Gevrey-Chambertin and Nuits-Saint-Georges, by contrast, are in the Côte de Nuits to the north. Pouilly-Fuissé is a Mâconnais appellation known for white wine, not Pinot Noir.":"最著名的黑皮諾村莊位於 Côte d'Or。在它的南半部 Côte de Beaune，Beaune 和 Pommard 尤為突出。相反地，Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 位於北邊的 Côte de Nuits。Pouilly-Fuissé 是以白酒而非黑皮諾著稱的 Mâconnais 法定產區。","Which of these Pinot Noir village appellations is in the Côte de Nuits?":"下列哪一個黑皮諾村莊級法定產區位於 Côte de Nuits？","Gevrey-Chambertin, like Nuits-Saint-Georges, is in the Côte de Nuits.":"Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 一樣，位於 Côte de Nuits。","The Côte de Nuits is the northern half of the Côte d'Or and is home to celebrated Pinot Noir villages such as Gevrey-Chambertin and Nuits-Saint-Georges. Beaune and Pommard belong to the Côte de Beaune further south. Meursault is also in the Côte de Beaune and is best known for Chardonnay.":"Côte de Nuits 是 Côte d'Or 的北半部，有 Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 等著名的黑皮諾村莊。Beaune 和 Pommard 屬於更南邊的 Côte de Beaune。Meursault 也位於 Côte de Beaune，最著名的是夏多內。","Which description fits a typical red Bourgogne AOC?":"哪一項描述符合典型的 Bourgogne AOC 紅酒？","Light, low tannin, fresh red fruit, for drinking young":"輕盈、低單寧、新鮮紅色水果，適合趁年輕喝","Full-bodied, very tannic, for long ageing":"酒體飽滿、單寧非常多，適合長期陳年","Sweet, low alcohol, simple red fruit":"甜、低酒精、簡單的紅色水果","Ripe black fruit, marked new oak":"成熟的黑色水果，明顯的新橡木桶味","Red Bourgogne AOC is light, fresh and fruity, made to be drunk young.":"Bourgogne AOC 紅酒輕盈、清爽、果香豐富，是要趁年輕喝的。","Bourgogne AOC is the broadest regional appellation, covering the whole of Burgundy. Its reds are light to medium-bodied, with low tannins, high acidity and fresh red fruit. They lack the intensity to age, so they are meant to be drunk young. Although it is the base of the pyramid, strong demand for red Burgundy can still make it expensive.":"Bourgogne AOC 是範圍最廣的地區級法定產區，涵蓋整個布根地。它的紅酒酒體輕盈至中等，單寧低，酸度高，帶有新鮮的紅色水果。它們缺乏陳年所需的濃郁度，所以是要趁年輕喝的。雖然它位於金字塔的底層，但由於布根地紅酒需求強勁，價格仍可能很昂貴。","What is the top level of Burgundy's appellation hierarchy?":"布根地法定產區分級的最高等級是什麼？","Village appellation":"村莊級法定產區","Grands crus are the best single vineyards and sit at the top of the pyramid.":"Grand cru 是最好的單一葡萄園，位於金字塔的頂端。","Burgundy's hierarchy climbs from Bourgogne AOC, the regional appellation, to the village appellations, then Premier Cru vineyards and finally Grand Cru. The grands crus are a handful of small, well-placed vineyards that regularly give outstanding grapes. They have their own appellations and make the most concentrated, complex and long-lived wines, at very high prices.":"布根地的分級從地區級法定產區 Bourgogne AOC 開始，往上是村莊級法定產區，接著是 Premier Cru 葡萄園，最後是 Grand Cru。Grand cru 是少數幾座位置絕佳的小型葡萄園，經常產出傑出的葡萄。它們擁有各自的法定產區，釀出最濃縮、最複雜、最長壽的酒，價格非常高昂。","How is a Burgundy Premier Cru shown on the label?":"布根地的 Premier Cru 如何在酒標上標示？","Village name with Premier Cru, sometimes the vineyard":"村莊名稱加上 Premier Cru，有時還有葡萄園名稱","Only the vineyard name with Grand Cru":"只有葡萄園名稱加上 Grand Cru","Bourgogne followed by the grape name":"Bourgogne 後面接品種名稱","Name of the Côte followed by Supérieur":"Côte 的名稱後面接 Supérieur","A Premier Cru shows the village plus Premier Cru, and may name the vineyard.":"Premier Cru 標示村莊名稱加上 Premier Cru，也可能標示葡萄園名稱。","Some high-quality vineyards within village appellations are classified as premier cru. Wines made only from these vineyards may put Premier Cru next to the village name, for example Gevrey-Chambertin Premier Cru. If the wine comes from a single premier cru vineyard, it can name that vineyard too. Grands crus, by contrast, show the vineyard name with Grand Cru.":"村莊級法定產區內有些高品質的葡萄園被列為 premier cru。只用這些葡萄園的葡萄釀造的酒，可以在村莊名稱旁加上 Premier Cru，例如 Gevrey-Chambertin Premier Cru。如果酒來自單一 premier cru 葡萄園，也可以標示該葡萄園的名稱。相反地，grand cru 則標示葡萄園名稱加上 Grand Cru。","Why do Burgundy village wines usually show more intensity than Bourgogne AOC?":"為什麼布根地村莊級酒款通常比 Bourgogne AOC 更濃郁？","Better-sited vineyards on slopes with good drainage":"位置更好、排水良好的坡地葡萄園","Higher yields and younger vines":"更高的產量和更年輕的葡萄樹","Blending with other grape varieties":"與其他品種混調","Compulsory use of new small barrels":"規定必須使用小型新橡木桶","Village vineyards are often on well-exposed, well-drained slopes that give more concentrated grapes.":"村莊級葡萄園常位於日照良好、排水良好的坡地上，能產出更濃縮的葡萄。","Village appellations are generally better situated than basic Bourgogne AOC vineyards. Many lie on slopes with favourable aspect and free-draining soils, where grapes ripen better. The result is wine with more intensity, complexity and length, and the best can age. The grape is the same; it is the place that makes the difference.":"村莊級法定產區的位置一般比基本的 Bourgogne AOC 葡萄園更好。許多位於坡向有利、土壤排水良好的坡地上，葡萄成熟得更好。結果是更濃郁、更複雜、餘韻更長的酒，最好的還能陳年。品種是一樣的；造成差異的是地方。","What cools the vineyards of Los Carneros?":"是什麼讓 Los Carneros 的葡萄園降溫？","Morning fog from San Pablo Bay":"來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧","Breezes from the Southern Ocean":"來自南冰洋的微風","A ring of mountains":"一圈環繞的山脈","Los Carneros is cooled by morning fog from San Pablo Bay.":"Los Carneros 受到來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧降溫。","Most of California is too warm for Pinot Noir, but some coastal areas are exceptions. In the north of the state, Los Carneros gets morning fog from San Pablo Bay, which lowers temperatures and preserves the fruit. Southern Ocean breezes, by contrast, cool Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula, while a ring of mountains protects Central Otago.":"加州大部分地方對黑皮諾來說太溫暖，但有些沿海地區是例外。在加州北部，Los Carneros 受到來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧影響，降低了溫度並保留了果味。相反地，南冰洋的微風讓 Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 降溫，而一圈山脈則保護著 Central Otago。","Why is Oregon generally cooler than California?":"為什麼奧勒岡一般比加州涼爽？","More northerly latitude and Pacific exposure":"緯度更偏北，並受到太平洋的影響","Very high vineyard altitude":"葡萄園海拔非常高","Fog from San Pablo Bay":"來自 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣","Southern Ocean breezes":"南冰洋的微風","Its northerly position and Pacific influence give Oregon a mostly moderate climate.":"偏北的位置和太平洋的影響讓奧勒岡大致屬於溫和氣候。","Oregon lies further north than California and is exposed to the Pacific Ocean. Together these make it generally cooler, with a mostly moderate climate that suits Pinot Noir ideally. The best wines have complex, fresh red fruit, subtle oak and, with age, earthy and mushroom notes. San Pablo Bay fog, by contrast, cools Los Carneros.":"奧勒岡比加州更偏北，並受到太平洋的影響。兩者結合讓它一般較涼爽，大致屬於溫和氣候，非常適合黑皮諾。最好的酒帶有複雜、新鮮的紅色水果，細緻的橡木味，陳年後還有泥土和蘑菇氣息。相反地，San Pablo Bay 的霧氣讓 Los Carneros 降溫。","In which country is Casablanca Valley, known for good-value Pinot Noir?":"以物超所值的黑皮諾聞名的 Casablanca Valley 位於哪個國家？","Casablanca Valley is a coastal area of Chile, north of Santiago.":"Casablanca Valley 是智利的沿海地區，位於聖地牙哥以北。","Casablanca Valley is a coastal sub-region of Chile, north of Santiago. Sea breezes and morning fog from the Pacific keep it cool, which suits Pinot Noir. The wines show red fruit such as strawberry, sometimes with herbal notes. Pinot Noir is rarely cheap, but Chile's examples often offer excellent value for money.":"Casablanca Valley 是智利的沿海子產區，位於聖地牙哥以北。來自太平洋的海風和晨霧讓它保持涼爽，適合黑皮諾。這裡的酒展現草莓等紅色水果，有時帶有草本氣息。黑皮諾很少便宜，但智利的酒款常常非常物超所值。","Which South African region, cooled by strong southerly breezes, is known for Pinot Noir?":"南非哪個受強勁南風降溫的產區以黑皮諾聞名？","Walker Bay in South Africa is cooled by strong southerly sea breezes.":"南非的 Walker Bay 受到強勁的南方海風降溫。","In South Africa, Pinot Noir is focused on the coolest coastal regions. In Walker Bay, strong southerly sea breezes keep the grapes cool and encourage vibrant red fruit; a number of very good and outstanding wines are made here. Casablanca Valley is in Chile, Yarra Valley in Australia and Martinborough in New Zealand.":"在南非，黑皮諾集中在最涼爽的沿海產區。在 Walker Bay，強勁的南方海風讓葡萄保持涼爽，造就鮮明的紅色水果；這裡出產許多非常好和傑出的酒款。Casablanca Valley 在智利，Yarra Valley 在澳洲，Martinborough 則在紐西蘭。","What makes Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula cool enough for Pinot Noir?":"是什麼讓 Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 涼爽到足以種植黑皮諾？","A protective ring of mountains":"一圈具保護作用的山脈","A latitude above 50°":"高於 50° 的緯度","Southern Ocean breezes cool these two Victorian regions.":"南冰洋的微風讓維多利亞的這兩個產區降溫。","Australia's wine regions are generally warm. In Victoria, however, Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula receive cool breezes from the Southern Ocean and are among the few areas suited to Pinot Noir. Styles range from light and fragrant to riper wines with cooked red fruit such as red plum and strawberry, and medium tannins.":"澳洲的葡萄酒產區一般都很溫暖。不過在維多利亞，Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 受到來自南冰洋的涼爽微風吹拂，是少數適合黑皮諾的地區。風格從輕盈芬芳，到帶有紅李和草莓等煮過的紅色水果、單寧中等的較成熟酒款都有。","Which region makes New Zealand's ripest and most powerful Pinot Noir?":"哪個產區出產紐西蘭最成熟、最強勁的黑皮諾？","Central Otago, mountain-sheltered and very sunny, gives the country's most powerful Pinot Noir.":"受山脈屏障且陽光非常充足的 Central Otago，出產這個國家最強勁的黑皮諾。","Despite its far-southern latitude, Central Otago makes New Zealand's ripest and most powerful Pinot Noir. The wines show pronounced strawberry and red cherry, medium to full body and medium tannins, often with time in oak. Martinborough and Marlborough have cooler climates, while Mornington Peninsula is in Australia.":"儘管緯度極南，Central Otago 出產紐西蘭最成熟、最強勁的黑皮諾。這些酒展現濃郁的草莓和紅櫻桃，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等，常經過橡木桶。Martinborough 和 Marlborough 的氣候較涼爽，而 Mornington Peninsula 在澳洲。","Why can Central Otago ripen Pinot Noir so well despite its southerly latitude?":"儘管緯度偏南，為什麼 Central Otago 能讓黑皮諾成熟得這麼好？","Sheltering mountains and intensely sunny days":"具屏障作用的山脈和陽光強烈的白天","Morning fogs that warm the vineyards":"讓葡萄園變暖的晨霧","Strong southerly sea breezes":"強勁的南方海風","Warm nights and frequent rain":"溫暖的夜晚和頻繁的降雨","A ring of mountains blocks breezes and rain; days are sunny and nights cool.":"一圈山脈擋住了微風和雨水；白天晴朗，夜晚涼爽。","Central Otago is ringed by mountains that shield it from sea breezes and rain. The vines enjoy intensely sunny days followed by cool nights: the strong sun drives ripening, while the cool nights help preserve the fruit. The result is ripe, powerful Pinot Noir with pronounced fruit, medium to full body and medium tannins.":"Central Otago 四周群山環繞，為它擋住海風和雨水。葡萄樹享有陽光強烈的白天，接著是涼爽的夜晚：強烈的陽光推動成熟，涼爽的夜晚則幫助保留果味。結果是成熟、強勁的黑皮諾，果味濃郁，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等。","What problem has resulted from planting Pinot Noir in regions that are too warm?":"把黑皮諾種在太溫暖的產區造成了什麼問題？","Overly alcoholic wines lacking typical Pinot fruit":"酒精過高、缺乏黑皮諾典型果味的酒","Wines that are too acidic and thin":"太酸、太單薄的酒","Wines that are too tannic and harsh":"單寧太多、太粗糙的酒","Wines with too much fresh red fruit":"新鮮紅色水果過多的酒","In over-warm sites Pinot Noir gives alcoholic wines lacking the fruit needed for balance.":"在過於溫暖的園地，黑皮諾釀出酒精高、缺乏平衡所需果味的酒。","Pinot Noir's popularity and limited supply have led to planting in regions that are too warm. There the grapes build up lots of sugar but lose their typical fresh fruit, so the wines end up overly alcoholic and unbalanced. Comparing them with wines from cool or moderate sites shows how important it is to match the grape to the right climate.":"黑皮諾的人氣和有限的供應，導致它被種在太溫暖的產區。在那裡，葡萄累積大量糖分，卻失去了典型的新鮮果味，所以酒最後酒精過高、失去平衡。把它們與涼爽或溫和園地的酒比較，就能看出讓品種與合適氣候搭配有多重要。","Which New Zealand regions are noted for cool climates suited to Pinot Noir?":"紐西蘭哪些產區以適合黑皮諾的涼爽氣候著稱？","Martinborough and Marlborough":"Martinborough 和 Marlborough","Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula":"Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula","Sonoma and Los Carneros":"Sonoma 和 Los Carneros","Walker Bay and Casablanca Valley":"Walker Bay 和 Casablanca Valley","Martinborough and Marlborough have cool climates and make very good to outstanding Pinot Noir.":"Martinborough 和 Marlborough 屬於涼爽氣候，出產非常好到傑出的黑皮諾。","In New Zealand, Pinot Noir is the leading black grape. Martinborough and Marlborough, with their cool climates, both make very good and outstanding examples. Central Otago, more sheltered and sunny, gives the ripest and most powerful style instead. The other pairs of regions are in Australia, California, South Africa and Chile.":"在紐西蘭，黑皮諾是首要的黑葡萄。氣候涼爽的 Martinborough 和 Marlborough 都出產非常好和傑出的酒款。更受屏障、陽光更充足的 Central Otago 則出產最成熟、最強勁的風格。其他組合的產區分別位於澳洲、加州、南非和智利。","Pinot Noir has thin skins. What is the effect on the wine?":"黑皮諾果皮薄。這對酒有什麼影響？","A colour that is usually pale to medium":"顏色通常淺至中等","Very deep colour and very high tannins that need years to soften":"顏色非常深、單寧非常高，需要多年才能柔化","Black-fruit flavours":"黑色水果風味","Thin skins give little colour and low to medium tannin: Pinot Noir is usually pale.":"薄果皮帶來的顏色很少，單寧低至中等：黑皮諾通常顏色淺。","Colour and tannin are extracted from the skins; thin skins mean a pale, soft wine. Pinot Noir's acidity is high, not low, and its fruit is red (strawberry, raspberry, cherry), not black. Thin skins also make it prone to rot.":"顏色和單寧是從果皮萃取的；果皮薄就代表酒顏色淺、口感柔和。黑皮諾的酸度高而不是低，它的果味是紅色水果（草莓、覆盆子、櫻桃），而不是黑色水果。薄果皮也讓它容易腐爛。","What often happens to Pinot Noir in poor vintages?":"在不佳的年份，黑皮諾常會怎樣？","It can be a struggle to make even small amounts of good wine":"連釀出少量好酒都可能很困難","Yields rise sharply":"產量大幅上升","It turns darker and more tannic, with intense black-fruit flavours":"顏色變深、單寧變多，帶有濃郁的黑色水果風味","Pinot Noir is prone to rot and disease: in poor years, good quality is scarce.":"黑皮諾容易腐爛和感染病害：在不佳的年份，好品質很稀少。","Thin skins and susceptibility to disease make Pinot Noir a difficult grape for growers. A cold, wet year does not raise yields of good fruit or make the wine darker or more tannic.":"薄果皮和易感病害讓黑皮諾成為種植者眼中難種的品種。寒冷多雨的年份不會提高好果實的產量，也不會讓酒顏色更深或單寧更多。","Which statement about ageing Pinot Noir is correct?":"關於黑皮諾的陳年，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Most are for drinking young; the finest improve for years":"大多數要趁年輕喝；最優質的能逐年變好","All Pinot Noirs need at least ten years in bottle to be enjoyable":"所有黑皮諾都需要在瓶中至少十年才好喝","No Pinot Noir can age":"沒有任何黑皮諾能陳年","It ages only when blended":"它只有在混調時才能陳年","Many Pinot Noirs are fruity and ready young; only the finest gain complexity over years.":"許多黑皮諾果香豐富、年輕時就適飲；只有最優質的會隨著歲月增添複雜度。","Pinot Noir is refreshing and rarely needs a long wait; the best examples, however, develop forest floor and mushroom and may take years to show their best. It is usually single-varietal, so blending is not needed for ageing.":"黑皮諾令人清爽，很少需要久等；不過最好的酒款會發展出森林地表和蘑菇，可能需要多年才能展現最佳狀態。它通常是單一品種，所以陳年不需要混調。","What decides whether Pinot Noir's red fruit tastes fresh or cooked?":"是什麼決定了黑皮諾的紅色水果嚐起來是新鮮還是像煮過？","The ripeness of the grapes":"葡萄的成熟度","The serving temperature":"侍酒溫度","The amount of yeast added to the juice during fermentation":"發酵期間加入果汁的酵母量","Just-ripe grapes give fresh fruit; overripe grapes from warm areas give cooked fruit.":"剛成熟的葡萄帶來新鮮果味；溫暖地區的過熟葡萄帶來煮過的果味。","This is why climate matters so much: in climates that are too warm, Pinot Noir loses its fresh fruit. In Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula, for example, styles range from light and fragrant to riper with cooked red fruit. Bottle, temperature and yeast do not change the fruit's character.":"這就是為什麼氣候如此重要：在太溫暖的氣候中，黑皮諾會失去新鮮果味。例如在 Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula，風格從輕盈芬芳到帶有煮過紅色水果的較成熟酒款都有。酒瓶、溫度和酵母都不會改變果味的特徵。","Which oak aromas are found, well balanced, in the best Pinot Noirs?":"在最好的黑皮諾中，可以找到哪些平衡良好的橡木香氣？","Smoke, cloves, vanilla":"煙燻、丁香、香草","Honey, petrol and dried apricot":"蜂蜜、汽油和杏桃乾","Oak gives Pinot Noir subtle notes of smoke, cloves and vanilla, balanced by the fruit.":"橡木為黑皮諾帶來細微的煙燻、丁香和香草氣息，與果味平衡。","In great Pinot Noirs the wood stays discreet so as not to hide the delicate fruit. Butter and cream come from malolactic in whites such as Chardonnay; grass and asparagus belong to Sauvignon Blanc; honey and petrol to aged Riesling.":"在偉大的黑皮諾中，木頭保持低調，以免掩蓋細緻的果味。奶油和鮮奶油來自夏多內等白酒的乳酸轉化；青草和蘆筍屬於白蘇維濃；蜂蜜和汽油屬於陳年麗絲玲。","A producer matures a delicate Pinot Noir in small new barrels. What is the risk?":"一位生產者把細緻的黑皮諾放在小型新橡木桶中熟成。有什麼風險？","The oak may overwhelm the delicate fruit":"橡木可能壓過細緻的果味","The wine may turn paler and more acidic":"酒可能變得更淡、更酸","The wine may referment and turn fizzy":"酒可能再次發酵而產生氣泡","It may lose all its tannin and turn white within months":"它可能在幾個月內失去所有單寧而變成白色","Small new barrels give a lot of flavour and can overwhelm a delicate Pinot Noir.":"小型新橡木桶帶來大量風味，可能壓過細緻的黑皮諾。","This is why many producers prefer older or larger barrels, which give less flavour. Oak does not make the wine paler or more acidic, does not cause refermentation and does not remove tannin.":"這就是為什麼許多生產者偏好給風味較少的較舊或較大的橡木桶。橡木不會讓酒更淡或更酸，不會導致再次發酵，也不會去除單寧。","In Burgundy, where does Pinot Noir perform best?":"在布根地，黑皮諾在哪裡表現最好？","In the moderate areas, where it fully ripens":"在溫和的地區，那裡它能完全成熟","In the coldest northern areas, where grapes keep more acidity":"在最冷的北部地區，那裡葡萄保留更多酸度","On the most fertile plains":"在最肥沃的平原","Burgundy ranges from cool in the north to moderate further south; Pinot Noir prefers the moderate parts.":"布根地從北部的涼爽到更南的溫和；黑皮諾偏好溫和的地方。","In moderate areas such as the Côte d'Or, Pinot Noir ripens fully. In the north it is too cool to guarantee this. In Burgundy small site differences matter a lot, so it is not 'the same everywhere', and the best vineyards are on slopes, not fertile plains.":"在 Côte d'Or 等溫和地區，黑皮諾能完全成熟。在北部，天氣太涼爽，無法保證這一點。在布根地，園地之間的細微差異非常重要，所以並非「到處都一樣」，而最好的葡萄園位於坡地，不是肥沃的平原。","Why can even a basic red Bourgogne AOC be expensive?":"為什麼即使是基本的 Bourgogne AOC 紅酒也可能很昂貴？","Because of strong demand for red Burgundy":"因為布根地紅酒的需求強勁","Because it always comes from grand cru vineyards":"因為它總是來自 grand cru 葡萄園","Because it must age at least ten years before release":"因為它上市前必須陳年至少十年","Because it is a sweet wine":"因為它是甜酒","Demand for red Burgundy is so high that even the entry level is costly.":"布根地紅酒的需求如此之高，連入門等級都很昂貴。","Bourgogne AOC is the bottom step of the hierarchy: light, fresh, for drinking young. Its price reflects supply and demand, not site quality. It does not come from grands crus, has no long-ageing rule and is not sweet.":"Bourgogne AOC 是分級的最底層：輕盈、清爽、要趁年輕喝。它的價格反映的是供需，而不是園地品質。它不是來自 grand cru，沒有長期陳年的規定，也不是甜酒。","A label says only 'Gevrey-Chambertin – Appellation Gevrey-Chambertin Contrôlée'. What type of wine is it?":"一張酒標上只寫著「Gevrey-Chambertin – Appellation Gevrey-Chambertin Contrôlée」。這是什麼類型的酒？","A village appellation wine":"村莊級法定產區酒款","A grand cru":"Grand cru","A regional Bourgogne AOC":"地區級的 Bourgogne AOC","A single-vineyard premier cru whose name is not shown":"未標示名稱的單一葡萄園 premier cru","The village name alone indicates a village appellation.":"只有村莊名稱表示是村莊級法定產區。","A premier cru adds 'Premier Cru' to the village name, sometimes with the vineyard. A grand cru carries the vineyard name with 'Grand Cru'. Bourgogne AOC uses the region's name. Village wines offer more intensity and complexity than Bourgogne AOC.":"Premier cru 會在村莊名稱後加上「Premier Cru」，有時還有葡萄園名稱。Grand cru 標示葡萄園名稱加上「Grand Cru」。Bourgogne AOC 使用地區的名稱。村莊級酒款比 Bourgogne AOC 更濃郁、更複雜。","A label reads 'Gevrey-Chambertin – Clos Saint-Jacques – Premier Cru'. What does 'Clos Saint-Jacques' indicate?":"一張酒標上寫著「Gevrey-Chambertin – Clos Saint-Jacques – Premier Cru」。「Clos Saint-Jacques」代表什麼？","The single premier cru vineyard the wine comes from":"這款酒來自的單一 premier cru 葡萄園","The producer's name":"生產者的名稱","A grand cru vineyard with its own appellation, separate from the village":"擁有獨立法定產區、與村莊分開的 grand cru 葡萄園","A neighbouring village":"鄰近的村莊","A wine from one premier cru vineyard may show its name next to the village and the words Premier Cru.":"來自單一 premier cru 葡萄園的酒，可以在村莊名稱和 Premier Cru 字樣旁標示該葡萄園的名稱。","Premier crus are high-quality vineyards within a village appellation: the label gives the village plus 'Premier Cru' and, if the wine comes from one vineyard, its name. Grands crus have their own appellations and need no village name.":"Premier cru 是村莊級法定產區內的高品質葡萄園：酒標標示村莊名稱加上「Premier Cru」，如果酒來自單一葡萄園，還會標示它的名稱。Grand cru 擁有各自的法定產區，不需要村莊名稱。","A label reads 'Le Chambertin – Grand Cru'. Why is no village name used as the appellation?":"一張酒標上寫著「Le Chambertin – Grand Cru」。為什麼沒有使用村莊名稱作為法定產區？","Each grand cru has its own appellation":"每個 grand cru 都有自己的法定產區","Because it is a basic regional wine":"因為它是基本的地區級酒款","Because the producer forgot it":"因為生產者忘了標示","Because the wine blends grapes from several Côte de Nuits villages":"因為這款酒混調了 Côte de Nuits 數個村莊的葡萄","Grands crus have their own appellations: the label shows the vineyard name and 'Grand Cru'.":"Grand cru 擁有各自的法定產區：酒標標示葡萄園名稱和「Grand Cru」。","Grands crus are a handful of small, well-sited vineyards, Burgundy's best, giving the rarest and most age-worthy wines. That is the opposite of a basic regional wine or a multi-village blend.":"Grand cru 是少數幾座位置絕佳的小型葡萄園，是布根地最好的，出產最稀有、最適合陳年的酒。這與基本的地區級酒款或多村莊混調正好相反。","What is the correct order of Burgundy's hierarchy, from bottom to top?":"布根地分級由下而上的正確順序是什麼？","Village, regional, grand cru, premier cru":"村莊級、地區級、grand cru、premier cru","Regional, premier cru, village, grand cru":"地區級、premier cru、村莊級、grand cru","Grand cru, premier cru, village, regional":"Grand cru、premier cru、村莊級、地區級","It starts with regional Bourgogne AOC, then village, premier cru and, at the top, grand cru.":"從地區級的 Bourgogne AOC 開始，接著是村莊級、premier cru，最頂端是 grand cru。","Each step means a smaller area and generally more concentrated wines. Premier crus sit within villages and below grands crus. The last option lists the same hierarchy, but from top to bottom.":"每往上一級，代表區域越小，酒一般也越濃縮。Premier cru 位於村莊之內，低於 grand cru。最後一個選項列出的是同樣的分級，但是由上而下。","Which profile best describes a mature Burgundy premier or grand cru Pinot Noir?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述成熟的布根地 premier cru 或 grand cru 黑皮諾？","Concentrated fruit, subtle oak, pronounced forest floor and mushroom":"濃縮的果味、細緻的橡木味、濃郁的森林地表和蘑菇","Light, fresh fruit with no tertiary notes":"輕盈、新鮮的果味，沒有三級氣息","Very ripe black fruit, very high tannin and dominant new-oak vanilla":"非常成熟的黑色水果、非常高的單寧和主導的新橡木桶香草味","Sweet, with honey":"甜，帶有蜂蜜","The best vineyards give concentrated strawberry and cherry, subtle oak and pronounced tertiary notes.":"最好的葡萄園帶來濃縮的草莓和櫻桃、細緻的橡木味和濃郁的三級氣息。","Facing south or south-east, premier and grand crus get more sun and warmth and make the most complex wines, which evolve for a long time in bottle. Light fruit with no tertiary notes describes Bourgogne AOC; black fruit and very high tannin are not typical of Pinot Noir; it is not a sweet wine.":"朝南或東南的 premier cru 和 grand cru 獲得更多陽光和熱量，釀出最複雜的酒，能在瓶中長時間演變。輕盈、沒有三級氣息的果味描述的是 Bourgogne AOC；黑色水果和非常高的單寧不是黑皮諾的典型特徵；它也不是甜酒。","Why is most of California unsuited to Pinot Noir?":"為什麼加州大部分地方不適合黑皮諾？","It is too warm":"太溫暖了","It is too cold and wet":"太冷太濕了","The law bans French grapes outside designated coastal zones":"法律禁止在指定沿海區域以外種植法國品種","The soils are too poor":"土壤太貧瘠","Most of California is too warm: quality Pinot Noir comes from a few areas near the coast.":"加州大部分地方太溫暖：優質黑皮諾來自少數靠近海岸的地區。","Coastal fog and breezes cool areas such as Los Carneros, western Sonoma and Santa Barbara County, avoiding over-cooked flavours. The problem is heat, not cold; there is no legal ban of this kind and soils are not the factor.":"沿海的霧氣和微風讓 Los Carneros、Sonoma 西部和 Santa Barbara County 等地區降溫，避免風味過熟。問題是高溫，不是寒冷；沒有這類法律禁令，土壤也不是相關因素。","What cools the western parts of Sonoma, suited to Pinot Noir?":"是什麼讓適合黑皮諾的 Sonoma 西部降溫？","Pacific Ocean breezes":"太平洋的微風","The altitude of nearby mountains":"鄰近山脈的海拔","Cold Southern Ocean currents":"寒冷的南冰洋洋流","A ring of mountains that blocks afternoon sun and keeps out rain":"一圈擋住午後陽光、阻隔雨水的山脈","Western Sonoma is cooled by Pacific breezes.":"Sonoma 西部受到太平洋微風的降溫。","In California much depends on closeness to the coast: Los Carneros has San Pablo Bay fogs, western Sonoma ocean breezes. The Southern Ocean concerns Australia and South Africa; the ring of mountains describes Central Otago, which actually has very sunny days.":"在加州，很多事取決於與海岸的距離：Los Carneros 有 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣，Sonoma 西部有海風。南冰洋與澳洲和南非有關；一圈山脈描述的是 Central Otago，那裡其實白天陽光非常充足。","Where is Santa Barbara County and what cools it?":"Santa Barbara County 在哪裡？是什麼讓它降溫？","On the Central Coast; sea breezes from the west and south":"在中部海岸；來自西方和南方的海風","In Northern California; San Pablo Bay fogs":"在北加州；San Pablo Bay 的霧氣","Inland in the Central Valley; the altitude of surrounding hills":"在內陸的 Central Valley；周圍丘陵的海拔","In Oregon; latitude":"在奧勒岡；緯度","Santa Barbara County, on the Central Coast, is cooled by sea breezes from the west and south.":"位於中部海岸的 Santa Barbara County，受到來自西方和南方的海風降溫。","These influences stop Pinot Noir from developing over-cooked flavours. San Pablo fogs concern Los Carneros, in the north; the Central Valley is hot and far from the sea; Oregon is a different state further north.":"這些影響讓黑皮諾不會發展出過熟的風味。San Pablo 的霧氣與北部的 Los Carneros 有關；Central Valley 炎熱且遠離海洋；奧勒岡則是更北邊的另一個州。","A Pinot Noir with ripe strawberry and red cherry and noticeable smoke, cloves and vanilla is most likely:":"一款帶有成熟草莓和紅櫻桃、以及明顯煙燻、丁香和香草的黑皮諾，最可能是：","Californian":"加州的","A basic Bourgogne AOC":"基本的 Bourgogne AOC","A light, fragrant very-cool-climate Pinot Noir made in steel":"在不鏽鋼槽中釀造、輕盈芬芳的極涼爽氣候黑皮諾","A herbal Casablanca Valley wine":"帶有草本氣息的 Casablanca Valley 酒款","Californian Pinot Noirs usually show ripe red fruit and noticeable oak.":"加州黑皮諾通常展現成熟的紅色水果和明顯的橡木味。","The Californian style combines ripe fruit and noticeable oak; the best develop forest floor and mushroom. Bourgogne AOC is light and fresh, without obvious oak; a steel-made wine would show no oak; Casablanca is known for strawberry and herbal notes.":"加州風格結合了成熟的果味和明顯的橡木味；最好的酒款會發展出森林地表和蘑菇。Bourgogne AOC 輕盈清爽，沒有明顯的橡木味；在不鏽鋼槽中釀造的酒不會有橡木味；Casablanca 則以草莓和草本氣息著稱。","Which tertiary notes can a good Oregon Pinot Noir develop?":"優質的奧勒岡黑皮諾可以發展出哪些三級氣息？","Earth and mushroom":"泥土和蘑菇","Cut grass, green pepper and asparagus":"青草、青椒和蘆筍","With age the best Oregon Pinot Noirs develop earthy and mushroom notes.":"隨著陳年，最好的奧勒岡黑皮諾會發展出泥土和蘑菇氣息。","Oregon's mostly moderate climate gives fresh, complex red fruit, subtle oak and, in bottle, earth and mushroom. Petrol and honey belong to Riesling, butter and cream to malolactic in whites, grass and asparagus to Sauvignon Blanc.":"奧勒岡大致溫和的氣候帶來新鮮、複雜的紅色水果、細緻的橡木味，在瓶中則有泥土和蘑菇。汽油和蜂蜜屬於麗絲玲，奶油和鮮奶油屬於白酒的乳酸轉化，青草和蘆筍屬於白蘇維濃。","Which description fits Casablanca Valley Pinot Noir?":"哪一項描述符合 Casablanca Valley 的黑皮諾？","Strawberry, sometimes herbal notes; often excellent value":"草莓，有時帶草本氣息；常常非常物超所值","Black fruit, high tannin and a big body":"黑色水果、高單寧和厚實的酒體","South America's most powerful, expensive Pinot Noir, made in tiny amounts":"南美洲最強勁、最昂貴、產量極少的黑皮諾","A sweet wine":"甜酒","Cooled by Pacific breezes and fog, Casablanca gives strawberry-fruited, sometimes herbal Pinot Noir at good value.":"受到太平洋微風和霧氣降溫的 Casablanca，以實惠的價格出產帶草莓果味、有時帶草本氣息的黑皮諾。","Casablanca Valley, north of Santiago, makes very good Pinot Noir. Although Pinot Noir is rarely cheap, Chile's can offer excellent value. Black fruit and high tannin are not typical of the grape, and the wine is not sweet.":"聖地牙哥以北的 Casablanca Valley 出產非常好的黑皮諾。雖然黑皮諾很少便宜，智利的酒款卻可能非常物超所值。黑色水果和高單寧不是這個品種的典型特徵，這款酒也不是甜的。","Where is Casablanca Valley in relation to Santiago, Chile?":"Casablanca Valley 相對於智利聖地牙哥的位置在哪裡？","North of Santiago, near the coast":"聖地牙哥以北，靠近海岸","South of Santiago, in the hot interior":"聖地牙哥以南，在炎熱的內陸","In the Andes above 2,000 metres, near the Argentine border":"在安地斯山脈海拔 2,000 公尺以上，靠近阿根廷邊境","In the Atacama Desert":"在阿他加馬沙漠","Casablanca Valley is a coastal sub-region north of Santiago.":"Casablanca Valley 是聖地牙哥以北的沿海子產區。","Closeness to the ocean is the key: Pacific sea breezes and morning fog cool the vineyards and allow fresh Pinot Noir, Chardonnay and Sauvignon Blanc. The hot interior is the Central Valley; the Andes and the desert are not where it lies.":"靠近海洋是關鍵：太平洋的海風和晨霧讓葡萄園降溫，造就清新的黑皮諾、夏多內和白蘇維濃。炎熱的內陸是 Central Valley；安地斯山脈和沙漠都不是它所在的位置。","Which Pinot Noir style is found in Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula?":"Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 出產哪一種黑皮諾風格？","From light and fragrant to riper, with red plum and medium tannin":"從輕盈芬芳到較成熟、帶紅李和中等單寧","Only very tannic, dark wines":"只有單寧非常多、顏色很深的酒","Only sparkling wines":"只有氣泡酒","Sweet wines made from grapes left to freeze on the vine":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的甜酒","In these Victorian areas, the style runs from light and fragrant to riper, with cooked red fruit.":"在維多利亞的這些地區，風格從輕盈芬芳到較成熟、帶煮過的紅色水果都有。","Australia is warm overall, but Southern Ocean breezes make these two regions cool enough for Pinot Noir. The riper style shows red plum and strawberry with medium tannin. They are not known for dark, tannic wines or for sweet wines.":"澳洲整體很溫暖，但南冰洋的微風讓這兩個產區涼爽到足以種植黑皮諾。較成熟的風格帶有紅李和草莓，單寧中等。它們不以深色、單寧多的酒或甜酒著稱。","What role does Pinot Noir play in New Zealand?":"黑皮諾在紐西蘭扮演什麼角色？","It is the country's premier black grape":"它是這個國家首要的黑葡萄","It is used only for rosé":"它只用來釀粉紅酒","It is almost absent":"它幾乎不存在","It is grown only on the North Island, as the South Island is too cold":"它只種在北島，因為南島太冷","Pinot Noir is New Zealand's most important black grape.":"黑皮諾是紐西蘭最重要的黑葡萄。","The country makes very good and outstanding Pinot Noir in Martinborough, Marlborough and Central Otago. Marlborough and Central Otago are on the South Island, so the last option is wrong.":"這個國家在 Martinborough、Marlborough 和 Central Otago 出產非常好和傑出的黑皮諾。Marlborough 和 Central Otago 位於南島，所以最後一個選項是錯的。","Which profile is typical of a Central Otago Pinot Noir?":"哪一種風味特徵是 Central Otago 黑皮諾的典型特徵？","Pronounced fruit, medium to full body, medium tannin, often oak":"濃郁的果味、酒體中等至飽滿、單寧中等、常經橡木桶","Very pale, very light-bodied and delicate, for drinking within months":"顏色非常淺、酒體非常輕盈細緻，要在幾個月內喝掉","Very high tannin and black fruit":"非常高的單寧和黑色水果","Sweet and lightly sparkling":"甜而微帶氣泡","Central Otago gives ripe, powerful Pinot Noir with strawberry and cherry and medium tannin.":"Central Otago 出產成熟、強勁的黑皮諾，帶有草莓和櫻桃，單寧中等。","Very sunny days and cool nights give intense wines, often oak-matured, that may need a few years in bottle. The very light style does not match the country's ripest region; black fruit and very high tannin are not typical of Pinot Noir.":"陽光非常充足的白天和涼爽的夜晚帶來濃郁的酒，常經橡木桶熟成，可能需要在瓶中放幾年。非常輕盈的風格不符合這個國家最成熟的產區；黑色水果和非常高的單寧不是黑皮諾的典型特徵。","What is Pinot Noir famous for among Burgundy enthusiasts?":"黑皮諾在布根地愛好者之間以什麼著稱？","Expressing small differences between nearby vineyards":"能表現相鄰葡萄園之間的細微差異","Tasting the same wherever it is grown":"無論種在哪裡嚐起來都一樣","Its very high tannins":"它非常高的單寧","Always being a cheap wine, easy to find in any supermarket":"總是便宜的酒，任何超市都買得到","Pinot Noir reflects the vineyard it comes from with great precision.":"黑皮諾非常精準地反映它所來自的葡萄園。","The most experienced enthusiasts claim to detect differences between plots just metres apart. This is why the Burgundy system gives so much weight to individual vineyards. Pinot Noir has low to medium tannin and is rarely cheap.":"最資深的愛好者宣稱能察覺相距僅數公尺的地塊之間的差異。這就是為什麼布根地的體系如此重視個別葡萄園。黑皮諾的單寧低至中等，而且很少便宜。","A customer wants a refreshing red, enjoyable with or without food and ready to drink. Which grape suits well?":"一位顧客想要一款令人清爽、搭不搭餐都好喝、已經適飲的紅酒。哪個品種很適合？","Young, very tannic Cabernet Sauvignon that needs years in bottle":"年輕、單寧非常多、需要在瓶中多年的卡本內蘇維濃","A Riesling Trockenbeerenauslese":"麗絲玲 Trockenbeerenauslese","Pinot Noir is a fresh red, good with or without food, and rarely needs long ageing.":"黑皮諾是清爽的紅酒，搭不搭餐都好，很少需要長期陳年。","High acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit make Pinot Noir enjoyable young. A young Cabernet can be too tannic; Sauternes and TBA are sweet whites, not reds.":"高酸度、低至中等的單寧和紅色水果，讓黑皮諾年輕時就好喝。年輕的卡本內可能單寧太多；Sauternes 和 TBA 是甜白酒，不是紅酒。","How can regions closer to the equator than Burgundy make excellent Pinot Noir?":"比布根地更接近赤道的產區，如何能釀出優秀的黑皮諾？","Thanks to moderating influences such as sea, fog or altitude":"靠著海洋、霧氣或海拔等調節因素","By always picking very late":"總是非常晚才採收","By adding deeper-coloured black grapes":"加入顏色更深的黑葡萄","By heavy irrigation to cool the vines and lengthen the season":"大量灌溉以讓葡萄樹降溫並延長生長季","Ocean, fog and altitude create cool enough climates even at warmer latitudes.":"即使在較溫暖的緯度，海洋、霧氣和海拔也能創造夠涼爽的氣候。","Los Carneros (fog), Casablanca (breezes and fog), Walker Bay (southerly winds) and Yarra Valley (Southern Ocean) are examples. Picking late in warm areas would give cooked fruit; blending or irrigating does not create a cool climate.":"Los Carneros（霧氣）、Casablanca（微風和霧氣）、Walker Bay（南風）和 Yarra Valley（南冰洋）都是例子。在溫暖地區晚採會帶來煮過的果味；混調或灌溉都無法創造涼爽的氣候。","Which description fits a typical single-varietal Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一項描述符合典型的單一品種卡本內蘇維濃？","Deep colour, high acidity, high tannins":"顏色深、高酸度、高單寧","Pale colour, high acidity, low tannins":"顏色淺、高酸度、低單寧","Medium colour, medium acidity, medium tannins":"顏色中等、酸度中等、單寧中等","Deep colour, low acidity, low tannins":"顏色深、低酸度、低單寧","Thick skins give lots of colour and tannin, and the grape keeps high acidity.":"厚果皮帶來大量顏色和單寧，而這個品種保有高酸度。","Cabernet's grapes have thick skins rich in colour, flavour and tannin. The wine is therefore deeply coloured, dry, with high acidity, high tannins and a medium to full body. Medium acidity and tannins describe Merlot instead, while a pale colour and low tannin do not fit a grape with such thick skins.":"卡本內的葡萄果皮厚，富含顏色、風味和單寧。因此酒的顏色深、不甜，酸度高、單寧高，酒體中等至飽滿。中等的酸度和單寧描述的則是梅洛，而顏色淺、單寧低不符合果皮這麼厚的品種。","Which group of flavours is typical of young Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一組風味是年輕卡本內蘇維濃的典型特徵？","Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint, green bell pepper":"黑醋栗、黑櫻桃、薄荷、青椒","Strawberry, raspberry, violet, white pepper":"草莓、覆盆子、紫羅蘭、白胡椒","Cooked blackberry, liquorice, leather, meat":"煮過的黑莓、甘草、皮革、肉","Red plum, dried fruit, tobacco, earth":"紅李、果乾、菸草、泥土","Cabernet combines intense black fruit with herbal or herbaceous notes.":"卡本內結合了濃郁的黑色水果和草本或植物性氣息。","Cabernet's primary flavours are black fruits such as blackcurrant and black cherry, usually with mint or green bell pepper. Leather, meat, tobacco, earth and dried fruit come with age or belong to other grapes, while liquorice and cooked fruit are typical of warm-climate Shiraz.":"卡本內的一級風味是黑醋栗和黑櫻桃等黑色水果，通常帶有薄荷或青椒。皮革、肉、菸草、泥土和果乾隨陳年出現，或屬於其他品種，而甘草和煮過的果味是溫暖氣候希拉茲的典型特徵。","What does Cabernet Sauvignon need to ripen fully?":"卡本內蘇維濃需要什麼才能完全成熟？","A long, warm growing season":"漫長而溫暖的生長季","A short, cool growing season":"短而涼爽的生長季","Very high yields and irrigation":"非常高的產量和灌溉","Its thick-skinned grapes need plenty of time and warmth to ripen.":"它果皮厚的葡萄需要充足的時間和熱量才能成熟。","Cabernet grows in moderate and warm climates, but in a moderate climate it ripens with difficulty except on the warmest sites. That is why heat-holding gravel matters so much in Bordeaux, and why New Zealand needs its warmest sites. In Napa Valley, by contrast, the warmth and long season are ideal.":"卡本內生長在溫和和溫暖的氣候中，但在溫和氣候中，除了最溫暖的園地外，它很難成熟。這就是為什麼能保溫的礫石在波爾多如此重要，也是紐西蘭需要最溫暖園地的原因。相反地，在 Napa Valley，溫暖和漫長的生長季非常理想。","Why can the best Cabernet Sauvignons age for many years?":"為什麼最好的卡本內蘇維濃能陳年多年？","High tannin and acidity act as preservatives":"高單寧和高酸度起到防腐作用","High residual sugar protects the wine":"高殘糖保護了酒","Low alcohol slows oxidation":"低酒精減緩氧化","Thin skins release few unstable compounds":"薄果皮釋放的不穩定化合物很少","High tannin and acidity are natural preservatives that support long ageing.":"高單寧和高酸度是支撐長期陳年的天然防腐劑。","Cabernet has thick skins and high acidity, so its wine is rich in tannin and freshness. These two elements protect the wine and let it mature for a long time in bottle. Over time the tannins soften and tertiary notes appear, such as dried fruit, earth and forest floor. Typical red Cabernet is dry and thick-skinned.":"卡本內果皮厚、酸度高，所以它的酒富含單寧和清新感。這兩個元素保護酒，讓它能在瓶中長時間熟成。隨著時間，單寧變柔和，並出現果乾、泥土和森林地表等三級氣息。典型的卡本內紅酒是不甜的，果皮也很厚。","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon often matured in oak barrels before bottling?":"為什麼卡本內蘇維濃常在裝瓶前於橡木桶中熟成？","Slow oxygen contact softens the tannins":"緩慢的氧氣接觸讓單寧變柔和","Oak raises the wine's acidity":"橡木提高酒的酸度","Oak removes colour from an overly dark wine":"橡木去除顏色過深的酒的顏色","Oak adds strawberry and red plum notes":"橡木增添草莓和紅李氣息","Fresh from fermentation it is very tannic; oxygen through the wood softens the tannins.":"剛發酵完時單寧非常多；透過木頭進入的氧氣讓單寧變柔和。","A newly fermented Cabernet can taste unpleasantly tannic. In barrel, small amounts of oxygen reach the wine over months or years and soften its tannins. If the barrel is new, it also adds secondary flavours such as smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar. Strawberry and red plum are primary grape flavours instead.":"剛發酵完的卡本內嚐起來可能單寧多得令人不悅。在橡木桶中，少量氧氣在數月或數年間接觸到酒，讓單寧變柔和。如果是新桶，還會增添煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松等二級風味。草莓和紅李則是葡萄的一級風味。","Which secondary flavours does a new oak barrel add to Cabernet?":"新橡木桶為卡本內增添哪些二級風味？","Smoke, vanilla, cloves, cedar":"煙燻、香草、丁香、雪松","Dried fruit, earth, forest floor":"果乾、泥土、森林地表","Leather, meat, black pepper":"皮革、肉、黑胡椒","Smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar come from new oak, not from the grape.":"煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松來自新橡木桶，而不是葡萄。","Secondary flavours come from the winery. In Cabernet, new oak brings smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar, on top of the grape's black fruit. Dried fruit, earth and forest floor are tertiary notes from bottle age, while blackcurrant, black cherry and mint are primary grape flavours.":"二級風味來自酒廠。在卡本內中，新橡木桶在葡萄的黑色水果之上，再帶來煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松。果乾、泥土和森林地表是瓶中陳年的三級氣息，而黑醋栗、黑櫻桃和薄荷是葡萄的一級風味。","Which tertiary flavours does a fine Cabernet Sauvignon develop with age?":"優質的卡本內蘇維濃隨陳年會發展出哪些三級風味？","Dried fruit, earth and forest floor":"果乾、泥土和森林地表","Vanilla, coconut and smoke":"香草、椰子和煙燻","Strawberry, red plum and bell pepper":"草莓、紅李和甜椒","Flowers, black pepper and cherry":"花香、黑胡椒和櫻桃","With bottle age, tannins soften and dried fruit, earth and forest floor appear.":"經過瓶中陳年，單寧變柔和，出現果乾、泥土和森林地表。","Tertiary flavours come from slow ageing. In very good or outstanding Cabernets, time in bottle turns fresh fruit into dried fruit and brings earth and forest floor notes, while the tannins soften. Vanilla, coconut and smoke come from oak, and strawberry and bell pepper are primary flavours.":"三級風味來自緩慢的陳年。在非常好或傑出的卡本內中，瓶中的時間把新鮮果味變成果乾，帶來泥土和森林地表氣息，同時單寧變柔和。香草、椰子和煙燻來自橡木桶，而草莓和甜椒是一級風味。","Why do the Left Bank's gravel soils help Cabernet Sauvignon?":"為什麼左岸的礫石土壤對卡本內蘇維濃有幫助？","They drain fast and hold heat into the evening":"排水快，並能把熱量保持到傍晚","They hold water through dry summers":"在乾燥的夏天保存水分","They are very fertile and raise yields":"非常肥沃，能提高產量","They reflect light and cool the vineyards":"反射光線，讓葡萄園降溫","Gravel sheds water after rain and releases the day's heat, aiding ripening.":"礫石在雨後迅速排水，並釋放白天的熱量，幫助成熟。","Bordeaux has a rainy maritime climate, and Cabernet struggles to ripen on the coolest sites. Left Bank gravel lets water drain away quickly after heavy rain and, by soaking up heat during the day, keeps the vineyard warm into the evening. Cabernet therefore ripens better and gives the great blends of the Haut-Médoc and Graves.":"波爾多屬於多雨的海洋性氣候，卡本內在最涼爽的園地很難成熟。左岸的礫石讓大雨後的水迅速排走，並在白天吸收熱量，讓葡萄園一直溫暖到傍晚。因此卡本內成熟得更好，造就 Haut-Médoc 和 Graves 偉大的混調酒。","Why does the share of Merlot in Bordeaux blends rise in some years?":"為什麼某些年份波爾多混調中梅洛的比例會上升？","Cabernet Sauvignon has not ripened well":"卡本內蘇維濃沒有好好成熟","Merlot has suffered from excess heat":"梅洛受到過熱的影響","The rules require more Merlot in hot years":"法規要求炎熱年份使用更多梅洛","Cabernet has become too soft":"卡本內變得太柔軟","When Cabernet ripens poorly, more Merlot softens the blend's tannin and acidity.":"卡本內成熟不佳時，更多的梅洛能柔化混調的單寧和酸度。","Bordeaux weather varies a lot from year to year, and in some years Cabernet fails to ripen well even on gravel. Under-ripe Cabernet has even harder tannin and acidity and marked herbaceous notes. By raising the share of Merlot, which has medium tannins and ripens more easily, the producer gets a better-balanced blend.":"波爾多的天氣年年差異很大，有些年份即使在礫石上，卡本內也無法好好成熟。未完全成熟的卡本內單寧和酸度更硬，草本氣息也很明顯。提高單寧中等、較容易成熟的梅洛的比例，生產者就能得到更平衡的混調。","Which of these appellations lies within the Haut-Médoc?":"下列哪一個法定產區位於 Haut-Médoc 之內？","Pauillac, like Margaux, is a smaller appellation within the Haut-Médoc.":"Pauillac 和 Margaux 一樣，是 Haut-Médoc 之內較小的法定產區。","Haut-Médoc AOC lies north of the city of Bordeaux, on the Left Bank, and includes appellations such as Margaux and Pauillac, famous for Cabernet-led blends. Pessac-Léognan is part of Graves, south of the city. Pomerol and Saint-Émilion are on the Right Bank, where Merlot dominates.":"Haut-Médoc AOC 位於波爾多市以北的左岸，包括 Margaux 和 Pauillac 等以卡本內為主的混調著稱的法定產區。Pessac-Léognan 屬於波爾多市以南的 Graves。Pomerol 和 Saint-Émilion 位於右岸，那裡以梅洛為主。","Pessac-Léognan AOC lies within which area?":"Pessac-Léognan AOC 位於哪個地區之內？","Pessac-Léognan is the high-quality appellation within Graves, south of Bordeaux.":"Pessac-Léognan 是波爾多以南 Graves 之內的高品質法定產區。","Graves AOC lies south of the city of Bordeaux, on the Left Bank, and includes Pessac-Léognan AOC. As in the Haut-Médoc, Cabernet Sauvignon is usually the leading grape in the blend, supported by Merlot. Saint-Émilion and Pomerol are on the Right Bank instead.":"Graves AOC 位於波爾多市以南的左岸，包括 Pessac-Léognan AOC。和 Haut-Médoc 一樣，卡本內蘇維濃通常是混調中的主要品種，由梅洛輔助。Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 則位於右岸。","Why does Cabernet Sauvignon ripen reliably in Languedoc-Roussillon?":"為什麼卡本內蘇維濃在 Languedoc-Roussillon 能穩定成熟？","Warm climate and steadier weather than Bordeaux":"溫暖的氣候，天氣比波爾多穩定","Gravel soils and heavy Atlantic rain":"礫石土壤和大西洋的大量降雨","Cloud and cool breezes that lengthen the season":"延長生長季的雲層和涼爽微風","High altitude and south-facing slopes":"高海拔和朝南的坡地","The steady warmth of southern France lets Cabernet ripen every year.":"法國南部穩定的溫暖讓卡本內每年都能成熟。","In Languedoc-Roussillon the climate is warm and the weather varies less than in Bordeaux. Cabernet, which needs warmth to ripen, manages it reliably here. You find varietal wines and blends with Merlot and other black grapes, usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. Gravel and Atlantic rain describe Bordeaux instead.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 氣候溫暖，天氣變化比波爾多小。需要熱量才能成熟的卡本內在這裡能穩定成熟。這裡有單一品種酒，也有與梅洛和其他黑葡萄的混調，通常標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。礫石和大西洋的降雨描述的則是波爾多。","Which Napa Valley sub-regions are known for full Cabernets with high, ripe tannins?":"Napa Valley 的哪些子產區以單寧高而成熟的飽滿卡本內著稱？","Oakville and Rutherford":"Oakville 和 Rutherford","Maipo and Colchagua":"Maipo 和 Colchagua","Margaux and Pauillac":"Margaux 和 Pauillac","Coonawarra and Margaret River":"Coonawarra 和 Margaret River","Oakville and Rutherford, in Napa Valley, give full Cabernets with ripe black fruit.":"Napa Valley 的 Oakville 和 Rutherford 出產帶有成熟黑色水果的飽滿卡本內。","Napa Valley has a warm, sunny climate and a long season, ideal for Cabernet. The sub-regions of Oakville and Rutherford give full-bodied wines with intense ripe black fruit and high but ripe tannins. Maipo and Colchagua are in Chile, Margaux and Pauillac in Bordeaux, Coonawarra and Margaret River in Australia.":"Napa Valley 氣候溫暖晴朗，生長季漫長，非常適合卡本內。Oakville 和 Rutherford 這兩個子產區出產酒體飽滿、帶有濃郁成熟黑色水果、單寧高而成熟的酒。Maipo 和 Colchagua 在智利，Margaux 和 Pauillac 在波爾多，Coonawarra 和 Margaret River 在澳洲。","What sets Calistoga apart within Napa Valley?":"Calistoga 在 Napa Valley 中有什麼不同之處？","It is warmer and gives some of the ripest wines":"它更溫暖，出產最成熟的酒款之一","It is cooler and gives light, herbaceous wines":"它更涼爽，出產輕盈、帶草本氣息的酒","It has gravel soils like the Left Bank":"它有和左岸一樣的礫石土壤","It mainly makes wines labelled California":"它主要出產標示 California 的酒","Calistoga, at the valley's far north, is warmer still and gives very ripe, full wines.":"位於山谷最北端的 Calistoga 更加溫暖，出產非常成熟、飽滿的酒。","Napa Valley is already warm, but in the far north, at Calistoga, it is warmer still. Here you find some of the ripest, fullest-bodied Cabernets in the valley. More heat means more ripeness, so richer black fruit and fuller body, not light, herbaceous wines.":"Napa Valley 已經很溫暖，但在最北端的 Calistoga 更加溫暖。這裡有山谷中最成熟、酒體最飽滿的卡本內。熱量越多代表越成熟，因此有更豐富的黑色水果和更飽滿的酒體，而不是輕盈、帶草本氣息的酒。","What should you expect from a Cabernet Sauvignon labelled simply California?":"只標示 California 的卡本內蘇維濃，你應該預期什麼？","Grapes from across the state, a wine to drink young":"來自全州各地的葡萄，適合趁年輕喝的酒","Grapes only from Oakville, a wine for long ageing":"只來自 Oakville 的葡萄，適合長期陳年的酒","Grapes from cool slopes, a light herbaceous wine":"來自涼爽坡地的葡萄，輕盈帶草本氣息的酒","Sonoma grapes, aged only in new barrels":"Sonoma 的葡萄，只在新橡木桶中陳年","The California label allows grapes from the whole state, often the hot Central Valley, for early drinking.":"California 標示允許使用全州的葡萄，常來自炎熱的 Central Valley，適合早飲。","Wines labelled California can blend grapes grown anywhere in the state. Much of the fruit comes from the hot, irrigated vineyards of the Central Valley, and the wines are made for immediate drinking. Any oak flavour often comes from alternatives such as chips or staves, which are cheaper than barrels.":"標示 California 的酒可以混調在全州任何地方種植的葡萄。大部分的果實來自 Central Valley 炎熱、經灌溉的葡萄園，這些酒是為立即飲用而釀的。若有橡木風味，常來自比橡木桶便宜的橡木片或橡木條等替代品。","Which grape is the most widely planted in Chile?":"智利種植最廣泛的品種是哪一個？","Cabernet Sauvignon is Chile's most widely planted grape.":"卡本內蘇維濃是智利種植最廣泛的品種。","Cabernet Sauvignon is Chile's most planted grape, with key sub-regions such as Maipo Valley and Colchagua Valley in the Central Valley. Carmenère is the local speciality, often blended with Cabernet and Merlot, but it is not the most planted. Merlot matters mainly for soft, high-volume wines.":"卡本內蘇維濃是智利種植最多的品種，Central Valley 的 Maipo Valley 和 Colchagua Valley 是重要的子產區。卡門內爾是當地特色品種，常與卡本內和梅洛混調，但不是種植最多的。梅洛主要用於柔和的大量生產酒款。","Maipo Valley and Colchagua Valley are sub-regions of which region?":"Maipo Valley 和 Colchagua Valley 是哪個產區的子產區？","Central Valley (Chile)":"Central Valley（智利）","Central Valley (California)":"Central Valley（加州）","Maipo and Colchagua are key Cabernet sub-regions within Chile's Central Valley.":"Maipo 和 Colchagua 是智利 Central Valley 之內重要的卡本內子產區。","Watch the name: California also has a hot, irrigated Central Valley, the source of wines labelled California. Maipo and Colchagua, however, are Chilean valleys running from the Andes foothills to the Coastal Ranges, with flatter, more fertile valley floors. This range of sites gives producers plenty of choice.":"注意名稱：加州也有一個炎熱、經灌溉的 Central Valley，是標示 California 的酒的來源。不過 Maipo 和 Colchagua 是智利的山谷，從安地斯山脈山麓延伸到海岸山脈，谷底較平坦、較肥沃。這樣多樣的園地給了生產者充分的選擇。","Which notes do Chilean Cabernets from the mountain foothills often show?":"來自山麓的智利卡本內常展現哪些氣息？","Mint and green bell pepper with black fruit":"薄荷和青椒，加上黑色水果","Flowers and black pepper with red fruit":"花香和黑胡椒，加上紅色水果","Coconut and vanilla with no fruit":"椰子和香草，沒有果味","Leather and meat with dried fruit":"皮革和肉，加上果乾","Andean foothill wines pair mint and green bell pepper with black fruit and oak.":"安地斯山麓的酒把薄荷和青椒與黑色水果和橡木結合在一起。","In Chile producers can choose between slopes and valley floors. Cabernets from the Andes foothills often show herbal mint and herbaceous green bell pepper notes alongside black fruit and oak. Flowers and black pepper point to Syrah, while leather and meat are notes of age.":"在智利，生產者可以在坡地和谷底之間選擇。來自安地斯山麓的卡本內常在黑色水果和橡木之外，展現草本的薄荷和植物性的青椒氣息。花香和黑胡椒指向希哈，而皮革和肉是陳年的氣息。","What is a Cape Blend?":"什麼是 Cape Blend？","A South African blend including Pinotage":"含有皮諾塔吉的南非混調","A Chilean blend including Carmenère":"含有卡門內爾的智利混調","An Australian blend including Shiraz":"含有希拉茲的澳洲混調","A French blend including Grenache":"含有格那希的法國混調","In South Africa, Cabernet and Merlot are sometimes blended with Pinotage: the Cape Blend.":"在南非，卡本內和梅洛有時會與皮諾塔吉混調：這就是 Cape Blend。","Pinotage is South Africa's local speciality. When it is blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, the wine is often called a Cape Blend. Carmenère is Chile's speciality, blended with Cabernet in Chilean wines, while Shiraz and Grenache belong to other countries and traditions.":"皮諾塔吉是南非的在地特色品種。當它與卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛混調時，這款酒常被稱為 Cape Blend。卡門內爾是智利的特色品種，在智利酒中與卡本內混調，而希拉茲和格那希則屬於其他國家和傳統。","Why do Stellenbosch Cabernets range from fresh and herbal to full and alcoholic?":"為什麼 Stellenbosch 的卡本內從清爽帶草本到飽滿高酒精都有？","The climate changes with vineyard altitude":"氣候隨葡萄園海拔而變化","The rules impose different styles per zone":"法規對各區規定不同的風格","Yields vary with irrigation":"產量隨灌溉而變化","Gravel soils vary from site to site":"礫石土壤因園地而異","A mountainous region: high vineyards are cooler, low ones warmer.":"多山的產區：高處的葡萄園較涼爽，低處較溫暖。","Stellenbosch is mountainous and its climate ranges from moderate to warm with altitude. On cooler sites Cabernet ripens more slowly and keeps fresh, herbal notes; on warmer sites it ripens further and gives full wines with cooked fruit and high alcohol. A clear case of climate shaping style.":"Stellenbosch 多山，氣候隨海拔從溫和到溫暖。在較涼爽的園地，卡本內成熟得較慢，保留清新的草本氣息；在較溫暖的園地，它成熟得更充分，釀出帶有煮過果味、酒精高的飽滿酒款。這是氣候塑造風格的清楚例子。","What tempers Margaret River's warm climate?":"是什麼緩和了 Margaret River 的溫暖氣候？","Coastal breezes and plentiful winter rain":"海岸微風和充沛的冬季降雨","Cloud cover and cold southerly winds":"雲層和寒冷的南風","The altitude of Andean foothills":"安地斯山麓的海拔","Gravel soils that drain water":"能排水的礫石土壤","Margaret River is warm but cooled by sea breezes and abundant winter rain.":"Margaret River 很溫暖，但受到海風和充沛冬雨的降溫。","Margaret River in Western Australia is known for quality Cabernet, sometimes blended with Merlot. Its heat is tempered by coastal breezes and plentiful winter rain, and the wines show ripe black fruit and subtle oak. Cloud cover and southerly winds are the cooling factors of Coonawarra instead.":"西澳的 Margaret River 以優質的卡本內著稱，有時與梅洛混調。它的高溫受到海岸微風和充沛冬雨的緩和，酒款展現成熟的黑色水果和細緻的橡木味。雲層和南風則是 Coonawarra 的降溫因素。","An Australian Cabernet with marked mint, intense blackcurrant, smoke and cedar, built to age. Where is it most likely from?":"一款帶有明顯薄荷、濃郁黑醋栗、煙燻和雪松、適合陳年的澳洲卡本內。它最可能來自哪裡？","Mint, intense blackcurrant, and smoke and cedar from oak are Coonawarra Cabernet's signature.":"薄荷、濃郁的黑醋栗以及來自橡木的煙燻和雪松，是 Coonawarra 卡本內的招牌特徵。","Coonawarra, a small South Australian region, is cooled by cloud cover and southerly breezes. Its Cabernets show mint, intense blackcurrant, and smoke and cedar from oak, and can develop for many years. Barossa and Hunter Valley are famous for Shiraz, while South Eastern Australia means inexpensive, high-volume wine.":"南澳的小產區 Coonawarra 受到雲層和南方微風的降溫。它的卡本內展現薄荷、濃郁的黑醋栗以及來自橡木的煙燻和雪松，能發展多年。Barossa 和 Hunter Valley 以希拉茲聞名，而 South Eastern Australia 代表平價的大量生產酒款。","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon often blended with Merlot in Hawke's Bay?":"為什麼在 Hawke's Bay，卡本內蘇維濃常與梅洛混調？","In a moderate climate Cabernet ripens only on the warmest sites":"在溫和氣候中，卡本內只在最溫暖的園地成熟","Extreme heat makes Cabernet too alcoholic":"極端高溫讓卡本內酒精太高","The rules forbid varietal Cabernet":"法規禁止單一品種的卡本內","Merlot adds missing tannin and colour":"梅洛補足所缺的單寧和顏色","Hawke's Bay is moderate: Cabernet ripens with difficulty and the more common Merlot completes the blend.":"Hawke's Bay 屬於溫和氣候：卡本內很難成熟，由種植較普遍的梅洛補足混調。","In Hawke's Bay's moderate climate, Cabernet needs the warmest sites to ripen fully. It is therefore often combined with Merlot, which is more widely grown there, giving wines with fresh red and black fruit and herbaceous green bell pepper notes, a sign of a not-too-warm climate. Merlot has medium tannins, so it does not add tannin.":"在 Hawke's Bay 的溫和氣候中，卡本內需要最溫暖的園地才能完全成熟。因此它常與當地種植更廣的梅洛結合，釀出帶有新鮮紅色和黑色水果以及植物性青椒氣息的酒，這是氣候不太溫暖的跡象。梅洛的單寧中等，所以不會增添單寧。","Which recent trend lets Cabernet Sauvignon be enjoyed younger?":"近年的哪一個趨勢讓卡本內蘇維濃可以更年輕時就享用？","Gentler methods that extract less tannin":"較溫和、萃取較少單寧的方法","Longer ageing in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中陳年更久","Later harvests for riper grapes":"更晚採收以獲得更成熟的葡萄","Blending in more Syrah for colour":"混入更多希哈以增添顏色","Extracting less tannin gives fresh, fruity Cabernet for early drinking; Chile succeeds with this style.":"萃取較少的單寧能帶來適合早飲的清新果香卡本內；智利在這種風格上很成功。","Cabernet remains popular with big brands and premium producers, and food helps soften its tannin and acidity. Some producers use gentler winemaking that extracts less tannin, so the wine can be enjoyed young while it is fresh and fruity. Chilean producers are having particular success with this style.":"卡本內在大品牌和頂級生產者中仍很受歡迎，而食物有助於柔化它的單寧和酸度。有些生產者使用較溫和、萃取較少單寧的釀造方式，讓酒可以在年輕、清新、果香豐富時享用。智利生產者在這種風格上尤其成功。","Which statement about Napa Valley and Sonoma wines labelled Cabernet Sauvignon is correct?":"關於標示 Cabernet Sauvignon 的 Napa Valley 和 Sonoma 酒款，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They may contain small amounts of other grapes":"它們可能含有少量其他品種","They must all come from the Central Valley":"它們必須全部來自 Central Valley","They are always light and for drinking young":"它們總是輕盈、要趁年輕喝","They may not be aged in oak":"它們不得在橡木桶中陳年","Even labelled Cabernet Sauvignon, these wines may include a little of other varieties.":"即使標示 Cabernet Sauvignon，這些酒也可能含有少量其他品種。","Napa Valley and Sonoma make many very good to outstanding Cabernets: full, ripe and powerful, especially in Sonoma's warmer inland areas and in Napa sub-regions such as Oakville, Rutherford and Calistoga. Even when the label says only Cabernet Sauvignon, the wine may contain small amounts of other grapes. It is wines labelled California that often come from the Central Valley.":"Napa Valley 和 Sonoma 出產許多非常好到傑出的卡本內：飽滿、成熟、強勁，尤其是在 Sonoma 較溫暖的內陸地區，以及 Oakville、Rutherford 和 Calistoga 等 Napa 子產區。即使酒標只寫 Cabernet Sauvignon，酒中也可能含有少量其他品種。常來自 Central Valley 的是標示 California 的酒。","Where does Cabernet Sauvignon originally come from?":"卡本內蘇維濃原本來自哪裡？","South-west France":"法國西南部","The Northern Rhône, on its steep hillsides":"北隆河的陡峭山坡","Chile's Central Valley":"智利的 Central Valley","Cabernet Sauvignon is a black grape from south-west France.":"卡本內蘇維濃（Cabernet Sauvignon）是來自法國西南部的黑葡萄。","It is the grape behind many of the most famous Left Bank Bordeaux wines and is now grown worldwide. The Northern Rhône is Syrah's home and Burgundy is Pinot Noir's; Chile plants it more than any other grape, but that is not where it began.":"它是左岸許多最著名波爾多酒背後的品種，現在種植於世界各地。北隆河是希哈的故鄉，布根地是黑皮諾的故鄉；智利種植它比任何其他品種都多，但那不是它的發源地。","A grower in a moderate climate wants to plant Cabernet Sauvignon. Which sites suit it best?":"一位溫和氣候的種植者想種卡本內蘇維濃。哪些園地最適合它？","Only the warmest ones":"只有最溫暖的園地","The coolest, windiest ones, to keep acidity":"最涼爽、風最大的園地，以保留酸度","Fertile, damp valley-floor sites":"肥沃潮濕的谷底園地","North-facing sites, sheltered from the sun":"朝北、避開陽光的園地","In a moderate climate Cabernet struggles to ripen except on the warmest sites.":"在溫和氣候中，卡本內除了最溫暖的園地外都很難成熟。","Its thick skins and late ripening need a long, warm season. Cool, windy or north-facing sites would slow ripening further and give green, harsh wines; fertile valley floors give high yields but less ripe grapes.":"它的厚果皮和晚熟特性需要漫長而溫暖的生長季。涼爽、多風或朝北的園地會讓成熟更慢，釀出青澀粗糙的酒；肥沃的谷底產量高，但葡萄較不成熟。","What do Cabernet Sauvignon's thick skins contain in large amounts?":"卡本內蘇維濃的厚果皮含有大量的什麼？","Colour, flavour and tannin":"顏色、風味和單寧","Sugar, water and wild yeast":"糖、水和野生酵母","Floral aromas and black pepper notes":"花香和黑胡椒氣息","Noble rot and honey aromas":"貴腐菌和蜂蜜香氣","The thick skins are rich in colour, flavour and tannin.":"厚果皮富含顏色、風味和單寧。","This is why a single-varietal Cabernet is deeply coloured and very tannic. Black pepper belongs to Syrah, flowers to aromatic grapes, and noble rot to certain sweet wines, not to Cabernet.":"這就是為什麼單一品種的卡本內顏色深、單寧非常多。黑胡椒屬於希哈，花香屬於芳香型品種，貴腐菌則屬於某些甜酒，都不屬於卡本內。","Which of these is NOT a typical primary aroma of Cabernet Sauvignon?":"下列哪一項不是卡本內蘇維濃典型的一級香氣？","Mint":"薄荷","Vanilla comes from new oak barrels: it is a secondary aroma.":"香草來自新橡木桶：它是二級香氣。","Blackcurrant and black cherry are Cabernet's fruit, often with mint or green bell pepper. Smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar come from new oak during maturation instead.":"黑醋栗和黑櫻桃是卡本內的果味，常帶有薄荷或青椒。煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松則來自熟成期間的新橡木桶。","How does Cabernet Sauvignon's fruit change in a warm climate?":"在溫暖氣候中，卡本內蘇維濃的果味如何變化？","It can take on a cooked character":"可能帶有煮過的特徵","It turns more vegetal, with lots of green bell pepper":"變得更有植物味，帶大量青椒","It shifts to fresh red fruit":"轉向新鮮的紅色水果","It develops citrus and white-flower notes":"發展出柑橘和白花氣息","With heat, Cabernet's black fruit can become cooked.":"在高溫下，卡本內的黑色水果可能變得像煮過。","Green bell pepper notes are linked to less ripe grapes, so to cooler climates or years. Cabernet remains a black-fruit grape: fresh red fruit, citrus and white flowers are not its profile.":"青椒氣息與較不成熟的葡萄有關，也就是較涼爽的氣候或年份。卡本內始終是黑色水果品種：新鮮的紅色水果、柑橘和白花都不是它的風味特徵。","Why is blending especially useful for Cabernet in cool vintages in moderate climates?":"在溫和氣候的涼爽年份，為什麼混調對卡本內特別有用？","It softens very high tannin and acidity":"柔化非常高的單寧和酸度","It adds colour and tannin to a wine that is too light and pale":"為太輕盈、太淡的酒增添顏色和單寧","It allows an earlier harvest than planned":"讓採收能比計畫中更早","It removes the need for barrel maturation":"不再需要橡木桶熟成","A blend, for instance with Merlot, tones down the tannin and acidity of under-ripe Cabernet.":"混調（例如與梅洛）能緩和未完全成熟的卡本內的單寧和酸度。","In cool years Cabernet ripens poorly and tastes even harsher. It lacks neither colour nor tannin; if anything it has too much. Blending does not change the harvest date or replace oak maturation.":"在涼爽的年份，卡本內成熟不佳，嚐起來更加粗糙。它既不缺顏色也不缺單寧；如果有什麼問題，是太多了。混調不會改變採收日期，也無法取代橡木桶熟成。","How long is Cabernet Sauvignon often matured in oak before bottling?":"卡本內蘇維濃裝瓶前常在橡木桶中熟成多久？","Several months or even years":"數個月甚至數年","A few days, just long enough to settle":"幾天，剛好足以沉澱","Never: it is always bottled straight after fermentation":"從不：總是在發酵後立刻裝瓶","At least twenty years by law":"依法至少二十年","Freshly fermented Cabernet is very tannic, so it often spends months or years in barrel.":"剛發酵完的卡本內單寧非常多，所以常在橡木桶中待上數月或數年。","A newly fermented Cabernet can taste unpleasantly tannic; slow oxygen contact in barrel softens it. A few days would not be enough; younger styles exist, but it is not always bottled at once, and no rule demands twenty years.":"剛發酵完的卡本內嚐起來可能單寧多得令人不悅；在橡木桶中緩慢的氧氣接觸能讓它變柔和。幾天是不夠的；較年輕的風格是存在的，但它並非總是立刻裝瓶，也沒有規定要求二十年。","A Cabernet Sauvignon shows dried fruit, earth, forest floor and soft tannins. What does this suggest?":"一款卡本內蘇維濃展現果乾、泥土、森林地表和柔和的單寧。這表示什麼？","A high-quality wine aged many years in bottle":"一款在瓶中陳年多年的高品質酒款","A young wine just out of a new barrel":"一款剛從新橡木桶出來的年輕酒款","Grapes picked too early in a cool year":"涼爽年份中太早採收的葡萄","A simple wine made with oak chips":"用橡木片釀的簡單酒款","Dried fruit, earth and forest floor are tertiary notes of aged Cabernet.":"果乾、泥土和森林地表是陳年卡本內的三級氣息。","High tannin and acidity act as natural preservatives: over time tannins soften and tertiary notes appear. A young wine from new oak shows smoke, vanilla and cedar; unripe grapes give vegetal notes; oak chips flavour wines meant to be drunk young.":"高單寧和高酸度是天然的防腐劑：隨著時間，單寧變柔和，並出現三級氣息。來自新橡木桶的年輕酒款展現煙燻、香草和雪松；未成熟的葡萄帶來植物性氣息；橡木片則用來為要趁年輕喝的酒增添風味。","In which Bordeaux vineyards can Cabernet Sauvignon fail to ripen reliably?":"在波爾多哪些葡萄園，卡本內蘇維濃可能無法穩定成熟？","The coolest sites":"最涼爽的園地","The free-draining gravel soils of the Left Bank":"左岸排水良好的礫石土壤","The warmest, sunniest vineyards":"最溫暖、陽光最充足的葡萄園","Irrigated inland vineyards":"經灌溉的內陸葡萄園","In Bordeaux's moderate climate, the coolest sites are not enough for Cabernet.":"在波爾多的溫和氣候中，最涼爽的園地對卡本內來說不夠。","This is exactly why Cabernet dominates on the Left Bank gravels, which drain water and hold heat. Bordeaux is not a region of irrigated vineyards, and warm, sunny sites are where it ripens best.":"這正是卡本內在左岸礫石上佔主導的原因，礫石能排水並保留熱量。波爾多不是灌溉葡萄園的產區，而溫暖晴朗的園地正是它成熟得最好的地方。","Which grape usually leads the wines of Margaux and Pauillac?":"Margaux 和 Pauillac 的酒通常以哪個品種為主？","Margaux and Pauillac lie in the Haut-Médoc on the Left Bank: Cabernet-led blends.":"Margaux 和 Pauillac 位於左岸的 Haut-Médoc：以卡本內為主的混調。","On the Left Bank Merlot is usually in the blend but does not lead; it leads in Saint-Émilion and Pomerol. Syrah and Pinot Noir are not Bordeaux grapes.":"在左岸，梅洛通常也在混調中，但不佔主導；它在 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 才佔主導。希哈和黑皮諾不是波爾多的品種。","A customer wants a red to cellar for many years. Which choice suits best?":"一位顧客想要一款能窖藏多年的紅酒。哪個選擇最合適？","A top Pauillac AOC":"頂級的 Pauillac AOC","A high-volume Cabernet labelled simply California":"只標示 California 的大量生產卡本內","A big-brand Chilean Merlot for drinking now":"適合現在喝的大品牌智利梅洛","A simple, fruity Bordeaux AOC":"簡單、果香豐富的 Bordeaux AOC","The best Left Bank wines, such as Pauillac, have very long ageing potential.":"最好的左岸酒款，例如 Pauillac，有非常長的陳年潛力。","Haut-Médoc Cabernet-led blends combine tannin, acidity and concentration. Wines labelled California, big-brand Chilean Merlot and simple Bordeaux AOC are made to be drunk young.":"Haut-Médoc 以卡本內為主的混調結合了單寧、酸度和濃縮度。標示 California 的酒、大品牌智利梅洛和簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 都是要趁年輕喝的。","Where are the Haut-Médoc and Graves in relation to the city of Bordeaux?":"Haut-Médoc 和 Graves 相對於波爾多市的位置在哪裡？","Haut-Médoc to the north, Graves to the south":"Haut-Médoc 在北，Graves 在南","Haut-Médoc to the south, Graves to the north":"Haut-Médoc 在南，Graves 在北","Both east of the Dordogne, on the Right Bank":"兩者都在多爾多涅河以東的右岸","Both on the Atlantic coast":"兩者都在大西洋沿岸","The Haut-Médoc is north of the city and Graves south of it, both on the Left Bank.":"Haut-Médoc 在波爾多市以北，Graves 在以南，兩者都位於左岸。","The Haut-Médoc, in the Médoc district, includes Margaux and Pauillac; Graves includes Pessac-Léognan. The Right Bank, north and east of the Gironde and Dordogne, is Merlot country with Saint-Émilion and Pomerol.":"位於 Médoc 地區的 Haut-Médoc 包括 Margaux 和 Pauillac；Graves 包括 Pessac-Léognan。吉倫特河和多爾多涅河以北和以東的右岸是梅洛的天下，有 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol。","A single-varietal Cabernet Sauvignon from France's warm south: how is it most likely labelled?":"一款來自法國溫暖南部的單一品種卡本內蘇維濃：它最可能如何標示？","In Languedoc-Roussillon, Cabernet, alone or blended, is usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP.":"在 Languedoc-Roussillon，卡本內無論單獨或混調，通常都標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。","Languedoc-Roussillon's warm, steady climate ripens Cabernet every year. Haut-Médoc and Bordeaux Supérieur are Bordeaux appellations; Crozes-Hermitage is a Northern Rhône Syrah appellation.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 溫暖穩定的氣候讓卡本內每年都能成熟。Haut-Médoc 和 Bordeaux Supérieur 是波爾多的法定產區；Crozes-Hermitage 是北隆河的希哈法定產區。","Which climate makes Napa Valley ideal for Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一種氣候讓 Napa Valley 非常適合卡本內蘇維濃？","Warm and sunny, with a long growing season":"溫暖晴朗，生長季漫長","Cool and cloudy, with southerly breezes":"涼爽多雲，有南方微風","Very rainy, with gravel soils":"非常多雨，有礫石土壤","Cold, with frequent spring frosts":"寒冷，經常有春霜","Napa's sun and long season bring Cabernet to full ripeness.":"Napa 的陽光和漫長的生長季讓卡本內完全成熟。","This is why Oakville, Rutherford and Calistoga wines are full and ripe. Cloud and southerly breezes describe Coonawarra, rain and gravel describe Bordeaux; a cold, frosty climate would not ripen Cabernet.":"這就是為什麼 Oakville、Rutherford 和 Calistoga 的酒飽滿而成熟。雲層和南方微風描述的是 Coonawarra，雨水和礫石描述的是波爾多；寒冷多霜的氣候無法讓卡本內成熟。","In which part of Sonoma can Cabernets as powerful as Napa Valley's be made?":"在 Sonoma 的哪個地方能釀出和 Napa Valley 一樣強勁的卡本內？","The warmer inland areas":"較溫暖的內陸地區","The coolest coast, swept by Pacific fogs":"受太平洋霧氣籠罩的最涼爽海岸","Very cool high-altitude vineyards":"非常涼爽的高海拔葡萄園","Nowhere: Sonoma makes only white wines":"哪裡都不行：Sonoma 只出產白酒","Sonoma's warmer inland areas give similarly powerful Cabernets.":"Sonoma 較溫暖的內陸地區出產同樣強勁的卡本內。","Cabernet needs warmth: the cool coast and cool heights give less ripe grapes. Sonoma, Napa Valley's neighbour, makes many quality reds, not only whites.":"卡本內需要熱量：涼爽的海岸和涼爽的高處帶來的葡萄較不成熟。Napa Valley 的鄰居 Sonoma 出產許多優質紅酒，不只有白酒。","Where does much of the fruit for Cabernets labelled simply California come from?":"只標示 California 的卡本內，大部分的果實來自哪裡？","The hot, irrigated vineyards of the Central Valley":"Central Valley 炎熱、經灌溉的葡萄園","The best plots of Oakville and Rutherford":"Oakville 和 Rutherford 最好的地塊","Cool, hand-picked coastal hillsides":"涼爽、人工採收的沿海山坡","Old, low-yielding vines in Calistoga":"Calistoga 低產量的老藤","These state-wide wines use a lot of fruit from the hot, irrigated Central Valley.":"這些全州性的酒使用大量來自炎熱、經灌溉的 Central Valley 的果實。","These are wines to drink young, with any oak flavour often coming from chips or staves. Oakville, Rutherford and Calistoga are Napa Valley sub-regions for more ambitious wines that carry their own names on the label.":"這些是要趁年輕喝的酒，若有橡木風味常來自橡木片或橡木條。Oakville、Rutherford 和 Calistoga 是 Napa Valley 的子產區，出產更有企圖心、在酒標上標示自己名稱的酒。","How do the Maipo and Colchagua valleys extend?":"Maipo 和 Colchagua 山谷如何延伸？","From the Andes in the east to the Coastal Ranges in the west":"從東邊的安地斯山脈到西邊的海岸山脈","North to south along the Pacific, always on flat land":"沿著太平洋南北延伸，始終在平地上","Over a single steep, south-facing hill":"在單一朝南的陡峭山丘上","On both banks of a large Atlantic estuary":"在一個大型大西洋河口的兩岸","These Central Valley sub-regions run from the Andean foothills to the Coastal Ranges.":"這些 Central Valley 子產區從安地斯山麓延伸到海岸山脈。","Between the two ranges lie slopes and a flatter, more fertile valley floor, giving producers a broad choice of sites. The single hill describes Hermitage, the estuary describes Bordeaux.":"在兩座山脈之間有坡地，也有較平坦、較肥沃的谷底，給了生產者廣泛的園地選擇。單一山丘描述的是 Hermitage，河口描述的是波爾多。","With which local speciality is Cabernet Sauvignon sometimes blended in Chile?":"在智利，卡本內蘇維濃有時會與哪個在地特色品種混調？","In Chile Cabernet appears alone or with Merlot and Carmenère, the local speciality.":"在智利，卡本內可以單獨出現，或與梅洛和在地特色品種卡門內爾一起。","Pinotage is South Africa's speciality used in Cape Blends. Grenache mainly partners Syrah; Viognier is a white grape sometimes co-fermented with Syrah in Côte-Rôtie.":"皮諾塔吉是用於 Cape Blend 的南非特色品種。格那希主要是希哈的搭檔；維歐尼耶是白葡萄，在 Côte-Rôtie 有時與希哈共同發酵。","A Stellenbosch Cabernet comes from a low, warm vineyard. Which style is most likely?":"一款 Stellenbosch 卡本內來自低海拔、溫暖的葡萄園。最可能是什麼風格？","Full body, cooked fruit, high alcohol":"酒體飽滿、煮過的果味、高酒精","Fresh and herbal, with light body and modest alcohol":"清爽帶草本氣息，酒體輕盈，酒精適中","Delicate red fruit and low tannin":"細緻的紅色水果和低單寧","Sweet, made from nobly rotten grapes":"甜，用貴腐葡萄釀造","At low altitude Stellenbosch is warm: full, alcoholic wines with cooked fruit.":"在低海拔，Stellenbosch 很溫暖：帶有煮過果味的飽滿高酒精酒款。","In this mountainous region the climate runs from moderate to warm depending on altitude. The fresh, herbal style comes from higher vineyards. Cabernet stays tannic with black fruit, and it is not used here for sweet botrytis wines.":"在這個多山的產區，氣候依海拔從溫和到溫暖。清爽帶草本氣息的風格來自較高的葡萄園。卡本內依然單寧多、帶黑色水果，而這裡也不用它來釀貴腐甜酒。","Which profile describes a typical Margaret River Cabernet?":"哪一種風味特徵描述典型的 Margaret River 卡本內？","Ripe black fruit and subtle oak notes":"成熟的黑色水果和細緻的橡木氣息","Fresh red fruit, black pepper and floral Viognier notes":"新鮮的紅色水果、黑胡椒和維歐尼耶的花香","Cooked fruit, liquorice and very high alcohol":"煮過的果味、甘草和非常高的酒精","Citrus, honey and residual sweetness":"柑橘、蜂蜜和殘留的甜味","Margaret River gives Cabernet with ripe black fruit and subtle oak.":"Margaret River 出產帶有成熟黑色水果和細緻橡木味的卡本內。","The region is warm but tempered by coastal breezes and plentiful winter rain; Cabernet is sometimes blended with Merlot. Black pepper and Viognier point to Syrah, liquorice and very high alcohol to hotter styles.":"這個產區很溫暖，但受到海岸微風和充沛冬雨的緩和；卡本內有時會與梅洛混調。黑胡椒和維歐尼耶指向希哈，甘草和非常高的酒精則指向更炎熱的風格。","What moderates the climate of Coonawarra?":"是什麼調節了 Coonawarra 的氣候？","Cloud cover and cooling southerly breezes":"雲層和帶來涼意的南方微風","Andean altitude":"安地斯山脈的海拔","Morning fogs from a nearby bay":"來自鄰近海灣的晨霧","A large estuary nearby":"附近的大型河口","Small Coonawarra, in South Australia, is cooled by cloud and southerly breezes.":"南澳的小產區 Coonawarra 受到雲層和南方微風的降溫。","The result is Cabernet with mint, intense blackcurrant and often smoke and cedar from oak, able to age. Andean altitude belongs to Chile, bay fogs to Los Carneros in California, the estuary to Bordeaux.":"結果是帶有薄荷、濃郁黑醋栗、常有來自橡木的煙燻和雪松、能陳年的卡本內。安地斯山脈的海拔屬於智利，海灣的霧氣屬於加州的 Los Carneros，河口屬於波爾多。","What style does a Hawke's Bay Cabernet-Merlot blend usually have?":"Hawke's Bay 的卡本內與梅洛混調通常是什麼風格？","Fresh red and black fruit with green bell pepper":"新鮮的紅色和黑色水果，帶青椒","Cooked black fruit and liquorice":"煮過的黑色水果和甘草","Strawberry and raspberry with no tannin at all":"草莓和覆盆子，完全沒有單寧","Apricot and honey from noble rot":"來自貴腐菌的杏桃和蜂蜜","The moderate climate gives blends with fresh red and black fruit and herbaceous notes.":"溫和的氣候帶來有新鮮紅色和黑色水果以及草本氣息的混調。","In Hawke's Bay Cabernet needs the warmest sites and is joined with the more widely grown Merlot. Cooked fruit and liquorice belong to warm climates; the tannin does not disappear, and noble rot concerns sweet wines.":"在 Hawke's Bay，卡本內需要最溫暖的園地，並與種植較廣的梅洛結合。煮過的果味和甘草屬於溫暖氣候；單寧不會消失，而貴腐菌與甜酒有關。","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon a popular choice with food?":"為什麼卡本內蘇維濃是受歡迎的佐餐選擇？","Food can help soften its tannin and acidity":"食物有助於柔化它的單寧和酸度","Its residual sugar balances salty dishes":"它的殘糖能平衡鹹的菜餚","Its tannins are low enough to suit any dish":"它的單寧低到適合任何菜餚","Its floral aromas enhance desserts":"它的花香能提升甜點","At the table, food helps tone down Cabernet's high tannin and acidity.":"在餐桌上，食物有助於緩和卡本內的高單寧和高酸度。","Cabernet is dry with high tannin and acidity: it is not sweet, low in tannin or floral. It is also very familiar to consumers and popular with both big brands and premium producers.":"卡本內不甜，單寧和酸度都高：它不甜、不低單寧，也沒有花香。消費者對它也非常熟悉，大品牌和頂級生產者都很喜愛它。","In which country are gently extracted Cabernets, made to drink young and fruity, proving successful?":"在哪個國家，以溫和萃取、要趁年輕果香豐富時喝的卡本內獲得成功？","France, on Bordeaux's Left Bank":"法國，波爾多左岸","Chilean producers are succeeding with this lower-tannin, younger style.":"智利生產者在這種單寧較低、較年輕的風格上獲得成功。","Extracting less tannin lets the wine be enjoyed fresh and fruity without long ageing. The Left Bank is known for long-lived Cabernet; New Zealand grows little of it and Germany is not Cabernet country.":"萃取較少的單寧，讓酒不需長期陳年就能在清新果香時享用。左岸以長壽的卡本內著稱；紐西蘭種得很少，而德國也不是卡本內的產地。","Which of these regions is NOT a key region for Cabernet Sauvignon?":"下列哪一個產區不是卡本內蘇維濃的重要產區？","Hunter Valley is known for Shiraz, not Cabernet.":"Hunter Valley 以希拉茲而不是卡本內著稱。","Coonawarra and Margaret River are Australia's key Cabernet regions, Stellenbosch is South Africa's. Hunter Valley, in New South Wales, is famous for medium-bodied Shiraz.":"Coonawarra 和 Margaret River 是澳洲重要的卡本內產區，Stellenbosch 是南非的。新南威爾斯的 Hunter Valley 以酒體中等的希拉茲聞名。","A label reads Oakville, Napa Valley, Cabernet Sauvignon. What wine can you expect?":"一張酒標上寫著 Oakville, Napa Valley, Cabernet Sauvignon。你可以預期什麼樣的酒？","Full body, ripe black fruit, high ripe tannins":"酒體飽滿、成熟的黑色水果、高而成熟的單寧","Light and herbal, from grapes grown across the state":"輕盈帶草本氣息，用全州各地種植的葡萄釀造","A Pinotage blend typical of the coast":"典型的沿海皮諾塔吉混調","A sweet late-harvest wine":"甜型晚收酒","Oakville is a Napa Valley sub-region for full, ripe Cabernet.":"Oakville 是 Napa Valley 出產飽滿成熟卡本內的子產區。","The warm, sunny climate gives full wines with high but ripe tannins; they may contain small amounts of other grapes. Wines from across the state are labelled California; Pinotage is South African.":"溫暖晴朗的氣候帶來單寧高而成熟的飽滿酒款；它們可能含有少量其他品種。來自全州的酒標示為 California；皮諾塔吉是南非的。","Which structure is typical of a single-varietal Merlot?":"哪一種結構是單一品種梅洛的典型特徵？","Medium acidity and medium tannins":"中等酸度和中等單寧","High acidity and high tannins":"高酸度和高單寧","Low acidity and low tannins":"低酸度和低單寧","High acidity and low tannins":"高酸度和低單寧","Merlot usually gives dry wines with both acidity and tannins at a medium level.":"梅洛通常釀出酸度和單寧都在中等水準的不甜酒。","This medium structure explains Merlot's softness and its versatility. It is why the grape is used to soften more tannic varieties such as Cabernet Sauvignon, which has high acidity and tannins. A light style can be drunk young and unoaked, while a richer style handles barrel ageing well.":"這種中等的結構解釋了梅洛的柔和與多才多藝。這就是為什麼它被用來柔化卡本內蘇維濃等單寧更多的品種，卡本內的酸度和單寧都很高。輕盈的風格可以趁年輕喝且不經橡木桶，較豐潤的風格則很能承受橡木桶陳年。","Which flavours are typical of Merlot made from just-ripe grapes?":"哪些風味是用剛成熟葡萄釀造的梅洛的典型特徵？","Strawberry, red plum and green bell pepper":"草莓、紅李和青椒","Cooked blackberry, black plum and liquorice":"煮過的黑莓、黑李和甘草","Black cherry, black pepper and leather":"黑櫻桃、黑胡椒和皮革","Just-ripe grapes give fresh red fruit and a herbaceous green bell pepper note.":"剛成熟的葡萄帶來新鮮的紅色水果和植物性的青椒氣息。","Merlot's profile depends on ripeness. Just-ripe grapes give light to medium-bodied wines with strawberry, red plum and green bell pepper. Riper grapes bring medium to full body and cooked black fruit such as blackberry and black plum. Blackcurrant and mint point instead to Cabernet Sauvignon, black pepper to Syrah.":"梅洛的風味特徵取決於成熟度。剛成熟的葡萄釀出酒體輕盈至中等、帶有草莓、紅李和青椒的酒。較成熟的葡萄則帶來中等至飽滿的酒體，以及黑莓和黑李等煮過的黑色水果。黑醋栗和薄荷則指向卡本內蘇維濃，黑胡椒指向希哈。","How can a grower in a moderate climate make a riper, fuller Merlot?":"溫和氣候的種植者如何釀出更成熟、更飽滿的梅洛？","By harvesting later":"更晚採收","By increasing yields":"提高產量","By using oak chips":"使用橡木片","By co-fermenting with Viognier":"與維歐尼耶共同發酵","Picking later lets the grapes ripen further, giving fuller body and cooked black fruit.":"較晚採收讓葡萄更成熟，帶來更飽滿的酒體和煮過的黑色水果。","Merlot's rich style, with medium to full body and cooked black fruit, comes from very ripe grapes. A warm climate delivers this easily, but in a moderate climate it can be reached by leaving the grapes on the vine longer. Oak adds flavour but does not make grapes riper, and higher yields would tend to work the other way.":"梅洛的豐潤風格，酒體中等至飽滿、帶有煮過的黑色水果，來自非常成熟的葡萄。溫暖的氣候很容易做到這一點，但在溫和氣候中，可以藉由讓葡萄在樹上留得更久來達成。橡木桶會增添風味，但不會讓葡萄更成熟，而提高產量往往會產生反效果。"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/l2"]=1;
